<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover"><style>body{margin:0;background:#080808}[hidden]{display:none!important}</style>
<title>BL00D.MONEY · The Genocide Economy, Mapped</title>
<meta name="description" content="Who is profiting from Israel's genocidal campaign on the Middle East? A sourced map of the money, weapons and people.">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Hanken+Grotesk:wght@300;400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap">
<style>
/* Layout: one full-bleed network canvas; thin index rail left, dossier right, mode strip bottom. Single dark world by design. */
:root{
  --bg:#080808; --panel:#0e0e0d; --fg:#f1f1ed; --fg2:#949494; --fg3:#5c5c5a; --line:#343434; --rule:#1f1f1e;
  --signal:#e8ff00;
  --c-person:#a7d8e0; --c-company:#e8ff00; --c-gov:#4f9dff; --c-country:#b48cff; --c-fund:#ff5c2b; --c-weapon:#e5322d; --c-contract:#e2e2da; --c-org:#6fd38a; --c-agg:#8b8b86; --sel:#ffffff;
  --paper:#ecebe4; --ink:#141412; --ink2:#5d5b54; --red:#c8102e;
  --f-own:#ff5c2b; --f-contract:#e5322d; --f-money:#ffc93c; --f-politics:#6fd38a; --f-oppose:#ff3b8d; --f-role:#a7d8e0; --f-tech:#4f9dff;
  --sans:"Hanken Grotesk","Helvetica Neue",Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;
  --mono:"IBM Plex Mono",ui-monospace,"SFMono-Regular",Menlo,Consolas,monospace;
  color-scheme:dark;
}
html,body{height:100%}
body{background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font-family:var(--sans);overflow:hidden;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
*{box-sizing:border-box;scrollbar-width:none}
*::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
::selection{background:var(--fg);color:var(--bg)}
button{font:inherit;color:inherit;background:none;border:0;cursor:pointer;padding:0}
:focus-visible{outline:1px solid var(--signal);outline-offset:2px}
.mono{font-family:var(--mono);letter-spacing:.02em}
.tiny{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--fg2)}
#app{position:fixed;inset:0;padding-top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);padding-bottom:env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)}
canvas#net{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;display:block;cursor:grab}
canvas#net.hovering{cursor:pointer}

/* header */
header{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:env(safe-area-inset-top,0px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr auto;align-items:start;gap:16px;padding:14px 18px;pointer-events:none;z-index:8}
header>*{pointer-events:auto}
.mark{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:3px}
.mark b{font-weight:500;font-size:15px;letter-spacing:.08em}
.mark b i{font-style:normal;color:var(--signal)}
.searchwrap{justify-self:center;width:min(440px,100%);position:relative}
#q{width:100%;background:transparent;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--fg);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.06em;padding:6px 0 6px 18px;text-transform:uppercase}
#q::placeholder{color:var(--fg3)}
.searchwrap:before{content:"/";position:absolute;left:0;top:6px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--signal)}
#results{position:absolute;top:34px;left:0;right:0;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--rule);max-height:60vh;overflow:auto;padding:6px 0}
#results .grp{padding:8px 12px 2px}
#results button{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;width:100%;text-align:left;padding:5px 12px;font-size:13px}
#results button:hover,#results button.on{background:#161615;color:var(--signal)}
#results button span:last-child{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--fg3)}
nav.top{display:flex;gap:18px;align-items:center}
nav.top button{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--fg2)}
nav.top button[aria-pressed="true"],nav.top button:hover{color:var(--fg)}
nav.top button[aria-pressed="true"]:before{content:"● ";color:var(--signal)}

/* left rail */
#rail{position:absolute;left:0;top:78px;bottom:64px;width:224px;padding:10px 18px;overflow:auto;z-index:4;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:22px;scrollbar-width:none}
#rail h3{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:400;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--fg3);margin:0 0 8px;padding-bottom:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);display:flex;justify-content:space-between}
.opt{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;width:100%;padding:3px 0;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--fg2);text-align:left}
.opt .dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;border:1px solid currentColor;flex:none}
.opt[aria-pressed="true"]{color:var(--fg)}
.opt[aria-pressed="true"] .dot{background:currentColor}
.opt .n{margin-left:auto;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--fg3)}
.opt .sw{width:6px;height:6px;flex:none}
.typ{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:2px 0;font-size:12.5px}
.typ .dotb{width:16px;height:16px;display:grid;place-items:center;flex:none}
.typ .dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;border:1px solid currentColor}
.typ .dotb[aria-pressed="true"] .dot{background:currentColor}
.typ .lab{color:var(--fg2);text-align:left;flex:1;padding:2px 4px;margin-left:-4px;border-radius:2px}
.typ .lab:hover{color:var(--fg)}
.typ .lab[aria-pressed="true"]{color:var(--bg);background:var(--hl,var(--fg))}
.typ .n{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--fg3)}
.railtabs{display:flex;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);gap:18px;margin-bottom:-8px}
.railtabs button{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--fg3);padding:4px 0 7px;border-bottom:1px solid transparent;margin-bottom:-1px}
.railtabs button[aria-pressed="true"]{color:var(--fg);border-color:var(--signal)}
.hint{font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--fg3);margin:0}
/* case files: a drawer of index cards, tabs staggered like a card catalogue */
.drawer{display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:4px}
.file{position:relative;height:31px;width:100%;text-align:left;color:var(--fg2)}
.file:before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;height:9px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:0;border-radius:4px 4px 0 0;background:var(--bg)}
.file .tab{position:absolute;bottom:8px;left:var(--off);width:118px;height:22px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:0 12px;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.02em;z-index:1}
.file .tab:before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;border:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:0;border-radius:5px 5px 0 0;background:var(--bg);transform:perspective(26px) rotateX(7deg);transform-origin:bottom;z-index:-1;transition:background .3s,border-color .3s}
.file .tab b{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:400;font-size:10px;color:var(--fg3)}
.file:hover{color:var(--fg)}.file:hover .tab:before{border-color:var(--fg2)}
.file[aria-pressed="true"]{color:var(--bg)}.file[aria-pressed="true"] .tab b{color:var(--bg)}
.file[aria-pressed="true"] .tab:before{background:var(--fg);border-color:var(--fg)}
.drawerfoot{width:100%;height:34px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-top:0;display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-top:-1px;cursor:pointer;transition:border-color .2s,background .2s}.drawerfoot span{white-space:nowrap}.drawerfoot i{font-style:normal;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--fg3);transition:color .2s}.drawerfoot:hover{border-color:var(--signal);background:rgba(232,255,0,.04)}.drawerfoot:hover i{color:var(--signal)}
.drawerfoot span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#111;background:var(--signal);padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px}
.seg{display:flex;gap:0;border:1px solid var(--rule)}
.seg button{flex:1;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;padding:5px 0;color:var(--fg2)}
.seg button[aria-pressed="true"]{background:var(--fg);color:var(--bg)}
.legend-line{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:12px;color:var(--fg2);padding:2px 0}
.legend-line svg{flex:none}

/* right dossier */
#dossier{position:absolute;right:0;top:78px;bottom:64px;width:360px;padding:6px 20px 24px;overflow:auto;z-index:4;background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(8,8,8,0),rgba(8,8,8,.86) 14%);scrollbar-width:none}
#dossier .idrow{display:flex;justify-content:space-between}
#dossier h1{font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(26px,3vw,38px);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.015em;margin:10px 0 14px;text-wrap:balance}
.kv{display:grid;grid-template-columns:96px 1fr;gap:6px 12px;font-size:12.5px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}
.kv dt{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--fg3);padding-top:2px}
.kv dd{margin:0;color:var(--fg)}
.sec{border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:12px 0 6px}
.sec h4{margin:0 0 10px;font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:400;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--fg3);display:flex;justify-content:space-between}
.prose{font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#d8d8d3;max-width:62ch}
.srcs{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 10px;margin-top:8px}
.srcs a{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--fg2);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.srcs a:hover{color:var(--signal);border-color:var(--signal)}
.big{font-size:40px;font-weight:300;letter-spacing:-.02em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;line-height:1}
.counts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:8px 16px}
.counts div{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:8px}
.counts b{font-weight:400;font-size:22px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.own{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 52px;gap:4px 10px;align-items:center;font-size:12px}
.own .dots{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:1px;color:var(--fg2);white-space:nowrap}
.own .pct{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.rel{display:grid;grid-template-columns:14px 1fr auto;gap:2px 8px;width:100%;text-align:left;padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #141413;font-size:12.5px;align-items:baseline}
.rel:hover .who{color:var(--signal)}
.rel .g{font-size:10px;color:var(--fg2)}
.rel .what{grid-column:2/4;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--fg3);text-transform:uppercase}
.rel .amt{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.nums{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:8px;padding:12px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}
.nums b{display:block;font-weight:300;font-size:21px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:var(--signal)}
.nums b.dim{color:var(--fg)}
.hold{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 64px;gap:2px 10px;width:100%;text-align:left;padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #141413;font-size:12.5px}
.hold:hover .who{color:var(--signal)}
.hold .v{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--signal)}
.hold .bar{grid-column:1/3;height:3px;background:#1a1a19;position:relative}
.hold .bar i{position:absolute;left:0;top:0;bottom:0;background:var(--c-fund)}
.hold .sub{grid-column:1/3;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--fg3);letter-spacing:.04em}
.grp{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--fg2);margin:14px 0 2px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px}
.grp i{width:10px;height:2px;display:inline-block}
.rel .ctx{grid-column:2/4;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.45;color:var(--fg2)}
.mx{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.mx th{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:400;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--fg3);padding:4px 2px;text-align:right;white-space:nowrap}
.mx th:first-child,.mx td:first-child{text-align:left}
.mx td{padding:0;border-bottom:1px solid #141413;text-align:right}
.mx td button{width:100%;text-align:right;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;padding:6px 2px}
.mx td button:hover{outline:1px solid var(--signal)}
.mx td.co{font-size:11.5px;padding:6px 6px 6px 0;white-space:nowrap;max-width:104px;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.mx td.tot{font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--signal);padding-left:6px}
.case h1{margin-top:6px}
.chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 6px}
.chips button{font-size:11.5px;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:3px 8px;border-radius:999px;color:var(--fg2);display:flex;gap:6px;align-items:center}
.chips button:hover{color:var(--fg);border-color:var(--fg2)}
.chips i{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;display:inline-block}
.plain{font-size:15px;line-height:1.4;margin:8px 0 10px;color:var(--fg)}
.plain em{font-style:normal;color:var(--signal);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px}
.path{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--fg2)}
.path button{color:var(--fg2);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:var(--line);text-underline-offset:3px}
.path button:hover{color:var(--signal)}
.intro p{font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.55;color:#cfcfca;margin:0 0 12px;max-width:60ch}
.stat3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:10px;margin:8px 0 10px}
#dossier p.sub{font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.45;color:var(--signal);margin:-4px 0 16px;max-width:40ch}
.moneystat{border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:10px 0 12px;margin:0 0 18px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;column-gap:12px;align-items:baseline}
.moneystat b{font-weight:300;font-size:30px;color:var(--signal);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.moneystat.casetot,.moneystat.profit{margin:8px 0 12px}.moneystat .mparts{grid-column:1/-1}
.wantedS{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;border:3px solid #e5322d;color:#e5322d;padding:4px 10px 6px;margin:8px 0 10px;transform:rotate(-1deg);width:max-content;max-width:100%}.wantedS b{font-weight:800;font-size:34px;letter-spacing:.08em;line-height:1}.wantedS span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.1em}
.moneystat .blocks{grid-column:1/-1;display:flex;height:14px;gap:2px;margin:10px 0 8px}.moneystat .blocks i{display:block;min-width:3px}
.mparts{grid-column:1/-1;list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:3px}.mparts li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:10px 1fr auto;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;font-size:11px;color:var(--fg2)}.mparts .sw{width:10px;height:10px;align-self:center}.mparts .v{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--fg)}
.moneystat .note{grid-column:1/-1;font-size:11px;line-height:1.45;color:var(--fg3);margin-top:4px}
.stat3 b{display:block;font-weight:300;font-size:30px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.closebtn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--fg2)}
.closebtn:hover{color:var(--signal)}

/* bottom bar */
#modes{position:absolute;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);bottom:calc(16px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px));display:flex;gap:6px;z-index:5;max-width:calc(100% - 32px);overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:none}
#modes button{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;padding:7px 14px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;color:var(--fg2);white-space:nowrap;transition:border-color .4s,color .4s,background .4s}
#modes button:hover{color:var(--fg);border-color:var(--fg2)}
#modes button[aria-pressed="true"]{color:var(--bg);background:var(--fg);border-color:var(--fg)}
#modes button[disabled]{opacity:.35;cursor:not-allowed}
#crumbs{position:absolute;left:18px;bottom:calc(20px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px));z-index:5;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--fg3);max-width:28vw}
#crumbs button{color:var(--fg2)}#crumbs button:hover{color:var(--signal)}#crumbs .back{font-size:13px;line-height:1;padding:0 8px 0 0;margin-right:4px;border-right:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--fg3)}
#meta{position:absolute;right:378px;bottom:calc(62px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px));z-index:5;text-align:right;line-height:1.6}
#ctrls{position:absolute;right:386px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;z-index:5}
#ctrls button{width:30px;height:30px;border:1px solid var(--rule);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--fg2);background:rgba(8,8,8,.7)}
#ctrls button:hover{color:var(--fg);border-color:var(--fg2)}
#zoomlbl{position:absolute;left:242px;top:84px;z-index:3}

/* relationship inspector */
#insp{position:absolute;z-index:8;width:min(380px,calc(100vw - 32px));max-height:min(62vh,560px);overflow:auto;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);padding:14px 16px 12px;font-size:12.5px;box-shadow:0 10px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.6)}
#insp .ends{font-size:15px;line-height:1.3;margin:8px 0 10px}
#insp .ends .arr{font-family:var(--mono);color:var(--signal);display:block;margin:2px 0}
#insp .ex{font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#c9c9c4;border-left:1px solid var(--line);padding-left:10px;margin:8px 0}
#insp a{color:var(--fg);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.06em}
#insp a:hover{color:var(--signal)}

/* overlays scroll under the header: give it a ground while one is open */
#app:has(#tips:not([hidden])) header,#app:has(#caselist:not([hidden])) header,#app:has(#index:not([hidden])) header{background:var(--bg)}
@media (max-width:900px){nav.top{gap:11px}nav.top button{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.06em;white-space:nowrap}#tips{padding-top:120px}}
/* tips page */
#tips{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:7;background:var(--bg);overflow:auto;overscroll-behavior:contain;padding:84px 18px 90px;scrollbar-width:none}#tips::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
#tips .wrap{max-width:720px;margin:0 auto}
#tips .head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:18px}
#tips h2{font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,56px);letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:0;line-height:1}
#tips h2 mark{background:none;color:var(--signal)}
#tips p.lede{font-size:16px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--fg);max-width:62ch;margin:0 0 10px}
#tips p.note{font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--fg2);max-width:62ch;margin:0 0 22px}
#tips form{display:grid;gap:16px;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:20px;background:#0b0b0a}
#tips label{display:grid;gap:6px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--fg2)}
#tips label span{color:var(--fg3);letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:none;font-family:inherit}
#tips textarea,#tips input,#tips select{font:inherit;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:0;color:var(--fg);background:#050505;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:10px 12px;border-radius:0;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}
#tips textarea{min-height:170px;resize:vertical;line-height:1.5}
#tips textarea:focus,#tips input:focus,#tips select:focus{outline:none;border-color:var(--signal)}
#tips .hp{position:absolute;left:-9999px;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden}
#tips .row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}
#tips button.send{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;background:var(--signal);color:#111;padding:11px 18px}
#tips button.send:disabled{opacity:.5}
#tips .count{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--fg3)}
#tips .msg{font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.5;padding:12px 14px;border-left:2px solid var(--signal);background:rgba(232,255,0,.05)}
#tips .ts{min-height:65px;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--fg2)}
#tips ul.safe{margin:22px 0 0;padding-left:18px;color:var(--fg2);font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6}

/* case-file list */
#caselist .head .closebtn{margin-left:auto}@media (max-width:900px){#caselist{padding-top:120px}}
ol.cl{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(100%,340px),1fr));gap:22px 18px;max-width:1500px}
.cf{display:flex;flex-direction:column;width:100%;height:100%;text-align:left;cursor:pointer;color:var(--ink,#141412)}
.cft{align-self:flex-start;display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;background:#e7e2d3;color:#141412;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.12em;padding:5px 14px 4px 10px;clip-path:polygon(0 0,calc(100% - 10px) 0,100% 100%,0 100%)}
.cft b{font-weight:700}
.cfb{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;background:#e7e2d3;color:#141412;padding:14px 16px 14px;border-top:0;transition:transform .25s ease,box-shadow .25s}
.cf.sp .cft,.cf.sp .cfb{background:var(--signal)}
.cf:hover .cfb{transform:translateY(-3px);box-shadow:0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.6)}
.cfh{font-size:18px;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.01em;text-wrap:balance}
.cfn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#4b4a44;margin-top:-4px}
.cfd{font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.45;color:#3a3934;display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:3;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden}
.cfm{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 12px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#4b4a44;margin-top:auto;padding-top:6px;border-top:1px solid rgba(20,20,18,.2)}
.cfbar{display:block;height:3px;background:rgba(20,20,18,.14)}.cfbar i{display:block;height:100%;background:#141412}

/* index */
#index,#caselist{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:7;background:var(--bg);overflow:auto;padding:84px 18px 90px;scrollbar-width:none}#caselist::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
#caselist .head,#index .head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:18px}
#caselist h2,#index h2{font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,5vw,56px);letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:0;line-height:1}
.tblwrap{overflow-x:auto}
table.idx{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12.5px;min-width:640px}
table.idx th{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:400;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--fg3);text-align:left;padding:6px 10px 6px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);white-space:nowrap}
table.idx th button{color:inherit;letter-spacing:inherit}
table.idx th button[aria-sort]:after{content:" ↓";color:var(--signal)}
table.idx td{padding:3px 10px 3px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #121211;vertical-align:baseline}
table.idx td.m{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--fg2);white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
table.idx td.r,table.idx th.r{text-align:right}
table.idx tr{cursor:pointer}
table.idx tr:hover td{color:var(--signal)}


#rail,#dossier,#modes,#ctrls,#zoomlbl,#meta,#crumbs,header{transition:opacity 1.4s ease}
#app.intro #rail,#app.intro #dossier,#app.intro #modes,#app.intro #ctrls,#app.intro #zoomlbl,#app.intro #meta,#app.intro #crumbs{opacity:0;pointer-events:none}
#skip{position:absolute;right:18px;bottom:calc(18px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px));z-index:6;width:34px;height:34px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:50%;color:var(--fg2);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;opacity:0;pointer-events:none;transition:opacity .6s}
#app.intro #skip{opacity:1;pointer-events:auto}#skip:hover{color:var(--fg);border-color:var(--fg2)}
#app.intro header{opacity:0;pointer-events:none}
#names{position:absolute;left:242px;top:102px;z-index:3;display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center}
#backbtn{position:absolute;left:242px;top:126px;z-index:3;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--fg2);padding:3px 8px 3px 6px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:rgba(8,8,8,.6)}#backbtn:hover{color:var(--signal);border-color:var(--signal)}#app.intro #backbtn{opacity:0;pointer-events:none}
#names button{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--fg3);padding:2px 0}
#names button[aria-pressed="true"]{color:var(--fg);border-bottom:1px solid var(--signal)}
#app.intro #names{opacity:0;pointer-events:none}
/* ---------- arsenal ---------- */
#arsenal{--abg:#0f3260;--aln:#e3eeff;--adim:rgba(227,238,255,.55);--agrid:rgba(227,238,255,.07);--aacc:#ffe14d;--apan:rgba(5,20,45,.45);position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:11;overflow:auto;background:var(--abg);color:var(--aln);
  background-image:linear-gradient(var(--agrid) 1px,transparent 1px),linear-gradient(90deg,var(--agrid) 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:24px 24px}
#arsenal.st-ink{--abg:#080808;--aln:#f1f1ed;--adim:rgba(241,241,237,.5);--agrid:rgba(255,255,255,.035);--aacc:var(--signal);--apan:rgba(255,255,255,.03)}
#arsenal.st-paper{--abg:#e7e2d3;--aln:#141412;--adim:rgba(20,20,18,.55);--agrid:rgba(20,20,18,.06);--aacc:#c8102e;--apan:rgba(20,20,18,.04)}
#arsenal .tiny{color:var(--adim)}
#arsenal .ah{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:2;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:10px 18px;padding:14px 20px;background:var(--abg);border-bottom:1px solid var(--adim)}
#arsenal .brand{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;margin-right:auto}#arsenal .brand b{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:.3em;font-size:14px}
#arsenal .seg{display:flex;gap:0}#arsenal .seg.wrap{flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px}
#arsenal .seg button,#arsenal .close,#arsenal .xbtn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--aln);border:1px solid var(--adim);padding:5px 10px;margin-left:-1px}
#arsenal .seg button[aria-pressed=true],#arsenal .xbtn[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--aln);color:var(--abg)}
#arsenal .close{border:0}
#arsenal .wpage{display:grid;grid-template-columns:250px minmax(0,1fr);gap:0}
#arsenal .wl{border-right:1px solid var(--adim);padding:14px 0;position:sticky;top:53px;align-self:start;max-height:calc(100vh - 53px);overflow:auto;scrollbar-width:none}
#arsenal .grp{display:block;margin:0 0 14px;font-family:var(--sans);letter-spacing:0;color:inherit;font-size:13px}#arsenal button{font-family:var(--sans,inherit)}#arsenal .grp h4{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:400;font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--adim);margin:0 20px 4px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between}
#arsenal .wl button{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;width:100%;text-align:left;padding:5px 20px;font-size:13px;color:var(--aln)}
#arsenal .wl button span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--adim)}
#arsenal .wl button:hover{background:var(--apan)}#arsenal .wl button[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--aln);color:var(--abg)}#arsenal .wl button[aria-pressed=true] span{color:var(--abg)}
#arsenal .wv{padding:22px clamp(16px,3vw,40px) 60px;min-width:0}
#arsenal .wh{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-end;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
#arsenal h2{font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:6px 0 2px;line-height:1.05}
#arsenal .aka{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--adim)}
#arsenal .xbtn{border-color:var(--aacc);color:var(--aacc);padding:8px 14px}#arsenal .xbtn[aria-pressed=true]{background:var(--aacc);color:var(--abg)}
#arsenal .draw{margin:16px 0 8px;border:1px solid var(--adim);background:var(--apan);overflow-x:auto}
#arsenal svg.bp{display:block;width:100%;min-width:560px;height:auto;color:var(--aln);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px}
.bp .cl{stroke:var(--adim);stroke-dasharray:14 4 2 4;stroke-width:.7}
.bp .b{fill:var(--apan);stroke:var(--aln);stroke-width:1.3}.bp .f{fill:none;stroke:var(--aln);stroke-width:1.1}.bp .h{stroke:var(--adim);stroke-width:.6}
.bp line{stroke:var(--aln)}.bp .part line:not(.h){stroke-width:1.2}
.bp circle.cn{fill:var(--abg);stroke:var(--aln);stroke-width:.8}.bp text.cn{fill:var(--aln);font-size:9.5px}
.bp .part{transition:transform .9s cubic-bezier(.6,0,.2,1);transition-delay:var(--d)}
.bp.ex .part{transform:translate(var(--dx),var(--dy))}
.bp .dim{transition:opacity .4s}.bp.ex .dim{opacity:0}
.bp .dim line{stroke:var(--adim);stroke-width:.8}.bp .dim text{fill:var(--aln);font-size:11px}.bp .dim .bg{fill:var(--abg)}
.bp .call{opacity:0;transition:opacity .5s;transition-delay:0ms;pointer-events:none}.bp.ex .call{opacity:1;transition-delay:var(--d);pointer-events:auto}
.bp .call polyline{fill:none;stroke:var(--aacc);stroke-width:.9}.bp .call circle{fill:var(--aacc)}
.bp .call .pn{fill:var(--aln);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.06em}.bp .call .mk{fill:var(--aacc);font-size:11px}.bp .call .mk[data-go]{cursor:pointer;text-decoration:underline}
.bp .in .b{fill:none;stroke-dasharray:4 3;stroke-width:1}.bp.ex .in .b{fill:var(--abg);stroke-dasharray:none;stroke-width:1.2}.bp .nb{fill:var(--adim);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.1em}
#arsenal .evd{font-size:12.5px!important;color:var(--adim)}#arsenal .evd b{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:500;font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--aln);margin-right:6px}
.bp .sh{fill:none;stroke:var(--adim);stroke-width:.55}.bp .sh.hi{stroke-dasharray:2 3}.bp .sm{fill:none;stroke:var(--aln);stroke-width:.7;opacity:.85}.bp .hg{fill:none;stroke:var(--aln);stroke-width:.7;stroke-dasharray:3 2}.bp circle.rt{fill:var(--aln);stroke:none}.bp .dt{fill:var(--abg);stroke:var(--aln);stroke-width:.9}.bp .dt.win{fill:var(--agrid)}.bp .hx{fill:url(#hx);color:var(--aln)}.bp .cav{fill:none;stroke:var(--adim);stroke-dasharray:3 2;stroke-width:.8}.bp .in.fill .b{fill:url(#hx);color:var(--aln)}.bp.ex .in.fill .b{fill:url(#hx)}.bp .secA{transition:opacity .4s}.bp.ex .secA{opacity:0}
.bpx .hx{fill:url(#hx2);color:var(--aln);stroke:none}.bpx .cutbg{fill:var(--abg);stroke:none}.bpx .tk{fill:var(--apan)}.bpx .fin{fill:var(--apan);stroke-width:1.1}
.bpx .sta line{stroke:var(--adim);stroke-width:.7}.bpx .sta text{fill:var(--adim);font-size:8.5px}
.bpx .tblock rect,.bpx .tblock line{fill:none;stroke:var(--adim);stroke-width:.8}.bpx .tblock text{fill:var(--aln);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.1em}
.bpx .asm{transition:opacity .4s}.bpx.ex .asm{opacity:0}
.bp .tb{fill:var(--adim);font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.12em}
#arsenal .wph{margin:10px 0 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,320px) 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:end}#arsenal .wph img{width:100%;display:block;filter:grayscale(1) contrast(1.1);border:1px solid var(--adim)}#arsenal .wph figcaption{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;color:var(--adim);line-height:1.4}
#arsenal .sum{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.6;max-width:72ch;margin:14px 0 6px}
#arsenal h3{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:500;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin:28px 0 10px;padding-top:8px;border-top:1px solid var(--adim)}
#arsenal .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:0 34px}
#arsenal .spec{margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;border-top:1px solid var(--adim);border-left:1px solid var(--adim)}
#arsenal .spec div{border-right:1px solid var(--adim);border-bottom:1px solid var(--adim);padding:6px 9px 8px;min-width:0}
#arsenal .spec dt{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--adim);text-transform:uppercase}#arsenal .spec dd{margin:3px 0 0;font-size:13.5px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
#arsenal ul.mk{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}#arsenal ul.mk li{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;padding:6px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--agrid);font-size:13.5px}
#arsenal ul.mk button{color:var(--aacc);text-align:left;font-size:13.5px}#arsenal ul.mk em{font-style:normal;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--adim);text-align:right}
#arsenal .tr{font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--aln)}
#arsenal .evl{display:grid;gap:0}
#arsenal .ev{position:relative}
#arsenal .evpic{grid-column:2;width:min(240px,78%);margin:4px 0 6px 6px;padding:6px 6px 8px;background:var(--abg);border:1px solid var(--aln);transform:rotate(var(--r));position:relative}
#arsenal .evpic img{display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;object-fit:cover}#arsenal .evpic figcaption{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.5px;line-height:1.4;color:var(--aln);margin-top:5px}#arsenal .evpic .cr{display:block;font-size:7.5px;color:var(--adim);text-decoration:none;overflow-wrap:anywhere}#arsenal .evpic figcaption b{color:var(--aacc);font-weight:500;margin-right:4px}
@media (min-width:1180px){
 #arsenal .evpage.evpage{max-width:1560px}#arsenal .evl .ev{border-bottom-color:var(--agrid)}#arsenal .ev .toll{max-width:680px}
 #arsenal .evl .ev{grid-template-columns:120px minmax(0,680px) minmax(300px,1fr)}
 #arsenal .evpic{display:block;grid-column:3;justify-self:start;align-self:start;position:relative;width:300px;max-width:calc(100% - 40px);margin:var(--dy) 0 10px 80px;padding:8px 8px 10px;background:var(--abg);border:1px solid var(--aln);transform:rotate(var(--r));box-shadow:0 14px 34px rgba(0,0,0,.45)}
 #arsenal .evpic img{display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/3;object-fit:cover;filter:grayscale(.35) contrast(1.05)}
 #arsenal .evpic figcaption{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;line-height:1.4;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--aln);margin-top:6px}
 #arsenal .evpic figcaption b{color:var(--aacc);font-weight:500;margin-right:4px}
 #arsenal .evpic .cr{display:block;font-size:7.5px;color:var(--adim);margin-top:3px;text-decoration:none;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
 #arsenal .evpic .pin{position:absolute;top:-5px;left:50%;width:9px;height:9px;border:1px solid var(--aacc);border-radius:50%;background:var(--abg);transform:translateX(-50%)}
 #arsenal .ev .ldr{position:absolute;height:0;border-top:1px dashed var(--aacc);opacity:.8;pointer-events:none}#arsenal .ev .ldr:before{content:"";position:absolute;left:-3px;top:-3px;width:5px;height:5px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--aacc)}
}
#arsenal .ev{display:grid;grid-template-columns:120px minmax(0,1fr);gap:16px;padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--agrid)}
#arsenal .ev .d{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px}#arsenal .ev .d span{font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--aacc)}
#arsenal .ev h4{margin:0 0 2px;font-size:17px;font-weight:500}#arsenal .ev .pl{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;color:var(--adim)}
#arsenal .ev .toll{margin:8px 0 2px;font-size:13px}#arsenal .ev .toll b{font-size:20px;font-weight:500;color:var(--aacc)}#arsenal .ev .toll i{font-style:normal;color:var(--adim);font-size:11px}
#arsenal .ev p{font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;max-width:70ch;margin:6px 0}
#arsenal .wc{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px;align-items:center}#arsenal .wc button{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.04em;border:1px solid var(--aln);color:var(--aln);padding:2px 7px}
#arsenal .wc button:hover{background:var(--aln);color:var(--abg)}#arsenal .wc .st{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;color:var(--adim);margin-left:6px}
#arsenal .srcs{font-size:11px;color:var(--adim);margin-top:6px}#arsenal .srcs a{color:var(--adim)}
#arsenal .none,#arsenal .empty{color:var(--adim);font-size:13px}#arsenal .empty{padding:60px 20px;font-family:var(--mono)}
#arsenal .evpage{padding:22px clamp(16px,3vw,40px) 60px;max-width:1100px}#arsenal .intro2 p{max-width:66ch;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--aln)}
.arsbtn{display:grid;grid-template-columns:44px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:center;width:100%;text-align:left;margin-top:10px;padding:6px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:#0c0c0b;color:#e9e6dc;background-image:linear-gradient(rgba(233,230,220,.05) 1px,transparent 1px),linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(233,230,220,.05) 1px,transparent 1px);background-size:8px 8px}
.arsbtn{animation:arsglow 3.6s ease-in-out infinite}@keyframes arsglow{0%,100%{box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(232,255,0,.22),0 0 12px rgba(232,255,0,.2)}50%{box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(232,255,0,.5),0 0 24px rgba(232,255,0,.38)}}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.arsbtn{animation:none;box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(232,255,0,.35),0 0 18px rgba(232,255,0,.28)}}
.arsbtn:hover{border-color:#e9e6dc}.arsbtn svg{width:44px;height:16px}.arsbtn b{display:inline;font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:500;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.24em;margin-right:8px}.arsbtn span{font-size:10.5px;opacity:.6}
.file.special .tab:before{border-color:var(--signal);background:#1a1800}.file.special{color:var(--signal)}.file.special[aria-pressed=true] .tab:before{background:var(--signal)}.file.special[aria-pressed=true]{color:#0a0a0a}
@media (max-width:900px){#arsenal .wpage{grid-template-columns:1fr}#arsenal .wl{position:static;max-height:none;border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--adim);display:flex;overflow-x:auto;padding:10px 0}#arsenal .grp{flex:0 0 auto;margin:0}#arsenal .grp h4{display:none}#arsenal .wl button{white-space:nowrap;padding:5px 12px}#arsenal .wl button span{display:none}#arsenal .ev{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:4px}#arsenal .spec{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
/* slide-out photo tab, attached to the left edge of the dossier */
#photo{position:absolute;right:360px;top:96px;z-index:3;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;transition:transform .5s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1),opacity .4s}
#photo.tucked{transform:translateX(128px)}#photo .card{transition:opacity .45s,transform .5s}#photo.tucked .card{opacity:0;pointer-events:none}
#photo .card{width:128px;background:#d8ceb2;color:#1b1a16;padding:10px 10px 12px;box-shadow:0 12px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.6);position:relative;transform:rotate(-1.5deg)}
#photo .clip{position:absolute;top:-14px;left:22px;width:16px;height:40px;border:2px solid #9a9a96;border-radius:9px;border-bottom-color:transparent}
#photo .lab{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.08em;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:6px}
#photo .pic{aspect-ratio:35/45;background:#2a2926;overflow:hidden;display:grid;place-items:center;position:relative}
#photo .pic img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block}
#photo .pic.person img{filter:grayscale(1) contrast(1.15) brightness(.95)}
#photo .pic svg{width:100%;height:100%;display:block}
#photo .nm{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;margin-top:7px;text-transform:uppercase;line-height:1.35}
#photo .cr,#report .dpic .cr{display:block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:7px;line-height:1.3;letter-spacing:.02em;color:#5d5b54;margin-top:4px;text-decoration:none;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
#photo .stamp{position:absolute;right:8px;top:118px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--red);border:1px solid var(--red);padding:1px 4px;transform:rotate(-8deg);opacity:.85;background:rgba(216,206,178,.6)}
#photo .arrow{width:18px;height:46px;margin-top:22px;background:#d8ceb2;color:#1b1a16;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;display:grid;place-items:center;border-radius:3px 0 0 3px;order:-1}
#photo.tucked .arrow{transform:rotate(180deg);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0}
/* case-file paper peeking out from the rail */
#paperwrap{position:absolute;left:224px;top:150px;width:230px;height:300px;overflow:hidden;z-index:4;pointer-events:none}
#paper{position:absolute;left:0;top:10px;width:200px;height:260px;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);padding:14px 14px;transform:translateX(-180px) rotate(-2deg);transition:transform .45s cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.2,1);pointer-events:auto;text-align:left;box-shadow:6px 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.6)}
#paper:hover,#paper:focus-visible{transform:translateX(-24px) rotate(-1deg)}
#paper .k{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--ink2)}
#paper .t{font-size:16px;line-height:1.15;margin:8px 0;font-weight:500;padding-right:30px}
#paper .lines{height:90px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(var(--paper) 0 9px,#cfcdc3 9px 10px);margin:8px 0;padding-right:30px}
#paper .go{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--red)}
#paper .edge{position:absolute;right:6px;top:14px;writing-mode:vertical-rl;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--red)}
/* case-file report: a paper document over the map */
#report{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:9;background:rgba(5,5,5,.86);overflow:auto;overscroll-behavior:contain;padding:70px 16px 60px;backdrop-filter:blur(2px)}#report.solid{background:#050505;backdrop-filter:none}#caselist{overscroll-behavior:contain}
#report .doc{--pp:#e7e2d3;--pp2:#d9d3c1;--hi:var(--signal);--rule2:rgba(20,20,18,.2);max-width:880px;margin:0 auto;background:var(--pp);color:var(--ink);padding:30px clamp(18px,5vw,60px) 56px;position:relative;box-shadow:0 30px 80px rgba(0,0,0,.7)}
#report .x{position:fixed;top:14px;right:14px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--fg);z-index:10;background:#141412;border:1px solid #3a3a36;padding:7px 11px}
#report .hd{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 12px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--ink2);padding-bottom:10px}
#report .dossier{position:relative;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px;border:1.5px solid var(--ink);padding:26px 16px 14px;margin-top:14px}
#report .dossier.withpic{grid-template-columns:120px 1fr}
#report .tabno{position:absolute;top:-1px;left:-1px;background:var(--ink);color:var(--pp);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;padding:4px 10px 4px 8px}
#report .tabno::after{content:"";position:absolute;right:-26px;top:0;width:26px;height:100%;background:var(--signal)}
#report .dpic{position:relative;background:#d8ceb2;padding:8px;transform:rotate(-1.5deg);box-shadow:0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.25);align-self:start}
#report .dpic .clip{position:absolute;top:-12px;left:18px;width:14px;height:34px;border:2px solid #77766f;border-radius:8px;border-bottom-color:transparent}
#report .dpic .pic{aspect-ratio:35/45;background:#2a2926;overflow:hidden}#report .dpic .pic svg,#report .dpic .pic img{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;object-fit:cover}#report .dpic img.person{filter:grayscale(1) contrast(1.15)}
#report .fields{margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-left:1px solid var(--ink);align-self:start}
#report .fields div{border-right:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink);padding:5px 8px 7px;min-width:0}
#report .fields .wide{grid-column:1/-1}
#report .fields dt{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--ink2)}
#report .fields dd{margin:2px 0 0;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.02em;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
#report .fields .wide dd{font-size:15px}
#report h1{font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,50px);letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.02;margin:30px 0 14px;text-wrap:balance}
#report h1 mark{background:linear-gradient(transparent 58%,var(--hi) 58%);color:inherit;box-decoration-break:clone;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone}
#report .dek{font-size:17px;line-height:1.5;max-width:62ch;margin:0 0 22px}
#report h2{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:500;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;margin:38px 0 14px;padding:6px 0 0;border-top:2px solid var(--ink);display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px}
#report h3{font-size:19px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:24px 0 6px;text-wrap:balance}
#report .kf{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(170px,1fr));gap:4px;margin-top:6px}
#report .kf div{padding:12px 12px 14px;min-height:96px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;background:var(--ink);color:var(--pp)}
#report .kf div:nth-child(4n+2){background:var(--signal);color:var(--ink)}
#report .kf div:nth-child(4n+3){background:#6f7a00;color:#f4f6d8}
#report .kf div:nth-child(4n+4){background:var(--pp2);color:var(--ink)}
#report .kf b{display:block;font-size:28px;font-weight:500;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;letter-spacing:-.01em;line-height:1}
#report .kf span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;line-height:1.4;opacity:.9}
#report p{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.62;max-width:66ch}
#report p.fn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.04em;margin-top:-6px}#report p.fn a{text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink2)}
#report p.cap{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;color:var(--ink2);margin-top:6px}
#report blockquote{margin:22px 0;padding:4px 0 4px 18px;border-left:6px solid var(--hi)}
#report blockquote p{font-size:20px;line-height:1.4;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 6px}
#report blockquote cite{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;font-style:normal;color:var(--ink2);text-transform:uppercase}
#report .chart{overflow-x:auto}
#report .chart svg{display:block;max-width:100%;height:auto}
#report .bkey{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 14px;margin-top:8px;font-size:12px}#report .bkey i{display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;margin-right:5px;vertical-align:-1px}#report .bkey b{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:400;font-size:11px}
#report .chain{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:0}
#report .chain li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:52px 1fr;gap:14px;position:relative;padding-bottom:18px}
#report .chain li::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:25px;top:44px;bottom:0;width:1.5px;background:var(--ink)}
#report .chain li:last-child::before{display:none}
#report .chain .n{width:52px;height:44px;display:grid;place-items:center;background:var(--ink);color:var(--pp);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:15px;letter-spacing:.05em}
#report .chain li:nth-child(odd) .n{background:var(--signal);color:var(--ink)}
#report .chain h4{margin:2px 0 4px;font-size:17px;font-weight:600}
#report .chain p{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:14.5px}
#report .chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px}
#report .chips span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:2px 6px;border:1px solid var(--ink)}
#report .chips .sys{background:var(--ink);color:var(--pp)}
#report table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12.5px}
#report th{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:400;font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--ink2);text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink);padding:5px 8px 5px 0}
#report td{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule2);padding:6px 8px 6px 0;vertical-align:top}
#report td.v{font-family:var(--mono);text-align:right;white-space:nowrap}
#report a{color:var(--ink);text-underline-offset:3px}
#report .pending{border:1px dashed var(--ink2);padding:14px 16px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--ink2);line-height:1.6}
#report .src{font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--ink2);padding-left:22px;margin:0}#report .src li{margin-bottom:3px}
#report .tblwrap{overflow-x:auto}
@media (max-width:600px){#report .kf{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}#report .kf div{min-height:84px}#report .fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}#report .dossier.withpic{grid-template-columns:84px 1fr}#report .kf b{font-size:22px}}
#report .doc{overflow:visible}
#report .hd .dl{font:inherit;font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--ink);border:1px solid var(--ink);padding:4px 9px}#report .hd .dl:hover{background:var(--ink);color:var(--pp)}
#report .spine{position:absolute;top:120px;bottom:60px;right:-30px;width:30px;pointer-events:none}
#report .spine div{position:sticky;top:90px;filter:drop-shadow(5px 6px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.4));color:var(--ink);writing-mode:vertical-rl;padding:18px 0 20px;width:30px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.2em;isolation:isolate}
#report .spine div::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;background:var(--pp);border-radius:0 7px 7px 0;clip-path:polygon(0 0,100% 9px,100% calc(100% - 9px),0 100%);z-index:-1}
#report .spine b{font-weight:500;color:var(--ink);background:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent 22%,var(--signal) 22%,var(--signal) 78%,transparent 78%);padding:4px 0}
#report .wanted{grid-column:1/-1;display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:4px 18px;border:4px solid #c8102e;color:#c8102e;padding:8px 16px 10px;transform:rotate(-1.2deg);margin:6px 4px 2px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(135deg,transparent 0 9px,rgba(200,16,46,.05) 9px 10px)}
#report .wanted b{grid-row:span 2;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:800;font-size:clamp(46px,9vw,84px);letter-spacing:.06em;line-height:.9}
#report .wanted span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:500}
#report .wanted i{font-style:normal;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.04em;line-height:1.45;color:#7d0b1d}
#report .rs{position:relative}
#report .sn{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--ink2);margin:28px 0 -14px}
#report .sn::after{content:"";display:inline-block;width:38px;height:6px;background:var(--signal);margin-left:10px;vertical-align:middle}
#report p.dc::first-letter{float:left;font-size:58px;line-height:.86;font-weight:600;padding:6px 10px 0 0;color:var(--ink);text-shadow:4px 4px 0 var(--signal)}
#report .inter{margin:30px 0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px 1fr;gap:18px;align-items:end;border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink);padding:14px 0}
#report .inter .ph{aspect-ratio:35/45;background:#2a2926;overflow:hidden;filter:grayscale(1) contrast(1.08)}#report .inter .ph img,#report .inter .ph svg{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block}
#report .inter figcaption{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.06em;line-height:1.5;color:var(--ink2);display:grid;gap:4px}
#report .inter figcaption b{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:22px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer;background:linear-gradient(transparent 62%,var(--signal) 62%);justify-self:start}
#report .inter .cr{color:var(--ink2);font-size:8px;text-decoration:none}
#report blockquote{font-size:inherit}#report blockquote p{font-size:clamp(20px,3vw,26px);line-height:1.3;max-width:30ch}
#report .brk{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin:30px 0 8px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.2em;color:var(--ink2)}#report .brk::before,#report .brk::after{content:"";flex:1;height:1px;background:var(--rule2)}
#report blockquote.lead{border:0;padding:18px 0 22px;margin:8px 0 26px;border-top:2px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink)}#report blockquote.lead p{font-size:clamp(30px,5.4vw,52px);line-height:1.04;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;max-width:none;background:linear-gradient(transparent 70%,var(--signal) 70%);display:inline;box-decoration-break:clone;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone}#report blockquote.lead cite{display:block;margin-top:14px}
#report .endmark{margin-top:36px;padding-top:10px;border-top:2px solid var(--ink);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.2em;text-align:center}
#report .rv{opacity:0;transform:translateY(10px);transition:opacity .45s ease,transform .45s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)}
#report .rv.in{opacity:1;transform:none}
#report .chart.rv svg rect{transform-box:fill-box;transform-origin:left center;transform:scaleX(0);transition:transform .9s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1)}
#report .chart.rv.in svg rect{transform:scaleX(1)}
#report .chart.rv svg path{opacity:0;transition:opacity .9s ease}#report .chart.rv.in svg path{opacity:1}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){#report .rv,#report .chart.rv svg rect,#report .chart.rv svg path{opacity:1;transform:none;transition:none}}
@media (max-width:1000px){#report .spine{right:0;width:22px}#report .spine div{width:22px;font-size:8px}#report .doc{padding-right:clamp(34px,6vw,60px)}}
@media (max-width:600px){#report .inter{grid-template-columns:96px 1fr}#report .inter figcaption b{font-size:18px}#report .wanted{grid-template-columns:1fr}#report .wanted b{grid-row:auto}}
.legend-line .inh{width:26px;height:6px;flex:none}
#railtoggle,#dossiertoggle{display:none}
@media (max-width:900px){
  header{grid-template-columns:1fr auto;padding:12px 16px}
  .searchwrap{grid-column:1/3;grid-row:2;justify-self:stretch;width:100%}
  #rail{display:none;background:rgba(8,8,8,.96);width:min(280px,86vw);top:100px;bottom:0;padding-bottom:80px}
  #rail.open{display:flex}
  #dossier{width:100%;top:auto;height:48%;bottom:calc(56px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px));background:rgba(8,8,8,.96);border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-bottom:20px}
  #dossier.collapsed{height:auto;max-height:46px;overflow:hidden}
  #ctrls{right:16px;top:116px;transform:none}
  #zoomlbl,#meta,#crumbs,#names{display:none}#backbtn{left:16px;top:calc(64px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px))}
  #photo{display:none}
  #paperwrap{left:0;top:118px}
  #railtoggle{display:inline}
  #modes{bottom:calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px))}
  nav.top{gap:12px}
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{transition:none!important}}

/* ---------- phone layout: these rules apply only at 900px and narrower, desktop is untouched ---------- */
@media (max-width:900px){
  header{padding:12px 16px 12px;row-gap:12px;background:linear-gradient(var(--bg) 72%,rgba(8,8,8,0))}
  #app.intro header{background:none}
  .mark .tiny{display:none}
  .mark b{font-size:14px;line-height:18px}
  #backbtn{top:calc(100px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px))}
  #ctrls{top:calc(100px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px))}
  #zin,#zout,#zfull,#paperwrap{display:none}
  #modes{-webkit-mask-image:linear-gradient(90deg,#000 82%,transparent);mask-image:linear-gradient(90deg,#000 82%,transparent);left:16px;transform:none;max-width:calc(100% - 16px);padding-right:40px}
  #rail{top:calc(92px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px));left:0;width:100%;background:var(--bg);z-index:9;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:14px 16px calc(40px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px));overscroll-behavior:contain}
  #app:has(#rail.open) #modes,#app:has(#rail.open) #dossier,#app:has(#rail.open) #ctrls,#app:has(#rail.open) #backbtn{visibility:hidden}
  #dossier{height:56%;padding-top:0;border-radius:14px 14px 0 0;overscroll-behavior:contain;transition:height .3s ease,max-height .3s ease,top .3s ease}
  #dossier::before{content:"";display:block;position:sticky;top:0;z-index:2;height:24px;margin:0 -20px 2px;background:linear-gradient(#5b5b55,#5b5b55) center 10px/40px 4px no-repeat,linear-gradient(rgba(8,8,8,.98) 75%,rgba(8,8,8,0))}
  #dossier.collapsed{height:84px;max-height:84px;-webkit-mask-image:linear-gradient(#000 72%,transparent);mask-image:linear-gradient(#000 72%,transparent)}
  #dossier.collapsed h1{white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;font-size:22px;margin:8px 0 0}
  #dossier.full{height:auto;max-height:none;top:calc(92px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px));bottom:0;padding-bottom:calc(36px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px))}
  #app:has(#dossier.full) #modes{opacity:0;pointer-events:none}
  #index table.idx th:nth-child(3),#index table.idx td:nth-child(3),#index table.idx th:nth-child(4),#index table.idx td:nth-child(4){display:none}
}
@media (max-width:600px){
  #report{padding:62px 0 40px}
  #report .spine{display:none}
  #report .doc{padding:24px 18px 44px}
  #report .chart svg.wide{min-width:620px;max-width:none}
}

/* ---------- phone page (760px and narrower): one long scroll, the map is only the backdrop of the opening screen ---------- */
#phone{display:none}
#app.ph>header,#app.ph #rail,#app.ph #modes,#app.ph #ctrls,#app.ph #names,#app.ph #backbtn,#app.ph #meta,#app.ph #zoomlbl,#app.ph #crumbs,#app.ph #photo,#app.ph #paperwrap,#app.ph #skip{display:none!important}
#app.ph #dossier{display:none}
#app.ph #phone:not([hidden]){display:block;position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:6;overflow-y:auto;overflow-x:hidden;overscroll-behavior:contain;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch;scrollbar-width:none}
#phone::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
#phone .phbar{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:3;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:calc(12px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px)) 16px 12px;background:linear-gradient(var(--bg) 70%,rgba(8,8,8,0))}
#phone .phbar b,#phone .phfoot b{font-weight:500;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.08em}
#phone .phbar b i,#phone .phfoot b i{font-style:normal;color:var(--signal)}
#phone .phbar nav{display:flex;gap:12px}
#phone .phbar nav button{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--fg2);padding:6px 0}
#phone .phhero{height:calc(100svh - 48px);min-height:520px;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;pointer-events:none}
#phone .phhead{padding:0 16px 28px;pointer-events:auto;background:linear-gradient(rgba(8,8,8,0),rgba(8,8,8,.85) 30%);width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding-top:40px}
#phone .phhead h1{font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(34px,10vw,46px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:8px 0 10px;text-wrap:balance}
#phone .phhead p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;color:var(--signal);margin:0 0 18px;max-width:30ch}
#phone .phdown{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--fg2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;padding:8px 14px}
#phone .phbody{background:var(--bg);padding:8px 16px calc(40px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px))}
#phone .phsec{padding:34px 0 30px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
#phone .phsec:first-child{border-top:0}
#phone .phh{display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;font-weight:400;font-size:28px;letter-spacing:-.015em;margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.05}
#phone .phh span{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--signal)}
#phone .phlede,#phone .phsec>p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--fg);margin:0 0 14px}
#phone .phsec>p.phnote{font-size:13px;color:var(--fg3)}
#phone .stat3 b{font-size:28px}
#phone .moneystat b{font-size:34px}
#phone .mparts li{font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.35}
#phone ol.cl{list-style:none;margin:0 0 14px;padding:0;display:grid;gap:12px}
#phone .phmore{display:block;width:100%;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--fg);border:1px solid var(--line);padding:14px;text-align:center}
#phone .pharsenal{display:grid;gap:8px;width:100%;text-align:left;padding:20px 18px;border:1px solid var(--adim,#4a5a2a);background:#0d1830;color:#e9eef8}
#phone .pharsenal b{font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:500;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.3em}
#phone .pharsenal span{font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:#c7d0e2}
#phone .pharsenal em{font-style:normal;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--signal)}
#phone #phq{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;background:#050505;border:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--fg);font-size:16px;padding:12px 14px;border-radius:0;margin:0 0 12px}
#phone #phq:focus{outline:none;border-color:var(--signal)}
#phone .phchips{display:flex;gap:6px;overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:none;margin:0 -16px 12px;padding:0 16px}
#phone .phchips::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
#phone .phchips button{flex:0 0 auto;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--fg2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:999px;padding:7px 12px;white-space:nowrap}
#phone .phchips button i{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;display:block}
#phone .phchips button[aria-pressed="true"]{background:var(--fg);color:var(--bg);border-color:var(--fg)}
#phone .phcount{margin:0 0 6px}
#phone .phrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:10px 1fr auto;gap:12px;align-items:center;width:100%;text-align:left;padding:13px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}
#phone .phrow i{width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%}
#phone .phrow .n{font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.25;min-width:0}
#phone .phrow .n small{display:block;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.35;color:var(--fg3);margin-top:3px;overflow:hidden;display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical}
#phone .phrow .d{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:14px;color:var(--fg);text-align:right}
#phone .phrow .d small{display:block;font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--fg3)}
#phone #phlist{margin:0 0 16px}
#phone .phnone{color:var(--fg3);font-size:14px}
#phone .phcta{display:block;width:100%;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;background:var(--signal);color:#111;padding:16px}
#phone .phfoot{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;padding:24px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
#app.ph #dossier.page{display:block;position:absolute;inset:0;top:0;bottom:0;width:auto;height:auto;max-height:none;z-index:8;background:var(--bg);border:0;border-radius:0;padding:calc(58px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px)) 18px calc(40px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px));-webkit-mask-image:none;mask-image:none;overflow-y:auto}
#app.ph #dossier.page::before{display:none}
#app.ph #dossier.page h1{white-space:normal;font-size:34px}
#phback{display:none}
#app.ph #phback:not([hidden]){display:block;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:8;text-align:left;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--fg);background:var(--bg);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px)) 16px 14px}
#app.ph #insp{z-index:10;left:16px!important;right:16px;width:auto}
#app.ph #index,#app.ph #caselist,#app.ph #tips{padding-top:calc(24px + env(safe-area-inset-top,0px))}

#app.ph #arsenal .wltog{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;gap:4px 12px;width:100%;text-align:left;padding:14px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--adim);color:var(--aln)}
#app.ph #arsenal .wltog span{grid-column:1/-1;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;opacity:.7}
#app.ph #arsenal .wltog b{font-weight:500;font-size:17px;line-height:1.25}
#app.ph #arsenal .wltog em{font-style:normal;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;align-self:center;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid currentColor;padding:6px 9px}
#app.ph #arsenal .wl{display:none;overflow:visible;padding:4px 0 10px}
#app.ph #arsenal .wpage.open .wl{display:block}
#app.ph #arsenal .grp{margin:6px 0 10px}
#app.ph #arsenal .grp h4{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin:10px 16px 4px;font-family:var(--mono);font-weight:400;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.12em;opacity:.7}
#app.ph #arsenal .wl button{white-space:normal;font-size:15px;padding:11px 16px;line-height:1.3}
#app.ph #arsenal .wl button span{display:inline}
#phone .pharsbtn{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:14px;margin:0;padding:22px 18px 20px;animation:phglow 3s ease-in-out infinite}
#phone .pharsbtn svg{width:100%;height:58px}
#phone .pharsbtn b{display:block;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.32em;margin:0 0 8px}
#phone .pharsbtn span{display:block;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;opacity:.75}
#phone .pharsbtn em{display:block;margin-top:12px;font-style:normal;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;color:var(--signal)}
@keyframes phglow{0%,100%{box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(232,255,0,.35),0 0 18px rgba(232,255,0,.25)}50%{box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(232,255,0,.75),0 0 38px rgba(232,255,0,.5)}}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){#phone .pharsbtn{animation:none;box-shadow:0 0 0 1px rgba(232,255,0,.5),0 0 26px rgba(232,255,0,.35)}}
#phnote{display:none}
#app.ph #phnote:not([hidden]){display:flex;position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:12;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;background:rgba(5,5,5,.72);backdrop-filter:blur(3px);padding:16px 16px calc(20px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px))}
#phnote .box{width:100%;max-width:440px;background:#0c0c0b;border:1px solid var(--signal);box-shadow:0 0 30px rgba(232,255,0,.25);padding:22px 20px 18px;display:grid;gap:12px;animation:phin .45s ease-out}
@keyframes phin{from{transform:translateY(24px);opacity:0}to{transform:none;opacity:1}}
#phnote h3{font-weight:400;font-size:26px;line-height:1.1;margin:0;letter-spacing:-.01em}
#phnote p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;margin:0;color:var(--fg)}
#phnote .url{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:10px 12px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:13px;color:var(--signal)}
#phnote .url button{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--fg);border:1px solid var(--line);padding:6px 9px}
#phnote .ok{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;background:var(--signal);color:#111;padding:14px}
</style>

<div id="app" class="intro">
  <canvas id="net" aria-label="Network map of entities and relationships" role="img"></canvas>

  <header>
    <div class="mark">
      <b>BL<i>0</i><i>0</i>D.MONEY</b>
      <span class="tiny">Database / 2026 · ongoing investigation</span>
    </div>
    <div class="searchwrap">
      <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Search entity, system, fund…" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-label="Search the database">
      <div id="results" hidden></div>
    </div>
    <nav class="top" aria-label="Views">
      <button id="railtoggle" aria-expanded="false">FILES</button>
      <button data-view="map" aria-pressed="true">MAP</button>
      <button data-view="index" aria-pressed="false">INDEX</button>
      <button data-view="about" aria-pressed="false">ABOUT</button>
      <button data-view="tips" aria-pressed="false">SUBMIT</button>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <aside id="rail" aria-label="Filter network"></aside>
  <div id="zoomlbl" class="tiny"></div>
  <div id="names" role="group" aria-label="Names on map"><span class="tiny">NAMES</span><button data-l="off" aria-pressed="true">OFF</button><button data-l="key" aria-pressed="false">KEY</button><button data-l="all" aria-pressed="false">ALL</button></div>
  <div id="photo" hidden></div>
  <div id="paperwrap" hidden><button id="paper" aria-label="Open the full case file"></button></div>
  <aside id="dossier" aria-live="polite"></aside>

  <div id="ctrls" aria-label="Map controls">
    <button id="zin" title="Zoom in" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
    <button id="zout" title="Zoom out" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
    <button id="zreset" title="Reset view" aria-label="Reset view">◎</button>
    <button id="zfull" title="Full screen" aria-label="Full screen">□</button>
  </div>

  <div id="modes" role="group" aria-label="Layout">
    <button data-mode="network" aria-pressed="true">● NETWORK</button>
    <button data-mode="orbit" aria-pressed="false">○ ORBIT</button>
    <button data-mode="clusters" aria-pressed="false">○ CLUSTERS</button>
    <button data-mode="flow" aria-pressed="false">○ FLOW</button>
    <button data-mode="holdings" aria-pressed="false">○ HOLDINGS</button>
    <button data-mode="timeline" aria-pressed="false" disabled title="Next round">○ TIMELINE</button>
  </div>
  <div id="crumbs"></div>
  <button id="backbtn" hidden title="Back" aria-label="Back to the previous node">← BACK</button>
  <div id="meta" class="tiny"></div>

  <button id="skip" aria-label="Skip intro" title="Skip">»</button>
  <div id="insp" hidden role="dialog" aria-label="Relationship"></div>
  <section id="index" hidden aria-label="Entity index"></section>
  <section id="caselist" hidden aria-label="All case files"></section>
  <section id="tips" hidden aria-label="Submit a tip"></section>
  <section id="report" hidden aria-label="Case file report"></section>
  <section id="arsenal" hidden aria-label="Weapons catalogue"></section>

</div>

<script type="application/json" id="data">{"entities":[{"id":"COM-00001","name":"RTX","type":"Company","role":"Arms maker; its Tomahawk struck a school in Minab, Iran","country":"USA","slug":"rtx","profile":"RTX is the U.S. weapons conglomerate behind Raytheon missiles and Pratt & Whitney jet engines, and its charge sheet starts with a school. Raytheon makes the Tomahawk cruise missile. A preliminary U.S. military investigation, reported by the New York Times, found that a U.S. Tomahawk struck the Shajareh Tayyebeh elementary school in Minab, Iran on Feb 28, 2026, the first day of the U.S. war on Iran. Between 156 and 168 people were killed, most of them children. Pratt & Whitney builds the engines of the F-35, the jet Israel has flown over Gaza and Iran. R2S, Raytheon's joint venture with Israel's state-owned Rafael, won a $1.25B contract in Nov 2025 to build Tamir interceptors for Iron Dome in Camden, Arkansas. The proceeds: about $285B in sales and $18.9B in net income from 2023 to June 2026, a $289B backlog, $119B of it military, as of June 30, 2026, and a Sept 2026 U.S. AMRAAM contract worth up to $20.7B. BlackRock (8.2%) and Vanguard (7.47%) are its top owners.","profile_src":["https://www.rtx.com/raytheon/what-we-do/sea/tomahawk-cruise-missile","https://www.trtworld.com/article/6112ba851a95","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Minab_school_attack","https://www.militarytimes.com/news/your-military/2026/03/24/deadly-iran-school-strike-casts-shadow-over-pentagons-ai-targeting-push/","https://investigate.afsc.org/company/rtx","https://www.rtx.com/news/news-center/2025/11/21/r2s-receives-1-25-billion-tamir-production-contract-for-facility-in-camden-arka","https://www.rtx.com/news/news-center/2026/01/27/rtx-reports-2025-results-and-announces-2026-outlook","https://www.rtx.com/news/news-center/2026/07/23/rtx-reports-q2-2026-results","https://raytheon.mediaroom.com/2026-09-28-RTXs-Raytheon-awarded-20-7-billion-multi-year-contract-for-AMRAAM-under-landmark-production-agreement","https://13f.info/data/13f/000201238326003238","https://www.secform4.com/13dg/2100119/0002100119-26-001059.html"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00002","name":"Lockheed Martin","type":"Company","role":"Arms maker; F-35 and Hellfire supplier to Israel","country":"USA","slug":"lockheed-martin","profile":"Lockheed Martin is the world's largest weapons manufacturer and prime contractor for the F-35 and F-16, the jets that, according to UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report, were integral to Israel's ability to drop an estimated 85,000 tons of bombs on Gaza. Israeli F-35I jets also struck Iran in June 2025 and again from Feb 28, 2026. In June 2024 Israel signed for 25 more F-35s for about $3B, paid with U.S. military aid. Lockheed also makes the AGM-114 Hellfire: Bellingcat's 2026 investigation found Hellfire remnants after a June 2024 strike on a Gaza City health clinic and a Nov 2025 strike outside Al-Aqsa Martyrs Hospital. The U.S. notified Congress of 3,000 more Hellfires for Israel ($660M) in Feb 2025 and of a $3.8B Apache package naming Lockheed and Boeing in Jan 2026. The proceeds: about $251.7B in sales and $20.6B in net earnings from 2023 to June 2026, and a record $230B backlog at June 28, 2026. CEO James Taiclet took about $70M for 2023–2025.","profile_src":["https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://defence-industry.eu/israeli-air-force-deploys-f-35i-adir-fighter-fleet-in-operation-roaring-lion-amid-pngoing-strikes-on-targets-in-iran/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-inks-deal-to-buy-25-more-f-35-fighter-jets-for-3-billion/","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060949/israel-agm-114-hellfire-missiles","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4394583/israel-ah-64e-apache-helicopters","https://news.lockheedmartin.com/2026-07-23-Lockheed-Martin-Reports-Second-Quarter-2026-Financial-Results","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/936468/000093646826000004/R2.htm"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00003","name":"Boeing","type":"Company","role":"Arms maker; its GBU-39 and JDAM kits hit camps, schools, journalists","country":"USA","slug":"boeing","profile":"Boeing makes the bombs that have killed displaced families in Gaza and Lebanon. New York Times and CNN video analysis identified its GBU-39 Small Diameter Bomb in the May 26, 2024 strike on a displacement camp in Tal al-Sultan, Rafah, which killed 45 to 50 people. A CNN weapons expert traced shrapnel at al-Tabi'in school in Gaza City, where at least 80 people were killed on Aug 10, 2024, to a Boeing GBU-39. Bellingcat found GBU-39 remnants at 20 strikes on schools. Human Rights Watch found a Boeing JDAM kit in the bomb that killed three journalists in Hasbaya, Lebanon on Oct 25, 2024, and called the attack an apparent war crime. The repeat business followed: in 2026 Boeing won $8.6B for 25 F-15IA jets for Israel and reportedly agreed a deal worth up to $289M for up to 5,000 more bombs. It also builds 40–50% of Israel's Arrow 3 interceptor. Revenue reached $46.8B in H1 2026, about $280.6B since 2023, and backlog hit a record $715B at June 30, 2026.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tel_al-Sultan_attack","https://www.cnn.com/2024/05/28/middleeast/gaza-us-munitions-rafah-strike-analysis-intl-hnk/index.html","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Tabaeen_school_attack","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/11/25/lebanon-us-arms-used-israeli-strike-journalists","https://spectrumlocalnews.com/mo/st-louis/STLPartners/2026/01/02/boeing-awarded--8-6b-contract-to-build-25-fighter-jets-for-israel","https://finance.yahoo.com/news/boeing-lands-israel-bomb-deal-180300119.html","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4394583/israel-ah-64e-apache-helicopters","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrow_3","https://investors.boeing.com/investors/news/press-release-details/2026/Boeing-Reports-Second-Quarter-Results/","https://investors.boeing.com/investors/news/press-release-details/2026/Boeing-Reports-Second-Quarter-Results/default.aspx"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00004","name":"General Dynamics","type":"Company","role":"Arms maker; built the MK-84 bomb bodies that flattened Gaza","country":"USA","slug":"general-dynamics","profile":"General Dynamics is the U.S. weapons manufacturer whose Garland, Texas plant made bodies for the 2,000-pound MK-84 bomb, the weapon behind much of Gaza's destruction. In Feb 2025 the U.S. notified Congress of 35,529 MK-84 or BLU-117 bomb bodies and 4,000 penetrator warheads for Israel ($2.04B), naming GD's Garland plant as principal contractor. Bellingcat counts over 14,000 MK-84s delivered to Israel since Oct 2023, and documented MK-80 series bombs with JDAM kits, alongside GBU-39s, in the July 27, 2024 strikes on Khadija school in Deir al-Balah, which killed at least 30 people, 15 of them children. In April 2025 GD sold the Garland plant to Turkish-owned REPKON, handing the bomb line to someone else. From 2023 to June 2026 GD booked about $170.1B in revenue and $13.6B in net earnings, with a $136.5B backlog at the end of June 2026. CEO Phebe Novakovic took about $72.3M for 2023–2025. Vanguard (6.88%) and BlackRock (6.4%) are among its top holders.","profile_src":["https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088258/israel-munitions-and-munitions-support","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/repkon-usa-announces-acquisition-of-general-dynamics-ordnance-and-tactical-systems-garland-operations-expanding-its-capabilities-in-defense-and-aerospace-manufacturing-302418890.html","https://s22.q4cdn.com/891946778/files/doc_financials/2026/q2/GD-2026-07-05-Exhibit-99-1.pdf","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/40533/000130817926000168/R2.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000040533/000201238326002579/xslSCHEDULE_13G_X02/primary_doc.xml","https://www.secform4.com/13dg/2100119/0002100119-26-001059.html"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00005","name":"Northrop Grumman","type":"Company","role":"Arms maker; builds the F-35 centre fuselage flown over Gaza","country":"USA","slug":"northrop-grumman","profile":"Northrop Grumman is a U.S. weapons manufacturer that builds the center fuselage of the F-35, including the jets delivered to Israel's air force. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese says these jets were integral to dropping an estimated 85,000 tons of bombs on Gaza, and they struck Iran in 2025 and 2026. According to AFSC research, Northrop also makes the fire-control radar and electronic-warfare systems on Israel's F-16s. With Lockheed Martin it makes the Longbow radar that guides Hellfire missiles fired from Apache helicopters, and it supplied Sa'ar 5 warships to Israel's navy. The proceeds: about $143B in sales and $12.4B in net earnings from 2023 to June 2026, with a record $104.7B backlog at June 30, 2026. Its largest shareholders are the same asset managers that own the rest of the industry: State Street (9.27%) and BlackRock (8.29%) as of June 30, 2026, and Vanguard (7.22%) and Capital Group (5.2%) as of March 31, 2026.","profile_src":["https://investor.northropgrumman.com/news-releases/news-release-details/northrop-grumman-delivers-center-fuselage-first-israeli-f-35","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://defence-industry.eu/israeli-air-force-deploys-f-35i-adir-fighter-fleet-in-operation-roaring-lion-amid-pngoing-strikes-on-targets-in-iran/","https://investigate.afsc.org/company/northrop-grumman","https://investor.northropgrumman.com/static-files/7f6ee108-63ac-43e2-a2bb-bee8faefffe7","https://13f.info/data/13f/000009375126000583","https://13f.info/data/13f/000201238326003238","https://www.secform4.com/13dg/2100119/0002100119-26-001059.html","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001133421/000156223026000095/xslSCHEDULE_13G_X02/primary_doc.xml"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00006","name":"BAE Systems","type":"Company","role":"Arms maker; builds the rear fuselage of every F-35, Israel's included","country":"UK","slug":"bae-systems","profile":"BAE Systems is Britain's largest arms manufacturer and Lockheed Martin's main F-35 partner. It holds a 13–15% workshare in each jet and builds the rear fuselage of every F-35 in the world, Israel's included. When the UK suspended 30 of 350 arms export licences to Israel in Sept 2024, F-35 components were exempted. On June 30, 2025 the High Court threw out a challenge by Al-Haq, which called the exemption a deliberate loophole, ruling the issue was one for ministers. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese says the F-35s BAE helps build were integral to Israel dropping an estimated 85,000 tons of bombs on Gaza; they also struck Iran in 2025 and 2026. The loophole paid well. BAE's sales rose from £25.3B in 2023 to £30.7B in 2025, then £15.8B in H1 2026, and it made about £7.2B in profit from 2023 to H1 2026, with an £84.0B backlog at mid-2026. Capital Group (11.04%, Jan 2026) and BlackRock (9.52%, July 2026) are its largest holders.","profile_src":["https://www.baesystems.com/en/product/f35-lightning-ii","https://www.euronews.com/my-europe/2025/06/30/uk-high-court-rejects-challenge-against-selling-military-parts-to-israel","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://defence-industry.eu/israeli-air-force-deploys-f-35i-adir-fighter-fleet-in-operation-roaring-lion-amid-pngoing-strikes-on-targets-in-iran/","https://investors.baesystems.com/financial-information/five-year-summary","https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/07/30/3335814/1953/en/BAE-Systems-2026-Half-Year-Results.html","https://www.investegate.co.uk/announcement/rns/bae-systems--ba./holding-s-in-company/9396456","https://www.investing.com/equities/bae-systems-plc-ownership"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00007","name":"Elbit Systems","type":"Company","role":"Israeli arms maker; its drone killed World Central Kitchen aid workers","country":"Israel","slug":"elbit-systems","profile":"Elbit Systems is Israel's largest private arms manufacturer and the main supplier of the drones Israel's military flies over Gaza and Lebanon. On April 1, 2024 an Elbit Hermes 450 drone fired the missiles that killed seven World Central Kitchen aid workers in a convoy in Gaza. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report names drones largely developed and supplied by Elbit and IAI as flying alongside Israel's fighter jets. For Elbit, the wars have meant record business. Israel's Ministry of Defense gave it $183M for air munitions in Jan 2026, about $200M more in April 2026 tied to the Iran campaign, and $48M for tens of thousands of 155mm artillery shells. Elbit also makes the ATMOS howitzer and PULS rocket launcher, which it sells to NATO armies as products with a track record. In H1 2026 it reported $4.48B in revenue and $334M in net income, with a record $32.0B backlog at June 30, 2026. Federmann Enterprises controls 41.2% of its shares.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbit_Hermes_450","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://thedefensepost.com/2026/04/24/israel-elbit-airborne-munitions-deals/","https://www.elbitsystems.com/news/elbit-systems-awarded-two-contracts-aggregate-amount-252-million-supply-atmos-and-puls","https://www.elbitsystems.com/news/elbit-systems-reports-second-quarter-2026-results","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm"],"profile_status":"documented","profile (sentence)":"Elbit also makes the PULS (Lahav) rocket launcher, which fired more than 50 'Bar' rockets at targets in Lebanon in 2026, and the Ro'em 155mm self-propelled howitzer, first fired in combat in Lebanon in April 2026."},{"id":"COM-00008","name":"Israel Aerospace Industries (IAI)","type":"Company","role":"Israeli state arms maker; drones over Gaza, Arrow interceptors for export","country":"Israel","slug":"israel-aerospace-industries-iai","profile":"Israel Aerospace Industries is the Israeli state's own arms manufacturer and maker of the Arrow interceptors used against Iranian missiles. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report names IAI, with Elbit, as the main developer of the drones that fly alongside Israel's fighter jets over Gaza. Arrow 3, built with Boeing, intercepted Iran's missile attack of April 2024 and Houthi missiles from Yemen. The genocide years delivered record profits. Sales rose from $5.3B in 2023 to $7.4B in 2025. In H1 2026 IAI reported $4.28B in sales and $449M in net profit, up 40%, with a record $35B backlog. Its missiles and space division, which makes Arrow, passed $1B in half-year sales for the first time. It sells the same technology abroad: Germany's Arrow 3 purchases exceeded $6.5B by Jan 2026, and Slovakia bought the Barak MX. Exports made up 66% of H1 2026 sales, so foreign buyers help bankroll the state that owns it.","profile_src":["https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrow_3","https://www.iai.co.il/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/IAI-FS-CONSOLIDATED-AND-SOLO-12.25.pdf","https://www.ynetnews.com/business/article/sjn6uuj8ze","https://www.iai.co.il/press/israel-aerospace-industries-announces-31-billion-usd-contract-expansion-arrow-3-missile-defence/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00009","name":"Rafael Advanced Defense Systems","type":"Company","role":"Israeli state arms maker; Spike missiles, Iron Dome, David's Sling","country":"Israel","slug":"rafael-advanced-defense-systems","profile":"Rafael Advanced Defense Systems is wholly owned by the State of Israel and makes Iron Dome, David's Sling, SPYDER and the Spike missile family. According to reports, Spike missiles fired from an Elbit Hermes 450 drone killed seven World Central Kitchen aid workers in Gaza on April 1, 2024. Israel's navy fired Spike NLOS missiles at the Gaza coast during the 2023 invasion. R2S, Rafael's U.S. joint venture with Raytheon, won a $1.25B contract in Nov 2025 for Tamir Iron Dome interceptors to be built in Arkansas, so U.S. workers now refill the shield that lets the bombing continue. Sales reached about $6.8B in 2025, with $423M net profit, and H1 2026 sales were NIS 10.63B. Its backlog stood at NIS 76.4B ($24B) on March 31, 2026, and Israel's Ministry of Defense owed it almost NIS 7B for equipment received. Greece's Aug 2026 'Achilles Shield' deal, worth about €3B, includes David's Sling and SPYDER.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spike_(missile)","https://www.rtx.com/news/news-center/2025/11/21/r2s-receives-1-25-billion-tamir-production-contract-for-facility-in-camden-arka","https://euro-sd.com/2026/03/news/industry-news/50222/rafael-reports-another-record-year/","https://www.bizportal.co.il/capitalmarket/news/article/20040791","https://www.ynetnews.com/business/article/s1funrbxmg","https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00010","name":"Palantir Technologies","type":"Company","role":"Targeting-software maker; Israel's 'war-related missions' partner, Maven builder","country":"USA","slug":"palantir-technologies","profile":"Palantir Technologies, co-founded by CEO Alex Karp and chairman Peter Thiel, sells targeting and surveillance software to armies and police. In January 2024 it agreed a strategic partnership with Israel's Ministry of Defense 'in support of war-related missions'. Al Jazeera reports its software 'integrates intercepted communications, satellite imagery and other datasets to help generate military targeting lists for Israeli forces', and UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese found reasonable grounds to believe it supplied Israel with predictive policing technology and its AI Platform. Karp's answer to the charge that Palantir kills Palestinians: 'mostly terrorists, that's true.' Its Maven Smart System, with a contract ceiling of nearly $1.3B, became the Pentagon's main targeting platform for the war on Iran; Bloomberg found Maven recommended the Minab school as a day-one target. Business is excellent: Q2 2026 revenue was $1.94B, up 93%, and its 2026 forecast is about $8.15B.","profile_src":["https://www.palantir.com/assets/xrfr7uokpv1b/3MuEeA8MLbLDAyxixTsiIe/9e4a11a7fb058554a8a1e3cd83e31c09/C134184_finaleprint.pdf","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/4/tech-giant-palantir-posts-otherworldly-growth-despite-criticism-over-gaza","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://defensescoop.com/2025/05/23/dod-palantir-maven-smart-system-contract-increase/","https://gizmodo.com/pentagon-investigators-say-overreliance-on-palantir-ai-tech-contributed-to-u-s-strike-that-killed-123-iranian-children-2000814477"],"profile_status":"reported","profile (sentence)":"The Washington Post reported that Palantir's Maven Smart System, running Anthropic's Claude, proposed and ranked targets for the U.S. war on Iran, and a Bloomberg investigation tied overreliance on Maven to the Feb 28, 2026 strike on a girls' school in Minab."},{"id":"COM-00011","name":"Amazon","type":"Company","role":"Tech conglomerate; AWS runs Israel's military cloud under Project Nimbus","country":"USA","slug":"amazon","profile":"Amazon is the U.S. retail and cloud giant founded by Jeff Bezos, and Amazon Web Services (AWS), its cloud division, is where part of Israel's war is stored. With Google, AWS holds Project Nimbus, the $1.2B (NIS 4B) Israeli government cloud contract that covers Israel's military. +972 Magazine and Local Call reported in Aug 2024 that AWS gives Israel's Military Intelligence Directorate a server farm to store masses of intelligence, which one source called 'endless storage'. A 2025 Guardian, +972 and Local Call investigation found Nimbus bars Amazon and Google from cutting off Israel's access, even when Israel breaks their policies. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report says Amazon, Microsoft and Alphabet give Israel 'virtually government-wide access' to cloud and AI. Amazon reported $382.1B in net sales for H1 2026, and its Q2 profit was boosted by a $53.4B gain mainly from its Anthropic stake. Bezos held about 8.8% (879M shares) in Aug 2026, and BlackRock about 6.6%.","profile_src":["https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/google-aws-win-12-billion-israel-nimbus-tender-for-cloud-services/","https://www.972mag.com/cloud-israeli-army-gaza-amazon-google-microsoft/","https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/israel-project-nimbus-google-amazon-winking-mechanism-data-leak-125103000892_1.html","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://ir.aboutamazon.com/news-release/news-release-details/2026/Amazon-com-Announces-Second-Quarter-Results/","https://www.nasdaq.com/press-release/amazoncom-announces-second-quarter-results-2026-07-30","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/much-amzn-stock-does-amazon-011405388.html"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00012","name":"Amazon Web Services (AWS)","type":"Company","role":"Amazon's cloud arm; 'endless storage' for Israeli military intelligence","country":"USA","slug":"amazon-web-services-aws","profile":"Amazon Web Services (AWS) is the cloud computing division of Amazon. Its revenue counts as Amazon's revenue, and its profits go to Amazon's shareholders, Jeff Bezos chief among them. With Google Cloud, AWS won Project Nimbus in 2021, Israel's $1.2B government cloud contract covering the Israeli military. In Aug 2024 +972 Magazine and Local Call reported that AWS supplies Israel's Military Intelligence Directorate with a server farm for intelligence, described by a source as 'endless storage'. Leaked Nimbus terms reported by the Guardian, +972 and Local Call in Oct 2025 bar AWS and Google from suspending Israel's access even when its conduct breaks their policies; the customer, in other words, cannot be fired. AWS opened a Tel Aviv region in July 2023 and plans to invest $7.2B in Israel through 2037. Since Nov 2024 it has hosted Anthropic's Claude for U.S. intelligence and military agencies through Palantir. AWS segment sales were $42.2B in Q2 2026, up 37%.","profile_src":["https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/google-aws-win-12-billion-israel-nimbus-tender-for-cloud-services/","https://www.972mag.com/cloud-israeli-army-gaza-amazon-google-microsoft/","https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/israel-project-nimbus-google-amazon-winking-mechanism-data-leak-125103000892_1.html","https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20230731044074/en","https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20241107699415/en/Anthropic-and-Palantir-Partner-to-Bring-Claude-AI-Models-to-AWS-for-U.S.-Government-Intelligence-and-Defense-Operations","https://ir.aboutamazon.com/news-release/news-release-details/2026/Amazon-com-Announces-Second-Quarter-Results/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00013","name":"Alphabet","type":"Company","role":"Google's parent; half of Israel's Project Nimbus military cloud","country":"USA","slug":"alphabet","profile":"Alphabet is the parent company of Google and Google Cloud, controlled by co-founders Larry Page and Sergey Brin and run by Sundar Pichai. Through Google Cloud it is half of Project Nimbus, Israel's $1.2B government and military cloud contract. The Washington Post reported in Jan 2025 that Google staff rushed Vertex AI tools to Israel's military in the weeks after Oct 7, 2023, and that the military also sought Gemini. Google fired more than 50 employees who protested Nimbus. Leaked contract terms reported by the Guardian, +972 and Local Call in Oct 2025 bar Google from cutting off Israel. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report says Alphabet, Microsoft and Amazon give Israel 'virtually government-wide access' to cloud and AI, and lists BlackRock as holding 6.6% of Alphabet. In March 2026 Alphabet completed its $32B purchase of Israeli cybersecurity firm Wiz, which became part of Google Cloud. Q2 2026 revenue was $119.8B.","profile_src":["https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/google-aws-win-12-billion-israel-nimbus-tender-for-cloud-services/","https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/google-provided-ai-technology-to-idf-during-israel-gaza-war/","https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/israel-project-nimbus-google-amazon-winking-mechanism-data-leak-125103000892_1.html","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/11/google-completes-32b-acquisition-of-wiz/","https://9to5google.com/2026/07/22/alphabet-q2-2026-earnings/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00015","name":"Google Cloud","type":"Company","role":"Alphabet's cloud arm; rushed AI tools to Israel's military after Oct 7","country":"USA","slug":"google-cloud","profile":"Google Cloud is the cloud and AI division of Google, owned by Alphabet; its earnings flow to Alphabet's shareholders. With Amazon Web Services it holds Project Nimbus, the $1.2B (NIS 4B) contract signed in 2021 to supply Israel's government and military with cloud computing and AI. According to the Washington Post, Google Cloud staff gave Israel's military access to its Vertex AI platform in the weeks after Oct 7, 2023, the military sought Gemini to process documents and audio, and its services were still in use in Nov 2024. Leaked Nimbus terms, reported by the Guardian, +972 and Local Call, bar Google from suspending Israel's access and set up a coded 'wink' payment to alert Israel when foreign authorities demand its data. Workers who objected fared worse than the client: Google fired more than 50 who protested the contract. In March 2026 the $32B Israeli firm Wiz joined Google Cloud. Revenue reached $24.77B in Q2 2026, up 82%.","profile_src":["https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/google-aws-win-12-billion-israel-nimbus-tender-for-cloud-services/","https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/google-provided-ai-technology-to-idf-during-israel-gaza-war/","https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/israel-project-nimbus-google-amazon-winking-mechanism-data-leak-125103000892_1.html","https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/11/google-completes-32b-acquisition-of-wiz/","https://9to5google.com/2026/07/22/alphabet-q2-2026-earnings/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00016","name":"Microsoft","type":"Company","role":"Cloud and AI giant; Azure stored Unit 8200's mass surveillance of Palestinians","country":"USA","slug":"microsoft","profile":"Microsoft, led by CEO Satya Nadella, ran the Azure cloud that held Israel's mass surveillance of Palestinians. An Aug 2025 investigation by The Guardian, +972 Magazine and Local Call found that Unit 8200, Israel's military intelligence unit, stored vast volumes of intercepted Palestinian phone calls on Azure servers in the Netherlands and Ireland; three Unit 8200 sources said the system helped guide deadly air strikes. In Feb 2025 AP reported that the Israeli military's use of Microsoft and OpenAI AI had spiked to nearly 200 times its pre-Oct 7 level by March 2024, and its data on Microsoft servers doubled to more than 13.6 petabytes. Microsoft had said in May 2025 that it found 'no evidence' of harm. In Sept 2025 it disabled 'specified' Israel Ministry of Defense subscriptions, but fired workers say most of the military contract remains. It fired at least four protesting employees in Aug 2025. Microsoft earned $133.7B on $331.8B revenue in FY2026 and owns 27% of OpenAI.","profile_src":["https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/8/7/microsoft-cloud-used-in-israeli-mass-surveillance-of-palestinians-report","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-02-22/how-us-tech-giants-supplied-israel-with-ai-models/104956164","https://blogs.microsoft.com/on-the-issues/2025/05/15/statement-technology-israel-gaza/","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/9/26/why-has-microsoft-cut-israel-off-from-some-of-its-services","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://news.microsoft.com/source/2026/07/29/microsoft-cloud-and-ai-strength-fuels-fourth-quarter-results-4/","https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2025/10/28/openai-restructures-into-public-benefit-firm-microsoft-takes-27-stake"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00017","name":"OpenAI","type":"Company","role":"AI company; quietly deleted its military ban, then joined the Pentagon","country":"USA","slug":"openai","profile":"OpenAI, led by CEO Sam Altman and president Greg Brockman, makes ChatGPT. Since its Oct 2025 restructuring into a public benefit corporation, Microsoft has owned 27%, worth about $135B. Until Jan 10, 2024 its usage policy banned 'military and warfare' use; it quietly deleted that language, The Intercept reported. In Feb 2025 AP found that the Israeli military's use of Microsoft and OpenAI AI, accessed through Microsoft's Azure, had spiked to nearly 200 times its pre-Oct 7 level by March 2024. The military used such models to transcribe and translate intelligence from mass surveillance, and Israeli intelligence officers described targeting errors caused by faulty machine translation. In June 2025 the Pentagon awarded OpenAI up to $200M for prototype frontier AI for 'warfighting' and back-office work. On Feb 27, 2026, hours after the Trump administration blacklisted Anthropic, OpenAI announced a deal to run its models on the Pentagon's classified network, promising they would not be used for domestic mass surveillance or autonomous weapons.","profile_src":["https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2025/10/28/openai-restructures-into-public-benefit-firm-microsoft-takes-27-stake","https://theintercept.com/2024/01/12/open-ai-military-ban-chatgpt/","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-02-22/how-us-tech-giants-supplied-israel-with-ai-models/104956164","https://breakingdefense.com/2025/06/openai-for-government-launches-with-200m-win-from-pentagon-cdao/","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/28/openai-strikes-deal-with-pentagon-to-use-tech-in-classified-network"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00018","name":"Anthropic","type":"Company","role":"AI company; Claude embedded in Maven, the Pentagon's Iran targeting system","country":"USA","slug":"anthropic","profile":"Anthropic, led by Dario Amodei, makes the Claude AI models. Since November 2024 it has supplied Claude to U.S. intelligence and military agencies through Palantir on AWS. Claude was embedded in Palantir's Maven Smart System during the 2026 Iran campaign and was reported by the Washington Post to support target generation and prioritization. Bloomberg's investigation found that Maven played a specific role in the Minab targeting chain and that overreliance on the system contributed to the strike. No public evidence currently establishes that Claude itself selected, recommended or processed the Minab school target. Reuters reported that Maven used multiple prompts and workflows built with Claude; The Guardian argued in March 2026 that Maven's target identification relies on older computer-vision systems, with Claude as a language layer. On 27 February 2026 Trump ordered agencies to drop Anthropic after it refused to allow fully autonomous weapons and mass domestic surveillance. Its investors still profit: Amazon booked a $53.4B gain in Q2 2026 mainly from its Anthropic stake.","profile_src":["https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20241107699415/en/Anthropic-and-Palantir-Partner-to-Bring-Claude-AI-Models-to-AWS-for-U.S.-Government-Intelligence-and-Defense-Operations","https://www.manton.org/2026/03/04/the-washington-post-reporting-on.html","https://gizmodo.com/pentagon-investigators-say-overreliance-on-palantir-ai-tech-contributed-to-u-s-strike-that-killed-123-iranian-children-2000814477","https://finance.yahoo.com/news/palantir-faces-challenge-remove-anthropic-213754143.html","https://aiweekly.co/alerts/guardian-minab-school-bombing-wasnt-a-claude-failure","https://abcnews.com/Politics/anthropic-latest-pentagon-contract-bar-ai-autonomous-weapons/story?id=130558898","https://www.nasdaq.com/press-release/amazoncom-announces-second-quarter-results-2026-07-30"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00019","name":"Oracle","type":"Company","role":"Database and cloud firm; software supplier to Israel's army and occupation","country":"USA","slug":"oracle","profile":"Oracle is the database and cloud company founded in 1977 by Larry Ellison, who remains its chairman. According to the Israeli research group Who Profits, Oracle's Israeli subsidiary develops and supplies software and services to the Israel Ministry of Defense and the army, provided ERP and planning software to the Military Intelligence Directorate, installed Exadata database machines for the air force in 2012, and supplies servers to the Civil Administration in the occupied West Bank, including for a system that monitors 'illegal construction', the pretext for demolishing Palestinian homes. Who Profits also reports that in January 2024, during the invasion of Gaza, Oracle donated seven tons of equipment worth more than half a million dollars. The Intercept reports a $319M Oracle data centre in Jerusalem, a confidential four-year project with the Israeli Air Force and an AI partnership with Rafael. Then-CEO Safra Catz stated the hiring policy plainly: 'if you're not for America or Israel, don't work here'.","profile_src":["https://www.whoprofits.org/companies/company/7396?oracle=","https://theintercept.com/2025/02/18/oracle-tiktok-israel-palestine-gaza/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00020","name":"Kaman Corporation","type":"Company","role":"Fuze maker; FMU-152 fuzes in the 2025 bomb package for Israel","country":"USA","slug":"kaman-corporation","profile":"Kaman Corporation is a U.S. maker of aerospace and weapons components that private equity firm Arcline Investment Management took private in April 2024, paying $46.00 per share, an enterprise value of about $1.8B; Kaman left the New York Stock Exchange. For two decades Kaman was the sole supplier to the U.S. Air Force of the FMU-152 Joint Programmable Fuze, the device that sets off a bomb at the chosen moment, and it sold the fuze to 26 other countries. The U.S. munitions package for Israel notified to Congress on Feb 7, 2025 includes 17,475 FMU-152A/B fuzes, to be paired with JDAM kits and GBU-39 bombs of the kind used in Gaza. The fuze business, Precision Fuzing & Sensors, now calls itself independent, a new name for the same trigger. Kaman's merger filing estimated golden-parachute payments of about $16.3M for its then-CEO, Ian Walsh.","profile_src":["https://kaman.com/arcline-completes-acquisition-of-kaman/","https://kaman.com/kaman-announces-324-million-joint-programmable-fuze-order/","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support","https://precisionfuzing.com/about/","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/54381/000114036124012403/ny20021849x2_defm14a.htm"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00021","name":"Arcline Investment Management","type":"Company","role":"Private equity buyer of Kaman, the bomb-fuze maker","country":"USA","slug":"arcline-investment-management","profile":"Arcline Investment Management is a U.S. private equity firm led by CEO Rajeev Amara since 2018 that specializes in buying aerospace and weapons suppliers. When it took Kaman Corporation private in April 2024 it had $8.9B in cumulative capital commitments. The Kaman deal paid $46.00 per share, an enterprise value of about $1.8B, and Kaman's then-CEO Ian Walsh was in line for about $16.3M in change-in-control payments. Kaman had been the sole supplier of the FMU-152 Joint Programmable Fuze to the U.S. Air Force since 2002. The U.S. munitions package for Israel notified on Feb 7, 2025 includes 17,475 FMU-152A/B fuzes, alongside 13,000 JDAM kits and 2,166 GBU-39 bombs, the weapon types found at Gaza strike sites. The fuze unit, Precision Fuzing & Sensors, now presents itself as independent. Whether Arcline still profits from it is not confirmed; private equity rarely volunteers the answer.","profile_src":["https://ir.arxis.com/corporate-governance/board-of-directors","https://kaman.com/arcline-completes-acquisition-of-kaman/","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/54381/000114036124012403/ny20021849x2_defm14a.htm","https://kaman.com/kaman-announces-324-million-joint-programmable-fuze-order/","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support","https://precisionfuzing.com/about/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00022","name":"REPKON USA","type":"Company","role":"Turkish-owned bomb-body maker; prime contractor for 12,000 bombs for Israel","country":"USA","slug":"repkon-usa","profile":"REPKON USA is the Texas subsidiary of Türkiye's Repkon Holdings. On April 2, 2025 it bought General Dynamics' 38-acre Garland plant north of Dallas, the site the U.S. had named weeks earlier as principal contractor for 35,529 MK-84 or BLU-117 bomb bodies for Israel. During the U.S.–Israeli war on Iran, Secretary of State Marco Rubio declared an emergency and skipped congressional review to approve a $151.8M sale to Israel of 12,000 BLU-110 1,000-pound bomb bodies, with REPKON USA as prime contractor. Ynet reported that the wider package was worth $660M and covered more than 20,000 MK-80 series bombs. A Turkish-owned company is therefore making bombs for Israel while Türkiye's government publicly condemns the genocide in Gaza, a contradiction that apparently survives contact with a purchase order. REPKON also signed a strategic memorandum with BAE Systems UK in Feb 2025.","profile_src":["https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/repkon-usa-announces-acquisition-of-general-dynamics-ordnance-and-tactical-systems-garland-operations-expanding-its-capabilities-in-defense-and-aerospace-manufacturing-302418890.html","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088258/israel-munitions-and-munitions-support","https://www.airforce-technology.com/news/us-state-department-israel-arms/","https://www.ynetnews.com/article/bkmojptkzx"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00024","name":"Rheinmetall","type":"Company","role":"German arms maker; reported tank-ammunition supplier to Israel","country":"Germany","slug":"rheinmetall","profile":"Rheinmetall is Germany's largest arms manufacturer, run by CEO Armin Papperger since 2013, and one of the biggest winners of Europe's rearmament: its backlog reached €63.8B, up from €49.9B a year earlier. In Jan 2024 German media reported that Berlin had provisionally approved an urgent Israeli request, made in Nov 2023, for 10,000 rounds of Rheinmetall tank ammunition. The delivery was reportedly still held up in Sept 2024, and AFSC rates the evidence of arrival inconclusive. Rheinmetall has not responded publicly to these reports. Germany has been one of Israel's main arms suppliers throughout the genocide in Gaza, which the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 was a genocide. Rheinmetall's shareholders include the same asset managers found across this network: BlackRock (about 7.15%, Feb 2026), Vanguard (3.84%), Fidelity's FMR (3.05%) and DWS (1.15%). The charge here is reported, not proven; the profits are not in dispute.","profile_src":["https://www.rheinmetall.com/en/rheinmetall_ag/group/gremien/executive_board/index.php","https://ir.rheinmetall.com/","https://investigate.afsc.org/company/rheinmetall","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.investing.com/equities/rheinmetall-ag-ownership"],"profile_status":"reported","profile (sentence)":"Rheinmetall's shareholders include the same asset managers found across this network: BlackRock (about 7.15%, Feb 2026), Vanguard (3.84%) and Fidelity's FMR (3.05%)."},{"id":"COM-00025","name":"Leonardo","type":"Company","role":"Italian state arms maker; naval guns on Israel's Gaza-shelling warships","country":"Italy","slug":"leonardo","profile":"Leonardo is Italy's state-controlled arms manufacturer. The Italian Treasury holds 30.2%, and Lorenzo Mariani has been CEO since May 7, 2026, succeeding former minister Roberto Cingolani. Its OTO Melara 76mm naval guns arm Israel's Sa'ar 4.5, Sa'ar 5 and Sa'ar 6 warships; according to AFSC, a Sa'ar 6 was used in combat for the first time on Oct 16, 2023, in the attacks on Gaza. Israel's 30 M-346 'Lavi' jet trainers, bought from Leonardo in 2012 for about $1B, train the pilots who fly Israel's bombing missions. Leonardo assembles F-35 wings and services the jets at Cameri for Lockheed Martin, but told shareholders in May 2026 that this work goes to third countries 'but NOT to the State of Israel', so this map draws no F-35 link from Leonardo to Israel. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report notes that BNP Paribas lent $410M to Leonardo and other firms supplying Israel. In H1 2026 Leonardo reported €10.0B in revenues and a €58.6B order backlog.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonardo_S.p.A.","https://www.leonardo.com/en/about/management/chief-executive-officer","https://investigate.afsc.org/company/leonardo","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.leonardo.com/documents/15646808/32047172/ComLDO_Risultati+1H2026_30_07_2026_ENG.pdf","https://www.leonardo.com/documents/15646808/31894715/File%2Bunico%2Bdomande%2Bpreassembleari.pdf?t=1777902622687"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00029","name":"Energean","type":"Company","role":"Gas producer; keeps Israel's grid running from the Karish field","country":"UK/Israel","slug":"energean","profile":"Energean is a gas producer listed in London and Tel Aviv, founded and run by Mathios Rigas. It pumps gas for Israel from the Karish and Tanin fields, which it bought in 2016 for $148M. Under the U.S.-brokered 2022 maritime deal with Lebanon, Israel keeps control of Karish, which began producing in Oct 2022. In H1 2026 Energean sold 2.13 bcm of gas into Israel's domestic market, and Israel produced 87 of the group's 124 kboe/d. The company reported $743M in revenue and $160M in after-tax profit, up 45%, and paid $26M in current Israeli tax, a modest contribution to the treasury of a state at war. When the U.S.–Israeli war on Iran began, Israel's energy ministry ordered Karish shut for 41 days, from Feb 28 to April 9, 2026. Energean's gas powers the economy of a state that the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 had committed genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Energean","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karish_gas_field","https://www.investegate.co.uk/announcement/rns/energean--enog/results-for-half-year-ended-30-june-2026/9761841","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-00035","name":"Federmann Enterprises","type":"Company","role":"Federmann family holding company; controls Elbit Systems","country":"Israel","slug":"federmann-enterprises","profile":"Federmann Enterprises is the private Israeli holding company of billionaire Michael Federmann, started by his father and uncle, and its main asset is control of Elbit Systems, Israel's largest private arms manufacturer. It held 19.3M Elbit shares (41.2%) as of June 17, 2026, a block worth about $13.6B at the end of Sept 2026. Its other big listed holding is Dan Hotels. Michael Federmann controls the vote. He and his sons David, Gideon and Daniel hold an indirect economic interest of about 25.5% of Elbit, and David has chaired Elbit since Aug 2023. Forbes estimated Michael Federmann's net worth at $6.6B in Nov 2025. The family fortune rises with Elbit's war business: a record $32.0B backlog at mid-2026 and new Israeli munitions orders in 2026. Elbit's Hermes 450 drone killed seven World Central Kitchen aid workers in Gaza. The drones pay for the hotels.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Federmann","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://www.elbitsystems.com/news/elbit-systems-reports-second-quarter-2026-results","https://thedefensepost.com/2026/04/24/israel-elbit-airborne-munitions-deals/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbit_Hermes_450"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"FND-00001","name":"BlackRock","type":"Fund/Asset Manager","role":"Asset manager; top owner of the arms and surveillance-tech industry","country":null,"slug":"blackrock","profile":"BlackRock, run by co-founder, chairman and CEO Larry Fink, is the world's largest asset manager, with a record $15.3T under management in Q2 2026. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report 'From economy of occupation to economy of genocide' names it the second-largest institutional investor in Palantir (8.6%), Microsoft (7.8%), Amazon (6.6%), Alphabet (6.6%) and IBM (8.6%), and third-largest in Lockheed Martin (7.2%) and Caterpillar (7.5%). The same report records BlackRock buying $68M of the Israeli treasury bonds that 'played a critical role in funding the ongoing assault on Gaza'. Its stakes have grown since: at 30 June 2026 it held RTX shares worth $21.0B, Boeing $13.2B and Lockheed Martin $9.6B, plus 8.3% of Northrop Grumman. Days after 7 October 2023 Fink told CNBC that 'we have the largest ETF in Israel' and that nobody was divesting 'for political reasons'. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://13f.info/data/13f/000201238326003238","https://www.cnbc.com/2023/10/13/cnbc-exclusive-cnbc-transcript-blackrock-chairman-ceo-larry-fink-speaks-with-cnbcs-squawk-on-the-street-today.html","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"FND-00002","name":"Vanguard","type":"Fund/Asset Manager","role":"Asset manager; bought $546M of Israeli war bonds","country":null,"slug":"vanguard","profile":"Vanguard is the second-largest asset manager in the world, with about $13.3T under management, owned by its own funds and run since July 2024 by former BlackRock executive Salim Ramji. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report names Vanguard the largest institutional investor in Caterpillar (9.8%), whose bulldozers demolish Palestinian homes, Chevron (8.9%) and Palantir (9.1%), and the second-largest in Lockheed Martin (9.2%) and Elbit Systems (2.0%). The report also records Vanguard buying $546M of Israeli treasury bonds, eight times BlackRock's purchase, as Israel borrowed to fund a military budget that doubled to 8.3% of GDP. As of 31 March 2026 Vanguard held 7.47% of RTX, 7.45% of Boeing, 7.22% of Northrop Grumman, 6.99% of Lockheed Martin and 6.88% of General Dynamics. Every new index contribution buys more of the companies arming a war the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 was a genocide. Passive investing, active consequences.","profile_src":["https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.secform4.com/13dg/2100119/0002100119-26-001059.html","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Vanguard_Group"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"FND-00003","name":"State Street","type":"Fund/Asset Manager","role":"Asset manager and custodian; largest single owner of Lockheed Martin","country":null,"slug":"state-street","profile":"State Street is the Boston bank and asset manager behind the SPDR index funds. At Dec 31, 2025 it held $53.8T in assets under custody or administration and $5.7T under management, and it is one of the largest owners of the U.S. weapons industry. As of June 30, 2026 it held about 14.3% of Lockheed Martin ($16.8B), 9.27% of Northrop Grumman ($6.7B), 4.81% of Boeing ($8.2B) and 4.37% of General Dynamics. RTX's 2026 proxy lists it as owner of 6.8% (91.9M shares) at the end of 2025, and it holds 1.73% of BAE Systems. These companies make the F-35s, Hellfires, GBU-39s and bomb bodies documented in strikes on Gaza. State Street's index model means every new pension contribution helps fund them, in a war the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 was a genocide. The savers are rarely asked.","profile_src":["https://investors.statestreet.com/investor-news-events/press-releases/news-details/2026/State-Street-Corporation-NYSE-STT-Reports-Fourth-Quarter-and-Full-Year-2025-Financial-Results/default.aspx","https://13f.info/data/13f/000009375126000583","https://materials.proxyvote.com/Approved/75513E/20260303/NPS_625722/40.html","https://www.investing.com/equities/bae-systems-plc-ownership","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"FND-00004","name":"Fidelity / FMR","type":"Fund/Asset Manager","role":"Johnson-family asset manager; one of Boeing's largest owners","country":null,"slug":"fidelity-fmr","profile":"Fidelity Investments, through parent FMR LLC, is the privately owned Boston investment house that the Johnson family has controlled since Edward C. Johnson II founded it in 1946. His granddaughter Abigail Johnson has been CEO since 2014 and chair since 2016, and she runs a firm that reported $18.0T in assets under administration, $7.1T in managed assets, $37.7B in revenue and $12.7B in operating income for 2025. Fidelity is one of Boeing's largest owners, with 55M shares (7.0%) at Dec 31, 2025; Boeing makes the GBU-39 bombs and JDAM kits documented in strikes on Gaza's schools and camps and on journalists in Lebanon. At June 30, 2026 Fidelity's 13F also showed 9.9M RTX shares ($1.9B), 4.1M General Dynamics shares, 1.7M Lockheed Martin shares and 1.3M Northrop Grumman shares. It notified BAE Systems of a 5.01% stake in 2024 and held about 3.05% of Rheinmetall in Jan 2026.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abigail_Johnson","https://about.fidelity.com/data-and-insights/2025-annual-report","https://www.secform4.com/13dg/315066/0000315066-26-000359.html","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tel_al-Sultan_attack","https://www.hrw.org/news/2024/11/25/lebanon-us-arms-used-israeli-strike-journalists","https://13f.info/data/13f/000031506626002260","https://www.investing.com/equities/rheinmetall-ag-ownership"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"FND-00005","name":"Capital Group","type":"Fund/Asset Manager","role":"Private asset manager; largest shareholder of BAE Systems","country":null,"slug":"capital-group","profile":"Capital Group is a privately owned Los Angeles investment firm founded in 1931, with more than $3.6T under management as of June 30, 2026. Through its American Funds units it is the single largest shareholder of BAE Systems, with 11.04% of voting rights as of Jan 22, 2026. BAE builds the rear fuselage of every F-35, including Israel's, and those components were exempted when the UK suspended arms licences to Israel; Capital Group's biggest arms holding is therefore the one Britain chose not to touch. As of March 31, 2026 its investment arms also held 5.2% of Boeing, 5.2% of Northrop Grumman and 3.9% of RTX, and at mid-2026 they held about 3.1M Lockheed Martin shares and 3.7M General Dynamics shares. Its returns are tied to the F-35s, GBU-39s and interceptors used in Gaza, Lebanon and Iran, during what the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 was a genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.capitalgroup.com/about-us.html","https://www.investegate.co.uk/announcement/rns/bae-systems--ba./holding-s-in-company/9396456","https://www.baesystems.com/en/product/f35-lightning-ii","https://www.euronews.com/my-europe/2025/06/30/uk-high-court-rejects-challenge-against-selling-military-parts-to-israel","https://www.secform4.com/13dg/1422849/0001422849-26-000086.html","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001133421/000156223026000095/xslSCHEDULE_13G_X02/primary_doc.xml","https://www.secform4.com/13dg/1422848/0001422848-26-000064.html"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"FND-00006","name":"Longview Asset Management","type":"Fund/Asset Manager","role":"Investment manager; 10% owner of bomb-body maker General Dynamics","country":null,"slug":"longview-asset-management","profile":"Longview Asset Management is a Chicago-area investment manager that holds a 10% owner position in General Dynamics, the U.S. weapons manufacturer whose Garland plant was named in Feb 2025 as principal contractor for 35,529 MK-84 or BLU-117 bomb bodies for Israel. In May 2026 Longview filed an initial Form 3 as a 10% owner after GD's buybacks shrank its share count, as disclosed in GD's April 29, 2026 Form 10-Q. The filing reports no pecuniary interest for Longview itself, which means it holds the stake for other beneficial owners who prefer not to be named. GD booked about $170.1B in revenue and $13.6B in net earnings from 2023 to June 2026, and its biggest owners gain as the bombs it supplied are used in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/GD/form-3-general-dynamics-corp-initial-statement-of-beneficial-ownershi-5291768768c4.html","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088258/israel-munitions-and-munitions-support","https://s22.q4cdn.com/891946778/files/doc_financials/2026/q2/GD-2026-07-05-Exhibit-99-1.pdf"],"profile_status":"reported","profile (sentence)":"Longview manages these shares for client accounts and says it has no pecuniary interest itself; who ultimately owns the stake is not disclosed."},{"id":"ORG-00001","name":"AIPAC","type":"Organization","role":"Pro-Israel lobby; buys primaries to unseat critics of the genocide","country":"USA","slug":"aipac","profile":"The American Israel Public Affairs Committee (AIPAC) is widely regarded as the most powerful pro-Israel lobby in Washington. It is a 501(c)(4) group that since late 2021 has also run two election vehicles: AIPAC PAC, which channels donations to candidates, and the United Democracy Project (UDP) super PAC. FEC filings show the two raised about $145M in the 2024 cycle (AIPAC PAC $57.9M, UDP $87.2M) and about $162M from January 2025 to August 2026 (AIPAC PAC $52.3M, UDP $109.7M). That money is used to defeat critics of Israel's war. In 2024 UDP spent about $9.9M against Jamaal Bowman and over $5.2M against Cori Bush, both of whom lost. In May 2026 it helped unseat Republican Thomas Massie, a vocal opponent of aid to Israel and of the Iran war. AIPAC presses Congress for unconditional military aid, and Congress obliges: the $26.38B supplemental passed in April 2024, and only 17 senators voted to advance a bid to block arms sales in November 2024.","profile_src":["https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00797670/?cycle=2024","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2024","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00797670/?cycle=2026","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026","https://www.factcheck.org/2024/09/united-democracy-project-2/","https://www.lpm.org/news/2026-07-17/a-record-shattering-37m-was-spent-on-kentuckys-massie-gallrein-race-heres-who-funded-it","https://responsiblestatecraft.org/massie-loss-aipac-primary/","https://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/house-passes-series-security-supplemental-bills","https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1182/vote_118_2_00294.htm"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"ORG-00002","name":"AIPAC PAC","type":"Organization","role":"AIPAC's federal PAC; bundles donations to both parties' candidates","country":"USA","slug":"aipac-pac","profile":"AIPAC PAC is the American Israel Public Affairs Committee's federal political action committee, registered with the FEC on 15 December 2021 (ID C00797670). It collects donations from individuals and passes them to candidates, so its money appears on the books of hundreds of members of Congress. In the 2024 cycle it raised $57.9M and spent $57.4M, of which $53.7M went to other committees, mainly candidate campaigns. From January 2025 to 31 August 2026 it raised $52.3M and gave $47.8M to other committees. It gives to both parties, so support for Israel rather than party decides who gets paid. The results speak for the investment: Congress passed the $26.38B Israel supplemental by 366 to 58 in the House in April 2024, and 80 senators voted against advancing a resolution to block a weapons export licence to Israel in November 2024.","profile_src":["https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00797670/?cycle=2024","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00797670/?cycle=2026","https://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/house-passes-series-security-supplemental-bills","https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1182/vote_118_2_00294.htm"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"ORG-00003","name":"United Democracy Project","type":"Organization","role":"AIPAC's super PAC; unlimited attack ads against Israel's critics","country":"USA","slug":"united-democracy-project","profile":"United Democracy Project (UDP) is AIPAC's super PAC, registered on 3 January 2022 (FEC ID C00799031). Unlike AIPAC PAC it can take unlimited money and spend it on attack ads. FEC filings show it raised $87.2M in the 2024 cycle and spent $37.9M on independent expenditures. From January 2025 to 31 August 2026 it raised $109.7M, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures and still had $54.9M in cash. Its main targets are critics of Israel's war. In 2024 it spent about $9.9M against Jamaal Bowman and over $5.2M against Cori Bush, both of whom lost, and about $4.6M against Dave Min. In 2026 FEC-based tallies show about $20.1M against Abdul El-Sayed in Michigan's Senate primary, which he won, about $10.5M for his rival Haley Stevens, $2.3M against Tom Malinowski, who lost, and $3.6M–$4.1M against Republican Thomas Massie, who lost his seat in May 2026. It also backed winners such as George Latimer and Wesley Bell. Its ads rarely mention Israel, the one subject it exists for.","profile_src":["https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2024","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026","https://www.factcheck.org/2024/09/united-democracy-project-2/","https://legis1.com/news/united-democracy-project-spending-spent-5341","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/8/5/abdul-el-sayed-wins-michigan-democratic-primary-for-senate-in-blow-to-aipac","https://www.lpm.org/news/2026-07-17/a-record-shattering-37m-was-spent-on-kentuckys-massie-gallrein-race-heres-who-funded-it","https://responsiblestatecraft.org/massie-loss-aipac-primary/","https://www.wbez.org/government-politics/elections/2026/03/18/illinois-primary-super-pac-spending-aipac-cryptocurrency-ai-sports-betting","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Democracy_Project","https://www.influencewatch.org/political-party/united-democracy-project-udp/","https://missouriindependent.com/2026/08/04/wesley-bell-beats-cori-bush-in-democratic-primary-for-st-louis-congressional-seat/","https://www.jta.org/2026/02/10/politics/aipac-defends-2-3m-spend-against-pro-israel-politician-in-nj-11-where-anti-israel-candidate-is-prevailing"],"profile_status":"documented","profile (sentence)":"FEC filings, the canonical record, show that from January 2025 to 31 August 2026 it raised $109.7M, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures and still had $54.9M in cash; per-candidate totals keep changing as new reports come in."},{"id":"ORG-00004","name":"Democratic Majority for Israel","type":"Organization","role":"Pro-Israel Democratic group and PAC; enforces loyalty to Israel's war","country":"USA","slug":"democratic-majority-for-israel","profile":"Democratic Majority for Israel (DMFI) is a 501(c)(4) group founded in January 2019 by Democratic strategists, including pollster Mark Mellman, to keep the Democratic Party firmly behind Israel. Its political arm, DMFI PAC (FEC ID C00710848), is a hybrid PAC that can give to candidates and also run independent ads. FEC filings show DMFI PAC raised $6.7M in the 2024 cycle and spent $4.2M on independent expenditures. From January 2025 to August 2026 it raised $7.4M and spent $2.8M on independent expenditures. Most of its receipts are filed as 'other receipts' rather than donations from individuals, which made up only about $0.5M in 2024 and $0.2M in 2025–26, so the grassroots are thin. Its record includes over $1.4M against Bernie Sanders in 2020 and campaigns against progressive critics of Israel such as Nina Turner. It works alongside AIPAC to make support for Israel's war a test of loyalty inside the Democratic Party.","profile_src":["https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00710848/?cycle=2024","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00710848/?cycle=2026","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Majority_for_Israel"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"ORG-00006","name":"Republican Jewish Coalition","type":"Organization","role":"Republican pro-Israel group; spent millions to oust Thomas Massie","country":"USA","slug":"republican-jewish-coalition","profile":"The Republican Jewish Coalition (RJC) is a 501(c)(4) group that ties Republican politics to hardline support for Israel. Matthew Brooks is executive director and Norm Coleman is chairman, and it reported about $13.4M in revenue for 2024. It funds election spending through the RJC Victory Fund super PAC and its own PAC. Its biggest 2026 target was Republican Thomas Massie, who voted against aid to Israel and backed war-powers votes against the war on Iran. Louisville Public Media found the RJC Victory Fund spent $3.9M on ads for challenger Ed Gallrein. Its largest disclosed donor was $5M from Kua Ventures LLC, an entity with no public footprint, which is a polite way of saying nobody knows whose money it is. Massie lost 54–45 in May 2026 in what Responsible Statecraft called the most expensive House primary in US history.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Jewish_Coalition","https://www.lpm.org/news/2026-07-17/a-record-shattering-37m-was-spent-on-kentuckys-massie-gallrein-race-heres-who-funded-it","https://responsiblestatecraft.org/massie-loss-aipac-primary/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"ORG-00008","name":"J Street","type":"Organization","role":"Liberal pro-Israel lobby and PAC; funds Democrats who vote for military aid","country":"USA","slug":"j-street","profile":"J Street is a 501(c)(4) lobby that calls itself 'pro-Israel, pro-peace', and JStreetPAC (FEC ID C00441949) is its candidate-funding arm. FEC filings show JStreetPAC raised $14.6M in the 2024 cycle and passed $14.4M to candidates and other committees. From January 2025 to August 2026 it raised $7.3M and gave $7.1M. It makes no independent expenditures. J Street long supported continued US military aid to Israel, and critics reported it pushed Democrats to resist early ceasefire calls in October 2023. It later broke with the mainstream lobby: in November 2024 it backed Bernie Sanders' resolutions to block certain arms sales, which only 17 senators voted to advance. In August 2025 its founder Jeremy Ben-Ami said he had been persuaded that international courts will one day find Israel broke the Genocide Convention. Its money still mostly backs Democrats who vote for military aid, so the conscience arrived before the cheque book changed.","profile_src":["https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00441949/?cycle=2024","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00441949/?cycle=2026","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J_Street","https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1182/vote_118_2_00294.htm"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"ORG-00010","name":"Christians United for Israel (CUFI)","type":"Organization","role":"Christian Zionist mass lobby; mobilises evangelicals behind Israeli expansion","country":"USA","slug":"christians-united-for-israel-cufi","profile":"Christians United for Israel (CUFI) is the largest Christian Zionist group in the United States. Founded by Texas televangelist John Hagee, it claims over 10 million members. It mobilises evangelical voters behind Israeli expansion and confrontation with Iran, holding an annual Washington summit where thousands of delegates lobby their representatives. Its political arm, the CUFI Action Fund, is a 501(c)(4) that runs the lobbying and campaigns. Its theology treats support for the Israeli state as a religious duty, which builds a large evangelical base that pushes Republican lawmakers against any conditions on aid. Reports say it campaigned for Israel's Gaza offensive and for confronting Iran during the 2023–2026 wars, but we could not verify this here. We also could not retrieve audited spending totals for 2024 or 2026, and CUFI has no FEC-registered PAC on this map, so its influence is measured in votes and pressure rather than disclosed dollars.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christians_United_for_Israel","https://cufiactionfund.org/"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"ORG-00012","name":"Zionist Organization of America","type":"Organization","role":"Hardline Zionist advocacy group; opposes any Palestinian state","country":"USA","slug":"zionist-organization-of-america","profile":"The Zionist Organization of America (ZOA), led since 1994 by Morton Klein, is one of the most hardline pro-Israel groups in the US. Its record: it opposes any Palestinian state, opposed Israel's 2005 withdrawal from Gaza and backed annexing parts of the occupied West Bank in 2020. It is a 501(c)(3) charity, so it cannot run a PAC, but it lobbies Congress and the executive branch and campaigns against Palestinian rights activism on US campuses, which makes it tax-exempt while doing so. We could not retrieve its 2024 or 2026 spending totals.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zionist_Organization_of_America"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"ORG-00013","name":"Friends of the IDF (FIDF)","type":"Organization","role":"US charity raising tax-deductible money for Israel's army","country":"USA","slug":"friends-of-the-idf-fidf","profile":"Friends of the Israel Defense Forces (FIDF) is a US 501(c)(3) charity that raises tax-deductible money for soldiers and units of the Israeli army. It reported $281.96M in revenue and $336.43M in total assets for fiscal 2023, up from $89.34M raised in 2022, and raised over $50M in the weeks after 7 October 2023. FIDF says it does not fund weapons, but its programmes directly support Israel's fighting force: 'Adopt a Brigade' sponsored 24 brigades (over 50,000 soldiers) with about $2.5M in 2022, and it builds facilities on IDF bases and pays scholarships for former combat soldiers. Its CEO is retired Israeli major general Nadav Padan. Billionaires fund it heavily: Oracle's Larry Ellison gave $16.6M at a 2017 gala that raised $53.8M. US taxpayers subsidise these gifts through the charitable deduction while the army it supports faces the ICC arrest warrants and the UN Commission of Inquiry genocide finding.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friends_of_the_Israel_Defense_Forces","https://www.jta.org/2017/11/05/united-states/record-53-8-million-raised-for-idf-soldiers-at-beverly-hills-gala","https://www.npr.org/2024/11/21/g-s1-35169/icc-israel-hamas-arrest-warrants-gaza","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"ORG-00015","name":"Pro-Israel America PAC","type":"Organization","role":"Defunct pro-Israel bundling PAC; forerunner of AIPAC's money machine","country":"USA","slug":"pro-israel-america-pac","profile":"Pro-Israel America PAC was a federal PAC (FEC ID C00699470), registered on 18 March 2019, that collected donations for pro-Israel candidates before AIPAC launched its own PAC in December 2021. The FEC lists it as terminated. Its last filing covered 1 January to 2 March 2023, with $2,529 in receipts and $8,650 in disbursements, ending with zero cash, so it spent nothing in the 2024 or 2026 cycles. It did not die so much as get absorbed: its function passed to AIPAC PAC and the United Democracy Project, which together raised about $145M in 2024 and $162M in 2025–26. It matters as an early part of the pro-Israel money network, which used the same donation-bundling model that AIPAC now runs at far larger scale. The site should label it as historic or terminated rather than active.","profile_src":["https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00699470/?cycle=2024","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00797670/?cycle=2024","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2024"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00001","name":"U.S. Government","type":"Government","role":"Israel's armourer, banker and diplomatic shield","country":"USA","slug":"u-s-government","profile":"Treasury's Monthly Treasury Statements record U.S. military outlays of $820.7B in FY2023, $874.0B in FY2024 and $916.6B in FY2025, and $481.1B in the first half of FY2026, about $3.09T in all. Brown University's Costs of War Project estimates that Washington spent $21.7B on military aid to Israel from October 2023 to September 2025, not counting arms sales agreed for later delivery; the Council on Foreign Relations counts over $300B in aid since 1948, adjusted for inflation. In 2026 it notified Congress of a $3.8B Apache sale on 30 January, then used emergency powers to skip congressional review of a $151.8M sale of 12,000 BLU-110 bomb bodies in March and a $992.4M sale of 10,000 APKWS-II rockets on 1 May, during Israel's war on Iran. In September 2026 it informally notified a $2.8B package of 20,000 MK-84 and 20,000 BLU-117 2,000-pound bombs, now on hold in Congress. And when the ICC issued an arrest warrant for Benjamin Netanyahu, Donald Trump answered in February 2025 with Executive Order 14203, sanctioning the court's personnel.","profile_src":["https://api.fiscaldata.treasury.gov/services/api/fiscal_service/v1/accounting/mts/mts_table_9?filter=record_calendar_month:eq:09,classification_desc:eq:National%20Defense","https://www.everycrsreport.com/reports/RL33222.html","https://api.fiscaldata.treasury.gov/services/api/fiscal_service/v1/accounting/mts/mts_table_9?filter=classification_desc:eq:National%20Defense,record_calendar_month:eq:09&sort=-record_date&page[size]=10","https://costsofwar.watson.brown.edu/paper/AidToIsrael","https://www.cfr.org/article/us-aid-israel-four-charts","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4394583/israel-ah-64e-apache-helicopters","https://www.forumarmstrade.org/us-israel-trump-era.html","https://www.globalsecurity.org/military/library/news/2026/05/mil-260501-state05.htm","https://www.airforce-technology.com/news/us-state-department-israel-arms/","https://www.turkishminute.com/2026/03/11/turkish-companys-us-unit-changes-name-after-backlash-over-sale-of-1000-pound-bombs-to-israel/","https://www.sanders.senate.gov/press-releases/news-sanders-files-joint-resolutions-of-disapproval-to-block-nearly-660-million-in-bomb-sales-to-israel/","https://www.ynetnews.com/article/bkmojptkzx","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/16/trump-administration-plans-2-8bn-sale-of-2000-pound-bombs-to-israel","https://umdmitzpeh.com/2026/09/28/trumps-arms-deal-remains-in-a-stalemate","https://democrats-foreignaffairs.house.gov/press-releases?ContentRecord_id=2AC6AE1D-BDCD-4E19-B8A7-BCA59F204151","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Criminal_Court_arrest_warrants_for_Israeli_leaders"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00002","name":"U.S. Department of Defense","type":"Government","role":"Pentagon; the arms industry's biggest customer and Iran war launcher","country":"USA","slug":"u-s-department-of-defense","profile":"The US Department of Defense is the world's largest buyer of weapons and the main source of revenue for US arms makers. USAspending shows contract obligations of $456.9B in FY2023, $445.8B in FY2024 and $491.8B in FY2025, about $1.76T including FY2026 data published so far. It runs the production lines that supply Israel. In May 2024 the Air Force awarded Boeing a $7.5B JDAM contract that included foreign-sales funds. Pentagon stocks were drawn down for Israel and then refilled with $4.4B from the April 2024 supplemental. On 28 February 2026 it launched Operation Epic Fury against Iran alongside Israel, which the CBO says cost about $38B by 1 August 2026. Amnesty found JDAM parts in Tehran neighbourhoods where US-Israeli strikes killed civilians, and said the attacks may amount to war crimes. The industry was rewarded promptly: weeks after the main fighting, RTX won a $20.7B multi-year AMRAAM contract in September 2026.","profile_src":["https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/agency/097/obligations_by_award_category/?fiscal_year=2025","https://www.gao.gov/assets/gao-25-107558.pdf","https://www.defensenews.com/air/2024/05/28/boeing-wins-75-billion-contract-from-us-air-force-for-guided-bombs/","https://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/house-passes-series-security-supplemental-bills","https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2026-09/62756-Iran.pdf","https://www.amnesty.org.au/investigation-into-us-israeli-strikes-on-tehran-neighbourhoods-reveals-devastating-civilian-harm/","https://raytheon.mediaroom.com/2026-09-28-RTXs-Raytheon-awarded-20-7-billion-multi-year-contract-for-AMRAAM-under-landmark-production-agreement"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00003","name":"U.S. Congress","type":"Government","role":"US legislature; funds and waves through Israel's weapons","country":"USA","slug":"u-s-congress","profile":"The US Congress holds the purse strings and can block arms sales, and it has consistently chosen to arm Israel through the genocide. In April 2024 the House passed the $26.38B Israel Security Supplemental by 366 to 58. The bill included $4B for Iron Dome and David's Sling, $1.2B for Iron Beam, $3.5B in Foreign Military Financing, $1B for artillery and munitions production, and $4.4B to refill US stocks sent to Israel. It also banned funding for UNRWA, the main UN aid agency for Palestinians. On 20 November 2024 the Senate voted 17 to 80 against even advancing Bernie Sanders' resolution to block a weapons export licence to Israel. Congress let the 2025 bomb and JDAM sales proceed without a block. Members who oppose aid to Israel, such as Thomas Massie, have been targeted with millions in AIPAC-linked spending. The UN Commission of Inquiry found in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide.","profile_src":["https://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/house-passes-series-security-supplemental-bills","https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1182/vote_118_2_00294.htm","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support","https://www.lpm.org/news/2026-07-17/a-record-shattering-37m-was-spent-on-kentuckys-massie-gallrein-race-heres-who-funded-it","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00005","name":"Government of Israel","type":"Government","role":"State found by UN inquiry to have committed genocide; owns IAI, Rafael","country":"Israel","slug":"government-of-israel","profile":"The Government of Israel directs the assault on Gaza and the wars on Lebanon and, in 2025–2026, Iran, and it owns two of its biggest arms makers, Rafael (99.9%) and Israel Aerospace Industries (100%). In January 2024 the ICJ found a plausible risk to Palestinians' rights under the Genocide Convention and ordered provisional measures, adding further orders in March and May 2024. On 21 November 2024 the ICC issued arrest warrants for Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and former Military Minister Yoav Gallant for alleged war crimes and crimes against humanity, including starvation as a method of warfare. In September 2025 the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded Israel had committed genocide and named Netanyahu, President Isaac Herzog and Gallant as having incited it. The Gaza Ministry of Health reported 74,016 Palestinians killed and 175,068 injured by 26 September 2026. The government also profits from the killing, through record arms exports of over $14.7B in 2024.","profile_src":["https://www.rafael.co.il/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Refael_ENGLISH120225MINA_All_compressed.pdf","https://www.iai.co.il/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/IAI-FS-CONSOLIDATED-AND-SOLO-12.21.pdf","https://www.icj-cij.org/node/203447","https://www.icj-cij.org/case/192","https://www.npr.org/2024/11/21/g-s1-35169/icc-israel-hamas-arrest-warrants-gaza","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://english.wafa.ps/Pages/Details/175165","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-147-billion-in-2024"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00006","name":"Israel Ministry of Defense","type":"Government","role":"Military ministry; buys the bombs, sells the 'combat-proven' results","country":"Israel","slug":"israel-ministry-of-defense","profile":"The Israel Ministry of Defense (IMOD) buys the military's weapons, including US sales such as JDAMs, Hellfires and 2,000-pound bombs, and runs SIBAT, the agency that markets Israeli weapons abroad. It reported record arms export deals of $13.07B in 2023 and over $14.7B in 2024, with Europe taking 54% in 2024 and interceptor systems 48%. It brokered Slovakia's €560M Barak MX deal, Germany's Arrow 3 expansion and Greece's €3B 'Achilles Shield'. It openly sells on the war, saying the Greek deal draws 'on the extensive operational experience Israel's military establishment has gained during the war'. IMOD also buys Big Tech services. Palantir agreed a strategic partnership with it in January 2024 'to help the country's war effort'. Microsoft provides IMOD with Azure cloud and AI services, and in September 2025 cut some subscriptions after finding evidence supporting reports of mass surveillance of Palestinians. Its former minister Yoav Gallant faces an ICC arrest warrant.","profile_src":["https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/for-the-third-consecutive-year-israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-13-billion-in-2023","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-147-billion-in-2024","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-mod-seals-560-million-euro-agreement-barak-mx-integrated-air-defense-system-produced-by-iai-sold-to-slovakia-in-landmark-agreement","https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement","https://www.palantir.com/assets/xrfr7uokpv1b/3MuEeA8MLbLDAyxixTsiIe/9e4a11a7fb058554a8a1e3cd83e31c09/C134184_finaleprint.pdf","https://blogs.microsoft.com/on-the-issues/2025/05/15/statement-technology-israel-gaza/","https://blogs.microsoft.com/on-the-issues/2025/09/25/update-on-ongoing-microsoft-review/","https://www.npr.org/2024/11/21/g-s1-35169/icc-israel-hamas-arrest-warrants-gaza"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00007","name":"Israel Defense Forces (IDF)","type":"Government","role":"Israel's military; the force carrying out the genocide in Gaza","country":"Israel","slug":"israel-defense-forces-idf","profile":"The Israel Defense Forces (IDF) carried out the assault on Gaza and the wars on Lebanon and Iran from October 2023, using US-made JDAMs, GBU-39s, Hellfires and 2,000-pound bombs. Gaza's Ministry of Health reported 74,016 Palestinians killed and 175,068 injured from 7 October 2023 to 26 September 2026. UN OCHA, citing the ministry, recorded 1,334 more killed after the 10 October 2025 ceasefire, as of 2 September 2026; the ceasefire, in other words, did not stop the killing. Amnesty, CNN, NPR and Bellingcat traced US bombs to strikes on homes, tent camps and UN schools, including Rafah on 26 May 2024 (at least 45 killed) and Nuseirat on 6 June 2024 (at least 32 killed). The ICJ ordered provisional measures in January 2024. The ICC issued arrest warrants in November 2024 alleging starvation as a method of warfare and attacks on civilians. In September 2025 the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded Israel committed genocide. In 2026 Amnesty said US-Israeli strikes on Tehran may amount to war crimes.","profile_src":["https://english.wafa.ps/Pages/Details/175165","https://www.ochaopt.org/content/humanitarian-situation-report-4-september-2026","https://amp.cnn.com/cnn/2024/05/28/middleeast/gaza-us-munitions-rafah-strike-analysis-intl-hnk","https://www.npr.org/2024/06/06/nx-s1-4995090/israel-gaza-school-strike-us-bomb","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.icj-cij.org/node/203447","https://www.npr.org/2024/11/21/g-s1-35169/icc-israel-hamas-arrest-warrants-gaza","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.amnesty.org.au/investigation-into-us-israeli-strikes-on-tehran-neighbourhoods-reveals-devastating-civilian-harm/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00008","name":"Government of Germany","type":"Government","role":"Israel's second-largest arms supplier; sued at the ICJ by Nicaragua","country":"Germany","slug":"government-of-germany","profile":"Germany both arms Israel and buys its weapons. It approved €326.5M in arms exports to Israel in 2023, a sharp rise on previous years, citing its Staatsräson commitment to Israel's security. In August 2025 Chancellor Friedrich Merz suspended exports of weapons that 'could be used in the Gaza Strip', but the suspension was lifted in November 2025, after three months of conscience. Germany is also the largest customer for Israeli weapons. It signed for IAI's Arrow 3 in September 2023, received the first battery at Holzdorf in December 2025, and in December 2025 the Bundestag approved a €3B expansion, taking the programme above $6.5B. Nicaragua sued Germany at the ICJ in March 2024 for allegedly facilitating genocide. The court declined provisional measures on 30 April 2024, but the case continues, with hearings on Germany's preliminary objections in September 2026.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germany–Israel_relations","https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-delivers-arrow-3-to-germany-in-largest-defense-export-deal-ever/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/german-parliament-approves-3-5b-expansion-of-arrow-3-deal-with-israel/","https://defence-industry.eu/iai-signs-usd-3-1-billion-follow-on-contract-to-expand-germanys-arrow-3-missile-defence-programme/","https://www.icj-cij.org/case/193"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00009","name":"Government of Finland","type":"Government","role":"Buyer of David's Sling, signed five weeks into the bombardment","country":"Finland","slug":"government-of-finland","profile":"Finland's government became the first export customer for Rafael and RTX's David's Sling. The Ministry of Defence authorised the purchase in April 2023, and the contract was signed with Israel's Ministry of Defense on 12 November 2023, five weeks into the bombardment of Gaza. The contract is worth about €317M, including €103M of options exercised immediately, with first deliveries expected from 2025 and full capability by 2030. Finland went ahead after the ICJ's January 2024 provisional-measures order. It is part of a wider European rush for Israeli interceptor systems: Europe took 54% of Israel's record $14.7B in 2024 arms export deals. The money goes to state-owned Rafael, whose systems are marketed on their wartime record, and to RTX. We could not confirm Finland's 2026 delivery status or any further Finnish purchases from Israel, which remain open questions.","profile_src":["https://militarnyi.com/en/news/finland-signs-agreement-with-israel-to-purchase-david-s-sling-system/","https://norskluftvern.com/2025/11/25/finlands-air-defense-transformation-from-neutral-defender-to-natos-northern-anchor/","https://www.icj-cij.org/node/203447","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-147-billion-in-2024","https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/factbox-what-israels-multi-layered-defence-against-iranian-missiles"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00010","name":"Government of Denmark","type":"Government","role":"Buyer of Elbit artillery used in Gaza; F-35 programme partner","country":"Denmark","slug":"government-of-denmark","profile":"Denmark's government bought 19 ATMOS howitzers and 8 PULS rocket launchers from Elbit Systems, Israel's largest private weapons maker, announced in January 2023. They replace CAESAR guns Denmark gave Ukraine, with deliveries from 2023 and full operation by 2025. Elbit announced $252M in matching contracts with a European NATO country in March 2023. Deliveries continued through the Gaza genocide, even though PULS was used 'extensively' by the Israeli army in Gaza and Lebanon. The money went to Elbit, which the UN Special Rapporteur's July 2025 report names as a key domestic supplier of weapons for the assault. Denmark is also a partner in the F-35 programme, whose jets Israel flies over Gaza and Lebanon; Danish company Terma makes more than 70 F-35 parts, and the UN Special Rapporteur calls the F-35 'pivotal to the Israeli air force'.","profile_src":["https://www.forsvaret.dk/da/nyheder/2023/atmospulse/","https://elbitsystems.com/pr-new/elbit-systems-awarded-two-contracts-in-an-aggregate-amount-of-252-million-to-supply-atmos-and-puls-artillery-systems-to-a-nato-member-country/","https://defence-industry.eu/idf-employs-puls-rocket-artillery-system-during-ongoing-war/","https://www.un.org/unispal/document/a-hrc-59-23-from-economy-of-occupation-to-economy-of-genocide-report-special-rapporteur-francesca-albanese-palestine-2025/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terma_A/S"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00011","name":"Government of Slovakia","type":"Government","role":"Buyer of IAI's Barak MX, paid straight to the Israeli state","country":"Slovakia","slug":"government-of-slovakia","profile":"Slovakia's government bought Israel Aerospace Industries' Barak MX anti-aircraft and anti-missile system for about €560M in a government-to-government deal that Israel's Ministry of Defense announced on 23 December 2024. Israel delivered the first battery to the Slovak Armed Forces in April 2026, with full readiness expected weeks later. The deal came after the ICJ's 2024 provisional-measures orders and a month after the ICC issued arrest warrants for Israel's prime minister and former military minister, so Bratislava cannot claim it was not warned. The full price goes to IAI, which is wholly owned by the Israeli state, so the payment flows directly to the state waging the war. IAI promotes Barak MX as 'combat-proven' against 'Iran and its proxies'. Slovakia's purchase added to the record European share of Israeli arms export deals in 2024.","profile_src":["https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-mod-seals-560-million-euro-agreement-barak-mx-integrated-air-defense-system-produced-by-iai-sold-to-slovakia-in-landmark-agreement","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-mod-delivers-iai-s-barak-mx-to-slovak-armed-forces","https://www.iai.co.il/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/IAI-FS-CONSOLIDATED-AND-SOLO-12.21.pdf","https://www.icj-cij.org/node/203447","https://www.npr.org/2024/11/21/g-s1-35169/icc-israel-hamas-arrest-warrants-gaza","https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-147-billion-in-2024"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-00012","name":"Government of Greece","type":"Government","role":"Buyer of Israel's biggest-ever European arms package, 'Achilles Shield'","country":"Greece","slug":"government-of-greece","profile":"Greece's government signed the 'Achilles Shield' deal with Israel on 31 August 2026, worth about €3B. Israel's Ministry of Defense calls it the largest arms export deal in the history of the two countries' relations and one of the largest in Israel's history. Rafael will supply David's Sling, SPYDER and a national command-and-control system, and IAI will supply Barak MX and ELTA radars, plus a €26M Drone Dome order. Israel's Ministry of Defense said the deal draws 'on the extensive operational experience Israel's military establishment has gained during the war', which is to say Athens is buying the Gaza track record. Greece had already selected Elbit's PULS rocket launcher in December 2025. The deal sends billions of euros to Israel's state-owned weapons makers almost a year after the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement","https://www.elbitsystems.com/land/weapons-systems-and-munitions/launchers/puls","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00001","name":"JDAM","type":"Weapon/System","role":"GPS/inertial guidance tail kit for unguided bombs (Boeing)","country":"USA","slug":"jdam","profile":"The Joint Direct Attack Munition (JDAM) is a Boeing-made tail kit that bolts GPS and inertial guidance onto unguided bombs such as the 2,000-pound MK-84, turning them into all-weather guided weapons. The US Air Force paid an average of $21,000 per kit in FY2021, and Defense News put the range at $25,000 to $84,000 depending on order size when Boeing won a $7.5B production contract in May 2024. JDAMs are central to Israel's bombing of Gaza. Amnesty International found JDAM parts in two October 2023 strikes on family homes in Deir al-Balah that killed 43 civilians. Bellingcat documented MK-80 series bombs with JDAM kits in the July 2024 Khadija school strike and in the 2025 demolition of at least seven Gaza City high-rises after evacuation orders. In September 2026 Amnesty reported JDAM components at a Tehran strike site from the 2026 US-Israeli war on Iran, saying the strikes may amount to war crimes.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joint_Direct_Attack_Munition","https://www.defensenews.com/air/2024/05/28/boeing-wins-75-billion-contract-from-us-air-force-for-guided-bombs/","https://www.amnestyusa.org/press-releases/israel-opt-us-made-munitions-killed-43-civilians-in-two-documented-israeli-air-strikes-in-gaza-new-investigation/","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.amnesty.org.au/investigation-into-us-israeli-strikes-on-tehran-neighbourhoods-reveals-devastating-civilian-harm/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00002","name":"KMU-556 JDAM kit","type":"Weapon/System","role":"JDAM guidance kit for 2,000-lb MK-84 bomb","country":"USA","slug":"kmu-556-jdam-kit","profile":"The KMU-556 is the JDAM tail-kit variant built for the MK-84, the 2,000-pound general-purpose bomb. Once fitted, the bomb is guided by GPS and inertial navigation to fixed coordinates, so a one-ton bomb can be aimed at a single building in a crowded neighbourhood. Boeing makes JDAM kits in St. Louis; the US Air Force paid about $21,000 per JDAM kit in FY2021. On 7 February 2025 the State Department notified Congress of a $6.75B sale to Israel that included 13,000 KMU-556 kits for MK-84 bomb bodies, with deliveries due to begin in 2025. Two-thousand-pound bombs are among the most destructive weapons Israel has used in Gaza: the New York Times counted 208 craters at least 40 feet across in a southern Gaza area where civilians had been told to go for safety. Bellingcat notes JDAM kits that fit the MK-84 are produced only in the US.","profile_src":["https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joint_Direct_Attack_Munition","https://www.newarab.com/analysis/us-israel-arms-transfers-2000-pound-bombs-destruction-gaza","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00006","name":"GBU-39 Small Diameter Bomb","type":"Weapon/System","role":"250-lb guided glide bomb (Boeing)","country":"USA","slug":"gbu-39-small-diameter-bomb","profile":"The GBU-39/B Small Diameter Bomb is a 250-pound guided glide bomb made by Boeing, the prime contractor named by the US Air Force; its unit cost was about $40,000 in FY2021. It became one of Israel's most-used bombs against shelters and schools in Gaza. CNN found a GBU-39 tail at the 26 May 2024 strike on the Kuwait Peace Camp in Rafah, where at least 45 displaced people were killed in the fire that followed. Pentagon officials told NPR a GBU-39 was used on the UN school in Nuseirat on 6 June 2024, killing at least 32 people, including seven children. CNN also linked it to the August 2024 al-Tabaeen school strike, and Bellingcat found GBU-39s in the July 2024 Khadija school strike and in a September 2025 strike that reportedly killed at least six others. The February 2025 US package added 2,166 more GBU-39s for Israel.","profile_src":["https://www.af.mil/About-Us/Fact-Sheets/Display/Article/104573/gbu-39b-small-diameter-bomb-weapon-system/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GBU-39_Small_Diameter_Bomb","https://amp.cnn.com/cnn/2024/05/28/middleeast/gaza-us-munitions-rafah-strike-analysis-intl-hnk","https://www.npr.org/2024/06/06/nx-s1-4995090/israel-gaza-school-strike-us-bomb","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00007","name":"AGM-114 Hellfire","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Laser-guided air-to-surface missile (Lockheed Martin)","country":"USA","slug":"agm-114-hellfire","profile":"The AGM-114 Hellfire is a laser-guided air-to-surface missile made by Lockheed Martin in Troy, Alabama, and fired by Israel's Apache helicopters and drones. Its listed unit cost was about $150,000 in FY2021. According to AFSC, some 2,000 Hellfires were delivered to Israel between 7 October and 14 November 2023. Bellingcat's 2026 investigation of US-made munitions in Gaza found that a Hellfire was used in a June 2024 strike on a Gaza City health clinic that killed Hani al-Jafarawi, director of Gaza's ambulance and emergency services. It also found Hellfires used in four strikes on tents within about 150 metres of Al-Aqsa Martyrs Hospital in Deir al-Balah, and Hellfire remnants after a July 2025 strike on Cairo Basic School that reportedly killed five people. In February 2025 the State Department notified a further $660M sale of 3,000 Hellfires to Israel, with Lockheed Martin as principal contractor.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AGM-114_Hellfire","https://afsc.org/gaza-genocide-companies","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060949/israel-agm-114-hellfire-missiles"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00008","name":"FMU-152A/B fuze","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Joint Programmable Fuze for US-made bombs","country":"USA","slug":"fmu-152a-b-fuze","profile":"The FMU-152A/B Joint Programmable Fuze sets off a bomb's explosive charge. Aircrew can program it in flight to detonate on impact or after a delay, so the bomb can penetrate a building before exploding. It is fitted to JDAM-guided MK-80 series bombs and penetrators. The fuze was made by Kaman Corporation, which announced a $324M direct commercial order for Joint Programmable Fuzes in January 2018; private-equity firm Arcline bought Kaman for $1.8B in 2024, and the fuze business now operates as Precision Fuzing & Sensors. The 7 February 2025 US sale to Israel included 17,475 FMU-152A/B fuzes, more than one for every JDAM kit in the package. Fuzes are rarely named in strike investigations, but they go with the JDAM-guided MK-80 series bombs that Amnesty and Bellingcat documented in strikes on homes, schools and high-rise buildings in Gaza. Without them those bombs do not work.","profile_src":["https://kaman.com/kaman-announces-324-million-joint-programmable-fuze-order/","https://kaman.com/arcline-completes-acquisition-of-kaman/","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.amnestyusa.org/press-releases/israel-opt-us-made-munitions-killed-43-civilians-in-two-documented-israeli-air-strikes-in-gaza-new-investigation/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00010","name":"Arrow 3","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Ballistic-missile interceptor","country":"Israel/USA","slug":"arrow-3","profile":"Arrow 3 is the top layer of Israel's missile shield, built to destroy ballistic missiles above the atmosphere. State-owned Israel Aerospace Industries (IAI) is prime contractor, Rafael is a key subcontractor, and the programme is co-funded with the US Missile Defense Agency. Calcalist reported in March 2026 that each interceptor costs just over NIS 2 million. It shielded Israel during the June 2025 and 2026 wars with Iran: Calcalist reported about 440 Iranian ballistic missiles in the first four weeks of the 2026 war, with about 92% intercepted. The weapon is also IAI's biggest export product. Germany received its first Arrow 3 battery at Holzdorf on 3 December 2025, and the Bundestag approved a further €3B expansion on 17 December 2025; IAI says the German programme now exceeds $6.5B. The UN Special Rapporteur's July 2025 report notes that Israeli weapons are marketed as \"battle-proven\" after use in its military campaigns, and IAI is among the firms it names.","profile_src":["https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-delivers-arrow-3-to-germany-in-largest-defense-export-deal-ever/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/german-parliament-approves-3-5b-expansion-of-arrow-3-deal-with-israel/","https://defence-industry.eu/iai-signs-usd-3-1-billion-follow-on-contract-to-expand-germanys-arrow-3-missile-defence-programme/","https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/h1dyauacbg","https://www.un.org/unispal/document/a-hrc-59-23-from-economy-of-occupation-to-economy-of-genocide-report-special-rapporteur-francesca-albanese-palestine-2025/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00011","name":"David's Sling","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Missile and rocket interceptor system","country":"Israel/USA","slug":"david-s-sling","profile":"David's Sling is Israel's middle interceptor layer. It intercepts ballistic missiles fired from 100–200 km away as well as heavy rockets, aircraft, drones and cruise missiles, using the Stunner interceptor. It is made jointly by state-owned Rafael Advanced Defense Systems and the US firm RTX. It was first used in combat on 10 May 2023, intercepting a heavy rocket fired from Gaza during Israel's \"Shield and Arrow\" bombing campaign. Reuters has since shown it in action against rockets fired from Lebanon. US taxpayers fund it directly: the April 2024 Israel supplemental gave $4B to replenish Iron Dome and David's Sling. Exports turn that combat use into sales. Finland signed for it in November 2023 (about €317M) and Greece included it in the €3B \"Achilles Shield\" deal of 31 August 2026. Israel's Ministry of Defense said that deal drew \"on the extensive operational experience Israel's military establishment has gained during the war\".","profile_src":["https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/factbox-what-israels-multi-layered-defence-against-iranian-missiles","https://defence-industry.eu/davids-sling-air-defense-system-proves-itself-in-real-combat/","https://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/house-passes-series-security-supplemental-bills","https://militarnyi.com/en/news/finland-signs-agreement-with-israel-to-purchase-david-s-sling-system/","https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00012","name":"SPYDER","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Mobile anti-aircraft missile system","country":"Israel","slug":"spyder","profile":"SPYDER is a truck-mounted anti-aircraft missile system made by Rafael Advanced Defense Systems, the weapons company 99.9% owned by the Israeli state. Its all-in-one version carries up to eight Python-5 and I-Derby interceptors with ranges of 15 to 40 km on one 8x8 vehicle. SPYDER is not a central part of Israel's own missile shield, but it is a steady export earner for Rafael. Its largest recent order is Greece's €3B \"Achilles Shield\" package, signed on 31 August 2026. Rafael called the systems it is supplying \"combat-proven\", and Israel's Ministry of Defense said the \"operational successes of Israeli systems on the battlefield continue to reinforce global demand\". Missile, rocket and interceptor systems were 48% of Israel's record $14.7B in arms export deals in 2024. Profits from sales like these go back to a state-owned company that also arms Israel's own military.","profile_src":["https://www.rafael.co.il/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/spyder-all-in-one-mobile-air-defense-system.pdf","https://www.rafael.co.il/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Refael_ENGLISH120225MINA_All_compressed.pdf","https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement","https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-147-billion-in-2024"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00013","name":"Barak MX","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Anti-aircraft and anti-missile system","country":"Israel","slug":"barak-mx","profile":"Barak MX is an anti-aircraft and anti-missile system made by Israel Aerospace Industries (IAI), which is wholly owned by the Israeli state. It can fire three interceptor types, with ranges of 35, 70 and 150 km, against aircraft, drones, cruise missiles and tactical ballistic missiles, from land or ships. IAI markets it on its wartime record: at the August 2026 Greek signing the company called it \"combat-proven\" and pointed to interceptions \"against Iran and its proxies\". Slovakia bought it for about €560M in December 2024 and took delivery of the first battery in April 2026. Greece included it in the €3B \"Achilles Shield\" deal of 31 August 2026. Europe accounted for 54% of Israel's 2024 arms export deals. The UN Special Rapporteur's July 2025 report names IAI among the firms that supply weapons to Israel at home and strengthen its military alliances through exports.","profile_src":["https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-mod-seals-560-million-euro-agreement-barak-mx-integrated-air-defense-system-produced-by-iai-sold-to-slovakia-in-landmark-agreement","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-mod-delivers-iai-s-barak-mx-to-slovak-armed-forces","https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-147-billion-in-2024","https://www.un.org/unispal/document/a-hrc-59-23-from-economy-of-occupation-to-economy-of-genocide-report-special-rapporteur-francesca-albanese-palestine-2025/","https://www.iai.co.il/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/IAI-FS-CONSOLIDATED-AND-SOLO-12.21.pdf"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00015","name":"PULS","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Multi-calibre rocket artillery launcher (Elbit Systems), called Lahav in Israeli service","country":"Israel","slug":"puls","profile":"PULS (Precise and Universal Launching System), called Lahav by the Israeli army, is Elbit Systems' rocket launcher. It fires Elbit's AccuLAR rockets, EXTRA ('Bar') rockets with a 150 km range and Predator Hawk missiles with a 300 km range. Arms industry Europe reported in February 2024 that PULS was being used \"extensively\" in Gaza and Lebanon and had \"destroyed a great number of targets on the two fronts\". In 2026 its use against Lebanon escalated: Elbit's own blog, translating N12 News, says Lahav launchers fired more than 50 'Bar' rockets at the start of the Iran operation toward anti-tank squads, buildings and Hezbollah targets, and that Battalion 334 in Lebanon used the rocket 'on an unprecedented scale'. Lebanon's Ministry of Public Health counts 8,953 people killed since October 2023. Exports turn this use into income: Denmark, the Netherlands ($305M for 20 systems), Germany and Greece have ordered PULS.","profile_src":["https://www.elbitsystems.com/land/weapons-systems-and-munitions/launchers/puls","https://defence-industry.eu/idf-employs-puls-rocket-artillery-system-during-ongoing-war/","https://www.elbitsystems.com/blog/air-force-was-surprised-new-missile-revealed-during-war-iran","https://moph.gov.lb/en/Media/view/87142/4/update-toll-of-the-aggression-25-9-2026","https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-inks-first-of-its-kind-305-million-sale-of-artillery-systems-to-netherlands/","https://www.forsvaret.dk/da/nyheder/2023/atmospulse/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00016","name":"AMRAAM","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Radar-guided air-to-air missile (RTX/Raytheon)","country":"USA","slug":"amraam","profile":"The AIM-120 AMRAAM is a radar-guided, beyond-visual-range air-to-air missile made by Raytheon, part of RTX. Israel buys it through U.S. Foreign Military Sales: on 13 August 2024, ten months into the Gaza genocide, the State Department approved 30 AIM-120C-8 missiles for Israel at an estimated $102.5M, with RTX in Tucson as principal contractor and the missiles to come from new production. On 28 September 2026, weeks after the US-Israeli war on Iran, RTX announced a $20.7B multi-year contract to raise AMRAAM output to 'record-setting levels'. This map shows AMRAAM as procurement only: we have found no evidence tying Israeli AMRAAM use to a specific strike in Gaza, Lebanon or Iran. Its role is to give U.S. and Israeli warplanes control of the air, which lets them bomb freely.","profile_src":["https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/israel/2024/08/israel-240813-dsca04.htm","https://www.dsca.mil/sites/default/files/mas/Press%20Release%20-%20Israel%2024-08%20CN_0.pdf","https://raytheon.mediaroom.com/2026-09-28-RTXs-Raytheon-awarded-20-7-billion-multi-year-contract-for-AMRAAM-under-landmark-production-agreement"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00001","name":"Larry Fink","type":"Person","role":"BlackRock chief; told investors to 'buy more' during the Iran war","country":null,"slug":"larry-fink","profile":"Larry Fink co-founded BlackRock in 1988 and runs it as chairman and CEO. His take: BlackRock paid him $37.7M for 2025, up about 23% from $30.8M in 2024, which was itself 14% above 2023. Forbes puts his net worth at $1.3B (4 Oct 2026), and GuruFocus lists 223,831 directly held BlackRock shares worth about $237M (July 2026). UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report 'From economy of occupation to economy of genocide' names BlackRock the second-largest institutional investor in Palantir (8.6%), Microsoft (7.8%), Amazon and Alphabet (6.6% each), firms it ties to Israel's genocide in Gaza. Days after 7 October 2023 Fink told CNBC Israel would 'have to be spending a lot more money on military' and that nobody was divesting from Israel. In 2025 he phoned Donald Trump's White House to pitch BlackRock's Panama Canal ports deal. During the 2026 Iran war he told Fox News: 'Buy more here. This is a good long-term opportunity.' He became chairman of the World Economic Forum in August 2025.","profile_src":["https://www.benzinga.com/markets/hedge-funds/26/03/51527216/blackrock-ceo-larry-fink-2025-pay-jumps-to-377-million-assets-hit-record-14-trillion","https://stocktwits.com/news-articles/markets/equity/blackrock-private-markets-push-reportedly-drove-pay-bump-for-senior-leadership/cZ3H1IORIml","https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/blackrock-ceo-larry-fink-s-pay-rises-14-to-30-8-million-in-2024-125040500115_1.html","https://www.forbes.com/profile/larry-fink/","https://www.gurufocus.com/insider/8589/laurence-fink","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.cnbc.com/2023/10/13/cnbc-exclusive-cnbc-transcript-blackrock-chairman-ceo-larry-fink-speaks-with-cnbcs-squawk-on-the-street-today.html","https://fortune.com/2025/03/05/larry-fink-phoned-trump-directly-to-pitch-blackrocks-panama-deal","https://www.foxnews.com/media/blackrock-ceo-larry-fink-argues-us-iran-conflict-wont-derail-economy-gas-prices-surge","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Larry_Fink"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00002","name":"Robert S. Kapito","type":"Person","role":"BlackRock co-founder and president; chaired a fund raising for Israel","country":null,"slug":"robert-s-kapito","profile":"Robert S. Kapito co-founded BlackRock in 1988 with Larry Fink and is its president and a director. BlackRock paid him $25.7M for 2025, up from $21.8M in 2024, and his share of a retention award tied to BlackRock's private-market funds was valued at $25.3M at the end of 2024. A 2022 Guardian headline, cited by Wikipedia, put his wealth at about $400M. Kapito helps lead the firm that Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report places, with Vanguard, among the largest institutional investors in companies it ties to Israel's genocide in Gaza, including Palantir, Microsoft, Amazon and Alphabet. From July 2016 he chaired the board of UJA-Federation of New York, which by December 2023 had raised $156M for its Israel Emergency Fund since 7 October, $75M of it from the Wall Street community. In 2022, as prices soared, he offered his diagnosis of ordinary people's problem: 'We have a very entitled generation that has never had to sacrifice.'","profile_src":["https://stocktwits.com/news-articles/markets/equity/blackrock-private-markets-push-reportedly-drove-pay-bump-for-senior-leadership/cZ3H1IORIml","https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/blackrock-ceo-larry-fink-s-pay-rises-14-to-30-8-million-in-2024-125040500115_1.html","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_S._Kapito","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://philanthropynewyork.org/news/jeffrey-schoenfeld-and-robert-kapito-appointed-president-and-chair-board-uja-federation-new","https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/uja-federation-of-new-york-raises-record-45-million-at-wall-street-dinner-additional-75-million-for-ujas-israel-emergency-fund-302008058.html","https://fortune.com/2022/03/30/blackrock-president-kapito-entitled-generation-seatbelts-high-inflation-spain-us-germany-scarcity/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00003","name":"Abigail Johnson","type":"Person","role":"Fidelity chair and CEO; her charity arm blocked gifts to UNRWA USA","country":null,"slug":"abigail-johnson","profile":"Abigail Johnson is chair and CEO of Fidelity Investments (FMR), a private, family-controlled firm that does not publish her pay. Forbes estimates she owns about 29% of Fidelity, which managed $7.1T in discretionary assets at December 2025, and puts her net worth at $41.6B (3 Oct 2026). Fidelity's flagship Contrafund alone held $10.9B of Amazon, $11.9B of Alphabet, $7.0B of Microsoft, $1.1B of Boeing, $124M of Northrop Grumman, $73M of General Dynamics, $18M of Palantir and $4M of Elbit Systems on 15 January 2026. Fidelity Charitable, the group's donor-advised fund, stopped donors giving to UNRWA USA in 2024 as Gaza starved while, Rolling Stone reported, it had passed $2.2M to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces, $2.7M to AIPAC's educational affiliate and $19.5M to the Central Fund of Israel, which pays for West Bank settlements. Aid for refugees was blocked; money for settlements was not. Johnson gave about $330,000 to Hillary Clinton's campaign and the DNC in 2016 and attended a Biden fundraiser in 2024.","profile_src":["https://www.forbes.com/profile/abigail-johnson/","https://www.fidelity.com/bin-public/060_www_fidelity_com/documents/mutual-funds/22.holdings.12.pdf","https://au.news.yahoo.com/major-u-charity-blocks-donations-143630243.html","https://forward.com/news/476306/fidelity-targeted-over-donations-to-group-funding-israeli-settlements/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abigail_Johnson"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00004","name":"Larry Ellison","type":"Person","role":"Oracle founder; record donor to Israel's army, Netanyahu's island host","country":null,"slug":"larry-ellison","profile":"Larry Ellison founded Oracle in 1977 and is its chairman and chief technology officer. Forbes puts his net worth at $184.2B (3 Oct 2026), built on roughly 40% of Oracle and nearly half of Paramount Skydance. Ellison gave $16.6M to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces in November 2017, then the largest single gift in its history, to build facilities on a new infantry training campus, saying 'there is no greater honor than supporting some of the bravest people in the world'. In August 2021 Benjamin Netanyahu holidayed on Lanai, the Hawaiian island Ellison owns, while Ellison was a prosecution witness in Netanyahu's corruption trial; the Times of Israel, citing Haaretz, reported Ellison had offered him an Oracle board seat, which Netanyahu denied. Witnesses do not usually host the defendant. Who Profits reports Oracle supplies the Israel Ministry of Defense, army and air force, and servers to the Civil Administration in the occupied West Bank. On 21 January 2025 he stood beside Donald Trump to launch the $500B Stargate AI project.","profile_src":["https://www.jta.org/2017/11/05/united-states/record-53-8-million-raised-for-idf-soldiers-at-beverly-hills-gala","https://www.timesofisrael.com/netanyahu-on-vacation-at-island-owned-by-larry-ellison-a-witness-in-graft-trial/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/netanyahus-lawyers-grill-ex-ceo-of-news-site-over-ties-with-other-politicians/","https://www.whoprofits.org/companies/company/7396?oracle=","https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/business-news/stargate-trump-openai-ellison-1236114430/"],"profile_status":"documented","profile (append sentence)":"Oracle's 2026 proxy reports his fiscal 2026 compensation at $131.0M, almost all of it stock awards."},{"id":"PER-00005","name":"Paul Singer","type":"Person","role":"Hedge-fund billionaire; bankroller of hawkish pro-Israel causes","country":null,"slug":"paul-singer","profile":"Paul Singer founded the hedge fund Elliott Management in 1977 with $1.3M; Forbes says it now oversees more than $80B and puts his net worth at $7.2B (19 Sep 2026). One of the Republican Party's largest funders, he gave $5M to Donald Trump's 2024 re-election effort, according to Wikipedia's account of filings. Singer is a 'longtime supporter of hawkish pro-Israel causes': a major funder of the Foundation for Defense of Democracies, a board member of the Republican Jewish Coalition, a former board member of the Jewish Institute for National Security Affairs, and an investor of about $20M in Start-Up Nation Central, which promotes Israel's tech sector. The Paul E. Singer Foundation reported grants to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces on its IRS filings, including $1.04M in fiscal 2015. Forbes notes he gives heavily to Jewish and pro-Israel groups and has put about $300M into his foundation since 2010. The think tanks argue for war; the foundation pays for the soldiers.","profile_src":["https://www.forbes.com/profile/paul-singer/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Singer_(businessman)"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00006","name":"Bernie Marcus","type":"Person","role":"Home Depot co-founder (died 2024); major funder of Israel's army charity","country":null,"slug":"bernie-marcus","profile":"Bernie Marcus co-founded Home Depot in 1978 and died on 4 November 2024, aged 95, when Forbes valued his fortune at $10.3B; by 2019 he had given away $2B. He was one of the largest private funders of Friends of the Israel Defense Forces, the US charity for Israeli soldiers, giving nearly $13M between 2009 and 2022, according to its Wikipedia entry. Days after 7 October 2023 Forbes reported he was supporting Magen David Adom and 'the IDF (the Israel Defense Forces)', and Wikipedia reports he gave $2M to AIPAC that year, the lobby that shields Israel's genocide in Gaza in Congress. He co-founded the Israel Democracy Institute in 1991 and with his wife gave $25M toward MDA's national blood centre. Marcus was among Donald Trump's biggest backers, giving $7M in 2016 and $10.7M to pro-Trump PACs in 2020.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernie_Marcus","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friends_of_the_Israel_Defense_Forces","https://www.forbes.com/sites/kerryadolan/2023/10/11/billionaire-tracker-mike-bloomberg-yuri-milner-and-the-other-ultra-wealthy-donors-to-israeli-groups-following-the-attacks-by-hamas/"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-00007","name":"Haim Saban","type":"Person","role":"Media billionaire; self-described 'one-issue guy', the issue being Israel","country":null,"slug":"haim-saban","profile":"Haim Saban built his fortune on the Power Rangers franchise and the 2007 $13.7B takeover of Univision; Forbes puts his net worth at $3.3B (15 Sep 2026). He states his motive plainly: 'I'm a one-issue guy, and my issue is Israel.' Long one of the Democratic Party's largest donors, he was its top overall contributor in the 2001–2002 cycle and in 2002 gave $13M to found the Saban Center for Middle East Policy at the Brookings Institution. Saban is listed among the prominent supporters of Friends of the Israel Defense Forces, which raised more than $50M in the weeks after 7 October 2023. In 2024, amid Democratic splits over Israel's genocide in Gaza, he offered his party an electoral calculation: 'Let's not forget there are more Jewish voters who care about Israel than Muslim voters who care about Hamas.' His money links Democratic Party finance to political cover for Israel's war.","profile_src":["https://www.forbes.com/profile/haim-saban/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haim_Saban","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friends_of_the_Israel_Defense_Forces"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-00008","name":"Jan Koum","type":"Person","role":"WhatsApp co-founder; funds Israel's army charity and settlement groups","country":null,"slug":"jan-koum","profile":"Jan Koum co-founded WhatsApp, which Facebook bought for $22B in 2014, and left the company in 2018. Forbes puts his net worth at $18.6B (19 Sep 2026), with his firm Newlands holding nearly 10 million Meta shares. Jewish Insider's review of his foundation's filing found a $5.3M gift in 2018 to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces, which funds programs for serving and former Israeli soldiers, and gifts of at least $1M that year to Friends of Ir David. Wikipedia tallies $6M to Friends of Ir David, $600,000 to the Maccabee Task Force and $175,000 to the Central Fund of Israel, which pays for West Bank settlements. The encrypted-messaging pioneer's giving is not encrypted: soldiers, settlements and campus campaigns. In 2022 Koum gave $2M to AIPAC during the Democratic primaries, the cycle in which AIPAC's new super PAC, United Democracy Project, began spending millions against progressive candidates.","profile_src":["https://www.forbes.com/profile/jan-koum/","https://jewishinsider.com/2020/04/whatsapp-co-founder-jan-koum-increases-giving-to-jewish-and-israel-groups/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_Koum","https://forward.com/news/476306/fidelity-targeted-over-donations-to-group-funding-israeli-settlements/"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-00009","name":"Miriam Adelson","type":"Person","role":"Casino billionaire; $106M Trump donor who sought West Bank annexation","country":null,"slug":"miriam-adelson","profile":"Miriam Adelson, widow of casino magnate Sheldon Adelson, is majority owner of Las Vegas Sands and, since 2023, of the Dallas Mavericks. Forbes puts her family's net worth at $31.4B (27 Sep 2026); a 2026 Schedule 13D filing records her personal holding at 52.7% of Sands. She was the third-largest donor to Donald Trump's 2024 campaign, at $106M, according to Wikipedia's tally, and Trump awarded her the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2018. She publishes Israel Hayom, Israel's most widely read newspaper. During the 2024 campaign she sought Trump's support for Israel's annexation of the occupied West Bank, and she funds US groups that raise money for the Israeli military. Then came the return on investment: weeks after Trump took office, his administration used an emergency declaration to bypass Congress and approve $2.04B in bomb bodies and penetrators for Israel in February 2025.","profile_src":["https://www.forbes.com/profile/miriam-adelson/","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001300514/000119312526345232/xslSCHEDULE_13D_X02/primary_doc.xml","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miriam_Adelson","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088258/israel-munitions-and-munitions-support"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-00011","name":"Jared Kushner","type":"Person","role":"Trump son-in-law and envoy; called Gaza 'valuable waterfront property'","country":null,"slug":"jared-kushner","profile":"Jared Kushner, Donald Trump's son-in-law and White House adviser in 2017–2021, runs the Miami private equity firm Affinity Partners. Forbes puts his net worth at $1B (28 Sep 2026). Affinity managed more than $5.4B by September 2025, after raising $4.6B mainly from the Saudi and Qatari sovereign wealth funds, including $2B from Saudi Arabia's Public Investment Fund six months after he left office. He brokered the 2020 Abraham Accords and has longstanding personal and family ties to Benjamin Netanyahu. In 2024 he called Gaza 'valuable waterfront property', proposing Palestinians be moved to the Negev or Egypt while the territory was 'cleaned up' so Israel could 'finish the job'; rights groups called it advocacy of forced displacement. A real-estate pitch, with the residents listed as debris. He sat on the national board of Friends of the IDF until about January 2017. Byline Times argued in October 2025 that pro-Trump tech billionaires were poised to cash in on the Gaza 'peace' deal Kushner helped shape.","profile_src":["https://www.forbes.com/profile/jared-kushner/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jared_Kushner","https://forward.com/fast-forward/361172/jared-kushners-name-scrubbed-from-pro-idf-group-board/","https://bylinetimes.com/2025/10/16/pro-trump-tech-billionaires-poised-cash-in-gaza-peace-deal/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00012","name":"James D. Taiclet","type":"Person","role":"Lockheed CEO; called the Iran war a 'golden opportunity'","country":null,"slug":"james-d-taiclet","profile":"James D. Taiclet is chairman, president and CEO of Lockheed Martin, maker of the F-35 that Israel flies over Gaza. Lockheed's proxy reports his total pay at $23.45M for 2025, $23.75M for 2024 and $22.81M for 2023, about $70M over three years. Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report calls the F-35 'the largest-ever military procurement programme', from which Israel benefits; Campaign Against Arms Trade confirmed an Israeli F-35 carried out the 13 July 2024 strike on the al-Mawasi 'safe zone' that killed 90 people. Ten days after 7 October 2023 Taiclet told investors there could be 'supplemental requests related to support Ukraine, Israel, and potentially Taiwan.' In February 2025 Lockheed was named principal contractor for 3,000 Hellfire missiles ($660M) sold to Israel. On the April 2026 earnings call, with the US–Israeli war on Iran under way, he summed up his philosophy: 'This is a golden opportunity right now based on who's in government.'","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/936468/000093646826000004/R2.htm","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://caat.org.uk/news/investigation-reveals-israel-used-partly-uk-made-f-35-in-attack-on-gaza-humanitarian-zone-in-july-killing-90/","https://www.vice.com/en/article/us-defense-contractor-ceos-see-profit-opportunity-in-israel-hamas-war/","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060949/israel-agm-114-hellfire-missiles","https://www.thestreet.com/investing/stocks/lockheed-martin-ceo-sends-strong-2-word-message-on-middle-east"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00013","name":"Phebe N. Novakovic","type":"Person","role":"General Dynamics CEO; her plant made the 2,000-pound bombs","country":null,"slug":"phebe-n-novakovic","profile":"Phebe N. Novakovic is chairman and CEO of General Dynamics, whose munitions arm makes the MK-80-series bomb bodies Israel drops on Gaza. GD's proxy shows her total pay at $25.92M for 2025, $23.79M for 2024 and $22.58M for 2023, about $72M over three years. AFSC reports that GD's MK-84 2,000-pound bombs 'have been used extensively by the Israeli Air Force during its frequent assaults on Gaza'. On 28 February 2025 the State Department invoked an emergency to bypass Congress and approved a $2.04B sale of bomb bodies and penetrators to Israel, with General Dynamics a prime contractor. In October 2023 her CFO told analysts that from 'the Israel situation' the incremental demand that 'really sticks out is probably on the artillery side', and in January 2024 Novakovic cited 'higher artillery and propellant volume' as a growth driver while noting the Gaza genocide's impact on an Israel-based supplier. In Q1 2026 GD's backlog rose 48% to $131B.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/40533/000130817926000168/R2.htm","https://investigate.afsc.org/company/general-dynamics","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088258/israel-munitions-and-munitions-support","https://www.airforce-technology.com/newsletters/hamas-has-created-additional-demand-general-dynamics-earnings-call/","https://finance.yahoo.com/news/general-dynamics-gd-q4-2023-223017370.html","https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/29/general-dynamics-gd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00014","name":"Christopher T. Calio","type":"Person","role":"RTX CEO; sells 'munitions depth' after the attack on Iran","country":null,"slug":"christopher-t-calio","profile":"Christopher T. Calio is chairman and CEO of RTX, the former Raytheon Technologies, with more than 180,000 employees. RTX's proxy reports his total pay at $24.85M for 2025, $18.0M for 2024 and $12.74M for 2023, about $55.6M over three years. RTX's Pratt & Whitney builds the engines for Israel's F-35 and F-15I jets. After the US and Israel attacked Iran on 28 February 2026, Calio told investors the 'current landscape clearly underscores the need for munitions depth, integrated air and missile-interception technology', and by July he cited combat performance of 'Patriot, Coyote, AMRAAM, AIM-9X and the Standard Missile family' as RTX reported a record $289B backlog, 48% international. His predecessor Greg Hayes set the tone in October 2023, telling investors the Israel war meant 'across the entire Raytheon portfolio, you're going to see a benefit of this restocking.' Between October 2023 and July 2025 RTX's share price rose 77%.","profile_src":["https://www.rtx.com/who-we-are/corporate-governance/christopher-calio","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/101829/000130817926000036/R2.htm","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_companies_involved_in_the_Gaza_war","https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/rtx-rtx-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/07/24/rtx-rtx-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","https://www.vice.com/en/article/us-defense-contractor-ceos-see-profit-opportunity-in-israel-hamas-war/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonardo_S.p.A."],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00015","name":"Robert K. Ortberg","type":"Person","role":"Boeing CEO; his bombs hit Gaza's schools and tent camps","country":null,"slug":"robert-k-ortberg","profile":"Robert K. 'Kelly' Ortberg is president and CEO of Boeing, which supplies Israel with JDAM guidance kits, GBU-39 small diameter bombs and F-15 fighters. Boeing's proxy reports his total pay at $23.58M for 2025 and $18.39M for 2024. Sludge counts $26.7B in US arms sales to Israel approved since 7 October 2023 that benefit Boeing, whose bombs have been used in strikes on schools and tent camps in Gaza. In February 2025 Boeing was named lead contractor in a $6.75B sale of munitions, guidance kits and fuzes to Israel, including 13,000 KMU-556 JDAM kits, and in December 2025 the Pentagon awarded it up to $8.6B to build F-15IA jets for Israel. After the US–Israeli attack on Iran, Ortberg reported the good news to investors in April 2026: 'We're already seeing higher demand in our military business given the increased operational tempo', citing an agreement with the US military to triple production of PAC-3 missile seekers.","profile_src":["https://www.boeing.com/features/2026/07/ceo-boeing-on-track-with-2026-plan-building-trust","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/12927/000119312526096787/R2.htm","https://readsludge.com/2025/10/13/boeings-arms-sales-thrive-on-gaza-genocide/","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_military_aid_to_Israel","https://leehamnews.com/2026/04/22/boeing-1q2026-earnings-defense-business-is-booming-due-to-iran-war/","https://thedefensepost.com/2026/04/18/boeing-defense-business-war/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00016","name":"Charles Woodburn","type":"Person","role":"BAE Systems chief executive; heads the maker of every F-35 rear fuselage","country":null,"slug":"charles-woodburn","profile":"Charles Woodburn has been chief executive of BAE Systems, Europe's largest arms maker, since 1 July 2017. Simply Wall St reports his total compensation for 2025 at £12.4M and a direct holding of 0.052% of BAE worth about £29.8M; in 2021 the board raised his salary to just over £1.1M and gave him a £2M share package to stop him leaving. The British arms industry, led by BAE, produces about 15% of every F-35, including Israel's fleet, according to Campaign Against Arms Trade, which confirmed that an Israeli F-35 carried out the 13 July 2024 strike on the al-Mawasi 'safe zone' in Gaza that killed 90 people and injured at least 300. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. Among BAE's owners, Vanguard alone held about 4.3% of its shares in June 2026. The 'safe zone' was not safe; the share package was.","profile_src":["https://www.baesystems.com/en/our-company/about-us/board-of-directors/charles-woodburn","https://simplywall.st/stocks/gb/capital-goods/lse-ba./bae-systems-shares/management","https://uk.finance.yahoo.com/news/bae-systems-gives-chief-executive-2m-pay-rise-to-stop-him-leaving-111743496.html","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_supplying_arms_to_Israel","https://caat.org.uk/news/investigation-reveals-israel-used-partly-uk-made-f-35-in-attack-on-gaza-humanitarian-zone-in-july-killing-90/","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.investing.com/equities/bae-systems-plc-ownership"],"profile_status":"documented","profile (sentence)":"BAE's 2025 annual report puts his total remuneration for 2025 at £12.4M"},{"id":"PER-00017","name":"Michael Federmann","type":"Person","role":"Elbit patriarch; family votes 41.2% of Israel's biggest arms maker","country":null,"slug":"michael-federmann","profile":"Michael Federmann, born in 1944, owns Federmann Enterprises, the family holding company that with an affiliate votes about 41.2% of Elbit Systems, Israel's largest weapons maker. He chaired Elbit's board until his son David took over in August 2023, and chairs Dan Hotels. Elbit's 2026 proxy credits him personally with about a 5.1% economic interest, and Forbes puts his family's net worth at $9.6B (16 Sep 2026). Elbit makes 85% of the drones used by the Israeli Air Force and 85% of the army's land equipment; an Elbit Hermes 450 drone was used in the 2024 strike that killed seven World Central Kitchen aid workers in Gaza. Elbit's revenue reached $7.94B in 2025. Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report describes Elbit as one of the 'pillars' of Israel's military-industrial complex. Federmann chairs the board of trustees of the Hebrew University of Jerusalem and holds an honorary British CBE for UK–Israel business ties, honours that sit comfortably beside the drones.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Federmann","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://www.forbes.com/profile/michael-federmann/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbit_Systems","https://aoav.org.uk/2025/an-economy-of-genocide-un-special-rapporteur-names-global-corporations-enabling-israels-assault-on-gaza/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00018","name":"David Federmann","type":"Person","role":"Elbit Systems chair through the genocide in Gaza","country":null,"slug":"david-federmann","profile":"David Federmann, son of Michael Federmann, has chaired the board of Elbit Systems since August 2023, after serving as vice chair, which puts him at the head of Israel's largest weapons maker throughout the assault on Gaza and the wars on Lebanon and Iran. Elbit's 2026 proxy credits him with the largest individual economic interest in the family chain, about 8.16% of Elbit; on the September 2026 market value used in this map that stake is worth roughly $2.7B. Under his chairmanship Elbit, which makes 85% of the Israeli Air Force's drones, reported 2025 revenue of $7.94B and in May 2026 won an Israel Ministry of Defense contract to develop external fuel tanks for the F-35I, so the jets can fly further. An Elbit Hermes 450 drone was used in the 2024 strike that killed seven World Central Kitchen aid workers in Gaza. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza, and Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report names Elbit among the companies sustaining it.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbit_Systems","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://aoav.org.uk/2025/an-economy-of-genocide-un-special-rapporteur-names-global-corporations-enabling-israels-assault-on-gaza/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00019","name":"Gideon Federmann","type":"Person","role":"Federmann heir; about $2.0B stake in Elbit Systems","country":null,"slug":"gideon-federmann","profile":"Gideon Federmann, a son of Michael Federmann, holds an indirect economic interest of about 6.12% in Elbit Systems through the Federmann family chain, according to Elbit's 2026 proxy statement; with his father and brothers David and Daniel, the family's combined look-through stake is about 25.5%. On the September 2026 market value used in this map, a 6.12% stake is worth roughly $2.0B. Elbit is Israel's largest weapons maker: it produces 85% of the drones used by the Israeli Air Force and 85% of the army's land equipment, and an Elbit Hermes 450 drone was used in the 2024 strike that killed seven World Central Kitchen aid workers in Gaza. Elbit's revenue reached $7.94B in 2025. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza; every Elbit contract for that genocide adds to the value of the family's holding. He does not need to run the company to collect from it.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbit_Systems","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00020","name":"Daniel Federmann","type":"Person","role":"Federmann heir; about $2.0B stake in Elbit Systems","country":null,"slug":"daniel-federmann","profile":"Daniel Federmann, a son of Michael Federmann, holds an indirect economic interest of about 6.12% in Elbit Systems through the Federmann family chain, according to Elbit's 2026 proxy statement; with his father and brothers David and Gideon, the family's combined look-through stake is about 25.5%. On the September 2026 market value used in this map, a 6.12% stake is worth roughly $2.0B. Elbit is Israel's largest weapons maker: it produces 85% of the drones used by the Israeli Air Force and 85% of the army's land equipment, and an Elbit Hermes 450 drone was used in the 2024 strike that killed seven World Central Kitchen aid workers in Gaza. Elbit's revenue reached $7.94B in 2025. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza; every Elbit contract for that genocide adds to the value of the family's holding. Inheritance, in this case, is denominated in drones.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbit_Systems","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00021","name":"Irith Federmann-Landeau","type":"Person","role":"Federmann family trust beneficiary; about $2.4B interest in Elbit","country":null,"slug":"irith-federmann-landeau","profile":"Irith Federmann-Landeau, a member of the Federmann family, holds an indirect, non-voting economic interest of about 7.2% in Elbit Systems' outstanding shares through a trust structure, according to Elbit's 2026 proxy statement. Voting control of the family block, about 41.2% of Elbit, sits with Michael Federmann through Federmann Enterprises and an affiliate; her stake carries the profits without the votes. On the September 2026 market value used in this map, a 7.2% economic interest is worth roughly $2.4B. Elbit is Israel's largest weapons maker, producing 85% of the drones used by the Israeli Air Force and 85% of the army's land equipment; an Elbit Hermes 450 drone was used in the 2024 strike that killed seven World Central Kitchen aid workers in Gaza. Elbit's 2025 revenue was $7.94B. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbit_Systems","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00022","name":"Alex Karp","type":"Person","role":"Palantir CEO; sells targeting and deportation software, calls Gaza dead 'mostly terrorists'","country":null,"slug":"alex-karp","profile":"Alex Karp, co-founder and, since 2005, CEO of Palantir, sells the software of killing and deportation. \"Palantir is here to disrupt ... and, when it's necessary, to scare enemies and on occasion kill them,\" he told investors in February 2025. In January 2024, with Gaza being pulverised, Karp and Peter Thiel flew to Tel Aviv, held Palantir's board meeting there 'in solidarity with Israel' and sealed a strategic partnership with Israel's Ministry of Defense to 'harness Palantir's advanced technology in support of war-related missions.' \"I am proud that we are supporting Israel in every way we can,\" he said. Confronted in April 2025 with the charge that Palantir kills Palestinians, he answered: \"mostly terrorists, that's true.\" Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report cites that answer as indicative of \"executive-level knowledge and purpose vis-à-vis the unlawful use of force by Israel.\" A 2025 biography says Palantir's technology was deployed by Israel in Lebanon in 2024, including the pager attacks. At home, Palantir builds ICE's hunting tools: ImmigrationOS ($30M, 2025) and ELITE, which maps deportation targets using addresses drawn from Medicaid data. Palantir's Maven Smart System, built under a $1.3B Pentagon contract, was used for US targeting in Israel's war on Iran; Pentagon investigators found overreliance on Maven contributed to the Minab school strike that killed at least 123 children. He gave $1M to MAGA Inc in December 2024. Palantir's 2026 proxy reports his 2025 pay at $8.62M, up from $4.36M in 2024; he sold more than $2B of stock in 2024, and Forbes puts his fortune at $20.2B (5 Oct 2026).","profile_src":["https://gizmodo.com/palantirs-billionaire-ceo-just-cant-stop-talking-about-killing-people-2000560597","https://www.palantir.com/assets/xrfr7uokpv1b/3MuEeA8MLbLDAyxixTsiIe/9e4a11a7fb058554a8a1e3cd83e31c09/C134184_finaleprint.pdf","https://investigate.afsc.org/company/palantir","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.aa.com.tr/en/middle-east/interview-expose-them-viral-palantir-protester-warns-all-complicit-in-gaza-horrors/3565328","https://news.antiwar.com/2025/12/10/new-book-palantir-helped-israel-carry-out-its-pager-attack-in-lebanon/","https://investigate.afsc.org/company/palantir","https://immpolicytracking.org/policies/reported-palantir-awarded-30-million-to-build-immigrationos-surveillance-platform-for-ice/","https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2026/01/report-ice-using-palantir-tool-feeds-medicaid-data","https://defensescoop.com/2025/05/23/dod-palantir-maven-smart-system-contract-increase/","https://responsiblestatecraft.org/ai-war-iran/","https://gizmodo.com/pentagon-investigators-say-overreliance-on-palantir-ai-tech-contributed-to-u-s-strike-that-killed-123-iranian-children-2000814477","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/new-megadonors-major-business-government-back-trumps-super-pac-rcna252867","https://investigate.afsc.org/company/palantir","https://www.quiverquant.com/news/Palantir+Technologies+Inc.+($PLTR)+CEO+2025+Pay+Revealed","https://gloom.sh/stocks/pltr/proxy/2026","https://www.sherwood.news/markets/palantirs-alex-karp-made-usd6-8-billion-last-year/","https://www.forbes.com/profile/alexander-karp/"],"profile_status":"documented","profile (sentence)":"Palantir's 2026 proxy reports his 2025 Summary Compensation Table total at $8.623M, up from $4.36M in 2024,"},{"id":"PER-00023","name":"Peter Thiel","type":"Person","role":"Palantir co-founder and chair; financier of the targeting machine and JD Vance","country":null,"slug":"peter-thiel","profile":"Peter Thiel is the money and ideology behind Palantir. He co-founded it in 2003 with about $30M of his own and has chaired its board ever since; he still holds roughly 3% of the company, worth more than $10B (Motley Fool, August 2026), and Forbes puts his fortune at $37.7B (4 Oct 2026). In January 2024, as Israel pulverised Gaza, Thiel and Karp met Israeli military officials in Tel Aviv, where Palantir held its board meeting 'in solidarity with Israel' and signed a strategic partnership with Israel's Ministry of Defense for 'war-related missions.' Middle East Eye reported in July 2024 that Palantir's capabilities include supplying Israel's military and intelligence agencies \"with the data to fire missiles at specific targets in Gaza - be it inside homes or in moving vehicles.\" Thiel has said he 'defers' to Tel Aviv on foreign policy and called the Israeli army's conduct 'broadly right.' His company also builds ICE's deportation targeting tools, ImmigrationOS and ELITE, and its Maven system was used for US targeting in Israel's war on Iran. His Founders Fund seeded the weapons maker Anduril in 2017 and has since put $1B into it; he was an early backer of the facial-recognition firm Clearview AI. \"I no longer believe that freedom and democracy are compatible,\" he wrote in 2009. He gave Donald Trump's campaign $1.25M in 2016 and bought JD Vance a Senate seat with $15M in 2021, then the most ever given to a single Senate candidate. In 2025 he branded climate activist Greta Thunberg among the 'legionnaires of the Antichrist.'","profile_src":["https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/08/06/peter-thiel-still-owns-roughly-3-of-palantir-a-sta/","https://www.forbes.com/profile/peter-thiel/","https://www.palantir.com/assets/xrfr7uokpv1b/3MuEeA8MLbLDAyxixTsiIe/9e4a11a7fb058554a8a1e3cd83e31c09/C134184_finaleprint.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/us-jd-vance-peter-thiel-founded-company-helps-israel-kill-lists-palestinians-gaza","https://unherd.com/newsroom/peter-thiel-afd-is-wrong-about-ukraine-and-israel/","https://immpolicytracking.org/policies/reported-palantir-awarded-30-million-to-build-immigrationos-surveillance-platform-for-ice/","https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2026/01/report-ice-using-palantir-tool-feeds-medicaid-data","https://responsiblestatecraft.org/ai-war-iran/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anduril_Industries","https://thenextweb.com/news/founders-fund-6-billion-ai-venture","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clearview_AI","https://www.cato-unbound.org/2009/04/13/peter-thiel/education-libertarian/","https://money.cnn.com/2016/10/15/technology/peter-thiel-donate-trump-campaign/index.html","https://www.ctvnews.ca/world/article/tech-billionaire-thiel-says-greta-thunberg-servant-of-antichrist/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00024","name":"Jeff Bezos","type":"Person","role":"Amazon founder; his cloud stores Israeli military intelligence","country":null,"slug":"jeff-bezos","profile":"Jeff Bezos founded Amazon in 1994 and has chaired its board since. Forbes puts his net worth at $371.2B (4 Oct 2026), resting on about 8% of Amazon plus Blue Origin and The Washington Post. Amazon Web Services and Google run Project Nimbus, the $1.2B Israeli government cloud contract signed in 2021. +972 Magazine and Local Call reported in August 2024 that AWS provides Israel's Military Intelligence Directorate with a server farm used 'to store masses of intelligence information that assists the army in the war' on Gaza, and Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report names Amazon among firms granting Israel 'virtually government-wide access' to cloud and AI. After the 2024 election Bezos moved toward Donald Trump: he blocked the Post's editorial board from endorsing Kamala Harris, Amazon gave $1M to Trump's inauguration, which Bezos attended, and he dined with Trump at Mar-a-Lago. In 2025 he announced the Post's opinion pages would champion 'personal liberties' and 'free markets', democracy's death in darkness apparently included.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1018724/000110465926041026/tm261382-1_def14a.htm","https://www.forbes.com/profile/jeff-bezos/","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-02-22/how-us-tech-giants-supplied-israel-with-ai-models/104956164","https://www.972mag.com/cloud-israeli-army-gaza-amazon-google-microsoft/","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeff_Bezos"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00025","name":"Andy Jassy","type":"Person","role":"Amazon CEO; runs the cloud behind Israel's Project Nimbus","country":null,"slug":"andy-jassy","profile":"Andy Jassy built Amazon Web Services and has been Amazon's president and CEO since July 2021. Amazon reports his 2025 compensation at about $2.1M, a $365,000 salary plus $1.7M of security and travel, but $43M of his stock vested in 2025 and he held $242M of unvested stock at year-end; his 2021 CEO grant took that year's pay above $200M. Under Jassy, AWS and Google have run Project Nimbus, Israel's $1.2B government cloud contract, and +972 Magazine and Local Call reported in 2024 that AWS hosts a server farm storing intelligence for Israel's Military Intelligence Directorate during the genocide in Gaza. Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report names Amazon among firms granting Israel 'virtually government-wide access' to cloud and AI technologies; two months later the UN Commission of Inquiry found that Israel had committed genocide. TechSpot noted Amazon laid off 30,000 workers while Jassy's reported pay rose about 30%. Efficiency, it seems, applies downward.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1018724/000110465926041026/tm261382-1_def14a.htm","https://www.techspot.com/news/112028-amazon-laid-off-30000-workers-while-ceo-andy.html","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-02-22/how-us-tech-giants-supplied-israel-with-ai-models/104956164","https://www.972mag.com/cloud-israeli-army-gaza-amazon-google-microsoft/","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00026","name":"Sundar Pichai","type":"Person","role":"Google CEO; fired Nimbus protesters, dropped the no-weapons AI pledge","country":null,"slug":"sundar-pichai","profile":"Sundar Pichai is CEO of Alphabet and Google. His reported total pay was $10.73M for 2024 and $8.8M for 2023; in March 2026 Alphabet approved a new three-year package potentially worth $692M, including $84M of restricted stock. Forbes puts his net worth at $1.6B (30 Sep 2026), noting he has sold more than $500M of shares. Google and Amazon run Project Nimbus, Israel's $1.2B government cloud contract, and Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report names Alphabet among firms granting Israel 'virtually government-wide access' to cloud and AI. In April 2024 Google fired about 50 employees after sit-ins against Nimbus, and Pichai told staff 'this is a business, and not a place to act in a way that disrupts coworkers or makes them feel unsafe.' Palestinians in Gaza were not consulted on feeling unsafe. In February 2025 Google dropped language from its AI principles that ruled out using AI for weapons and surveillance, AP reported. Two months after Albanese's report, the UN Commission of Inquiry found Israel had committed genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.storyboard18.com/how-it-works/sundar-pichais-2024-compensation-reaches-10-73-mn-up-from-8-8-mn-in-2023-63994.htm","https://www.thehansindia.com/technology/tech-news/sundar-pichais-pay-package-surges-to-692-million-1054565","https://www.forbes.com/profile/sundar-pichai/","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-02-22/how-us-tech-giants-supplied-israel-with-ai-models/104956164","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.axios.com/2024/04/23/google-fires-employees-protest-israel-contract-nimbus","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00027","name":"Larry Page","type":"Person","role":"Google co-founder; controlling shareholder, silent on Nimbus","country":null,"slug":"larry-page","profile":"Larry Page co-founded Google and was its CEO from 2011 to 2015 and Alphabet's CEO from 2015 to 2019. He remains an Alphabet board member and, with Sergey Brin, a controlling shareholder. Forbes puts his net worth at $281.8B (3 Oct 2026), making him one of the richest people alive. His fortune comes from the company that, with Amazon, runs Project Nimbus, Israel's $1.2B government cloud contract signed in 2021, and that Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report names among firms granting Israel 'virtually government-wide access' to cloud and AI technologies during its assault on Gaza. In February 2025 Google dropped language from its AI principles that ruled out weapons and surveillance uses. As a controlling shareholder Page holds the voting power to change that course; no public statement by him on Nimbus, Gaza or Google's military work has been found. Silence, at $281.8B, is a choice. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1652044/000130817926000342/goog2025_courtesy-pdf.pdf","https://www.forbes.com/profile/larry-page/","https://www.forbes.com/profile/sergey-brin/","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-02-22/how-us-tech-giants-supplied-israel-with-ai-models/104956164","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00028","name":"Sergey Brin","type":"Person","role":"Google co-founder; called the UN 'transparently antisemitic'","country":null,"slug":"sergey-brin","profile":"Sergey Brin co-founded Google, served as its and Alphabet's president until 2019 and remains an Alphabet board member and controlling shareholder. Forbes puts his net worth at $259.3B (4 Oct 2026). After Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report accused tech firms including Google of aiding Israel's genocide in Gaza, Brin wrote on an internal employee forum that 'throwing around the term genocide in relation to Gaza is deeply offensive to many Jewish people who have suffered actual genocides', adding: 'I would also be careful citing transparently antisemitic organizations like the UN in relation to these issues.' He later told The Washington Post he meant a 'plainly biased and misleading report.' Two months later the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza. Google, which he co-controls, runs Project Nimbus with Amazon, Israel's $1.2B government cloud contract, and in February 2025 dropped its pledge against AI for weapons and surveillance.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1652044/000130817926000342/goog2025_courtesy-pdf.pdf","https://www.forbes.com/profile/sergey-brin/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/google-co-founder-decries-antisemitic-un-for-report-on-tech-aid-to-gaza-genocide/","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-02-22/how-us-tech-giants-supplied-israel-with-ai-models/104956164"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00029","name":"Satya Nadella","type":"Person","role":"Microsoft CEO; struck the Azure deal with Unit 8200's commander","country":null,"slug":"satya-nadella","profile":"Satya Nadella is chairman and CEO of Microsoft. His pay for fiscal 2025 reached a record $96.5M, and Forbes puts his net worth at $1.4B (29 Sep 2026). A joint investigation by The Guardian, +972 Magazine and Local Call in August 2025 found that Israel's military intelligence Unit 8200 stored audio files of millions of phone calls made by Palestinians on Microsoft's Azure cloud, under an agreement made in 2021 between Nadella and the unit's then commander, Yossi Sariel. AP reported in February 2025 that the Israeli military's use of Microsoft and OpenAI AI spiked to nearly 200 times pre-7 October levels by March 2024, and that its data on Microsoft servers doubled to more than 13.6 petabytes by July 2024. In September 2025 Microsoft disabled services to a unit within the Israeli military; campaigners noted that most of its Israeli military contract stayed in place. Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report names Microsoft among firms granting Israel 'virtually government-wide access' to cloud and AI.","profile_src":["https://news.microsoft.com/source/exec/satya-nadella/","https://www.fortune.com/2025/10/22/microsoft-ceo-satya-nadella-pay-hits-a-record-96-5-million-dollars-usd-he-got-a-22-percent-pay-rise-mirroring-the-4-trillion-tech-giants-skyrocketing-shares","https://www.forbes.com/profile/satya-nadella/","https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/israels-military-surveillance-agency-stores-masses-of-intelligence-on-palestinians-on-microsoft-cloud/","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-02-22/how-us-tech-giants-supplied-israel-with-ai-models/104956164","https://www.cbc.ca/lite/story/1.7644413","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00030","name":"Sam Altman","type":"Person","role":"OpenAI CEO; Pentagon deal signed the night before the Iran war","country":null,"slug":"sam-altman","profile":"Sam Altman is CEO of OpenAI. Forbes puts his net worth at $3.3B (3 Oct 2026), drawn from stakes in Stripe, Reddit, Helion and other companies; Forbes says he holds no OpenAI equity. In early 2024 OpenAI dropped its ban on military use in favour of 'national security use cases', and AP reported that the Israeli military's use of Microsoft and OpenAI AI spiked to nearly 200 times pre-7 October levels by March 2024. Altman gave $1M to Donald Trump's inaugural committee in December 2024 and on 21 January 2025 stood in the White House to launch the $500B Stargate AI project with Trump and Larry Ellison, saying: 'I think if it were a different President, it might not have been possible.' On the night of 27–28 February 2026, hours after Trump ordered federal agencies to stop using rival Anthropic, Altman announced a Pentagon deal to put OpenAI models on classified networks; the US–Israeli war on Iran began on 28 February. The timing was excellent, for OpenAI.","profile_src":["https://openai.com/index/sam-altman-un-security-council-remarks/","https://www.forbes.com/profile/sam-altman/","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-02-22/how-us-tech-giants-supplied-israel-with-ai-models/104956164","https://abcnews.com/US/openais-sam-altman-warned-america-trump-now-partnering/story?id=118145337","https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/business-news/stargate-trump-openai-ellison-1236114430/","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/28/openai-strikes-deal-with-pentagon-to-use-tech-in-classified-network","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00031","name":"Greg Brockman","type":"Person","role":"OpenAI president; $25M couple's gift to Trump's super PAC","country":null,"slug":"greg-brockman","profile":"Greg Brockman co-founded OpenAI and is its president. In May 2026 testimony he disclosed owning about $20B of OpenAI equity, roughly 2.5% to 3% of the company, and Forbes puts his net worth at $25.5B (20 Sep 2026). In September 2025 Brockman gave $12.5M to MAGA Inc, Donald Trump's super PAC, and his wife Anna gave the same amount the same day, making the couple among the biggest new Trump donors, NBC News reported; Forbes counts $75M of the couple's 2025 political giving, split between MAGA Inc and the AI industry's Leading the Future super PAC. OpenAI, which he co-leads, rewrote its rules in early 2024 to allow 'national security use cases'; AP reported the Israeli military's use of Microsoft and OpenAI AI rose nearly 200-fold during the genocide in Gaza; and OpenAI agreed to put its models on Pentagon classified networks on the eve of the 2026 US–Israeli war on Iran. Safety research, meet political donations.","profile_src":["https://openai.com/index/openai-broadcom-jalapeno-inference-chip/","https://www.forbes.com/profile/greg-brockman/","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/new-megadonors-major-business-government-back-trumps-super-pac-rcna252867","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-02-22/how-us-tech-giants-supplied-israel-with-ai-models/104956164","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/28/openai-strikes-deal-with-pentagon-to-use-tech-in-classified-network"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00032","name":"Dario Amodei","type":"Person","role":"Anthropic CEO; his Claude sits inside the Pentagon's targeting system","country":null,"slug":"dario-amodei","profile":"Dario Amodei co-founded Anthropic in 2021 and is its CEO; Forbes puts his net worth at $15.5B (2 Oct 2026). Anthropic was the first AI company approved for US classified settings, and Claude is integrated in the Pentagon's Maven Smart System, built by Palantir under a $1.3B contract, which generates and ranks targets. In February 2026 Amodei refused Pentagon demands to drop two limits, no fully autonomous weapons and no mass domestic surveillance; Donald Trump then ordered every federal agency to stop using Anthropic and Military Secretary Pete Hegseth declared it a supply-chain risk. The next day the US and Israel attacked Iran, and a US Tomahawk strike on the Shajareh Tayyebeh elementary school in Minab killed 156 people, 120 of them children. Asked in June 2026 whether Claude was used in that targeting, Amodei said: 'We don't have access to, we don't know exactly how these models were used,' adding that 'a human makes the final decision.' Two red lines were drawn; the targeting itself was not one of them.","profile_src":["https://www.anthropic.com/company/leadership","https://www.forbes.com/profile/dario-amodei/","https://www.npr.org/2026/02/27/nx-s1-5729118/trump-anthropic-pentagon-openai-ai-weapons-ban","https://thenextweb.com/news/anthropic-amodei-claude-iran-school-strike-military-ai","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Minab_school_attack","https://abcnews.com/Politics/anthropic-latest-pentagon-contract-bar-ai-autonomous-weapons/story?id=130558898"],"profile_status":"documented","profile (append sentence)":"No public evidence currently establishes that Claude itself selected, recommended or processed the Minab school target."},{"id":"PER-00033","name":"Daniela Amodei","type":"Person","role":"Anthropic president; co-leads the maker of Maven's Claude layer","country":null,"slug":"daniela-amodei","profile":"Daniela Amodei co-founded Anthropic in 2021 with her brother Dario and is its president; Forbes puts her net worth at $15.5B (24 Sep 2026). She shares leadership of a company that was the first AI company approved for US classified settings and whose Claude models are integrated in Palantir's Maven Smart System, the Pentagon platform that generates and ranks targets and was used in the 2026 US–Israeli war on Iran. On that war's first day a US Tomahawk strike on an elementary school in Minab killed 156 people, including 120 children; Anthropic's CEO said in June 2026 that the company does not know exactly how its models were used and that a human made the final decision. In February 2026 the Trump administration ordered agencies to stop using Anthropic after it refused to allow fully autonomous weapons or mass domestic surveillance. No public statement by Daniela Amodei on Gaza or Israel has been found.","profile_src":["https://www.anthropic.com/company/leadership","https://www.forbes.com/profile/daniela-amodei/","https://www.npr.org/2026/02/27/nx-s1-5729118/trump-anthropic-pentagon-openai-ai-weapons-ban","https://thenextweb.com/news/anthropic-amodei-claude-iran-school-strike-military-ai","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Minab_school_attack","https://abcnews.com/Politics/anthropic-latest-pentagon-contract-bar-ai-autonomous-weapons/story?id=130558898"],"profile_status":"documented","profile (append sentence)":"No public evidence currently establishes that Claude itself selected, recommended or processed the Minab school target."},{"id":"PER-00034","name":"Safra Catz","type":"Person","role":"Former Oracle CEO; told staff to back Israel or leave","country":null,"slug":"safra-catz","profile":"Safra Catz ran Oracle as CEO from 2014 to September 2025 and is now executive vice chair of its board. Oracle's proxies, as compiled by the data site Gloom, show her total pay at $1.1M for fiscal 2025 and $10.1M for fiscal 2026; Forbes puts her net worth at $2.9B (14 Sep 2026). The Intercept reported in February 2025 that after 7 October 2023 Catz demanded 'Oracle Stands with Israel' be shown on company screens worldwide, called pro-Palestinian rights groups 'brainwashing organizations', and in November 2024 laid down the employment terms: 'For employees, it's clear: if you're not for America or Israel, don't work here.' The same report says Oracle under her built a $319M data center in Jerusalem, ran a confidential project with the Israeli Air Force and worked with the state weapons maker Rafael on AI. Who Profits says Oracle donated equipment worth more than $500,000 in January 2024 'amid the military invasion of Gaza'. A loyalty oath, with a hardware donation attached.","profile_src":["https://www.oracle.com/news/announcement/oracle-corporation-announces-promotion-of-clay-magouyrk-and-mike-scilia-2025-09-22/","https://gloom.sh/stocks/orcl/proxy/2025","https://gloom.sh/stocks/orcl/proxy/2026","https://www.forbes.com/profile/safra-catz/","https://theintercept.com/2025/02/18/oracle-tiktok-israel-palestine-gaza/","https://www.whoprofits.org/companies/company/7396?oracle="],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00035","name":"Rajeev Amara","type":"Person","role":"Arcline CEO; bought the bomb-fuze maker Kaman","country":null,"slug":"rajeev-amara","profile":"Rajeev Amara has been CEO of Arcline Investment Management, a US private equity firm, since 2018. In April 2024 Arcline completed its all-cash takeover of Kaman Corporation at $46 a share, an enterprise value of about $1.8B. Kaman's fuze business made the Joint Programmable Fuze (FMU-152) used on US air-dropped bombs, the component that decides when a bomb explodes; in 2018 it won a $324M direct commercial sale order for the fuzes, which Kaman called the largest single order in the program's history, and the unit now operates as Precision Fuzing & Sensors. The US arms package approved for Israel in February 2025, worth $6.75B, covered munitions, guidance kits and fuzes. His personal pay and stake in Arcline are not public, as is customary in private equity, where the returns are private and the bombs are not. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://ir.arxis.com/corporate-governance/board-of-directors","https://kaman.com/arcline-completes-acquisition-of-kaman/","https://kaman.com/kaman-announces-324-million-joint-programmable-fuze-order/","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-00036","name":"Ian K. Walsh","type":"Person","role":"Former Kaman CEO; golden parachute from the fuze-maker sale","country":null,"slug":"ian-k-walsh","profile":"Ian K. Walsh was chairman, president and CEO of Kaman Corporation, an aerospace and military components maker, until its takeover by Arcline Investment Management closed on 19 April 2024 at $46 a share, an enterprise value of about $1.8B. Kaman's March 2024 merger proxy estimated change-in-control ('golden parachute') payments of $16.27M for its named executive officers, Walsh among them. He called the sale 'a value-maximizing transaction', and for him it was. Kaman's portfolio included the Joint Programmable Fuze for US air-dropped bombs; in 2018 the line won a $324M direct commercial sale order, the largest in the program's history. Fuzes were part of the $6.75B munitions package the US approved for Israel in February 2025, during the assault on Gaza that the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 was a genocide.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/54381/000114036124012403/ny20021849x2_defm14a.htm","https://kaman.com/arcline-completes-acquisition-of-kaman/","https://kaman.com/kaman-announces-324-million-joint-programmable-fuze-order/","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-00037","name":"Armin Papperger","type":"Person","role":"Rheinmetall CEO; pay up two and a half times in a year","country":null,"slug":"armin-papperger","profile":"Armin Papperger has been CEO of Rheinmetall, the German arms maker, since 1 January 2013. His pay for 2025 rose to about €10.2M, two and a half times the previous year, placing him sixth among DAX chief executives, Börse Express reported in April 2026. Rearmament has been generous to him. US and German intelligence officials reportedly foiled a Russian plan to assassinate him in 2024. Germany supplied about 30% of Israel's arms imports in recent years, making it Israel's second-largest supplier after the United States, during the assault on Gaza that the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 was a genocide. No public investigation has yet tied a specific Rheinmetall product to a strike in Gaza; his place in this network rests on German arms flows to Israel and on war-driven profits.","profile_src":["https://www.rheinmetall.com/en/rheinmetall_ag/group/gremien/executive_board/index.php","https://www.boerse-express.com/news/articles/rheinmetall-aktie-chef-gehalt-explodiert-894668","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armin_Papperger","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_supplying_arms_to_Israel","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-00039","name":"Roberto Cingolani","type":"Person","role":"Former Leonardo CEO; ran Italy's arms maker through the genocide","country":null,"slug":"roberto-cingolani","profile":"Roberto Cingolani was Italy's minister for ecological transition in Mario Draghi's government from February 2021, then CEO and general manager of Leonardo, the Italian state-backed arms maker, from May 2023 until May 2026, when Lorenzo Mariani, nominated by the Italian Treasury as shareholder, replaced him. From green transition to gun turrets, his tenure at Leonardo spanned the genocide in Gaza. Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report identified Leonardo among corporations aiding Israel that 'may be embedded in an economy of genocide', and Leonardo's 'ongoing supply of equipment for Israel's military has attracted controversy'. Investors rewarded the war years: Leonardo's share price rose 234% between October 2023 and July 2025. Italy's sales of arms and ammunition to Israel amounted to €13.7M a year, according to the magazine Altreconomia. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roberto_Cingolani","https://www.leonardo.com/en/about/management/chief-executive-officer","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leonardo_S.p.A.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_supplying_arms_to_Israel","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-00045","name":"Mathios Rigas","type":"Person","role":"Energean founder and CEO; sells Israel the gas that runs its grid","country":null,"slug":"mathios-rigas","profile":"Mathios Rigas founded the oil and gas producer Energean and is its CEO, holding about 8.34% of the company. Energean bought the Karish and Tanin gas fields off Israel's coast for $148M in 2016 and sells their gas to Israeli power producers; Israel supplied about 65% of group revenue in H1 2026 and more than 70% of output. Group revenue was $1.73B in 2025. Israel's Ministry of Energy ordered production halted for 41 days, from 28 February to 9 April 2026, the opening weeks of the US–Israeli war on Iran, after which output 'recovered strongly'. In H1 2026 Energean's free cash flow rose 35% to $250M and profit after tax 45%, and it signed a ~$1.4B gas deal with the Sorek power station, which the company calls 'a nationally significant energy infrastructure project'. Energean's earnings are tied directly to keeping Israel's grid running through its assault on Gaza and its wars on Lebanon and Iran.","profile_src":["https://www.investegate.co.uk/announcement/rns/energean--enog/results-for-half-year-ended-30-june-2026/9761841","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Energean"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-00001","name":"US–Israel JDAM and munitions sale (notified 7 Feb 2025)","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"FMS notified Feb 7, 2025","country":null,"slug":"israel-jdam-munitions-package-feb-7-2025","profile":"On 7 February 2025 the State Department notified Congress of a $6.75B Foreign Military Sale to Israel. The approved maximum quantities were 2,166 GBU-39 Small Diameter Bombs, 2,800 MK-82 500-pound bomb bodies, 13,000 JDAM kits for 2,000-pound MK-84 bombs, 3,475 JDAM kits for BLU-109 bunker-busters, 1,004 JDAM kits for GBU-38s and 17,475 FMU-152 fuzes. Boeing and ATK Tactical Systems were the principal contractors, and deliveries were due to begin in 2025. Congress did not block the sale, and on 1 March 2025 the administration used emergency powers to speed about $4B of arms to Israel. Actual delivered quantities have not been published, so these numbers are ceilings, not deliveries. The same weapons kept appearing in strikes: Bellingcat documented JDAM-guided bombs destroying Gaza City towers in 2025, and Amnesty found JDAM parts in Tehran in March 2026.","profile_src":["https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/israel/2025/03/israel-250301-state01.htm","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://www.amnesty.org.au/investigation-into-us-israeli-strikes-on-tehran-neighbourhoods-reveals-devastating-civilian-harm/"],"profile_status":"documented","ctx (new)":"On 7 February 2025 the Trump administration formally notified Congress of a $6.75B Foreign Military Sales case for Israel: 2,166 GBU-39/B Small Diameter Bombs, 2,800 MK 82 bomb bodies, 17,479 JDAM guidance kits and 17,475 FMU-152 fuzes, with Boeing the lead contractor. The Congressional Research Service called it the largest single munitions sale to Israel since 2015. Deliveries were scheduled to begin in 2025. Israel's Ministry of Defense said that during the war on Iran launched on 28 February 2026, more than 115,600 tons of US military equipment, including thousands of air munitions, arrived on 403 flights and 10 ships. Amnesty International traced US-made JDAM kits to two Israeli strikes on family homes in central Gaza in October 2023 that killed 43 civilians, 19 of them children."},{"id":"CTR-00002","name":"US–Israel Hellfire sale (notified 7 Feb 2025)","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"FMS notified Feb 7, 2025","country":null,"slug":"israel-hellfire-package-feb-7-2025","profile":"On 7 February 2025 the State Department notified Congress of the sale of up to 3,000 AGM-114 Hellfire air-to-ground missiles to Israel, estimated at $660M, with Lockheed Martin in Troy, Alabama, as principal contractor. DSCA estimated that deliveries would begin in 2028, so the 3,000 is an approved maximum for future restocking, not a count of missiles delivered; no public source gives delivered numbers. The sale went through with no congressional block. The missiles restock the weapon Israel's Apache helicopters and drones use for targeted strikes. Bellingcat's 2026 review of US-made munitions in Gaza found Hellfires in strikes on a health clinic, on displacement tents within 150 metres of Al-Aqsa Martyrs Hospital, and on Cairo Basic School in July 2025, where five people were reported killed.","profile_src":["https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060949/israel-agm-114-hellfire-missiles","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/"],"profile_status":"documented","ctx (new)":"On 7 February 2025 the US notified Congress of a $660M sale to Israel of 3,000 AGM-114 Hellfire missiles, with Lockheed Martin (Troy, Alabama) the principal contractor and deliveries scheduled to begin in 2028. Lockheed's ties to Israel's attack helicopter fleet grew in January 2026, when the US notified a $3.8B sale of 30 AH-64E Apache helicopters naming Boeing and Lockheed Martin as principal contractors."},{"id":"CTR-00003","name":"US–Israel bomb bodies and penetrators sale (notified 28 Feb 2025)","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"FMS notified Feb 28, 2025","country":null,"slug":"israel-bomb-bodies-penetrators-package-feb-28-2025","profile":"On 28 February 2025 the State Department declared an emergency, waiving congressional review, and approved a $2.04B sale to Israel of up to 35,529 MK-84 or BLU-117 2,000-pound bomb bodies and 4,000 I-2000 penetrator warheads. General Dynamics (Garland, Texas), Ellwood National Forge and McAlester Army Ammunition Plant were named prime contractors; deliveries were due to begin in 2026. A separate emergency package the same day covered 201 MK-83 and 4,799 BLU-110 1,000-pound bomb bodies and 5,000 JDAM kits ($675.7M; Repkon USA and Boeing). These are approved maximums; actual deliveries are unpublished. The bodies are the casings JDAM kits turn into guided one-ton bombs, which Bellingcat documented destroying high-rises in Gaza City in 2025. In September 2026 the administration proposed 40,000 more 2,000-pound bombs worth $2.8B, now held in Congress.","profile_src":["https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088258/israel-munitions-and-munitions-support","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088252/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-and-munitions-support","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/","https://democrats-foreignaffairs.house.gov/press-releases?ContentRecord_id=2AC6AE1D-BDCD-4E19-B8A7-BCA59F204151"],"profile_status":"documented","ctx (new)":"On 28 February 2025 Secretary of State Marco Rubio invoked emergency powers to skip congressional review of a $2.04B sale to Israel of 35,529 MK 84 or BLU-117 2,000-pound bomb bodies and 4,000 I-2000 penetrator warheads, with deliveries scheduled to begin in 2026. General Dynamics' Garland, Texas plant was named a prime contractor; it was sold in April 2025 to Repkon USA (renamed Paligen Technologies in March 2026), which was then named contractor for a separate emergency sale of 12,000 1,000-pound bomb bodies in March 2026. In September 2026 the administration informally notified Congress of a further $2.8B package of 40,000 MK-84 and BLU-117 bombs with I-2000 warheads, funded with US Foreign Military Financing; Rep. Gregory Meeks and Sen. Jeanne Shaheen placed holds on it. CNN found that Israel dropped hundreds of 2,000-pound bombs on Gaza in the first month of the war alone.","profile (sentence)":"40,000 more 2,000-pound bombs worth $2.8B"},{"id":"CTR-00004","name":"Project Nimbus","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Israeli government cloud contract (Google, Amazon)","country":null,"slug":"project-nimbus","profile":"Project Nimbus is the Israeli government's cloud contract. Google Cloud and Amazon Web Services won it in April 2021, in a tender worth about NIS 4B ($1.2B), to provide cloud and AI services to ministries, state companies and the military. It runs for an initial seven years and can be extended up to 23. The UN Special Rapporteur's July 2025 report \"From economy of occupation to economy of genocide\" names the deal, says Israel awarded Google and Amazon \"a $1.2 billion contract (Project Nimbus)\" for core tech infrastructure, and finds that Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon \"grant Israel virtually government-wide access to their cloud and AI technologies\". Cloud capacity matters for mass surveillance. In September 2025 Microsoft said it had disabled some Israel Ministry of Defense subscriptions after finding evidence supporting Guardian reporting on Azure storage used for intercepted Palestinian phone calls. We found no report that Google or Amazon has ended its Nimbus work.","profile_src":["https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/inside-google-cloud/google-cloud-selected-to-provide-cloud-services-to-the-state-of-israel","https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/google-aws-win-12-billion-israel-nimbus-tender-for-cloud-services/","https://www.un.org/unispal/document/a-hrc-59-23-from-economy-of-occupation-to-economy-of-genocide-report-special-rapporteur-francesca-albanese-palestine-2025/","https://blogs.microsoft.com/on-the-issues/2025/09/25/update-on-ongoing-microsoft-review/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-00006","name":"Germany Arrow 3 procurement","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Arms procurement from Israel (IAI)","country":null,"slug":"germany-arrow-3-procurement","profile":"Germany's Arrow 3 purchase is the largest arms export deal in Israel's history. Berlin signed in September 2023, in the first weeks of the genocide in Gaza, for a deal worth about €4B. Israel handed over the first battery at Holzdorf Air Base on 3 December 2025. On 17 December 2025 the Bundestag approved a €3B expansion for more interceptors and launchers, and IAI then booked a $3.1B follow-on contract. IAI expects the programme to exceed $6.5B, while the Times of Israel put the total at about $8B. The money goes to state-owned Israel Aerospace Industries. Arrow 3's sales pitch rests on its record against Iranian missiles in the June 2025 and 2026 wars. Germany signed while Nicaragua was suing it at the ICJ over its support for Israel; hearings on Germany's preliminary objections were held in September 2026.","profile_src":["https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-delivers-arrow-3-to-germany-in-largest-defense-export-deal-ever/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/german-parliament-approves-3-5b-expansion-of-arrow-3-deal-with-israel/","https://defence-industry.eu/iai-signs-usd-3-1-billion-follow-on-contract-to-expand-germanys-arrow-3-missile-defence-programme/","https://www.icj-cij.org/case/193"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-00007","name":"Finland David's Sling procurement","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Arms procurement from Israel (Rafael/RTX)","country":null,"slug":"finland-david-s-sling-procurement","profile":"Finland was the first foreign customer for David's Sling. Its Military ministry chose the system in April 2023, and the contract with Israel's Ministry of Defense was signed on 12 November 2023, five weeks into the bombardment of Gaza. The contract is worth about €317M: a €213M main contract plus €103M in options exercised immediately. It covers Israeli-American interceptors, launchers and Israeli radars. Industry reporting expects initial deliveries from 2025 and full operational capability by 2030. We have not found a confirmed 2026 delivery date. The money goes to state-owned Rafael and its US partner RTX. The system's combat record, used to sell it, comes from intercepting rockets fired during Israel's campaigns in Gaza and Lebanon and missiles from Iran. Finland went ahead after the ICJ ordered provisional measures against Israel in January 2024.","profile_src":["https://militarnyi.com/en/news/finland-signs-agreement-with-israel-to-purchase-david-s-sling-system/","https://norskluftvern.com/2025/11/25/finlands-air-defense-transformation-from-neutral-defender-to-natos-northern-anchor/","https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/factbox-what-israels-multi-layered-defence-against-iranian-missiles","https://www.icj-cij.org/node/203447"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-00008","name":"Denmark ATMOS/PULS procurement","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Arms procurement from Israel (Elbit)","country":null,"slug":"denmark-atmos-puls-procurement","profile":"In January 2023 Denmark's Military announced it was buying 19 ATMOS truck-mounted howitzers and 8 PULS rocket launchers from Elbit Systems, to replace CAESAR guns Denmark had given to Ukraine. PULS deliveries were due from summer 2023, ATMOS from early 2024, and full operational status by 2025. The Danish announcement gave no price. In March 2023 Elbit announced two contracts worth $252M for ATMOS and PULS to an unnamed European NATO country, which matches the Danish order, and Janes put the PULS share at about $133M. The deal was signed nine months before the genocide in Gaza, but deliveries continued throughout it. PULS is used heavily by Israel's army in Gaza and Lebanon. Denmark's money went to Elbit, which the UN Special Rapporteur names as a key domestic supplier of weapons for Israel's war.","profile_src":["https://www.forsvaret.dk/da/nyheder/2023/atmospulse/","https://elbitsystems.com/pr-new/elbit-systems-awarded-two-contracts-in-an-aggregate-amount-of-252-million-to-supply-atmos-and-puls-artillery-systems-to-a-nato-member-country/","https://defence-industry.eu/idf-employs-puls-rocket-artillery-system-during-ongoing-war/","https://www.un.org/unispal/document/a-hrc-59-23-from-economy-of-occupation-to-economy-of-genocide-report-special-rapporteur-francesca-albanese-palestine-2025/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-00009","name":"Slovakia Barak MX procurement","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Arms procurement from Israel (IAI)","country":null,"slug":"slovakia-barak-mx-procurement","profile":"On 23 December 2024 Israel's Ministry of Defense announced that Slovakia would buy Israel Aerospace Industries' Barak MX anti-aircraft and anti-missile system for about €560M. The deal was made government to government through the ministry's export directorate, SIBAT. The first battery was delivered to the Slovak Armed Forces in April 2026, with full readiness expected weeks later. The money goes to IAI, which is wholly owned by the Israeli state. The deal was signed more than a year into Israel's genocide in Gaza, after the ICJ's January 2024 provisional-measures order and the ICC's November 2024 arrest warrants for Benjamin Netanyahu and Yoav Gallant. It added to a record year in which Europe accounted for 54% of Israel's arms export deals.","profile_src":["https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-mod-seals-560-million-euro-agreement-barak-mx-integrated-air-defense-system-produced-by-iai-sold-to-slovakia-in-landmark-agreement","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-mod-delivers-iai-s-barak-mx-to-slovak-armed-forces","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-147-billion-in-2024","https://www.icj-cij.org/node/203447","https://www.npr.org/2024/11/21/g-s1-35169/icc-israel-hamas-arrest-warrants-gaza"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-00010","name":"Greece 'Achilles Shield' air-interception deal (2026)","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Arms procurement from Israel (Rafael/IAI), ~€3B","country":null,"slug":"greece-air-defense-package-2026","profile":"On 31 August 2026 Israel and Greece signed the \"Achilles Shield\" deal, worth about €3B. Israel's Ministry of Defense calls it the largest arms export deal in the history of Israel–Greece relations and one of the largest in Israel's history. Rafael will supply David's Sling, SPYDER and a national command-and-control system; Israel Aerospace Industries will supply Barak MX; and its ELTA unit will supply MMR radars. A separate €26M deal covers Rafael Drone Dome systems. No delivery schedule was published. The ministry said the array draws \"on the extensive operational experience Israel's military establishment has gained during the war\", and that \"operational successes of Israeli systems on the battlefield continue to reinforce global demand\". The deal was signed almost a year after the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement","https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00001","name":"Israel","type":"Country","role":"State waging genocide in Gaza and wars on Lebanon and Iran; arms importer and exporter","country":null,"slug":"israel","profile":"Israel is the state whose wars on Gaza, Lebanon and Iran since October 2023 sit at the centre of this map. On September 16, 2025 the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded that Israeli authorities and security forces committed four of the five genocidal acts defined by the Genocide Convention, and called on all states to stop transferring arms that may be used for them. In Lebanon, the Ministry of Public Health counts 8,953 people killed and 30,649 wounded by Israeli attacks through 25 September 2026. In Iran, HRANA had verified at least 1,701 civilian deaths, including 254 children, from US and Israeli strikes by 7 April 2026, a minimum count. Israel spent $48.3B on its military in 2025, according to SIPRI, and imported most major arms from the United States (68%) and Germany (31%) in 2021–25. Its arms exports hit a record $19.2B in 2025.","profile_src":["https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.sipri.org/sites/default/files/2026-04/2604_milex_2025.pdf","https://www.sipri.org/sites/default/files/2026-03/fs_2603_at_2025.pdf","https://www.timesofisrael.com/israeli-arms-sales-break-record-for-5th-year-in-row-reaching-19-2-billion-in-2025/","https://www.sipri.org/sites/default/files/2026-03/fs_2603_at_2025.pdf","https://moph.gov.lb/en/Media/view/87142/4/update-toll-of-the-aggression-25-9-2026","https://www.en-hrana.org/day-39-of-u-s-and-israeli-attacks-on-iran-extensive-damage-to-the-rail-network-and-roads/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00059","name":"Glenn Ivey","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, Maryland 4th District (UDP-backed)","country":"USA","slug":"glenn-ivey","profile":"Glenn Ivey has represented Maryland's 4th Congressional District since January 2023. In the July 2022 Democratic primary the United Democracy Project (UDP), AIPAC's super PAC, spent about $1.7M supporting him and about $4.26M attacking his rival, former Representative Donna Edwards, according to FactCheck.org's tally of FEC filings; Wikipedia puts UDP's total in the race at $5.9M. Ivey won 51.8% to 35.2%, and told The Washington Post AIPAC's help was 'extremely helpful'. He supports a two-state solution, opposes the BDS movement and voted to fund Iron Dome. He was re-elected in 2024 with 88.4% and won his 2026 primary with 79.2%. In July 2026 he voted for an amendment to block $3.3B in annual US security assistance to Israel, citing Israel's conduct in Gaza, a shift for a candidate AIPAC's money helped elect.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2022/08/united-democracy-project","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenn_Ivey","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glenn_Ivey"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00060","name":"Haley Stevens","type":"Person","role":"Congresswoman; voted to sanction the ICC, backed by $15M AIPAC ads","country":"USA","slug":"haley-stevens","profile":"Haley Stevens is a Democratic US Representative from Michigan whose career has been underwritten by AIPAC's super PAC. In the August 2022 primary that pitted her against fellow incumbent Andy Levin after redistricting, the United Democracy Project (UDP) spent about $3.88M supporting her and about $342,000 against Levin, FactCheck.org reported; she won. Stevens voted to sanction the International Criminal Court after it issued arrest warrants over war crimes in Gaza, choosing to punish the court rather than the accused, and has called anti-Zionism 'a hate movement that has taken over in America'. In 2026 she ran for the open US Senate seat; Wikipedia reports UDP had spent $15M on advertising in that race by 13 July 2026. The investment failed: on 4 August 2026 she lost the Democratic primary narrowly to Abdul El-Sayed, 47.55% to 48.45%.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2022/08/united-democracy-project","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haley_Stevens"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-00061","name":"Adam Hollier","type":"Person","role":"Former Michigan state senator (UDP-backed, lost)","country":"USA","slug":"adam-hollier","profile":"Adam Hollier, a former Michigan state senator, was the favoured candidate of the United Democracy Project (UDP), AIPAC's super PAC, in the August 2022 Democratic primary for Michigan's 13th District. UDP spent about $2.74M supporting him and $1.43M opposing Shri Thanedar, FactCheck.org reported from FEC filings, more than $4M in one Detroit primary. Thanedar won. Governor Gretchen Whitmer then appointed Hollier director of the Michigan Veterans Affairs Agency from January 2023. He was disqualified from the 2024 primary ballot for lacking enough valid petition signatures, withdrew from later congressional and Secretary of State bids, and has filed to run for a non-consecutive second term in the Michigan Senate. His race showed that heavy AIPAC spending could fail in a district with a strong local opponent.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2022/08/united-democracy-project","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adam_Hollier"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00062","name":"Steve Irwin","type":"Person","role":"Former congressional candidate, Pennsylvania 12th (UDP-backed, lost)","country":"USA","slug":"steve-irwin","profile":"Steve Irwin was the favoured candidate of the United Democracy Project (UDP), AIPAC's super PAC, in the May 2022 Democratic primary for Pennsylvania's 12th District. UDP, registered with the FEC as an independent-expenditure super PAC in January 2022, spent about $660,000 supporting Irwin and about $2M attacking state Representative Summer Lee, nearly $2.7M in all, according to FactCheck.org's review of FEC filings. The race was one of UDP's first tests of direct spending in Democratic primaries. Lee narrowly won, then took the seat in November 2022 and held it in 2024. Irwin's defeat was an early sign that AIPAC money could not always stop progressive critics of Israel; two years later the same super PAC succeeded against Jamaal Bowman and Cori Bush.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2022/08/united-democracy-project","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2022","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer_Lee","https://www.factcheck.org/2024/09/united-democracy-project-2/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00063","name":"Tom Malinowski","type":"Person","role":"Former U.S. Representative, New Jersey (UDP-opposed, lost 2026)","country":"USA","slug":"tom-malinowski","profile":"Tom Malinowski, a former Democratic congressman from New Jersey, ran in the February 2026 special Democratic primary for New Jersey's 11th District, vacated when Mikie Sherrill became governor. The United Democracy Project (UDP), AIPAC's super PAC, spent about $2.3M on negative ads against him. Analilia Mejia won by fewer than 1,000 votes, and Malinowski conceded on 10 February 2026. JTA reported that AIPAC defended spending $2.3M against a pro-Israel politician in a race where a candidate it called anti-Israel prevailed. UDP's spending against Malinowski helped hand the seat to a candidate further from AIPAC's positions.","profile_src":["https://www.jta.org/2026/02/10/politics/aipac-defends-2-3m-spend-against-pro-israel-politician-in-nj-11-where-anti-israel-candidate-is-prevailing","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Malinowski"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-00065","name":"Donna Edwards","type":"Person","role":"Former U.S. Representative, Maryland (UDP-opposed, lost 2022)","country":"USA","slug":"donna-edwards","profile":"Donna Edwards represented Maryland's 4th District in Congress before running to return in 2022. Opposing her was the single largest target of the United Democracy Project (UDP), AIPAC's super PAC, that cycle: it spent about $4.27M in FEC-reported independent expenditures against her, and Wikipedia puts the anti-Edwards advertising at nearly $6M, while also spending $1.7M supporting her rival Glenn Ivey. J Street's PAC backed Edwards with $720,000. Edwards lost the July 2022 primary with 35% to Ivey's 52%. Her defeat made her the clearest early example of AIPAC's shift from lobbying to buying primary outcomes directly.","profile_src":["https://projects.propublica.org/itemizer/committee/C00799031/2022/independent-expenditures","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donna_Edwards","https://www.factcheck.org/2022/08/united-democracy-project"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00066","name":"Andy Levin","type":"Person","role":"Former U.S. Representative, Michigan (UDP-opposed, lost 2022)","country":"USA","slug":"andy-levin","profile":"Andy Levin, a Democratic congressman from Michigan, lost the August 2022 primary to fellow incumbent Haley Stevens after redistricting merged their seats into one with more of Stevens's voters. FactCheck.org's tally of FEC filings shows the United Democracy Project (UDP), AIPAC's super PAC, spent about $3.88M supporting Stevens and $342,000 directly against Levin; Wikipedia puts AIPAC-linked negative advertising against him at $4.5M. Levin said AIPAC targeted him because 'I am the clearest, strongest Jewish voice in Congress standing for a simple proposition: that there is no way to have a secure, democratic homeland for the Jewish people unless we achieve the political and human rights of the Palestinian people.' After leaving Congress in January 2023 he was a senior fellow at the Center for American Progress and returned to his clean-energy group, Lean & Green Michigan.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2022/08/united-democracy-project","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andy_Levin"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00067","name":"Summer Lee","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, Pennsylvania 12th District (UDP-opposed, won)","country":"USA","slug":"summer-lee","profile":"Summer Lee has represented Pennsylvania's 12th District since January 2023. In the May 2022 Democratic primary the United Democracy Project (UDP), AIPAC's super PAC, spent about $2M attacking her and $660,000 backing Steve Irwin, nearly $2.7M in all, FactCheck.org reported from FEC filings. Lee narrowly won, then beat Republican Mike Doyle 56.2% to 43.8% in November 2022. After 7 October 2023 she backed a ceasefire in Gaza and co-sponsored a resolution demanding one. In 2024 she again won her primary against Bhavini Patel, who unlike the challengers to Jamaal Bowman and Cori Bush did not receive AIPAC's backing, and was re-elected 56.4% to 43.6%. Lee is one of the few targets of UDP's first cycle still in Congress.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2022/08/united-democracy-project","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer_Lee","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer_Lee"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00068","name":"Shri Thanedar","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative (Michigan 13th); lost Aug 2026 primary","country":"USA","slug":"shri-thanedar","profile":"Shri Thanedar has represented Michigan's 13th District since January 2023. In the August 2022 primary the United Democracy Project (UDP), AIPAC's super PAC, spent about $1.43M opposing him and $2.74M backing Adam Hollier, FactCheck.org reported; Thanedar won anyway. He then moved toward AIPAC: in 2023 he left the Democratic Socialists of America, saying it had not adequately denounced Hamas, and in August 2023 travelled to Israel with an AIPAC affiliate, afterwards calling the US–Israel relationship 'mutually beneficial'. In 2024 an AIPAC-linked group, Blue Wave Action, spent nearly $2.3M attacking his opponent, and he won renomination with 54.9%. On 4 August 2026 he lost the Democratic primary to democratic socialist state Representative Donavan McKinney, 48.1% to 51.9%.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2022/08/united-democracy-project","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shri_Thanedar","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shri_Thanedar"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-00069","name":"Dave Min","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, California 47th District (UDP-opposed, won)","country":"USA","slug":"dave-min","profile":"Dave Min, then a California state senator, was targeted by the United Democracy Project (UDP), AIPAC's super PAC, in the March 2024 top-two primary for California's 47th District. UDP spent about $4.6M trying to defeat him, FactCheck.org reported from FEC filings, one of its largest outlays of the 2024 cycle, which reached about $56M overall by September. Min finished second and advanced. In November 2024 he beat Republican Scott Baugh 51.4% to 48.6% and took the seat in January 2025. He led the 2026 top-two primary with 45.5%. Min is one of the few candidates to survive a multimillion-dollar UDP campaign against him.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2024/09/united-democracy-project-2/","https://www.factcheck.org/2024/09/united-democracy-project-2/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dave_Min"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"FAM-N0001","name":"Michael + David + Gideon + Daniel Federmann","type":"Family","role":"Federmann family, controlling owners of Elbit Systems","country":null,"slug":"michael-david-gideon-daniel-federmann","profile":"The Federmann family, Michael Federmann and his sons David, Gideon and Daniel, together hold an indirect economic interest of about 25.5% of Elbit Systems, according to Elbit's 2026 proxy statement, worth about $8.4B at September 2026 prices as calculated in this map. Through Federmann Enterprises and an affiliate the family votes about 41.2% of Elbit, a block valued at about $13.6B. Forbes puts the family's net worth at $9.6B (16 Sep 2026) and also credits it with about 44% of Dan Hotels. Elbit is Israel's largest weapons maker, producing 85% of the Israeli Air Force's drones and 85% of the army's land equipment; its Hermes 450 drone was used in the 2024 killing of seven World Central Kitchen aid workers in Gaza. Elbit's revenue reached $7.94B in 2025, and Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report calls it a pillar of Israel's military-industrial complex. The family's fortune rises with every contract for Israel's wars.","profile_src":["https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://www.forbes.com/profile/michael-federmann/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbit_Systems","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elbit_Systems","https://aoav.org.uk/2025/an-economy-of-genocide-un-special-rapporteur-names-global-corporations-enabling-israels-assault-on-gaza/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"LBL-DEFENSE-SYSTEM","name":"U.S. military spending","type":"Aggregate","role":"Aggregate: total US national-military outlays","country":null,"profile":"This node is not a single organisation. It stands for the total money the US government spends on its military, the federal budget category Treasury calls \"military\" (function 050). Treasury statements record $820.7B in FY2023, $874.0B in FY2024 and $916.6B in FY2025, plus $481.1B in the first half of FY2026, about $3.09T from October 2022 to March 2026. Most of that money becomes contracts for private weapons makers: the Pentagon obligated about $1.76T on contracts from FY2023 through the FY2026 data published so far. The aid packages and arms sales to Israel on this map are paid from this pool or from add-ons such as the April 2024 $26.38B Israel supplemental. The 2026 Iran war added about $38B by 1 August 2026. The label \"Military system\" is a euphemism; this map should call the node \"U.S. military spending\".","profile_src":["https://api.fiscaldata.treasury.gov/services/api/fiscal_service/v1/accounting/mts/mts_table_9?filter=classification_desc:eq:National%20Defense,record_calendar_month:eq:09&sort=-record_date&page[size]=10","https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/agency/097/obligations_by_award_category/?fiscal_year=2025","https://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/house-passes-series-security-supplemental-bills","https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2026-09/62756-Iran.pdf"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"LBL-PRIVATE-CONTRACTORS","name":"Pentagon contractors","type":"Aggregate","role":"Aggregate: companies paid under Pentagon contracts","country":null,"profile":"This node is not a single company. It stands for all private firms paid under US Department of Defense contracts, from Lockheed Martin, RTX, Boeing, General Dynamics and Northrop Grumman down to thousands of subcontractors. USAspending records Pentagon contract obligations of $456.9B in FY2023, $445.8B in FY2024 and $491.8B in FY2025, about $1.39T over three years and about $1.76T including FY2026 data published so far. The GAO confirms about $456B for FY2023. Much of this money ends up with shareholders such as BlackRock, Vanguard and State Street, which hold large stakes in the prime contractors. Contracts tied to Israel, such as Boeing's JDAM line, General Dynamics' bomb bodies and Lockheed's Hellfires, are a small but highly profitable part of the total. A clearer label is \"Pentagon contractors\".","profile_src":["https://api.usaspending.gov/api/v2/agency/097/obligations_by_award_category/?fiscal_year=2025","https://www.gao.gov/assets/gao-25-107558.pdf"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"LBL-REGIONAL-MILITARY-OPERATIONS","name":"US regional military operations 2023–25","type":"Aggregate","role":"Aggregate: cost of US regional operations Oct 2023–Sep 2025","country":null,"profile":"This node is not a single operation. It stands for the extra cost of US military operations across the Middle East launched in support of Israel after October 2023. These include naval and air deployments, strikes on the Houthis in Yemen and the Red Sea, and the interception of Iranian and allied missiles and drones aimed at Israel. Brown University's Costs of War project, citing Harvard economist Linda Bilmes, estimates these operations cost $9.65B–$12.07B from October 2023 to September 2025. This is on top of the $21.7B in direct military aid to Israel over the same period. The April 2024 Israel supplemental alone included $2.4B for \"current U.S. military operations in the region\". The 2026 war on Iran is recorded separately. A clearer label is \"US regional military operations 2023–25\".","profile_src":["https://costsofwar.watson.brown.edu/paper/WiderMiddleEastCosts","https://costsofwar.watson.brown.edu/paper/AidToIsrael","https://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/house-passes-series-security-supplemental-bills"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"LBL-GLOBAL-CUSTOMERS","name":"Foreign buyers of Israeli weapons","type":"Aggregate","role":"Aggregate: all foreign governments signing Israeli arms deals","country":null,"profile":"This node is not a single buyer. It stands for every foreign government that signs arms deals with Israel's weapons industry, as reported each year by the Israel Ministry of Defense's export agency SIBAT. Israel reported record export deals of $13.07B in 2023 and over $14.7B in 2024, with missile, rocket and interceptor systems making up 48% in 2024. Europe was the largest regional customer, at 54% of 2024 deals. The buyers fund the companies that arm Israel's military at home. The UN Special Rapporteur's July 2025 report says Israeli weapons are marketed as \"battle-proven\" after use in the occupation and repeated military campaigns. Customers on this map include Germany, Finland, Denmark, Slovakia and Greece. A clearer label is \"Foreign buyers of Israeli weapons\".","profile_src":["https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/for-the-third-consecutive-year-israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-13-billion-in-2023","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-147-billion-in-2024","https://www.un.org/unispal/document/a-hrc-59-23-from-economy-of-occupation-to-economy-of-genocide-report-special-rapporteur-francesca-albanese-palestine-2025/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"LBL-ISRAELI-DEFENSE-INDUSTRY","name":"Israeli arms industry","type":"Aggregate","role":"Aggregate: Israel's weapons makers (Elbit, IAI, Rafael and others)","country":null,"profile":"This node is not a single company. It stands for Israel's arms industry as a whole. Its core is the state-owned Israel Aerospace Industries (100% state) and Rafael (99.9% state), plus Elbit Systems, which is controlled by the Federmann family, and hundreds of smaller suppliers. These companies arm Israel's own military: Elbit's PULS rockets were used \"extensively\" in Gaza and Lebanon, and Arrow and David's Sling interceptors defend against Iranian missiles. They also sell abroad, with record export deals of $13.07B in 2023 and over $14.7B in 2024. The UN Special Rapporteur's July 2025 report says Elbit and IAI \"provide a critical domestic supply of weaponry\" and strengthen Israel's military alliances through exports. It also says their products are marketed as \"battle-proven\". The label \"arms industry\" is a euphemism; use \"Israeli arms industry\".","profile_src":["https://www.rafael.co.il/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Refael_ENGLISH120225MINA_All_compressed.pdf","https://www.iai.co.il/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/IAI-FS-CONSOLIDATED-AND-SOLO-12.21.pdf","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://defence-industry.eu/idf-employs-puls-rocket-artillery-system-during-ongoing-war/","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/for-the-third-consecutive-year-israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-13-billion-in-2023","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-147-billion-in-2024","https://www.un.org/unispal/document/a-hrc-59-23-from-economy-of-occupation-to-economy-of-genocide-report-special-rapporteur-francesca-albanese-palestine-2025/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"LBL-EUROPE","name":"European buyers of Israeli weapons","type":"Aggregate","role":"Aggregate: European governments' share of Israeli arms deals","country":null,"profile":"This node stands for the combined purchases by European governments from Israel's arms industry. Israel's Ministry of Defense reported that Europe made up 35% of its export deals in 2023 and 54% in 2024, the largest regional share, out of a record $14.7B. European NATO states buying Israeli systems in this period include Germany (Arrow 3, over $6.5B), Greece (\"Achilles Shield\", €3B), Slovakia (Barak MX, €560M), Finland (David's Sling, €317M), Denmark (ATMOS and PULS) and the Netherlands (PULS, $305M). Many of these deals were signed or expanded after the ICJ's 2024 provisional-measures orders, the ICC's November 2024 arrest warrants and the UN Commission of Inquiry's September 2025 genocide finding. The site's $19.48B figure for 2023–2025 is an estimate derived from rounded regional shares, so it should be shown as approximate. A clearer label is \"European buyers of Israeli weapons\".","profile_src":["https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-sets-new-record-in-defense-exports-over-147-billion-in-2024","https://www.timesofisrael.com/german-parliament-approves-3-5b-expansion-of-arrow-3-deal-with-israel/","https://defence-industry.eu/iai-signs-usd-3-1-billion-follow-on-contract-to-expand-germanys-arrow-3-missile-defence-programme/","https://www.mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-and-greece-have-signed-the-massive-achilles-shield-agreement","https://mod.gov.il/en/press-releases/press-room/israel-mod-seals-560-million-euro-agreement-barak-mx-integrated-air-defense-system-produced-by-iai-sold-to-slovakia-in-landmark-agreement","https://militarnyi.com/en/news/finland-signs-agreement-with-israel-to-purchase-david-s-sling-system/","https://www.forsvaret.dk/da/nyheder/2023/atmospulse/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-inks-first-of-its-kind-305-million-sale-of-artillery-systems-to-netherlands/","https://www.icj-cij.org/node/203447","https://www.npr.org/2024/11/21/g-s1-35169/icc-israel-hamas-arrest-warrants-gaza","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"LBL-ISRAEL-SECURITY-SUPPLEMENTAL-APPROPRIATI","name":"Israel Security Supplemental Appropriations Act, 2024","type":"Aggregate","role":"US war-funding law for Israel, $26.38B (April 2024)","country":null,"profile":"The Israel Security Supplemental Appropriations Act, 2024 is a law, not an organisation. It was the Israel part of the April 2024 security supplemental package and passed the House 366 to 58. It provided $26.38B. That included $4B to replenish Iron Dome and David's Sling, $1.2B for the Iron Beam laser, $3.5B in Foreign Military Financing for Israel to buy US weapons, $1B for artillery and munitions production, $4.4B to refill US stocks already sent to Israel, and $2.4B for US military operations in the region. It also banned funding for UNRWA, the main UN agency providing food and shelter to Palestinians, during the genocide in Gaza. The money flowed mostly to US and Israeli arms makers, including RTX and Rafael, which build David's Sling. It is a proper name, so the label can stay.","profile_src":["https://appropriations.house.gov/news/press-releases/house-passes-series-security-supplemental-bills"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"LBL-U-S-MILITARY-OPERATIONS-AGAINST-IRAN","name":"US war on Iran 2026 (Operation Epic Fury)","type":"Aggregate","role":"Aggregate: cost and toll of the US–Israeli war on Iran from 28 Feb 2026","country":null,"profile":"This node stands for the US war on Iran, which the Pentagon calls Operation Epic Fury. It began on 28 February 2026 with US air and cruise-missile strikes alongside Israel; on the first day a US Tomahawk hit the Shajareh Tayyebeh elementary school in Minab, killing about 156 civilians, 120 of them children. The Iranian rights group HRANA had verified at least 1,701 civilian deaths, including 254 children, by 7 April 2026; fighting resumed afterwards, so that figure is a dated minimum, not a final toll. The Congressional Budget Office estimated the war had cost the Department of Defense about $38B by 1 August 2026. Arms makers gained new orders, such as RTX's $20.7B AMRAAM contract in September 2026. Amnesty International found JDAM components after US-Israeli strikes on Tehran neighbourhoods that killed at least 41 civilians and said they may amount to war crimes.","profile_src":["https://www.cbo.gov/system/files/2026-09/62756-Iran.pdf","https://raytheon.mediaroom.com/2026-09-28-RTXs-Raytheon-awarded-20-7-billion-multi-year-contract-for-AMRAAM-under-landmark-production-agreement","https://www.amnesty.org.au/investigation-into-us-israeli-strikes-on-tehran-neighbourhoods-reveals-devastating-civilian-harm/","https://www.en-hrana.org/day-39-of-u-s-and-israeli-attacks-on-iran-extensive-damage-to-the-rail-network-and-roads/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Minab_school_attack"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-2026-APACHE","name":"Israel AH-64E Apache package – Jan 30 2026","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"FMS notified to Congress","country":"USA/Israel","slug":"israel-ah-64e-apache-package-jan-30-2026","profile":"On Jan 30, 2026 the U.S. notified Congress of a sale of 30 AH-64E Apache attack helicopters to Israel, estimated at $3.8B, with Boeing and Lockheed Martin as principal contractors.","profile_src":["https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4394583/israel-ah-64e-apache-helicopters"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-2026-APKWS","name":"Israel APKWS-II emergency sale – May 1 2026","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Emergency FMS (review waived)","country":"USA/Israel","slug":"israel-apkws-ii-emergency-sale-may-1-2026","profile":"On 1 May 2026, during Israel's war on Iran, the State Department used emergency powers to skip congressional review of a $992.4M sale to Israel of 10,000 APKWS-II laser-guided rockets. BAE Systems (Nashua, NH) is the principal contractor.","profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-2026-BLU110","name":"Israel BLU-110 bomb bodies emergency sale – Mar 2026","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Emergency FMS (review waived)","country":"USA/Israel","slug":"israel-blu-110-bomb-bodies-emergency-sale-mar-2026","profile":"In March 2026 the State Department waived congressional review on emergency grounds for a $151.8M sale to Israel of 12,000 BLU-110A/B 1,000-pound bomb bodies. Repkon USA, which runs the former General Dynamics Garland bomb-body plant, is the principal contractor; it renamed itself Paligen Technologies days later after a backlash. Emergency sales that month also included $298M for 5,000 small-diameter bombs and $209M for 10,000 500-pound bombs.","profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-2026-MK84","name":"Israel 2,000-lb bomb package – Sept 2026 (informal notification, on hold)","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Proposed FMF-funded Foreign Military Sale, held in Congress","country":"USA/Israel","slug":"israel-2-000-lb-bomb-package-sept-2026-informal-notification-on-hold","profile":"In September 2026 the Trump administration informally notified Congress of a proposed $2.8B sale to Israel of 40,000 2,000-pound bombs: 20,000 MK-84 general-purpose bombs and 20,000 BLU-117s, plus I-2000 penetrator warheads, mostly paid for with U.S. Foreign Military Financing. On 16 September 2026 Rep. Gregory Meeks, the top Democrat on the House Foreign Affairs Committee, officially announced a hold on the proposed sale, saying the administration had 'not provided sufficient assurances that these weapons will be used by the Netanyahu government in accordance with U.S. law'. These are the one-ton bombs that JDAM kits turn into guided weapons and that Bellingcat documented destroying high-rises in Gaza City in 2025. No contractor has been named; General Dynamics made the bomb bodies in the comparable February 2025 sale.","profile_src":["https://democrats-foreignaffairs.house.gov/press-releases?ContentRecord_id=2AC6AE1D-BDCD-4E19-B8A7-BCA59F204151","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/16/trump-administration-plans-2-8bn-sale-of-2000-pound-bombs-to-israel","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-NEW-BLU110-2026","name":"Israel emergency bomb-body sale – Mar 2026","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Emergency FMS bypassing Congress","country":"USA/Israel","slug":"israel-emergency-bomb-body-sale-mar-2026","profile":"On March 7, 2026, during the Iran war, the U.S. used an emergency declaration to approve a $151.8M sale of 12,000 BLU-110 1,000-lb bomb bodies to Israel without congressional review. Turkish-owned REPKON USA is prime contractor.","profile_src":["https://www.airforce-technology.com/news/us-state-department-israel-arms/","https://www.ynetnews.com/article/bkmojptkzx"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-NEW-F35","name":"F-35 Lightning II (F-35I Adir)","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Stealth combat aircraft","country":"USA","slug":"f-35-lightning-ii-f-35i-adir","profile":"The F-35 is built by Lockheed Martin with Northrop Grumman, BAE Systems and Pratt & Whitney (RTX). According to the UN Special Rapporteur, F-35s and F-16s were integral to Israel dropping an estimated 85,000 tons of bombs on Gaza. Israeli F-35Is struck Iran in June 2025 and from Feb 28, 2026.","profile_src":["https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://defence-industry.eu/israeli-air-force-deploys-f-35i-adir-fighter-fleet-in-operation-roaring-lion-amid-pngoing-strikes-on-targets-in-iran/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-NEW-TOMAHAWK","name":"Tomahawk cruise missile","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Cruise missile","country":"USA","slug":"tomahawk-cruise-missile","profile":"The Tomahawk is Raytheon's (RTX) long-range cruise missile. A U.S. Tomahawk struck the Shajareh Tayyebeh elementary school in Minab, Iran on Feb 28, 2026, killing 156 to 168 people, most of them children.","profile_src":["https://www.rtx.com/raytheon/what-we-do/sea/tomahawk-cruise-missile","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Minab_school_attack","https://www.trtworld.com/article/6112ba851a95"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-NEW-R2S","name":"R2S (Raytheon-Rafael Protection Systems)","type":"Company","role":"RTX–Rafael joint venture; builds Iron Dome interceptors in Arkansas","country":"USA/Israel","slug":"r2s-raytheon-rafael-protection-systems","profile":"R2S is the joint venture of RTX's Raytheon and Israel's state-owned Rafael, and it is how Israel's missile shield came to be manufactured in Arkansas. In November 2025 it won a $1.25B contract from the Israel Missile Defense Organization to supply Israel with Tamir interceptors, to be built in Camden, Arkansas. RTX says the partners had used a $33M capital investment to set up the plant, which was established to support the Israel Missile Defense Organization inside Israel's Ministry of Defense. The arrangement lets Israel keep firing on Gaza, Lebanon and Iran while US industry refills the interceptors it burns through. This node duplicates COM-R2S, which carries the fuller record.","profile_src":["https://www.rtx.com/news/news-center/2025/11/21/r2s-receives-1-25-billion-tamir-production-contract-for-facility-in-camden-arka","https://www.boozman.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/2024/2/boozman-joins-gov-sanders-and-local-leaders-to-break-ground-on-new-defense-industry-manufacturing-facility-in-south-arkansas","https://www.rtx.com/news/news-center/2025/11/21/r2s-receives-1-25-billion-tamir-production-contract-for-facility-in-camden-arka","https://www.rtx.com/news/news-center/2025/11/21/r2s-receives-1-25-billion-tamir-production-contract-for-facility-in-camden-arka"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"GOV-NEW-ICE","name":"U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE)","type":"Government","role":"Immigration enforcement agency; Palantir's ImmigrationOS client","country":"USA","slug":"u-s-immigration-and-customs-enforcement-ice","profile":"U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) is the U.S. deportation agency, and it buys its tools from the same company that partnered with Israel's military. In April 2025 ICE granted a $30M contract to longtime contractor Palantir Technologies to build 'ImmigrationOS', a surveillance platform, as a modification of an earlier Palantir contract in support of presidential executive orders including EO 14159. According to the contract justification, ImmigrationOS is meant to streamline the identification and apprehension of people prioritized for removal, to track 'self-deportations' with 'near real-time visibility' and to make deportation logistics more efficient; Palantir was expected to deliver a prototype by September 2025. In January 2024 the same Palantir agreed a strategic partnership with the Israel Ministry of Defense to supply technology to help the country's war effort. The software is the same species in both places: a machine for deciding who gets removed.","profile_src":["https://immpolicytracking.org/policies/reported-palantir-awarded-30-million-to-build-immigrationos-surveillance-platform-for-ice/","https://www.palantir.com/assets/xrfr7uokpv1b/3MuEeA8MLbLDAyxixTsiIe/9e4a11a7fb058554a8a1e3cd83e31c09/C134184_finaleprint.pdf","https://immpolicytracking.org/policies/reported-palantir-awarded-30-million-to-build-immigrationos-surveillance-platform-for-ice/"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"GOV-NEW-UNIT8200","name":"Unit 8200","type":"Government","role":"Israeli signals-intelligence unit; stored Palestinians' calls on Microsoft Azure","country":"Israel","slug":"unit-8200","profile":"Unit 8200 is the Israeli military's signals intelligence unit and the collection engine of the AI kill chain. A joint investigation by The Guardian, +972 Magazine and Local Call found it stored intercepted Palestinian phone calls on Microsoft's Azure cloud, aiming for 'a million calls an hour', after its commander Yossi Sariel met Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella in November 2021. By 2025 about 11,500 terabytes sat in a Microsoft data center in the Netherlands. Sources said the data was used to plan lethal airstrikes in Gaza and to arrest Palestinians in the West Bank. In September 2025 Microsoft disabled some of the services; the unit planned to move the data to Amazon Web Services, shopping for a landlord with fewer questions. The same reporters revealed in March 2025 that it was building a ChatGPT-like model trained on 100 billion words of Arabic drawn partly from surveillance of Palestinians. Al Jazeera reports Palantir has actively recruited its veterans.","profile_src":["https://www.972mag.com/microsoft-cloud-israel-8200-expose/","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/8/7/microsoft-cloud-used-in-israeli-mass-surveillance-of-palestinians-report","https://blogs.microsoft.com/on-the-issues/2025/09/25/update-on-ongoing-microsoft-review/","https://www.972mag.com/israeli-intelligence-chatgpt-8200-surveillance-ai/","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/17/blood-tech-the-uk-ambassador-the-sex-offender-palantir-and-gaza"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"COM-NEW-TIKTOKUSDS","name":"TikTok USDS","type":"Company","role":"US TikTok joint venture; 15% owned by Israel-allied Oracle","country":"USA","slug":"tiktok-usds","profile":"TikTok USDS is the U.S. TikTok joint venture set up in Jan 2026, in which Oracle, MGX and Silver Lake each hold 15%. Its significance on this map is who now holds a key to the platform. Oracle, according to Who Profits, develops and provides software and services through its Israeli subsidiary to the Israel Ministry of Defense and the Israeli military, and The Intercept reports it has worked with the state weapons maker Rafael on cloud-based AI. Its founder Larry Ellison once offered Benjamin Netanyahu a seat on Oracle's board, The Intercept reported, and its then-CEO Safra Catz told staff in November 2024: 'if you're not for America or Israel, don't work here'. Those are now the people with a stake in the app's U.S. operations.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TikTok_USDS","https://www.whoprofits.org/companies/company/7396?oracle=","https://theintercept.com/2025/02/18/oracle-tiktok-israel-palestine-gaza/","https://theintercept.com/2025/02/18/oracle-tiktok-israel-palestine-gaza/","https://theintercept.com/2025/02/18/oracle-tiktok-israel-palestine-gaza/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-NEW-DAVIDELLISON","name":"David Ellison","type":"Person","role":"Paramount Skydance chief; Larry Ellison's son, now buying Warner Bros.","country":"USA","slug":"david-ellison","profile":"David Ellison, son of Oracle co-founder Larry Ellison, controls Paramount Skydance. Its $110B merger with Warner Bros. Discovery was approved by WBD shareholders in April 2026, with foreign financing partly from Saudi and Qatari funds, NPR reported; the deal would hand the Ellison family the Warner Bros. studio and cable channels including CNN and HBO. NPR also reported that critics in Hollywood say the merger gives too much power to an Ellison family that is friendly with President Trump, and that David Ellison planned an invitation-only dinner in Washington to honor Trump. The family's politics are on record: his father gave $16.6M to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces in 2017, the largest single gift in its history, and once offered Benjamin Netanyahu a seat on Oracle's board, The Intercept reported. A newsroom changes hands; the newsroom's owners do not change sides.","profile_src":["https://www.npr.org/2026/04/23/nx-s1-5793628/warner-bros-discovery-paramount-skydance-merger","https://www.jta.org/2017/11/05/united-states/record-53-8-million-raised-for-idf-soldiers-at-beverly-hills-gala","https://theintercept.com/2025/02/18/oracle-tiktok-israel-palestine-gaza/","https://www.npr.org/2026/04/23/nx-s1-5793628/warner-bros-discovery-paramount-skydance-merger"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-NEW-PARAMOUNT","name":"Paramount Skydance","type":"Company","role":"Media conglomerate controlled by the Ellisons; absorbing Warner Bros. and CNN","country":"USA","slug":"paramount-skydance","profile":"Paramount Skydance is the media conglomerate controlled by David Ellison, son of Oracle co-founder Larry Ellison. It agreed a $110B merger with Warner Bros. Discovery, approved by WBD shareholders in April 2026, which would bring the Warner Bros. studio and cable channels including CNN and HBO under Ellison control; NPR reported the foreign financing was partly sourced from Saudi Arabia and Qatar, and that the deal still faces regulatory review in the United States and Europe, with California's attorney general investigating it for antitrust violations. Critics in Hollywood, NPR reported, say the merger gives too much power to a family that is friendly with President Trump. That family's patriarch gave $16.6M to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces in 2017, the largest single gift in its history. Who owns the news decides whose dead are counted.","profile_src":["https://www.npr.org/2026/04/23/nx-s1-5793628/warner-bros-discovery-paramount-skydance-merger","https://www.jta.org/2017/11/05/united-states/record-53-8-million-raised-for-idf-soldiers-at-beverly-hills-gala","https://www.npr.org/2026/04/23/nx-s1-5793628/warner-bros-discovery-paramount-skydance-merger"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-NEW-WIZ","name":"Wiz","type":"Company","role":"Israeli cybersecurity firm bought by Google for $32B","country":"Israel/USA","slug":"wiz","profile":"Wiz is the Israeli cybersecurity firm that Google bought outright: Google completed its $32B cash acquisition on March 11, 2026, and Wiz joined Google Cloud. That makes Wiz part of the division that, with Amazon, holds Project Nimbus, the $1.2B contract under which Israel buys government and military cloud services from Alphabet and Amazon. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report says Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon grant Israel 'virtually government-wide access' to their cloud and AI technologies. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. Six months later, Google paid $32B in cash for an Israeli tech champion and folded it into the very division that serves Israel's military.","profile_src":["https://techcrunch.com/2026/03/11/google-completes-32b-acquisition-of-wiz/","https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/inside-google-cloud/google-cloud-selected-to-provide-cloud-services-to-the-state-of-israel","https://www.un.org/unispal/document/a-hrc-59-23-from-economy-of-occupation-to-economy-of-genocide-report-special-rapporteur-francesca-albanese-palestine-2025/","https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/google-aws-win-12-billion-israel-nimbus-tender-for-cloud-services/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-NEW-DANHOTELS","name":"Dan Hotels","type":"Company","role":"Luxury hotel chain controlled by Elbit's owners, the Federmanns","country":"Israel","slug":"dan-hotels","profile":"Dan Hotels is a listed Israeli luxury hotel operator and, alongside Elbit Systems, one of the two biggest publicly traded holdings of Federmann Enterprises, the family conglomerate owned since 2002 by Michael Federmann and started by his father and uncle. The same holding company held 19,318,508 Elbit shares as of June 17, 2026, and Michael Federmann controls the vote of about 41.2% of Elbit; he and his sons David, Gideon and Daniel hold an indirect economic interest in it. Elbit's revenue reached about $7.94B in 2025, and its PULS rocket artillery has been used extensively by Israel's army in Gaza and Lebanon. The family that sells the rockets also sells the rooms: Dan Hotels is the hospitality face of an arms fortune.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Federmann","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1027664/000102766426000021/elbit-2026agmproxystatement.htm","https://www.elbitsystems.com/news/elbit-systems-reports-fourth-quarter-and-full-year-2025-results","https://elbitsystems.com/pr-new/elbit-systems-awarded-two-contracts-in-an-aggregate-amount-of-252-million-to-supply-atmos-and-puls-artillery-systems-to-a-nato-member-country/","https://defence-industry.eu/idf-employs-puls-rocket-artillery-system-during-ongoing-war/","https://www.elbitsystems.com/land/weapons-systems-and-munitions/launchers/puls"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-N-TRUMP","name":"Donald Trump","type":"Person","role":"US president; armed Israel, launched the Iran war, sanctioned the ICC","country":"USA","slug":"donald-trump","profile":"Donald Trump returned to the presidency in January 2025, approved billions of dollars in bombs, guidance kits and fuzes for Israel within weeks, and on 27 February 2026 authorized the US–Israeli war on Iran. In February 2025, after the International Criminal Court issued an arrest warrant for Benjamin Netanyahu, he signed Executive Order 14203 sanctioning ICC personnel with asset freezes and travel bans, punishing the court rather than the accused. His market-moving announcements have repeatedly coincided with unusually well-timed trades. In April 2025 he posted 'THIS IS A GREAT TIME TO BUY!!!' hours before pausing tariffs, triggering a 9.5% S&P 500 rally; Reuters found bullish options trades placed minutes beforehand that could have generated tens of millions in gains. ProPublica later identified more than a dozen administration officials and aides making well-timed trades around tariff announcements. In March 2026 the FT found $580M in oil futures trades placed shortly before Trump announced purported Iran talks. These episodes prompted calls for investigations, but no public evidence has established that Trump personally tipped traders or directed illegal trades.","profile_src":["https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088258/israel-munitions-and-munitions-support","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/trump-told-investors-to-buy-on-social-media-hours-before-his-tariff-pause-rose-stocks-raising-questions-about-manipulation","https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/welltimed-options-trades-ahead-of-trumps-tariff-pause-draw-questions-3980430","https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/well-timed-options-trades-ahead-trumps-tariff-pause-draw-questions-2025-04-10/","https://www.propublica.org/article/us-officials-stock-sales-trump-tariffs","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economic_impact_of_the_2026_Iran_war","https://ca.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/factboxsome-trades-ahead-of-trump-policy-moves-raise-questions-4538711","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Criminal_Court_arrest_warrants_for_Israeli_leaders"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","name":"Benjamin Netanyahu","type":"Person","role":"Prime minister; ICC-wanted, named by UN inquiry for inciting genocide","country":"Israel","slug":"benjamin-netanyahu","profile":"Benjamin \"Bibi\" Netanyahu, also known as \"Satanyahu,\" is the ninth and longest-serving prime minister of the imaginary state of Israel, i.e. occupied Palestine. Bibi is one of the chief architects of Israel's apartheid regime, the genocide in Gaza, the ongoing annexation of the West Bank and the campaign of annihilation against South Lebanon. Since October 2023, he has directed Israel's wars on Gaza and Lebanon and helped drag the region into war with Iran, a country he has been publicly threatening since at least the 1990s. In November 2024, the ICC issued an arrest warrant for him over alleged war crimes and crimes against humanity in Gaza, including starvation as a method of warfare, murder and persecution. In September 2025, a UN Commission of Inquiry concluded that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza and found that Netanyahu, Isaac Herzog and Yoav Gallant had incited it. He ordered Israel's invasion of Lebanon in October 2024, presided over the June 2025 strikes that began the Twelve-Day War with Iran, and spent the following months lobbying Donald Trump for an even bigger one. When he is not bombing neighbouring countries, Bibi is also a criminal defendant at home: he has been under indictment for bribery, fraud and breach of trust since 2019. Somewhere along the way, billionaire Oracle founder Larry Ellison reportedly offered him a seat on Oracle's board worth roughly half a million dollars per year.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Criminal_Court_arrest_warrants_for_Israeli_leaders","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin_Netanyahu","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war","https://theintercept.com/2025/02/18/oracle-tiktok-israel-palestine-gaza/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-N-BOWMAN","name":"Jamaal Bowman","type":"Person","role":"Former U.S. Representative, New York 16th District (UDP-opposed, lost 2024)","country":"USA","slug":"jamaal-bowman","profile":"Jamaal Bowman, a member of the progressive 'Squad' and a frequent critic of US support for Israel's genocide in Gaza, was challenged in the June 2024 Democratic primary for New York's 16th District by Westchester County Executive George Latimer. The United Democracy Project, AIPAC's super PAC, spent almost $9.9M opposing Bowman and nearly $4.8M supporting Latimer, according to FactCheck.org's review of FEC filings, making it the most expensive House primary in US history. Latimer won 58.6% to 41.4%, and Bowman became the first Squad member to lose a primary. In February 2025 he launched Built to Win PAC to back progressive candidates, including against politicians who support Benjamin Netanyahu. His defeat is the clearest case of AIPAC money removing a critic of the war from Congress.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2024/09/united-democracy-project-2/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamaal_Bowman","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamaal_Bowman"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-N-BUSH","name":"Cori Bush","type":"Person","role":"Former U.S. Representative, Missouri 1st District (UDP-opposed, lost 2024 and 2026)","country":"USA","slug":"cori-bush","profile":"Cori Bush represented Missouri's 1st District and on 16 October 2023 introduced a House resolution calling for a ceasefire in Gaza. The United Democracy Project, AIPAC's super PAC, then targeted her: FactCheck.org's review of FEC filings found it spent more than $5.2M against Bush and $3.3M backing St. Louis County prosecutor Wesley Bell, about $8.5M in all; Wikipedia puts spending against her at $9M, the second most expensive House primary in history. Bush lost the 6 August 2024 primary to Bell. In October 2025 she announced a comeback, but lost the 2026 Democratic primary rematch to Bell by a wider margin, 36.9% to 59.2%. Her two defeats show how AIPAC money punished an early call to stop the killing in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2024/09/united-democracy-project-2/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cori_Bush","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cori_Bush"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-N-RAMJI","name":"Salim Ramji","type":"Person","role":"Vanguard CEO; top-five owner of every major US arms maker","country":"USA","slug":"salim-ramji","profile":"Salim Ramji, a BlackRock veteran, became CEO of Vanguard in July 2024, moving from the largest index giant to the second. Vanguard manages roughly $13T and, under its mutual structure, is owned by its funds and so its customers; as a private firm it does not publish his pay. As of 31 March 2026 Vanguard held 7.45% of Boeing, 7.47% of RTX, 7.22% of Northrop Grumman, 6.99% of Lockheed Martin and 6.88% of General Dynamics, according to SEC 13G filings. Francesca Albanese's July 2025 UN report names Vanguard the largest institutional investor in Caterpillar, Chevron and Palantir (9.1%) and, with BlackRock, among the largest investors in companies it ties to Israel's occupation and genocide in Gaza, including Lockheed Martin and Elbit Systems. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza; Vanguard's 2026 filings show it still among the top owners of the US arms makers supplying it.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Vanguard_Group","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000012927/000210011926000249/xslSCHEDULE_13G_X02/primary_doc.xml","https://www.secform4.com/13dg/2100119/0002100119-26-001059.html","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0000936468/000210011926000760/xslSCHEDULE_13G_X02/primary_doc.xml","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-N-LATIMER","name":"George Latimer","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, New York 16th District (UDP-backed)","country":"USA","slug":"george-latimer","profile":"George Latimer, Westchester County Executive, challenged Representative Jamaal Bowman in the June 2024 Democratic primary for New York's 16th District with heavy backing from AIPAC. The United Democracy Project, AIPAC's super PAC, spent nearly $4.8M supporting Latimer and almost $9.9M opposing Bowman, according to FactCheck.org's review of FEC filings, in what became the most expensive House primary in US history. Latimer won 58.6% to 41.4% and entered Congress in January 2025, replacing one of the House's most outspoken critics of US support for Israel's genocide in Gaza. Wikipedia puts total AIPAC-linked outside spending benefiting him at $15M.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2024/09/united-democracy-project-2/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamaal_Bowman","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamaal_Bowman"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-N-BELL","name":"Wesley Bell","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, Missouri 1st District (UDP-backed)","country":"USA","slug":"wesley-bell","profile":"Wesley Bell, then St. Louis County's prosecuting attorney, defeated Representative Cori Bush in the 6 August 2024 Democratic primary for Missouri's 1st District. The United Democracy Project, AIPAC's super PAC, spent $3.3M backing Bell and more than $5.2M against Bush, according to FactCheck.org's review of FEC filings; Wikipedia counts $9M spent against Bush, the second most expensive House primary in history. Bush had introduced a Gaza ceasefire resolution in October 2023. Bell entered Congress in January 2025 and beat Bush again in the 2026 primary rematch, 59.2% to 36.9%, keeping the seat in the hands of a candidate AIPAC's money helped elect.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2024/09/united-democracy-project-2/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cori_Bush","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cori_Bush"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00002","name":"United States","type":"Country","role":"Largest military spender and main arms supplier to Israel","country":"United States","slug":"united-states","profile":"The United States is the single largest military power on earth and the indispensable armourer of Israel's wars on Gaza, Lebanon and Iran. Treasury data show military outlays (the budget's 'National Defense' function) rising from $591B in FY2015 to $917B in FY2025, with $876B already spent in the first eleven months of FY2026; SIPRI counts $954B in 2025, a third of world military spending. The US supplied 68% of Israel's major arms imports in 2021–25. The Costs of War Project at Brown University counts at least $21.7B in US military aid to Israel from October 2023 to September 2025, and the Congressional Research Service puts total aid since 1946 at $298B in 2024 dollars. Since January 2025 Washington has notified Apache helicopters, bombs and guidance kits, using emergency waivers to bypass Congress, even after the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide and urged states to halt arms transfers.","profile_src":["https://api.fiscaldata.treasury.gov/services/api/fiscal_service/v1/accounting/mts/mts_table_9?filter=record_calendar_month:eq:09,classification_desc:eq:National%20Defense","https://api.fiscaldata.treasury.gov/services/api/fiscal_service/v1/accounting/mts/mts_table_9?filter=record_fiscal_year:eq:2026,classification_desc:eq:National%20Defense","https://www.sipri.org/sites/default/files/2026-04/2604_milex_2025.pdf","https://www.sipri.org/sites/default/files/2026-03/fs_2603_at_2025.pdf","https://costsofwar.watson.brown.edu/sites/default/files/2025-10/Hartung_US_Military_Aid_to_Israel_Oct.20.pdf","https://www.everycrsreport.com/reports/RL33222.html","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4394583/israel-ah-64e-apache-helicopters","https://www.timesofisrael.com/us-bypasses-congressional-review-to-approve-munitions-sale-to-israel/","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"COM-R2S","name":"Raytheon Rafael Area Protection Systems (R2S)","type":"Company","role":"RTX–Rafael joint venture; Iron Dome interceptors made in Arkansas","country":"United States","slug":"raytheon-rafael-area-protection-systems-r2s","profile":"Raytheon Rafael Area Protection Systems, known as R2S, is a joint venture between RTX's Raytheon and Israel's state-owned Rafael Advanced Defense Systems that manufactures Tamir interceptors for Iron Dome and its US variant, SkyHunter, in East Camden, Arkansas. Ground was broken on February 21, 2024, months into the bombardment of Gaza, with Senator John Boozman and Governor Sarah Huckabee Sanders holding the shovels; the partners said the capital investment would rise from $33M to $63M and create 60 jobs. On November 21, 2025 RTX announced that R2S had won a $1.25B Tamir production contract supporting the Israel Missile Defense Organization's push to accelerate serial production. The plant moves part of Israel's missile shield onto US soil, letting Israel keep firing on Gaza, Lebanon and Iran while US industry replenishes the interceptors it burns through, in the period the UN Commission of Inquiry found Israel committed genocide.","profile_src":["https://www.rtx.com/news/news-center/2025/11/21/r2s-receives-1-25-billion-tamir-production-contract-for-facility-in-camden-arka","https://www.boozman.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/2024/2/boozman-joins-gov-sanders-and-local-leaders-to-break-ground-on-new-defense-industry-manufacturing-facility-in-south-arkansas","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00003","name":"Germany","type":"Country","role":"Israel's second-largest arms supplier and major buyer of Israeli weapons","country":"Germany","slug":"germany","profile":"Germany is Israel's second-largest arms supplier, accounting for 31% of its major arms imports in 2021–25 according to SIPRI. Forensis, the research arm of Forensic Architecture, counts German licences worth €326.5M in 2023, €163.8M in 2024, €201.6M in 2025 and €799.3M in the first half of 2026 alone, about €1.41B since October 2023, covering Merkava and Eitan engines, a Dolphin-class submarine and 500,000 rounds of small-arms ammunition. Chancellor Friedrich Merz's partial halt on items usable in Gaza lasted only from August 8 to November 24, 2025. At the ICJ, Nicaragua accuses Berlin of complicity in genocide; the court declined provisional measures in April 2024 but kept the case. Germany is also a top customer of Israeli industry: the Arrow 3 deal now exceeds $6.5B and a €2B Spike missile contract was signed with Rafael-led EuroSpike in October 2025.","profile_src":["https://www.sipri.org/sites/default/files/2026-03/fs_2603_at_2025.pdf","https://content.forensic-architecture.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Forensis-Report-Addendum-German-Arms-Exports-to-Israel-2023-2026-1.pdf","https://content.forensic-architecture.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Forensis-Report-Addendum-German-Arms-Exports-to-Israel-2023-2026-1.pdf","https://en.yenisafak.com/world/germany-approves-930m-arms-exports-to-israel-3722689","https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/germany-asks-icj-dismiss-nicaragua-genocide-case-over-arms-supplies-israel","https://thedefensepost.com/2025/10/24/germany-spike-missiles-nato-israel/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00004","name":"Italy","type":"Country","role":"Arms exporter to Israel; home of Leonardo","country":"Italy","slug":"italy","profile":"Italy's government claimed in 2023 and again in October 2024 that shipments of weapons to Israel were blocked, but official figures tell a different story. In the EU's annual arms-export report, Italy declared €9.96M in military-export licences for Israel in 2023 and €16.21M in actual arms exports, deliveries running ahead of new licences. ISTAT foreign-trade data reviewed by The New Arab show €817,536 of 'weapons and ammunition' exported to Israel in October and November 2023 alone, and Il Fatto Quotidiano, citing ISTAT, reported about €5.8M of arms, ammunition and parts in 2024. Italy is home to Leonardo, whose naval guns arm Israel's warships; Leonardo says its F-35 work at Cameri is not destined for Israel. The UN Commission of Inquiry in September 2025 found that Israel committed genocide in Gaza and urged all states to stop arms transfers that may be used in genocidal acts; Rome's partial, opaque restrictions have not ended the flow of parts and ammunition.","profile_src":["https://www.newarab.com/investigations/italy-sent-israel-arms-during-gaza-war-contrary-denials","https://www.ilfattoquotidiano.it/2025/06/05/armi-italiane-israele-esportazioni-segrete-governo-meloni-ultime-notizie/8015461/","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.parlament.gv.at/dokument/XXVIII/EU/6974/imfname_11440265.pdf","https://www.leonardo.com/documents/15646808/31894715/File%2Bunico%2Bdomande%2Bpreassembleari.pdf?t=1777902622687"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00005","name":"United Kingdom","type":"Country","role":"F-35 component supplier to Israel","country":"United Kingdom","slug":"united-kingdom","profile":"The United Kingdom suspended only 30 of roughly 350 arms export licences to Israel in September 2024 and explicitly carved out F-35 components, even though British industry makes about 15% of every F-35, the jet Israel uses to bomb Gaza. CAAT found the UK approved £127.6M of single-issue licences for military equipment to Israel between October and December 2024, more than in 2020–2023 combined. Palestinian rights group Al-Haq challenged the F-35 exemption, but the High Court dismissed the case on June 30, 2025, leaving in place exports of components 'which could not be identified as destined for Israel'. BAE Systems, Britain's largest weapons manufacturer, is a principal F-35 partner. The UN Commission of Inquiry's September 2025 genocide finding and call to halt arms transfers has not changed the F-35 carve-out.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arms_embargoes_on_Israel_since_2023","https://caat.org.uk/news/new-figures-reveal-massive-increase-in-uk-arms-exports-to-israel-as-government-defends-f-35-exemption-in-court/","https://caselaw.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ewhc/admin/2025/1615","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00006","name":"France","type":"Country","role":"EU's top licensor of arms exports to Israel in 2024","country":"France","slug":"france","profile":"France granted the highest value of arms export licences to Israel of any EU state in 2024, about €362M according to EU data reported by EUobserver; the French Ministry of the Armed Forces' own report, obtained by Mediapart, shows the authorised amount more than doubled from €176.2M in 2023 to €387.8M in 2024, while Israeli orders hit €27.1M, the highest since 2017, and deliveries reached €16.1M. Investigative outlet Disclose revealed that Marseille-based Eurolinks shipped machine-gun links to Israel Military Industries, including one million M27 links in May 2025, believed compatible with the Negev 5 machine gun used by Israeli forces in Gaza. Paris insists the parts are for re-export, but has published no end-use verification. These licences continued while the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded Israel committed genocide.","profile_src":["https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/","https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/israeli-orders-french-arms-experienced-record-year-2024","https://disclose.ngo/en/article/france-to-deliver-equipment-for-machine-guns-in-israel","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00007","name":"Netherlands","type":"Country","role":"F-35 parts hub halted by court; buyer of Israeli rockets","country":"Netherlands","slug":"netherlands","profile":"The Netherlands hosts a European warehouse for US-owned F-35 spare parts. On February 12, 2024 the Hague Court of Appeal, in a case brought by Oxfam Novib and other groups, ordered the state to stop exporting F-35 parts to Israel because of a clear risk of serious violations of humanitarian law. The Supreme Court on October 3, 2025 scrapped the ban but ordered the minister to reassess within six weeks; the cabinet kept shipments halted in November 2025, saying a final decision would follow within six months. At the same time the Dutch state remains a customer of Israel's arms industry: in May 2023 it signed a $305M government-to-government deal for 20 Elbit PULS rocket artillery systems. EU data show Dutch licences to Israel of €1M or less in 2024.","profile_src":["https://nltimes.nl/2025/10/03/supreme-court-scraps-ban-exporting-f-35-parts-israel-orders-govt-reassess","https://nltimes.nl/2025/11/14/cabinet-delays-resumption-f-35-parts-deliveries-israel-pending-review","https://www.prnewswire.com/il/news-releases/elbit-systems-awarded-305-million-contract-to-supply-puls-rocket-artillery-systems-to-the-royal-netherlands-army-301828210.html","https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00008","name":"Spain","type":"Country","role":"Only EU state with a statutory arms embargo on Israel","country":"Spain","slug":"spain","profile":"Spain is the clearest European exception. Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez announced a total arms embargo in September 2025, and on October 8, 2025 parliament ratified it 178 to 169, banning exports and imports of military equipment to and from Israel and the transit of aviation fuel with military use, but allowing exceptions for dual-use goods when national interests are at stake. Madrid cancelled a nearly €700M contract for 12 SILAM rocket launchers derived from Elbit's PULS, of which Elbit would have received €150M. Yet Spain later switched a €285M deal for 1,680 Spike missiles to EuroSpike, the German company in which Rafael holds 20%. AOAV counts €99M of Spanish licences to Israel in 2014–2022, including ammunition and explosives.","profile_src":["https://www.timesofisrael.com/spanish-parliament-approves-arms-embargo-on-israel/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/spain-cancels-major-arms-deal-with-israel-amid-gaza-backlash/","https://www.jpost.com/defense-and-tech/article-886905","https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00009","name":"Czechia","type":"Country","role":"Supplier of body armour to Israel and buyer of SPYDER","country":"Czechia","slug":"czechia","profile":"Czechia has been one of Israel's most loyal partners in Europe. Within days of October 7, 2023, Czech industry rushed about 3,000 ballistic armour plates and vests to Israel, and EU data show Prague granted €35M of arms export licences to Israel in 2024. AOAV counts more than €127M of Czech licences in 2014–2022, including ammunition, armoured vehicles and small arms. Czechia is also a buyer of Israeli weapons: its 13.69 billion koruna ($627M) contract for four Rafael SPYDER launchers is due to be delivered by 2026, worth about $1B over 20 years with support. Prague has announced no suspension of licences despite the UN Commission of Inquiry's September 2025 finding of genocide and call on states to stop arms transfers.","profile_src":["https://www.yahoo.com/news/actions-not-words-three-european-224215466.html","https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/","https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/","https://www.defensenews.com/global/europe/2021/09/28/czech-republic-buys-israeli-spyder-air-defense-weapon-for-627-million/","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00010","name":"Romania","type":"Country","role":"Major licensor to Israel and multi-billion buyer of Israeli systems","country":"Romania","slug":"romania","profile":"Romania is one of the largest European licensors of arms exports to Israel: EU data show €103M in 2024, following €106M in 2022, and AOAV counts €427M in 2014–2022, the highest of any country it surveyed. Bucharest has also become a leading buyer of Israeli weapons. In July 2025 its Ministry of Military announced a framework agreement worth more than €2B ($2.3B) with Rafael for SPYDER anti-aircraft systems, and Romania Insider reports a $400M deal with Elbit for seven Watchkeeper X drone systems. A nationwide campaign against Elbit launched in Romania in 2025. No suspension of licences has been announced, despite the UN Commission of Inquiry's call in September 2025 for states to cease arms transfers to Israel.","profile_src":["https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/","https://aoav.org.uk/2025/is-europe-turning-its-back-on-arming-israel/","https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/romania-on-edge-over-russia-to-buy-israeli-anti-aircraft-system-for-2-3-billion/","https://www.romania-insider.com/romania-acquires-israeli-surveillance-drones-nov-2025","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00011","name":"Belgium","type":"Country","role":"De facto embargo undermined by transit through its ports and airports","country":"Belgium","slug":"belgium","profile":"Belgium has kept a de facto embargo on arms exports to Israel since 2009, and the Walloon government suspended licences for explosive powder in 2024 and banned arms transit through Liège and Charleroi airports. But its ports and airports remain transit routes. On July 17, 2025 a Brussels court, ruling on a case brought by 11.11.11, Vredeactie, Intal and the League for Human Rights, blocked a container of Merkava tank and Namer armoured vehicle components from leaving Antwerp and set €50,000 fines for future shipments. In June 2026 Amnesty joined a criminal complaint against FedEx Belgium for moving an ITAR-controlled shipment in October 2024 from Hill Air Force Base in Utah via Liège to Nevatim airbase, home of Israel's F-35s, without a transit licence. AOAV counts €46M of Belgian transfers in 2014–2022.","profile_src":["https://aoav.org.uk/2025/is-europe-turning-its-back-on-arming-israel/","https://www.amnestyusa.org/press-releases/belgium-amnesty-international-joins-complaint-against-fedex-for-unlawful-arms-transit-to-israel/","https://euobserver.com/27716/major-eu-port-ordered-to-stop-arms-shipments-to-israel/","https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00012","name":"Poland","type":"Country","role":"Licence producer of Rafael's Spike missiles","country":"Poland","slug":"poland","profile":"Poland's coalition government said in August 2024 that it had ceased supplying lethal weapons to Israel, and EU data show Polish licences to Israel of €1M or less in 2024. AOAV counts just under €4.9M of Polish licences in 2014–2022, more than €2M of it explosive devices. Poland's deeper tie is as a customer and licence producer for Israeli industry: in August 2023 Rafael announced a contract worth nearly $100M for state-owned Mesko to make hundreds more Spike anti-tank missiles, Poland's third Spike order, in a partnership running since 2003. With SIPRI recording that Poland spends 4.5% of GDP on its military, the highest burden in NATO, the Polish market sustains Israeli weapons manufacturers whose products are tested on Gaza.","profile_src":["https://caliber.az/en/post/deputy-fm-poland-halts-lethal-weapons-supplies-to-israel","https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/","https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/","https://www.defensenews.com/global/europe/2023/08/07/poland-to-make-hundreds-of-israeli-designed-spike-antitank-missiles/"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"CTY-00013","name":"Austria","type":"Country","role":"Small licensor and buyer of Elbit drones","country":"Austria","slug":"austria","profile":"Austria licenses only small volumes of arms exports to Israel, €1M or less in 2024 according to EU data and €1.7M in 2022, but AOAV counts €33M of Austrian licences in 2014–2022, including more than €5.6M of 'kinetic weapons'. Vienna is a growing customer of Israel's largest private weapons manufacturer: in August 2025 the Austrian army began receiving the first of 315 Magni-X tactical reconnaissance drones from Elbit Systems Deutschland, with an option for 300 more. Elbit markets its systems as combat-proven, a reference to their use by the Israeli military in Gaza, where the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide. Austria has announced no restrictions on purchases from Israeli manufacturers.","profile_src":["https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/","https://aoav.org.uk/2025/is-europe-turning-its-back-on-arming-israel/","https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/","https://www.israeldefense.co.il/en/node/65977","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00014","name":"Denmark","type":"Country","role":"F-35 parts maker and buyer of Elbit artillery","country":"Denmark","slug":"denmark","profile":"Denmark's arms trade with Israel runs through the F-35. Danish media Danwatch and Information revealed in 2023 that Israel's F-35s carry parts made by the Danish company Terma. Al-Haq, ActionAid Denmark and the Danish branches of Amnesty and Oxfam sued the state to stop the licences, but on March 18, 2026 the Supreme Court rejected the case, ruling that the organisations lacked legal standing, so no court has examined the substance. Denmark is also a direct buyer of Israeli weapons: in 2023 it ordered 19 ATMOS howitzers and 8 PULS rocket launchers from Elbit Systems to replace guns given to Ukraine. Danish licences to Israel were just over €400,000 in 2022, according to AOAV.","profile_src":["https://www.newarab.com/news/danish-supreme-court-rejects-case-arms-sales-israel","https://aoav.org.uk/2025/is-europe-turning-its-back-on-arming-israel/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00015","name":"Greece","type":"Country","role":"Licensor of €114M to Israel and Israel's largest new European customer","country":"Greece","slug":"greece","profile":"Greece has turned into one of Israel's closest military partners. EU data show Athens granted €114M of arms export licences to Israel in 2024, the third-highest in the EU, up from €7.6M across 2014–2022, according to AOAV. In April 2026 Greece signed a $750M deal with Elbit for PULS rocket artillery, including precision-guided rockets and loitering munitions, announced during a visit by Israeli Military Minister Israel Katz. On August 31, 2026 Israel's Ministry of Defense announced the roughly €3B Achilles Shield agreement for David's Sling, SPYDER, Barak MX and Israeli radars. That makes Greek public money one of the biggest foreign revenue streams for Rafael, IAI and Elbit in the year after the UN Commission of Inquiry found Israel committed genocide.","profile_src":["https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/","https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/","https://breakingdefense.com/2026/04/greece-inks-750m-deal-with-israel-for-elbits-puls-rocket-artillery-systems/","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00016","name":"Cyprus","type":"Country","role":"Buyer of Israeli Barak MX and close military partner","country":"Cyprus","slug":"cyprus","profile":"Cyprus is a close military partner of Israel in the eastern Mediterranean and one of the first EU buyers of IAI's Barak MX interceptor system, whose initial deliveries arrived in December 2024 as part of a shift away from Russian equipment. The contract value has not been disclosed. EU data show Cypriot arms export licences to Israel of €1M or less in 2024, and AOAV counts €97,000 of small-arms licences in 2014–2022. The island's role is less about export volume than about integration: Israel Aerospace Industries, a state-owned weapons manufacturer whose systems are used in Gaza, now anchors Cyprus's air shield. Whether the money for Barak MX flowed during the period the UN Commission of Inquiry described as genocide remains to be confirmed.","profile_src":["https://www.ynetnews.com/article/bjlgtoje1e","https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/","https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"CTY-00017","name":"Finland","type":"Country","role":"Buyer of David's Sling despite the Gaza genocide","country":"Finland","slug":"finland","profile":"Finland's main link to Israel's war economy is as a customer. It chose Rafael's David's Sling in April 2023 for about €316M with a further €213M option, and signed the contract with Israel's Ministry of Defense in November 2023, a month into the bombardment of Gaza, at NIS 1.3B. On August 12, 2025 Military Minister Antti Häkkänen rejected calls to cancel, saying 'there are no talks about cancelling the deal, it is proceeding as planned', and citing delays and contract penalties. Finland also licenses some exports to Israel: €17M in 2024, according to EU data. David's Sling is co-developed with RTX's Raytheon, so Finnish money supports both Israeli and US weapons manufacturers.","profile_src":["https://www.helsinkitimes.fi/finland/finland-news/domestic/27657-haekkaenen-gaza-conflict-will-not-halt-finland-s-arms-deals-with-israel.html","https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-00018","name":"Slovakia","type":"Country","role":"Buyer of Barak MX and past licensor to Israel","country":"Slovakia","slug":"slovakia","profile":"Slovakia is a buyer of Israeli weapons and a historic licensor of exports to Israel. In December 2024 Israel's Ministry of Defense announced a sale of IAI's Barak MX system to Slovakia for about €560M, and the first battery reached the Slovak armed forces in April 2026. AOAV counts €117M of Slovak licences to Israel in 2014–2022, including €12M related to vehicles and tanks. Slovakia does not appear among the EU states listed with 2024 licences to Israel in EUobserver's report on the latest EU data, and its current export flows to Israel are unverified. Prime Minister Robert Fico's government has not announced any restrictions, and the Barak MX money flowed to IAI during the Gaza genocide.","profile_src":["https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/","https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/"],"profile_status":"reported","profile (append sentence)":"Slovakia shows no military-list licence value for Israel in the EU's 2023 table."},{"id":"CTY-00019","name":"Hungary","type":"Country","role":"Political shield for Israel in the EU and Elbit customer","country":"Hungary","slug":"hungary","profile":"Hungary under Viktor Orbán has acted as Israel's political shield inside the European Union and as a customer of Israeli weapons manufacturers. EU data show Hungarian arms export licences to Israel of €6M in 2024, after more than €15M in 2014–2022, according to AOAV. The research database DIMSE records a December 2023 memorandum on military cooperation signed in Israel with Elbit, Rafael and IAI, Hungarian purchases of Elbit radios, and a $175M Elbit contract in December 2024 for electronic warfare and DIRCM self-protection suites for aircraft, widely attributed to Hungary although the announcement did not name it. Budapest has opposed EU measures against Israel while buying from the companies that equip its military.","profile_src":["https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/","https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/","https://dimse.info/hungary/"],"profile_status":"reported","profile (append sentence)":"In 2023 Hungary licensed €1.66M of military exports to Israel but delivered only €120,436, according to the EU's annual arms-export report."},{"id":"CTY-00020","name":"Bulgaria","type":"Country","role":"Former ammunition licensor and planned EuroPULS buyer","country":"Bulgaria","slug":"bulgaria","profile":"Bulgaria's arms trade with Israel has been driven by its munitions industry. AOAV counts €49M of Bulgarian licences to Israel in 2014–2022, including €11M of explosive devices and €8M of small arms, and €7.3M in 2022 alone. EU data show Bulgaria issued €1M or less in licences to Israel in 2024. The research database DIMSE reports that Bulgaria plans to buy 12 MARS 3 (EuroPULS) launchers based on Elbit's PULS system. Delivery flows of Bulgarian ammunition to Israel since October 2023 have not been verified and need further investigation, given the country's role as a major ammunition exporter.","profile_src":["https://aoav.org.uk/2024/who-is-arming-israel-other-global-exports-to-israel/","https://aoav.org.uk/2025/is-europe-turning-its-back-on-arming-israel/","https://euobserver.com/214004/france-topped-eu-arms-sales-to-israel-while-backing-mini-sanctions/","https://dimse.info/bulgaria/"],"profile_status":"reported","profile (append sentence)":"In 2023 Bulgaria licensed €17.42M of military exports to Israel and delivered €2.78M, according to the EU's annual arms-export report."},{"id":"CTY-00021","name":"Serbia","type":"Country","role":"Ammunition exporter to Israel and Elbit's biggest European customer","country":"Serbia","slug":"serbia","profile":"Serbia, outside the EU, has become one of Israel's most important arms partners in Europe. According to BIRN and Haaretz, Serbian ammunition exports to Israel reached €47.9M in 2024, and €55.5M in the first half of 2025 alone, more than all of 2024. In August 2025 Calcalist revealed Serbia as the undisclosed buyer of a $1.63B Elbit package of Hermes 900 drones, long-range precision missiles, electronic warfare and command systems. Serbian artillery shells and Israeli drones thus move in both directions, during a war that the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 amounted to genocide, and in which it called on all states to stop arms transfers to Israel.","profile_src":["https://www.serbianmonitor.com/en/birn-serbia-exported-more-ammunition-to-israel-in-the-first-half-of-2025-than-in-the-whole-of-2024/","https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/5vr2ehayj","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"CTY-00022","name":"Slovenia","type":"Country","role":"Imposed then reversed an arms embargo on Israel","country":"Slovenia","slug":"slovenia","profile":"Slovenia announced a complete ban on arms trade with Israel on July 30, 2025, one of the first EU states to do so after the Gaza famine warnings. According to an overview of embargoes since 2023, the government appointed in June 2026 reversed many of the measures its predecessor had imposed on Israel, including the arms embargo. Slovenia's case shows how quickly European restrictions can be dropped once political pressure fades, even after the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide and called on states to halt arms transfers. Trade volumes are small, and Slovenian licence values to Israel for 2023–2025 have not been verified.","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arms_embargoes_on_Israel_since_2023","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"WPN-NEW-ROEM","name":"Ro'em (Sigma) 155mm howitzer","type":"Weapon/System","role":"155mm automatic self-propelled howitzer (Elbit Systems)","country":"Israel","slug":"ro-em-sigma-155mm-howitzer","profile":"Ro'em is Elbit Systems' new automatic 155mm self-propelled howitzer, which Elbit began developing in 2019. Breaking Defense reported in April 2026 that the Israeli army carried out the first operational firing of Ro'em during operations in Lebanon, in support of forces maneuvering in the north, to attack what it called Hezbollah targets. Its combat debut came during Israel's war on Lebanon, in which the Lebanese Ministry of Public Health counts 8,953 people killed and 30,649 wounded since 8 October 2023, as of 25 September 2026, and during the destruction of South Lebanon's border villages. For Elbit, battlefield use is a sales argument: the UN Special Rapporteur's July 2025 report describes how Israeli weapons are marketed abroad as 'battle-proven'. Ro'em joins Elbit's PULS launcher as artillery first used on Lebanon and then offered for export.","profile_src":["https://breakingdefense.com/2026/04/israels-new-automatic-roem-howitzer-used-for-first-time-in-combat/","https://moph.gov.lb/en/Media/view/87142/4/update-toll-of-the-aggression-25-9-2026","https://www.un.org/unispal/document/a-hrc-59-23-from-economy-of-occupation-to-economy-of-genocide-report-special-rapporteur-francesca-albanese-palestine-2025/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-NEW-GALLREIN","name":"Ed Gallrein","type":"Person","role":"Republican nominee, Kentucky 4th District (UDP-backed; beat Thomas Massie)","country":"USA","slug":"ed-gallrein","profile":"Ed Gallrein is the Republican who defeated Rep. Thomas Massie in Kentucky's 4th District primary on 19 May 2026. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza; AIPAC's network spends to keep Congress arming Israel regardless. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, made the race one of its biggest Republican targets: FactCheck.org's review of FEC filings through 30 June 2026 found UDP spent over $3 million opposing Massie and nearly $500,000 supporting Gallrein. Louisville Public Media called the contest a record-shattering $37M race. UDP's FEC filings show $53.4M in independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, and its ads rarely mention Israel.","profile_src":["https://www.factcheck.org/2026/08/united-democracy-project-3/","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.lpm.org/news/2026-07-17/a-record-shattering-37m-was-spent-on-kentuckys-massie-gallrein-race-heres-who-funded-it"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"ORG-NEW-ISRAEL-LOBBY","name":"Israel lobby PACs and donors","type":"Organization","role":"Aggregate: pro-Israel PACs, super PACs and their large donors (as tallied by Track AIPAC)","country":"USA","slug":"israel-lobby-pacs-and-donors","profile":"This node gathers the money that pro-Israel PACs, super PACs and their large donors have given to U.S. politicians, as tallied by Track AIPAC from Federal Election Commission data. It includes AIPAC's own PAC and its super PAC United Democracy Project, plus groups such as Democratic Majority for Israel, NORPAC, Pro-Israel America, the Republican Jewish Coalition and J Street, which appear in the site's per-candidate lists. Track AIPAC's congress page reports federal career totals as of 5 July 2026, split into direct donations and independent (outside) expenditures. The top recipient, Rep. Haley Stevens, is credited with $36.28M, most of it super PAC spending in her failed 2026 Senate primary. The money keeps flowing while Israel's military is armed by Washington through the Gaza genocide, which the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 Israel had committed. These are advocacy tallies, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-BESHEAR","name":"Andy Beshear","type":"Person","role":"Governor of Kentucky (2028 presidential contender)","country":"USA","slug":"andy-beshear","profile":"Andy Beshear (Governor of Kentucky) appears on Track AIPAC's list of likely 2028 presidential contenders; Track AIPAC is an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics. The tracker shows no federal Israel-lobby money for Beshear, because he has not run for federal office, but still rates the record as pro-Israel. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/2028","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-BOOKER","name":"Cory Booker","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Senator, New Jersey (2028 presidential contender)","country":"USA","slug":"cory-booker","profile":"Cory Booker (U.S. Senator, New Jersey) appears on Track AIPAC's list of likely 2028 presidential contenders; Track AIPAC is an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics. Track AIPAC's 2028 tracker credits Booker with $846,471 in Israel-lobby money, all of it from PACs and donors. Its congress page, a career tally as of 5 July 2026, shows $851,721 ($851,721 donations, $0 outside spending). Listed groups: AIPAC, AUSD, COPAC, DMFI, FIPAC, GCSC, JAC, MDACC, NACPAC, NATPAC, NORPAC, TPOH. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/2028","https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-BUTTIGIEG","name":"Pete Buttigieg","type":"Person","role":"Former U.S. Secretary of Transportation (2028 presidential contender)","country":"USA","slug":"pete-buttigieg","profile":"Pete Buttigieg (Former U.S. Secretary of Transportation) appears on Track AIPAC's list of likely 2028 presidential contenders; Track AIPAC is an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics. Track AIPAC's 2028 tracker credits Buttigieg with $191,145 in Israel-lobby money. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/2028","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-EMANUEL","name":"Rahm Emanuel","type":"Person","role":"Former Mayor of Chicago and former U.S. Ambassador to Japan (2028 presidential contender)","country":"USA","slug":"rahm-emanuel","profile":"Rahm Emanuel (Former Mayor of Chicago and former U.S. Ambassador to Japan) appears on Track AIPAC's list of likely 2028 presidential contenders; Track AIPAC is an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics. Track AIPAC's 2028 tracker credits Emanuel with $42,250 in Israel-lobby money, all of it from PACs and donors. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/2028","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-GALLEGO","name":"Ruben Gallego","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Senator, Arizona (2028 presidential contender)","country":"USA","slug":"ruben-gallego","profile":"Ruben Gallego (U.S. Senator, Arizona) appears on Track AIPAC's list of likely 2028 presidential contenders; Track AIPAC is an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics. Track AIPAC's 2028 tracker credits Gallego with $83,219 in Israel-lobby money, all of it from PACs and donors. Its congress page, a career tally as of 5 July 2026, shows $141,670 ($99,419 donations, $42,251 outside spending). Listed groups: AIPAC, DMFI, GCSC, JAC, NORPAC, PIA. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/2028","https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-HARRIS","name":"Kamala Harris","type":"Person","role":"Biden's vice president through the Gaza genocide; refused any arms embargo on Israel","country":"USA","slug":"kamala-harris","profile":"Kamala Devi Harris, branded \"Killer Kamala\" by protesters and, alongside Joe Biden, one of the \"Butchers of Gaza\", was vice president through the first fifteen months of the genocide in Gaza and the Democratic nominee who campaigned on keeping the bombs flowing. She served in the administration that bypassed Congress to arm Israel, sent at least $17.9 billion in military aid in a single year and vetoed four UN Security Council ceasefire demands. Protesters at a June 2024 Jimmy Kimmel taping called her a \"war criminal\". At an August 2024 Detroit rally, when they chanted \"Kamala, Kamala, you can't hide, we won't vote for genocide\", she shot back: \"If you want Donald Trump to win, then say that. Otherwise, I'm speaking.\" When the Uncommitted movement, saying \"people we love are being killed with American bombs\", pressed her for an arms embargo, her national security adviser answered that she \"has not supported an arms embargo on Israel.\" From the convention stage she vowed: \"I will always ensure Israel has the ability to defend itself,\" and asked days later whether she would change arms policy, she said simply \"No.\" Her campaign took more than $6 million raised through the Israel lobby group J Street, and Track AIPAC credits her with $9.04M in Israel-lobby money. She is now listed among the 2028 presidential hopefuls.","profile_src":["https://www.cbsnews.com/amp/sanfrancisco/news/pro-palestinian-demonstrators-blast-kamala-harris-outside-san-francisco-fundraiser","https://www.palestinianyouthmovement.com/statements/biden-butcher-of-gaza","https://www.foxnews.com/media/kamala-harris-appearance-jimmy-kimmel-show-disrupted-anti-israel-protesters-calling-her-murderer","https://responsiblestatecraft.org/harris-gaza-protesters/","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/8/8/harris-campaign-denies-support-for-cutting-off-weapons-transfers-to-israel","https://www.commondreams.org/news/kamala-harris-gaza-dnc","https://www.npr.org/2024/08/23/g-s1-19232/kamala-harris-israel-gaza-dnc","https://www.timesofisrael.com/harris-says-she-wont-change-us-policy-on-arming-israel-stresses-need-for-hostage-deal/","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-military-aid-for-israel-tops-17-9-billion-since-last-oct-7","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/11/20/us-vetoes-un-security-council-resolution-demanding-gaza-ceasefire","https://readsludge.com/2024/10/16/pro-israel-lobby-j-street-raises-6-million-for-harris/","https://whofundsmyrep.com/2028","https://www.trackaipac.com/2028"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-KELLY","name":"Mark Kelly","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Senator, Arizona (2028 presidential contender)","country":"USA","slug":"mark-kelly","profile":"Mark Kelly (U.S. Senator, Arizona) appears on Track AIPAC's list of likely 2028 presidential contenders; Track AIPAC is an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics. Track AIPAC's 2028 tracker credits Kelly with $495,311 in Israel-lobby money, all of it from PACs and donors. Its congress page, a career tally as of 5 July 2026, shows $554,054 ($499,717 donations, $54,337 outside spending). Listed groups: AIPAC, DMFI, GCSC, HEARTLAND, JAC, J Street, SUNPAC. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/2028","https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-WMOORE","name":"Wes Moore","type":"Person","role":"Governor of Maryland (2028 presidential contender)","country":"USA","slug":"wes-moore","profile":"Wes Moore (Governor of Maryland) appears on Track AIPAC's list of likely 2028 presidential contenders; Track AIPAC is an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics. The tracker shows no federal Israel-lobby money for Moore, because he has not run for federal office, but still rates the record as pro-Israel. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/2028","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-NEWSOM","name":"Gavin Newsom","type":"Person","role":"Governor of California (2028 presidential contender)","country":"USA","slug":"gavin-newsom","profile":"Gavin Newsom (Governor of California) appears on Track AIPAC's list of likely 2028 presidential contenders; Track AIPAC is an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics. The tracker shows no federal Israel-lobby money for Newsom, because he has not run for federal office, but still rates the record as pro-Israel. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/2028","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-OSSOFF","name":"Jon Ossoff","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Senator, Georgia (2028 presidential contender)","country":"USA","slug":"jon-ossoff","profile":"Jon Ossoff (U.S. Senator, Georgia) appears on Track AIPAC's list of likely 2028 presidential contenders; Track AIPAC is an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics. Track AIPAC's 2028 tracker credits Ossoff with $954,187 in Israel-lobby money, of which $758,957 from PACs and donors and $195,230 in independent (outside) spending. Listed groups: DJOP, JAC, JDCA, J Street, DMFI ('20). AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use