 $151.8M sale of 12,000 BLU-110 1,000-pound bomb bodies, with Repkon USA as principal contractor. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money, lists him among likely 2028 presidential contenders and credits him with $420,421 in Israel-lobby money, all of it from PACs and donors; its numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/2028","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.globalsecurity.org/wmd/library/news/israel/2025/03/israel-250301-state01.htm","https://www.airforce-technology.com/news/us-state-department-israel-arms/","https://www.turkishminute.com/2026/03/11/turkish-companys-us-unit-changes-name-after-backlash-over-sale-of-1000-pound-bombs-to-israel/","https://www.sanders.senate.gov/press-releases/news-sanders-files-joint-resolutions-of-disapproval-to-block-nearly-660-million-in-bomb-sales-to-israel/","https://www.ynetnews.com/article/bkmojptkzx"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-VANCE","name":"JD Vance","type":"Person","role":"Thiel-made US vice president; excuses the Gaza genocide, backs Israel's war on Iran","country":"USA","slug":"jd-vance","profile":"James David \"JD\" Vance, vice president since January 2025 and a 2028 presidential hopeful, is the political creation of Peter Thiel, the billionaire co-founder of Palantir, the surveillance firm wired into Israel's killing machine. Thiel employed Vance at his venture firm Mithril Capital, then poured $15 million into the Protect Ohio Values super PAC behind Vance's 2022 Senate run. Palantir signed a January 2024 pact with Israel's military ministry for \"war-related missions\", and a UN Special Rapporteur found \"reasonable grounds\" to believe it helped generate target lists through AI systems like \"Lavender\" and \"Gospel\"; its quarterly revenue has since nearly doubled to $1.94 billion. Vance sits second in an administration that in March 2025 used emergency powers to rush some $4 billion in arms to Israel, including more than 35,500 MK-84 and BLU-117 bombs. He waved away the genocide in Gaza: \"I don't think that the Israelis are purposely trying to go in and murder every Palestinian,\" and threatened that Hamas \"would be obliterated\". He cheered the June 2025 US bombing of Iran (\"We're at war with Iran's nuclear program\") and defended the US-Israeli war on Iran launched on 28 February 2026: \"That is the goal of this operation.\" By September 2026, with thousands dead in Iran, he insisted: \"I wouldn't call it a war.\" Track AIPAC credits him with $81,985 in Israel-lobby money.","profile_src":["https://www.cbsnews.com/news/jd-vance-trump-vp-peter-thiel-billionaire/","https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/24/01/36613282/palantir-joins-forces-with-israeli-defense-ministry-in-war-tech-partnership-report","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/7/1/un-report-lists-companies-complicit-in-israels-genocide-who-are-they","https://www.aa.com.tr/en/americas/palantir-revenue-surges-93-amid-criticism-over-support-for-israel-s-gaza-war/4018270","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-approves-3-billion-arms-sale-israel","https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/vance-israel-not-committing-genocide-but-heart-breaks-for-children-suffering-in-gaza/","https://abcnews.com/Politics/vance-war-iran-war-irans-nuclear-program/story?id=123090085","https://www.newsonair.gov.in/us-vice-president-jd-vance-warns-hamas-of-obliteration-if-it-refuses-to-disarm","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/jd-vance/vance-anti-war-posture-collides-hawkish-views-iran-rcna261585","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/3/us-vice-president-jd-vance-declines-to-offer-timeline-for-end-of-iran-war","https://whofundsmyrep.com/2028","https://www.trackaipac.com/2028"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-YOUNGKIN","name":"Glenn Youngkin","type":"Person","role":"Former Governor of Virginia (2022–2026) (2028 presidential contender)","country":"USA","slug":"glenn-youngkin","profile":"Glenn Youngkin (Former Governor of Virginia (2022–2026)) appears on Track AIPAC's list of likely 2028 presidential contenders; Track AIPAC is an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics. The tracker shows no federal Israel-lobby money for Youngkin, because he has not run for federal office, but still rates the record as pro-Israel. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/2028","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-SCHIFF","name":"Adam Schiff","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Senator, California","country":"USA","slug":"adam-schiff","profile":"Adam Schiff (U.S. Senator, California) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Schiff No. 5 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $5.61M as of 5 July 2026: $581,595 in direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors and $5.03M in independent (outside) spending. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-COLLINS","name":"Susan Collins","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Senator, Maine","country":"USA","slug":"susan-collins","profile":"Susan Collins (U.S. Senator, Maine) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Collins No. 8 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $4.13M as of 5 July 2026: $3.57M in direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors and $565,000 in independent (outside) spending. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-DDAVIS","name":"Don Davis","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, North Carolina's 1st District","country":"USA","slug":"don-davis","profile":"Don Davis (U.S. Representative, North Carolina's 1st District) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, 