er's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-MESSMER","name":"Mark Messmer","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, Indiana's 8th District","country":"USA","slug":"mark-messmer","profile":"Mark Messmer (U.S. Representative, Indiana's 8th District) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Messmer No. 12 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $2.85M as of 5 July 2026: $329,491 in direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors and $2.52M in independent (outside) spending. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-GOMEZ","name":"Jimmy Gomez","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, California's 34th District","country":"USA","slug":"jimmy-gomez","profile":"Jimmy Gomez (U.S. Representative, California's 34th District) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Gomez No. 13 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $2.64M as of 5 July 2026: $368,917 in direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors and $2.27M in independent (outside) spending. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-GOTTHEIMER","name":"Josh Gottheimer","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, New Jersey's 5th District","country":"USA","slug":"josh-gottheimer","profile":"Josh Gottheimer (U.S. Representative, New Jersey's 5th District) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Gottheimer No. 16 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $2.33M as of 5 July 2026: all of it direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-ROSEN","name":"Jacky Rosen","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Senator, Nevada","country":"USA","slug":"jacky-rosen","profile":"Jacky Rosen (U.S. Senator, Nevada) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Rosen No. 17 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $2.26M as of 5 July 2026: $2.12M in direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors and $145,856 in independent (outside) spending. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-DEXTER","name":"Maxine Dexter","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, Oregon's 3rd District","country":"USA","slug":"maxine-dexter","profile":"Maxine Dexter (U.S. Representative, Oregon's 3rd District) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Dexter No. 18 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $2.21M as of 5 July 2026: all of it outside spending by super PACs. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-TORRES","name":"Ritchie Torres","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, New York's 15th District","country":"USA","slug":"ritchie-torres","profile":"Ritchie Torres (U.S. Representative, New York's 15th District) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Torres No. 19 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $2.11M as of 5 July 2026: $2.05M in direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors and $57,952 in independent (outside) spending. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-DEGETTE","name":"Diana DeGette","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, Colorado's 1st District","country":"USA","slug":"diana-degette","profile":"Diana DeGette (U.S. Representative, Colorado's 1st District) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks DeGette No. 20 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $1.65M as of 5 July 2026: $111,576 in direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors and $1.54M in independent (outside) spending. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-DWS","name":"Debbie Wasserman Schultz","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, Florida's 25th District","country":"USA","slug":"debbie-wasserman-schultz","profile":"Debbie Wasserman Schultz (U.S. Representative, Florida's 25th District) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Schultz No. 21 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $1.54M as of 5 July 2026: all of it direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-AGUILAR","name":"Pete Aguilar","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, California's 33rd District; House Democratic Caucus chair","country":"USA","slug":"pete-aguilar","profile":"Pete Aguilar (U.S. Representative, California's 33rd District; House Democratic Caucus chair) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Aguilar No. 22 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $1.53M as of 5 July 2026: all of it direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-JEFFRIES","name":"Hakeem Jeffries","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, New York's 8th District; House Democratic leader","country":"USA","slug":"hakeem-jeffries","profile":"Hakeem Jeffries (U.S. Representative, New York's 8th District; House Democratic leader) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Jeffries No. 23 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $1.50M as of 5 July 2026: all of it direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-NEW-BYNUM","name":"Janelle Bynum","type":"Person","role":"U.S. Representative, Oregon's 5th District","country":"USA","slug":"janelle-bynum","profile":"Janelle Bynum (U.S. Representative, Oregon's 5th District) sits in the current Congress. Track AIPAC, an advocacy project that follows pro-Israel lobby money in U.S. politics, ranks Bynum No. 24 among current members of Congress by Israel-lobby money, with a federal career total of $1.45M as of 5 July 2026: $25,700 in direct donations from pro-Israel PACs and donors and $1.43M in independent (outside) spending. AIPAC, its super PAC United Democracy Project and allied PACs use this money to reward politicians who keep U.S. weapons flowing to Israel; the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza. AIPAC's super PAC, United Democracy Project, spent $53.4M on independent expenditures in the 2025–2026 cycle through 31 August 2026, according to FEC filings. The tracker's numbers are an advocacy tally built from campaign-finance data, not official FEC totals.","profile_src":["https://www.trackaipac.com/congress","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.fec.gov/data/committee/C00799031/?cycle=2026"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"CTY-NEW-PORTUGAL","name":"Portugal","type":"Country","role":"EU arms licensor to Israel","country":"Portugal","slug":"portugal","profile":"Portugal licensed €11.28M of military exports to Israel in 2023 and delivered €5.38M in actual military exports that year, according to the EU's annual arms-export report, the Council's own compilation of member-state data. Those 16 licences were issued in the year Israel began the assault on Gaza that the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 amounts to genocide, and the Commission called on every state to stop transferring arms that may be used for genocidal acts. The EU data list licence values by military-list category but do not identify the products or Israeli end users, so the public record does not show what Portugal sold.","profile_src":["https://www.parlament.gv.at/dokument/XXVIII/EU/6974/imfname_11440265.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-NEW-MALTA","name":"Malta","type":"Country","role":"EU arms licensor to Israel","country":"Malta","slug":"malta","profile":"Malta, one of the EU's smallest states, licensed €7.41M of military exports to Israel in 2023, more than Sweden, Luxembourg or Hungary, and recorded €1.97M in actual arms exports, according to the EU's annual arms-export report. Three licences account for the total. They were issued in the year Israel began the assault on Gaza that the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 was genocide; the Commission urged all states to halt arms transfers that may be used for genocidal acts. The EU report does not say what equipment was licensed, a gap common to the annual data, which list licence values by category but not by product or end user.","profile_src":["https://www.parlament.gv.at/dokument/XXVIII/EU/6974/imfname_11440265.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-NEW-SWEDEN","name":"Sweden","type":"Country","role":"EU arms licensor to Israel (follow-on deliveries only since Oct 2023)","country":"Sweden","slug":"sweden","profile":"Sweden licensed €4.65M of military exports to Israel in 2023 and delivered €1.53M, according to the EU's annual arms-export report. The Swedish government says it has issued no export licence for the sale of military equipment to Israel since October 2023 and that later exports were follow-on deliveries to private companies of components that were not counted as military equipment at the time of the original delivery. It also says Sweden has not licensed sales of military equipment to Israel's armed forces or other state actors since the 1950s. Even so, components kept flowing to Israeli companies while Israel carried out what the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 was genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.parlament.gv.at/dokument/XXVIII/EU/6974/imfname_11440265.pdf","https://www.government.se/contentassets/f034be95c56340ccb68196196c177653/strategic-export-controls-in-2024--military-equipment-and-dual-use-items-skr.-202425114.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-NEW-LUXEMBOURG","name":"Luxembourg","type":"Country","role":"EU arms licensor to Israel","country":"Luxembourg","slug":"luxembourg","profile":"Luxembourg licensed €2.52M of military exports to Israel in 2023 across five licences, and recorded €66,472 in actual arms exports, according to the EU's annual arms-export report. The licences were issued in the year Israel launched the assault on Gaza that the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 constitutes genocide; the Commission called on all states to stop transferring arms that may be used for genocidal acts. Like most member states, Luxembourg publishes licence values by military-list category but not by product or end user, so the public record does not show what was sold. Small sums from many states add up: EU licences for Israel totalled €948.12M in 2023.","profile_src":["https://www.parlament.gv.at/dokument/XXVIII/EU/6974/imfname_11440265.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-NEW-LITHUANIA","name":"Lithuania","type":"Country","role":"EU arms licensor to Israel","country":"Lithuania","slug":"lithuania","profile":"Lithuania issued one military-export licence for Israel in 2023, worth €177,000, and delivered the full €177,000 that year, according to the EU's annual arms-export report. The licence came in the year Israel launched the assault on Gaza that the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 constitutes genocide; the Commission urged all states to halt arms transfers that may be used in genocidal acts. Its single licence shows how widely the EU's licensing for Israel was spread across member states. The EU data do not identify the equipment licensed. EU licences for Israel totalled €948.12M in 2023.","profile_src":["https://www.parlament.gv.at/dokument/XXVIII/EU/6974/imfname_11440265.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-NEW-ESTONIA","name":"Estonia","type":"Country","role":"EU arms licensor to Israel","country":"Estonia","slug":"estonia","profile":"Estonia issued four military-export licences for Israel in 2023 worth €52,500 and delivered €17,292 in actual arms exports, according to the EU's annual arms-export report. The sums are small, but they were approved in the year Israel launched the assault on Gaza that the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 constitutes genocide, after which the Commission called on all states to stop transferring arms that may be used for genocidal acts. The EU data list licence values by military-list category but do not identify products or end users. Across the EU, licences for Israel totalled €948.12M in 2023, led by Germany, Greece and France.","profile_src":["https://www.parlament.gv.at/dokument/XXVIII/EU/6974/imfname_11440265.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-NEW-IRELAND","name":"Ireland","type":"Country","role":"Dual-use exporter to Israel (no military-list licences)","country":"Ireland","slug":"ireland","profile":"Ireland shows no military-list licence value for Israel in the EU's 2023 arms-export table, but it is a sizeable dual-use exporter. The Irish government told the Dail in May 2024 that €70.37M of dual-use export licences for Israel were approved in 2023, and that the bulk were mainstream business ICT products, mostly software, classed as dual-use because they incorporate strong encryption. Dual-use items have civilian uses but can also serve militaries and intelligence services. This map therefore links Ireland to Israel on the dual-use layer only. The approvals came in the year Israel launched the assault on Gaza that the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 constitutes genocide.","profile_src":["https://www.oireachtas.ie/en/debates/question/2024-05-23/56/","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTY-NEW-NORWAY","name":"Norway","type":"Country","role":"No direct arms exports to Israel; indirect F-35 supply-chain role via Kongsberg","country":"Norway","slug":"norway","profile":"Norway has no direct arms edge on this map. Its government keeps a policy of not exporting arms to war zones, relaxed for Ukraine but not for Israel, according to The National. Officials have asked Norwegian weapons makers Nammo and Kongsberg to carry out due diligence on indirect links to Israel. The indirect link is the F-35: Kongsberg supplies parts to the global F-35 supply chain, and Israel flies F-35s over Gaza, Lebanon and Iran. That connection runs through Lockheed Martin's global parts pool rather than a Norwegian licence for Israel, so it is described here but not drawn as an edge.","profile_src":["https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/europe/2024/09/03/which-countries-have-suspended-arms-sales-to-israel/"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"CTY-NEW-SWITZERLAND","name":"Switzerland","type":"Country","role":"Dual-use and special military goods exporter to Israel","country":"Switzerland","slug":"switzerland","profile":"Switzerland has issued no direct war-materiel licences for Israel for years, but Swiss companies kept selling Israel goods that can serve its military. A SWI swissinfo.ch review published in March 2026 found that more than CHF24M of dual-use or specific military goods were exported to Israel from October 2023 to March 2025, about CHF6M of dual-use goods in the first quarter of 2024 alone, up from CHF238,000 in the last three months of 2023. The State Secretariat for Economic Affairs said the exports complied with the regulatory framework, an interpretation legal experts contest. The surge came as Israel carried out what the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 was genocide in Gaza.","profile_src":["https://www.swissinfo.ch/eng/war-peace/swiss-companies-continued-exports-linked-to-israeli-war-effort-in-gaza-despite-criticism/91078202","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"CTY-NEW-LEBANON","name":"Lebanon","type":"Country","role":"Country under Israeli bombardment and invasion; destruction of South Lebanon","country":"Lebanon","slug":"lebanon","profile":"Lebanon is the second front of Israel's wars since October 2023. Lebanon's Ministry of Public Health counts 8,953 people killed and 30,649 wounded by Israeli attacks from 8 October 2023 to 25 September 2026, including 4,386 killed and 12,413 wounded since 2 March 2026. The ministry does not split the toll into civilians and combatants, and no reliable comprehensive split exists, so this map does not call all 8,953 civilians. Israel's war on Lebanon has brought the destruction of South Lebanon's border villages and the first combat use of new Israeli weapons: Elbit's Ro'em howitzer fired operationally for the first time in Lebanon in April 2026, and Elbit's Lahav/PULS launchers fired more than 50 'Bar' rockets at buildings and other targets there in 2026. Each battlefield debut becomes a sales pitch for the Israeli arms industry.","profile_src":["https://moph.gov.lb/en/Media/view/87142/4/update-toll-of-the-aggression-25-9-2026","https://breakingdefense.com/2026/04/israels-new-automatic-roem-howitzer-used-for-first-time-in-combat/","https://www.elbitsystems.com/blog/air-force-was-surprised-new-missile-revealed-during-war-iran"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"CTR-NEW-2025-02-28-1000LB","name":"US–Israel 1,000-lb bomb bodies and JDAM kits sale (notified 28 Feb 2025)","type":"Contract/Deal","role":"Emergency Foreign Military Sale notified 28 Feb 2025 ($675.7M)","country":"USA/Israel","slug":"us-israel-1-000-lb-bomb-bodies-and-jdam-kits-sale-notified-28-feb-2025","profile":"On 28 February 2025, the same day as the $2.04B bomb-body sale, the State Department used emergency authority to waive congressional review and approve a second package for Israel worth $675.7M. It covered up to 201 MK-83 and 4,799 BLU-110 1,000-pound bomb bodies, 1,500 KMU-559C/B and 3,500 KMU-559J/B JDAM guidance kits, 5,000 kits in all. Repkon USA in Tampa and Boeing in St. Charles, Missouri, were named principal contractors, with deliveries estimated to begin in 2028. The quantities are approved maximums; actual deliveries are unpublished. Bellingcat has documented JDAM-guided US bombs destroying Gaza City towers in 2025.","profile_src":["https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088252/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-and-munitions-support","https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/"],"profile_status":"documented"},{"id":"PER-V001","name":"Valerie Foushee","type":"Person","role":"Candidate","country":"USA","slug":"valerie-foushee","profile":"Valerie Foushee is a US political candidate on AIPAC's map. In the 2022 NC-04 Dem primary, United Democracy Project, the super PAC run by AIPAC, spent about $2.0M to elect Valerie Foushee (result: won). AIPAC's money rewards candidates who back unconditional US arms flows to Israel during the genocide in Gaza.","profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-V002","name":"Shontel Brown","type":"Person","role":"Candidate","country":"USA","slug":"shontel-brown","profile":"Shontel Brown is a US political candidate on AIPAC's map. In the 2022 OH-11 Dem primary, United Democracy Project, the super PAC run by AIPAC, spent about $0.3M to elect Shontel Brown (result: won). AIPAC's money rewards candidates who back unconditional US arms flows to Israel during the genocide in Gaza.","profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-V003","name":"Henry Cuellar","type":"Person","role":"Candidate","country":"USA","slug":"henry-cuellar","profile":"Henry Cuellar is a US political candidate on AIPAC's map. In the 2022 TX-28 Dem primary, United Democracy Project, the super PAC run by AIPAC, spent about $1.2M to elect Henry Cuellar (result: won). AIPAC's money rewards candidates who back unconditional US arms flows to Israel during the genocide in Gaza.","profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-V004","name":"Sarah Elfreth","type":"Person","role":"Candidate","country":"USA","slug":"sarah-elfreth","profile":"Sarah Elfreth is a US political candidate on AIPAC's map. In the 2024 MD-03 Dem primary, United Democracy Project, the super PAC run by AIPAC, spent about $4.2M to elect Sarah Elfreth (result: won). AIPAC's money rewards candidates who back unconditional US arms flows to Israel during the genocide in Gaza.","profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-V005","name":"Melissa Conyears-Ervin","type":"Person","role":"Candidate","country":"USA","slug":"melissa-conyears-ervin","profile":"Melissa Conyears-Ervin is a US political candidate on AIPAC's map. In the 2026 IL-07 Dem primary, United Democracy Project, the super PAC run by AIPAC, spent about $5.0M to elect Melissa Conyears-Ervin (result: lost to La Shawn Ford). AIPAC's money rewards candidates who back unconditional US arms flows to Israel during the genocide in Gaza.","profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-V006","name":"Adrian Boafo","type":"Person","role":"Candidate","country":"USA","slug":"adrian-boafo","profile":"Adrian Boafo is a US political candidate on AIPAC's map. In the 2026 MD-05 Dem primary, United Democracy Project, the super PAC run by AIPAC, spent about $2.9M to elect Adrian Boafo (result: won (23 Jun 2026)). AIPAC's money rewards candidates who back unconditional US arms flows to Israel during the genocide in Gaza.","profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-V007","name":"Thomas Massie","type":"Person","role":"Candidate","country":"USA","slug":"thomas-massie","profile":"Thomas Massie is a US political candidate on AIPAC's map. In the 2026 KY-04 GOP primary, United Democracy Project, the super PAC run by AIPAC, spent about $4.1M to defeat Thomas Massie (result: lost to Ed Gallrein 54-45 (19 May 2026)). AIPAC's money rewards candidates who back unconditional US arms flows to Israel during the genocide in Gaza, and punishes those who call for a ceasefire or conditions on aid.","profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-V008","name":"Abdul El-Sayed","type":"Person","role":"Candidate","country":"USA","slug":"abdul-el-sayed","profile":"Abdul El-Sayed is a US political candidate on AIPAC's map. In the 2026 Michigan Senate Dem primary, United Democracy Project, the super PAC run by AIPAC, spent about $20.1M to defeat Abdul El-Sayed (result: won (4 Aug 2026)). AIPAC's money rewards candidates who back unconditional US arms flows to Israel during the genocide in Gaza, and punishes those who call for a ceasefire or conditions on aid.","profile_status":"reported"},{"id":"PER-V009","name":"Jason Friedman","type":"Person","role":"Candidate","country":"USA","slug":"jason-friedman","profile":"Jason Friedman is a US political candidate on AIPAC's map. In the 2026 IL-07 Dem primary, United Democracy Project, the super PAC run by AIPAC, spent about $0.1M to defeat Jason Friedman (result: lost). AIPAC's money rewards candidates who back unconditional US arms flows to Israel during the genocide in Gaza, and punishes those who call for a ceasefire or conditions on aid.","profile_status":"reported"},{"name":"Maven Smart System","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Palantir AI targeting platform used by the U.S. military","country":"United States","profile":"Maven Smart System is Palantir's AI targeting platform for the U.S. military. It began under a $480M contract in May 2024, its ceiling rose to nearly $1.3B through 2029 in May 2025, and in March 2026 the Pentagon made it a program of record, already the main AI system for U.S. strikes on Iran, Reuters reported. Anthropic's Claude was embedded in it during the Iran campaign. Bloomberg found that the Minab school, wrongly catalogued as a military site, was fed into Maven and came out as a recommended day-one target; the strike killed more than 150 people, at least 123 of them children.","id":"WPN-NEW-MAVEN","profile_src":["https://defensescoop.com/2025/05/23/dod-palantir-maven-smart-system-contract-increase/","https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/exclusive-pentagon-adopt-palantir-ai-232906085.html","https://gizmodo.com/pentagon-investigators-say-overreliance-on-palantir-ai-tech-contributed-to-u-s-strike-that-killed-123-iranian-children-2000814477"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"maven-smart-system"},{"name":"Lavender","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Israeli military AI system that marks people as targets","country":"Israel","profile":"Lavender is an Israeli military AI system revealed by +972 Magazine and Local Call in April 2024. It marked some 37,000 Palestinians as suspected militants; officers said they spent about 20 seconds per target and acted as a 'rubber stamp', though the system erred in about 10 percent of cases. The army allowed up to 15 or 20 civilian deaths for a junior suspect. Paired with 'Where's Daddy?', it led to strikes on family homes, often with unguided 'dumb' bombs. Sources said it played a central role in the bombing of Palestinians, especially in the early stages of the Gaza genocide. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report names Lavender among the AI systems Israel uses to process targets.","id":"WPN-NEW-LAVENDER","profile_src":["https://www.972mag.com/lavender-ai-israeli-army-gaza/","https://www.972mag.com/lavender-ai-israeli-army-gaza/","https://www.972mag.com/lavender-ai-israeli-army-gaza/","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"lavender"},{"name":"The Gospel (Habsora)","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Israeli military AI system that generates building targets","country":"Israel","profile":"Habsora, 'the Gospel', is an Israeli military AI system that generates building and structure targets almost automatically, revealed by +972 Magazine and Local Call in November 2023. A former intelligence officer described it as facilitating a 'mass assassination factory', and former chief of staff Aviv Kochavi said the machine produced 100 targets in one day where the army once created 50 a year. The same investigation described 'power targets': 'high-rises and residential towers in the heart of cities, and public buildings such as universities, banks, and government offices.' UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report names the Gospel among the AI systems Israel uses to process targets, and the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","id":"WPN-NEW-GOSPEL","profile_src":["https://www.972mag.com/mass-assassination-factory-israel-calculated-bombing-gaza/","https://www.972mag.com/mass-assassination-factory-israel-calculated-bombing-gaza/","https://www.972mag.com/mass-assassination-factory-israel-calculated-bombing-gaza/","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"the-gospel-habsora"},{"name":"Where's Daddy?","type":"Weapon/System","role":"Israeli military tracking system that flags targets at home","country":"Israel","profile":"'Where's Daddy?' is an automated Israeli military system revealed by +972 Magazine and Local Call in April 2024. It tracked people marked by Lavender and signalled when they entered their family homes, where they were bombed. 'It's much easier to bomb a family's home,' an intelligence officer said. 'The system is built to look for them in these situations.' The army permitted up to 15 or 20 civilian deaths when striking a junior suspect, according to the same investigation, so the system's design meant whole families were killed. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report names Where's Daddy? among the AI systems Israel uses to process targets.","id":"WPN-NEW-WHERESDADDY","profile_src":["https://www.972mag.com/lavender-ai-israeli-army-gaza/"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"where-s-daddy"},{"name":"Michael Bloomberg","type":"Person","role":"Media billionaire; $88M ambulance-and-vests drive for Israel after Oct 7","country":"US","profile":"Michael Bloomberg, founder and 88% owner of Bloomberg LP and former New York mayor, is worth $94.9B according to Forbes (4 Oct 2026). In a matching appeal posted on 9 October 2023 for Magen David Adom, Israel's national emergency medical service, he matched nearly $44M from about 34,000 donors for an $88M total, the largest gift in American Friends of MDA's history. The money paid for ambulances, medical equipment, ballistic vests and helmets. 'America has always been a friend to Israel and I am encouraged that so many of us are stepping up to help our ally during these challenging times,' he said. Bloomberg Philanthropies then committed $27.8M to 65 hard-hit towns in southern and northern Israel. These gifts flowed during Israel's assault on Gaza, a campaign the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 was a genocide; no comparable public Bloomberg gift to Palestinian emergency services was found. Charity, too, picks a side.","id":"PER-NEW-BLOOMBERG","profile_src":["https://afmda.org/news/bloomberg-gift/","https://www.foxbusiness.com/lifestyle/michael-bloomberg-leads-88-million-donation-to-israels-emergency-medical-service","https://ejewishphilanthropy.com/bloombergs-27-8-million-project-to-boost-israeli-cities-hit-hardest-by-war-is-up-and-running/","https://www.forbes.com/profile/michael-bloomberg/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"michael-bloomberg"},{"name":"Jonathan Gray","type":"Person","role":"Blackstone president; record $125M gift to Tel Aviv University","country":"US","profile":"Jonathan Gray has been president and chief operating officer of Blackstone since 2018 and is seen as a potential successor to Stephen Schwarzman; Forbes values him at $9.2B (13 Sep 2026). In May 2025, nineteen months into the bombardment of Gaza, he and his wife Mindy gave $125M to Tel Aviv University's Faculty of Medicine, the largest gift in the university's history, which renamed it the Gray Faculty of Medical & Health Sciences. Gray told CTech the idea grew out of discussions after 7 October 2023: 'we certainly have a huge amount of sympathy for the people of Israel and we just wanted to show up and say we support you and we want to help you.' Sympathy was allocated accordingly. The gift came during Israel's assault on Gaza, which the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 was a genocide.","id":"PER-NEW-GRAY","profile_src":["https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/r1zqekcxgl","https://english.tau.ac.il/news/gray_medical_faculty","https://www.forbes.com/profile/jonathan-gray/","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"jonathan-gray"},{"name":"Stephen Schwarzman","type":"Person","role":"Blackstone chief; backed Trump in May 2024, citing antisemitism","country":"US","profile":"Stephen Schwarzman co-founded the private-equity firm Blackstone and is its chairman and CEO; Forbes values him at $40.5B (3 Oct 2026). In February 2018 he gave $10M to the National Library of Israel for the Stephen A. Schwarzman Education Center, which he described as his first donation in Israel. A long-time Republican donor and former Trump adviser, he announced on 24 May 2024, in the middle of Israel's assault on Gaza and the campus protests against it, that he would back Donald Trump: 'The dramatic rise of antisemitism has led me to focus on the consequences of upcoming elections with greater urgency.' The urgency was about the protesters, not the bombing they were protesting. The candidate he backed went on to rush bombs to Israel, sanction the International Criminal Court and launch a war on Iran. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","id":"PER-NEW-SCHWARZMAN","profile_src":["https://www.timesofisrael.com/billionaire-trump-adviser-gives-10m-to-israels-national-library/","https://www.axios.com/2024/05/24/trump-2024-stephen-schwarzman-blackstone","https://www.forbes.com/profile/stephen-schwarzman/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Criminal_Court_arrest_warrants_for_Israeli_leaders","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088258/israel-munitions-and-munitions-support","https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088258/israel-munitions-and-munitions-support"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"stephen-schwarzman"},{"name":"Blackstone","type":"Company","role":"Private-equity giant whose two bosses bankroll Israeli institutions and Trump","country":"US","profile":"Blackstone is the New York private-equity and alternative-asset firm led by co-founder, chairman and CEO Stephen Schwarzman and president and COO Jonathan Gray. Its two top executives are among the largest individual donors to Israeli institutions in this file: Gray and his wife gave $125M to Tel Aviv University's medical faculty in May 2025, the largest gift in its history, and Schwarzman gave $10M to the National Library of Israel in 2018 before endorsing Donald Trump in May 2024, citing antisemitism, in the middle of the assault on Gaza and the campus protests against it. Forbes values Schwarzman at $40.5B and Gray at $9.2B. No direct Blackstone contract with Israel's military was found; its inclusion rests on its executives' money and political action. The firm earns the fortunes; the fortunes pick the side.","id":"COM-NEW-BLACKSTONE","profile_src":["https://www.forbes.com/profile/stephen-schwarzman/","https://www.forbes.com/profile/jonathan-gray/","https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/r1zqekcxgl"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"blackstone"},{"name":"Kathy Warden","type":"Person","role":"Northrop Grumman CEO; paid 224 times her median worker","country":"US","profile":"Kathy Warden is chair, CEO and president of Northrop Grumman, which designs and produces the centre fuselage for every F-35, including Israel's; it delivered the centre fuselage for Israel's first F-35 in 2015. Her total pay was $25.4M for 2025, up from $24.4M in 2024, which Northrop disclosed as 224 times its median employee's pay. Ten days after 7 October 2023 she told investors what the bombing meant for business: 'As we saw last week, the administration continues to make supplemental requests for urgent needs, including those in Ukraine and Israel.' State Street, BlackRock and Vanguard together own about a quarter of her company. An Israeli F-35 carried out the July 2024 al-Mawasi strike that killed 90 people, according to Campaign Against Arms Trade. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report says the F-35 and F-16 were integral to Israel's ability to drop an estimated 85,000 tons of bombs on Gaza.","id":"PER-NEW-WARDEN","profile_src":["https://aflcio.org/paywatch/NOC","https://www.quiverquant.com/news/NORTHROP+GRUMMAN+CORP+/DE/+($NOC)+Chair,+CEO+and+President+2025+Pay+Revealed","https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2015/11/18/788450/10156674/en/Northrop-Grumman-Delivers-Center-Fuselage-for-First-Israeli-F-35-Aircraft.html","https://www.vice.com/en/article/us-defense-contractor-ceos-see-profit-opportunity-in-israel-hamas-war/","https://caat.org.uk/news/investigation-reveals-israel-used-partly-uk-made-f-35-in-attack-on-gaza-humanitarian-zone-in-july-killing-90/","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"kathy-warden"},{"name":"Gregory J. Hayes","type":"Person","role":"Former RTX chief; saw 'a benefit' for Raytheon in Gaza's bombardment","country":"US","profile":"Gregory J. Hayes led RTX, the former Raytheon Technologies, as CEO until May 2024, when Christopher Calio succeeded him, and as executive chairman until 30 April 2025. In October 2023, days into Israel's assault on Gaza, he gave investors the sales pitch: 'I think really across the entire Raytheon portfolio, you're going to see a benefit of this restocking.' Under RTX, Raytheon's Pratt & Whitney unit builds the F-35's engines, and its R2S joint venture with Rafael won a $1.25B contract in November 2025 to build Tamir interceptors for Iron Dome in Arkansas. Shareholders were not disappointed. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","id":"PER-NEW-HAYES","profile_src":["https://aviationweek.com/defense/supply-chain/greg-hayes-leave-rtx-leadership-april-30","https://www.vice.com/en/article/us-defense-contractor-ceos-see-profit-opportunity-in-israel-hamas-war/","https://investigate.afsc.org/company/rtx","https://www.rtx.com/news/news-center/2025/11/21/r2s-receives-1-25-billion-tamir-production-contract-for-facility-in-camden-arka","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"gregory-j-hayes"},{"name":"Ronald P. O'Hanley","type":"Person","role":"State Street CEO; largest single owner of Lockheed Martin","country":"US","profile":"Ronald P. O'Hanley is chairman and CEO of State Street, the Boston bank whose index funds make it the largest single owner of Lockheed Martin, with about 14.3% ($16.8B) at 30 June 2026, and a 9.27% owner of Northrop Grumman. Those companies build the F-35s and Hellfire missiles supplied to Israel. State Street managed $5.7T at the end of 2025. During the 2026 US–Israeli war on Iran, O'Hanley's public worry was economic: 'I personally worry about what happens if this goes on much longer... Fertilizer is a big one.' The children of Minab did not make his list. The UN Commission of Inquiry, which concluded in September 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza, has called on states to ensure corporations are not involved in aiding genocide; State Street's holdings in the jet makers suggest the message has not yet reached Boston.","id":"PER-NEW-OHANLEY","profile_src":["https://www.statestreet.com/us/en/about/our-people/leadership/ronaldohanley","https://fortune.com/2026/05/08/state-street-ceo-ron-ohanley-iran-ai-investment/","https://13f.info/data/13f/000009375126000583"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"ronald-p-o-hanley"},{"name":"Magen David Adom","type":"Organization","role":"Israel's emergency medical service; magnet for US billionaire money after Oct 7","country":"Israel","profile":"Magen David Adom is Israel's national emergency medical, ambulance and blood service, recognised by law. After 7 October 2023 it became a major destination for US billionaire money: Michael Bloomberg matched nearly $44M for an $88M gift, the largest in American Friends of MDA's history, which paid for ambulances, ballistic vests and helmets, and Forbes reported Bernie Marcus was supporting it alongside the IDF. Marcus and his wife had earlier given $25M toward its national blood centre. This giving came during Israel's assault on Gaza, which the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 was a genocide. The charge here is not against paramedics but against the asymmetry: the same donors put no comparable public sums into Palestinian emergency services, as far as this research found.","id":"ORG-NEW-MDA","profile_src":["https://afmda.org/news/bloomberg-gift/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernie_Marcus"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"magen-david-adom"},{"name":"Tel Aviv University","type":"Organization","role":"Israeli university; record $125M gift from Blackstone's president","country":"Israel","profile":"Tel Aviv University received the largest gift in its history in May 2025: $125M from Blackstone president Jonathan Gray and his wife Mindy for its medical faculty, renamed the Gray Faculty of Medical & Health Sciences. The donors framed it as support for Israel after 7 October 2023. The gift came during Israel's assault on Gaza, which the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 was a genocide. The donors said: 'We can think of no better way to accelerate healing than by supporting an institution that touches the lives of so many.' The healing had a border. No comparable public gift by them to Palestinian universities or hospitals was found. A Wall Street fortune thus rewrote a faculty's name in the middle of a genocide.","id":"ORG-NEW-TAU","profile_src":["https://english.tau.ac.il/news/gray_medical_faculty","https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/r1zqekcxgl"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"tel-aviv-university"},{"name":"PIMCO","type":"Fund/Asset Manager","role":"Allianz bond manager; biggest named buyer of Israeli war bonds, $960M","country":"US","profile":"PIMCO, the bond-investment arm of German insurer Allianz, is named in UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report as the largest asset-manager buyer of the Israeli treasury bonds that funded the assault on Gaza, at $960M, ahead of Vanguard ($546M) and BlackRock ($68M). The report says those bonds 'played a critical role in funding the ongoing assault on Gaza' as Israel's military budget rose from 4.2% to 8.3% of GDP between 2022 and 2024, financed in part by $8B of bonds in March 2024 and $5B in February 2025. PIMCO did not make a weapon; it lent the money to buy them, and it collects the interest. The coupon payments are, in effect, a dividend on the bombardment. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza.","id":"FND-NEW-PIMCO","profile_src":["https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"pimco"},{"name":"Caterpillar","type":"Company","role":"Bulldozer maker; its machines demolish Palestinian homes, says UN","country":"US","profile":"Caterpillar is the US heavy-machinery maker whose bulldozers Israel uses in demolitions. UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's July 2025 report states that 'for decades, Caterpillar Inc. has provided Israel with equipment used to demolish Palestinian homes'. The same report names Vanguard its largest institutional investor (9.8%) and BlackRock its third-largest (7.5%), so that between them the two index giants held 17.3% of the company. Al Jazeera's coverage lists Caterpillar among the more than 60 companies named in the report alongside Lockheed Martin, Elbit Systems, Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon and Palantir. The UN Commission of Inquiry concluded in Sept 2025 that Israel committed genocide in Gaza and urged states to keep corporations from aiding it.","id":"COM-NEW-CATERPILLAR","profile_src":["https://www.ohchr.org/sites/default/files/documents/hrbodies/hrcouncil/sessions-regular/session59/advance-version/a-hrc-59-23-aev.pdf","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/7/3/un-expert-calls-on-world-to-end-trade-with-israels-economy-of-genocide","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"caterpillar"},{"name":"Itamar Ben Gvir","type":"Person","role":"National Security Minister of Israel","country":"Israel","profile":"Itamar Ben Gvir kept a portrait of the Israeli-American mass murderer Baruch Goldstein in his living room before he took office. He has been Israel's national security minister since late 2022, except for two months in early 2025: he quit over the January ceasefire and was reappointed in March. His record started before the job. In 2007 he was convicted of incitement to racism and of supporting a terrorist organisation, and he has at least eight convictions in all. On 17 October 2023 he wrote that \"not a gram of humanitarian aid\" should enter Gaza, only \"hundreds of tons of explosives\". In April 2025 he called for Gaza's food and aid depots to be bombed. By March 2024 his ministry had approved more than 100,000 civilian gun licences. In June 2025 the UK, Canada, Australia, New Zealand and Norway froze his assets and banned him from travelling there. Slovenia, the Netherlands, Spain, Belgium, Ireland and France have also banned him. Turkey issued a genocide arrest warrant for him in November 2025. A minister earns NIS 58,274 a month.","profit_since_2023":{"usd":669424,"basis":"Estimate: 43 months (Jan 2023 to Sep 2026 minus the two-month gap in 2025) x $15,568/month gross, the May 2025 rate reported by the Times of Israel. Salary only; earlier rates were lower, so this slightly overstates. No documented personal enrichment.","status":"estimate","sources":[{"url":"https://www.timesofisrael.com/ministers-struggling-financially-claims-mk-behind-controversial-salary-bill/","publisher":"Times of Israel","date":"2025-05-11","tier":"reputable_media","excerpt":"NIS 58,274 ($15,568) per month ... Prime Minister: NIS 59,000 ($16,280) ... President: NIS 68,000 ($18,764)"}]},"id":"PER-NEW-BENGVIR","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Itamar_Ben-Gvir","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Itamar_Ben-Gvir","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_sanctions_involving_Israel","https://www.anews.com.tr/world/2023/10/17/israeli-ministers-inhumane-comment-after-hospital-massacre-only-one-thing-should-enter-gaza-tons-of-explosives","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/4/23/ben-gvir-us-republicans-support-bombing-gaza-food-and-aid-depots","https://www.timesofisrael.com/ben-gvir-celebrates-issuing-100000-gun-licenses-since-october-7/","https://abc17news.com/news/national-world/cnn-world/2025/11/07/turkey-issues-genocide-arrest-warrants-against-netanyahu-and-other-israeli-officials/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/ministers-struggling-financially-claims-mk-behind-controversial-salary-bill/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"itamar-ben-gvir"},{"name":"Bezalel Smotrich","type":"Person","role":"Finance Minister of Israel; minister in the Israel Ministry of Defense with West Bank powers","country":"Israel","profile":"Bezalel Smotrich controls the money and the land permits. He has been finance minister since late 2022 and is also a minister inside the Israel Ministry of Defense. In February 2023 he was given control of settlement planning, land allocation and state-land registration in the occupied West Bank. In 2005 he was arrested with 700 litres of fuel on suspicion of taking part in a plot to blow up the Ayalon Highway. He said the Palestinian village of Huwara \"needs to be wiped out\". In August 2024 he said letting 2 million civilians in Gaza die of hunger \"might be justified and moral\", regretting only that \"nobody will let us\". He declared 2025 \"the year of sovereignty\". He pushed through 3,401 settler homes in E1 under the slogan \"Burying the idea of a Palestinian state\". In July 2026 he secured NIS 1.3 billion ($434M) for 34 new settlements. His record 2026 budget gives the Israel Ministry of Defense over NIS 142 billion ($45.3B). Eleven countries, from the UK and Canada to France, have sanctioned or banned him.","profit_since_2023":{"usd":700560,"basis":"Estimate: 45 months (Jan 2023 to Sep 2026) x $15,568/month gross, the May 2025 rate reported by the Times of Israel. Salary only; earlier rates were lower, so this slightly overstates. No documented personal enrichment.","status":"estimate","sources":[{"url":"https://www.timesofisrael.com/ministers-struggling-financially-claims-mk-behind-controversial-salary-bill/","publisher":"Times of Israel","date":"2025-05-11","tier":"reputable_media","excerpt":"NIS 58,274 ($15,568) per month ... Prime Minister: NIS 59,000 ($16,280) ... President: NIS 68,000 ($18,764)"}]},"id":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bezalel_Smotrich","https://www.timesofisrael.com/smotrich-handed-sweeping-powers-over-west-bank-control-over-settlement-planning/","https://www.arabnews.com/node/2563111/middle-east","https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2024/11/israels-smotrich-calls-annexation-occupied-west-bank-what-we-know","https://theprint.in/world/israels-smotrich-approves-settlement-in-bid-to-bury-idea-of-palestinian-state/2721096/","https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/07/israel-allocates-434-million-34-new-west-bank-settlements","https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/knesset-approves-2026-budget-the-largest-in-israeli-history-avoiding-early-elections/","https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/article-910242","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bezalel_Smotrich","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_sanctions_involving_Israel","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/6/9/six-countries-sanction-networks-enabling-settler-violence-in-west-bank","https://www.timesofisrael.com/ministers-struggling-financially-claims-mk-behind-controversial-salary-bill/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"bezalel-smotrich"},{"name":"Yoav Gallant","type":"Person","role":"Former military minister of Israel (to Nov 2024); ICC arrest-warrant subject","country":"Israel","profile":"Yoav Gallant was Israel's military minister when the Gaza genocide began. He ran its war machine for 13 months, until Benjamin Netanyahu fired him in November 2024. On 9 October 2023 he announced \"a complete siege on the Gaza Strip. There will be no electricity, no food, no water, no fuel. Everything is closed. We are fighting human animals and we are acting accordingly.\" On 21 November 2024 the International Criminal Court issued a warrant for his arrest. Its judges found reasonable grounds to believe that, from at least 8 October 2023 to at least 20 May 2024, he bore responsibility for the war crime of starvation as a method of warfare and for the crimes against humanity of murder, persecution and other inhumane acts. In September 2025 the UN Commission of Inquiry found that he, Netanyahu and President Isaac Herzog had incited genocide. He left the Knesset on 1 January 2025. No government has sanctioned him, and Amnesty International is asking the UK to. While in office, a minister earned NIS 58,274 a month.","profit_since_2023":{"usd":342496,"basis":"Estimate: 22 months (Jan 2023 to Sep 2026 cut to Jan 2023 to Oct 2024, his time as minister) x $15,568/month gross, the May 2025 rate reported by the Times of Israel. Salary only; earlier rates were lower, so this slightly overstates. No documented personal enrichment.","status":"estimate","sources":[{"url":"https://www.timesofisrael.com/ministers-struggling-financially-claims-mk-behind-controversial-salary-bill/","publisher":"Times of Israel","date":"2025-05-11","tier":"reputable_media","excerpt":"NIS 58,274 ($15,568) per month ... Prime Minister: NIS 59,000 ($16,280) ... President: NIS 68,000 ($18,764)"}]},"id":"PER-NEW-GALLANT","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoav_Gallant","https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/11/1157286","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Criminal_Court_arrest_warrants_for_Israeli_leaders","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.upi.com/Top_News/World-News/2025/01/01/former-defense-chief-Yoav-Gallant-resigns-knesset/8391735768537","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/6/9/six-countries-sanction-networks-enabling-settler-violence-in-west-bank","https://www.timesofisrael.com/ministers-struggling-financially-claims-mk-behind-controversial-salary-bill/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"yoav-gallant"},{"name":"Israel Katz","type":"Person","role":"Military minister of Israel (since Nov 2024)","country":"Israel","profile":"Israel Katz is the man Benjamin Netanyahu chose to replace Yoav Gallant. He was energy minister when the Gaza genocide began, became foreign minister in 2024 and has been military minister since November 2024. His career is a run of threats. Of Gaza he declared: \"They will not receive a drop of water or a single battery until they leave the world.\" In July 2025 he called for a \"humanitarian city\" on the ruins of Rafah. It would first hold 600,000 displaced Palestinians and then all 2.2 million, and people could not leave except to \"voluntarily emigrate\". On 14 June 2025 he warned that \"Tehran will burn\". On 22 August 2025 he promised that \"the gates of hell will soon open\" and that Gaza City could \"turn into Rafah and Beit Hanoun\". In November 2025 Turkey issued a genocide arrest warrant for him. He and Bezalel Smotrich first set the 2026 military budget at NIS 112 billion ($34B); the final budget passed in March 2026 raised it to more than NIS 142 billion. A minister earns NIS 58,274 a month.","profit_since_2023":{"usd":700560,"basis":"Estimate: 45 months (Jan 2023 to Sep 2026) x $15,568/month gross, the May 2025 rate reported by the Times of Israel. Salary only; earlier rates were lower, so this slightly overstates. No documented personal enrichment.","status":"estimate","sources":[{"url":"https://www.timesofisrael.com/ministers-struggling-financially-claims-mk-behind-controversial-salary-bill/","publisher":"Times of Israel","date":"2025-05-11","tier":"reputable_media","excerpt":"NIS 58,274 ($15,568) per month ... Prime Minister: NIS 59,000 ($16,280) ... President: NIS 68,000 ($18,764)"}]},"id":"PER-NEW-KATZ","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel_Katz","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/7/16/israel-presses-ahead-gaza-concentration-camp-plans-despite-criticism","https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/katz-if-khamenei-continues-to-fire-missiles-at-the-israeli-home-front-tehran-will-burn/","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/israeli-defense-minister-warns-of-gaza-citys-destruction-unless-hamas-yields-to-his-countrys-terms","https://abc17news.com/news/national-world/cnn-world/2025/11/07/turkey-issues-genocide-arrest-warrants-against-netanyahu-and-other-israeli-officials/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/smotrich-katz-agree-to-allocate-nis-112-billion-for-defense-spending-in-2026-budget/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/liveblog_entry/knesset-approves-2026-budget-the-largest-in-israeli-history-avoiding-early-elections/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/ministers-struggling-financially-claims-mk-behind-controversial-salary-bill/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"israel-katz"},{"name":"Isaac Herzog","type":"Person","role":"President of Israel","country":"Israel","profile":"Isaac Herzog has been Israel's eleventh president since 7 July 2021. He is the polished face the state sends abroad. In October 2023 he said of Gaza: \"It's an entire nation out there that is responsible. It is not true, this rhetoric about civilians who were not aware or not involved.\" At the turn of 2024 a photograph circulated of him writing \"I rely on you\" on a shell to be dropped on Gaza. He called South Africa's genocide case at the International Court of Justice a \"blood libel\". In September 2025 the UN Commission of Inquiry concluded that he, Benjamin Netanyahu and Yoav Gallant had incited genocide. Swiss federal prosecutors examined a criminal complaint against him during his 2024 visit to Davos. On 30 November 2025 Netanyahu, on trial for bribery, asked him for a pardon. In April 2026 Herzog put the request on hold and pushed for a plea deal instead. The president is paid NIS 68,000 a month, more than the prime minister.","profit_since_2023":{"usd":844380,"basis":"Estimate: 45 months (Jan 2023 to Sep 2026) x $18,764/month gross, the May 2025 rate reported by the Times of Israel. Salary only; earlier rates were lower, so this slightly overstates. No documented personal enrichment.","status":"estimate","sources":[{"url":"https://www.timesofisrael.com/ministers-struggling-financially-claims-mk-behind-controversial-salary-bill/","publisher":"Times of Israel","date":"2025-05-11","tier":"reputable_media","excerpt":"NIS 58,274 ($15,568) per month ... Prime Minister: NIS 59,000 ($16,280) ... President: NIS 68,000 ($18,764)"}]},"id":"PER-NEW-HERZOG","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Herzog","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-02-06/herzog-will-be-aware-controversy-wont-be-arrested-in-australia/106311734","https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20240103-it-could-have-hit-a-child-in-gaza-israel-writer-criticises-presidents-signing-on-shell/","https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2025/09/israel-has-committed-genocide-gaza-strip-un-commission-finds","https://www.upi.com/Top_News/World-News/2026/04/26/herzog-no-pardon-for-netanyahu-yet/7101777212068/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/ministers-struggling-financially-claims-mk-behind-controversial-salary-bill/","https://www.jpost.com/israel-news/article-852555"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"isaac-herzog"},{"name":"Bill Gates","type":"Person","role":"Microsoft co-founder and shareholder; Gates Foundation chair","country":"United States","profile":"Bill Gates co-founded Microsoft in 1975 and never fully left it: he stepped off the board in March 2020 but stayed on as \"Technology Advisor\" to Satya Nadella. Forbes valued him at $104B in March 2023 and $114.2B on 3 October 2026, a $10.2B gain during the years Microsoft's cloud served Israel's army. A 2025 Guardian, +972 and Local Call investigation found that Unit 8200 stored mass intercepts of Palestinian calls on Azure. Three unit sources said the system helped guide deadly air strikes. AP found that Israel's military bought OpenAI models through Azure. Forbes puts his own Microsoft stake below 1%. His foundation's trust sold its last Microsoft shares, worth $3.2B, in early 2026 and now holds about $31B in stocks such as Canadian National Railway and Waste Management. He saw the pandemic coming, and so did his money. In a 2015 TED talk he warned that a virus, \"rather than a war\", could kill over 10 million people. In 2019 his foundation put $55M into BioNTech and held about one million of its shares by late 2021.","profit_since_2023":{"usd":10200000000,"basis":"Forbes net worth $104B (10 Mar 2023) to $114.2B (real-time, 3 Oct 2026). Bloomberg's index, after a July 2025 revision, showed $102B on 7 Apr 2026, so the size of the change depends on the index used.","status":"documented","sources":[{"url":"https://www.forbes.com/sites/forbeswealthteam/2023/07/07/forbes-worlds-billionaires-list-2023-the-top-200/","publisher":"Forbes","date":"2023-03-10","tier":"reputable_media","excerpt":"Bill Gates ... $104 Billion ... To calculate net worths, we used stock prices and exchange rates from March 10, 2023"},{"url":"https://www.forbes.com/profile/bill-gates/","publisher":"Forbes","date":"2026-10-03","tier":"reputable_media","excerpt":"$114.2B ... his Microsoft stake is now less than 1%, Forbes estimates ... Gates, who's donated more than $63.9 billion to the Gates Foundation, announced in 2025 that the foundation will shut down in 20 years"},{"url":"https://nairametrics.com/2026/04/07/bill-gates-net-worth-drops-by-15-6-billion-ytd-2026/","publisher":"Nairametrics (Bloomberg Billionaires Index data)","date":"2026-04-07","tier":"secondary","excerpt":"As of April 7, 2026, Gates' net worth stands at $102 billion, representing a 13.3% year-to-date decline."}]},"id":"PER-NEW-GATES","profile_src":["https://news.microsoft.com/2020/03/13/microsoft-announces-change-to-its-board-of-directors/","https://www.forbes.com/sites/forbeswealthteam/2023/07/07/forbes-worlds-billionaires-list-2023-the-top-200/","https://www.forbes.com/profile/bill-gates/","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/8/7/microsoft-cloud-used-in-israeli-mass-surveillance-of-palestinians-report","https://fortune.com/2025/02/19/israel-microsoft-openai-raises-questions-powerful-tech","https://moneywise.com/news/investing/bill-gates-foundation-microsoft-stock-bill-ackman-pershing-square-capital","https://www.stockinsider.us/portfolio/bill-gates","https://www.geekwire.com/2020/bill-gates-warned-us-covid-19-like-pandemic-watch-ted-talk-2015/","https://www.go-bio.de/gobio/en/news/_documents/bill-gates-invests-in-mainz.html","https://www.morningstar.co.uk/uk/news/217431/whos-made-bank-on-biontech.aspx","https://www.thenation.com/article/economy/bill-gates-investments-covid/","https://nairametrics.com/2026/04/07/bill-gates-net-worth-drops-by-15-6-billion-ytd-2026/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"bill-gates"},{"name":"India","type":"Country","role":"Israel's largest arms customer, drone factory and parts supplier; labour reservoir","country":"India","profile":"India is the biggest node outside the West. Per SIPRI it took 29% of Israel's arms exports in 2021–25. Prime Minister Narendra Modi pledged \"solidarity with Israel\" on 7 October 2023 and, in February 2026, told the Knesset that \"India stands with Israel firmly\", signing 16 agreements with Benjamin Netanyahu as Gaza's dead passed 72,000. Adani–Elbit's Hyderabad plant delivered more than 20 Hermes 900 drones to Israel in early 2024 (Shephard). Amnesty counts at least 2,596 arms shipments from India to Israel between October 2023 and November 2025, including state-owned Munitions India's artillery rounds for Elbit. Around 16,000 Indian workers filled construction jobs emptied of Palestinians in 2024. India's Supreme Court declined to intervene, calling it foreign policy. Charge: supplying the supply chain.","id":"CTY-G-IN","profile_src":["https://www.sipri.org/sites/default/files/2026-03/fs_2603_at_2025.pdf","https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleseDetailm.aspx?PRID=1965443&reg=3&lang=2","https://aljazeera.com/features/2026/2/26/from-gaza-to-defence-five-key-takeaways-from-indian-pm-modis-israel-visit","https://english.news.cn/20260227/b11cf9624d1747bfbb6d3ff9f2b30fe7/c.html","https://www.shephardmedia.com/news/uv-online/india-sends-newly-assembled-male-uavs-to-israel/","https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2026/07/india-continuing-weapons-exports-to-israel-could-risk-complicity-in-ongoing-genocide-in-gaza-new-investigation/","https://m.thewire.in/article/trade/india-israel-palestine-defence-supply-chain-clear-public-warnings","https://www.siasat.com/16000-indian-workers-replace-palestinians-in-israels-construction-sector-in-2024-3157633/","https://www.jurist.org/news/2024/09/india-supreme-court-dismisses-petition-to-halt-arms-exports-to-israel-amid-gaza-conflict/","https://aljazeera.com/features/2026/2/26/from-gaza-to-defence-five-key-takeaways-from-indian-pm-modis-israel-visit"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"india","boost":7},{"name":"Adani-Elbit Advanced Systems India","type":"Company","role":"Hyderabad drone factory; joint venture of Adani Defence & Aerospace and Elbit Systems","country":"India","profile":"Adani-Elbit Advanced Systems India is the joint venture of Gautam Adani's Adani Defence & Aerospace and Israel's Elbit Systems, running what Shephard calls the first private UAV factory in India, at Adani Aerospace Park in Hyderabad. It was the first plant outside Israel to build the Hermes 900, a drone Al Jazeera notes can carry anti-tank guided missiles. In February 2024, Shephard reported it had delivered more than 20 Hermes 900 drones to Israel. Adani's own annual report boasted of exporting the first Hermes 900 fuselage ship set to Israel. Adani called the exports \"non-combat\". The Israeli military is the customer. Charge: assembling the eye in the sky over Gaza.","id":"COM-G-ADANIELBIT","profile_src":["https://www.shephardmedia.com/news/uv-online/india-sends-newly-assembled-male-uavs-to-israel/","https://m.thewire.in/article/diplomacy/indias-refusal-to-back-un-arms-embargo-on-israel-may-be-linked-to-adani-drone-exports","https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2024/6/26/india-exports-rockets-explosives-to-israel-amid-gaza-war-documents-reveal"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"adani-elbit-advanced-systems-india"},{"name":"Munitions India Limited","type":"Company","role":"Indian state-owned ammunition maker; artillery rounds to Elbit","country":"India","profile":"Munitions India Limited is an Indian government-owned ammunition manufacturer, carved out of the old Ordnance Factory Board. Amnesty International's July 2026 investigation \"Made in India\" names it among nine Indian companies supplying Israel's arms industry, and The Wire reports that it exported 1,000 155-mm high-explosive artillery rounds to Elbit Systems, Israel's largest weapons maker and a supplier of the army that has levelled Gaza. A second state-owned firm, Advanced Weapons and Equipment India, sent Elbit 120 81-mm mortar launchers in February 2024. The Indian state is the owner, so the money flows into public accounts. Charge: the taxpayer-owned shell, sold to the shell-firer.","id":"COM-G-MUNITIONSINDIA","profile_src":["https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2026/07/india-continuing-weapons-exports-to-israel-could-risk-complicity-in-ongoing-genocide-in-gaza-new-investigation/","https://m.thewire.in/article/trade/india-israel-palestine-defence-supply-chain-clear-public-warnings","https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2026/07/india-continuing-weapons-exports-to-israel-could-risk-complicity-in-ongoing-genocide-in-gaza-new-investigation/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"munitions-india-limited"},{"name":"Premier Explosives Ltd","type":"Company","role":"Hyderabad-based maker of rocket motors and explosives; Israel export order","country":"India","profile":"Premier Explosives is a listed Hyderabad company that Al Jazeera describes as specialising in fully assembled rocket motors. In June 2024, Al Jazeera reported that its executives told investors \"We have received the pending revenue from the Israel export order, and this has shown an exponential jump in the revenue of the quarter\", in the same period that the Borkum, loaded in India, sailed for Ashdod carrying 20 tonnes of rocket engines and 12.5 tonnes of rockets with explosive charges, and the Marianne Danica left Chennai for Haifa with 27 tonnes of explosives. Spain refused the Marianne Danica a port call. Charge: a quarterly earnings jump, explained by a genocide.","id":"COM-G-PREMIER","profile_src":["https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2024/6/26/india-exports-rockets-explosives-to-israel-amid-gaza-war-documents-reveal","https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2024/6/26/india-exports-rockets-explosives-to-israel-amid-gaza-war-documents-reveal","https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2024/6/26/india-exports-rockets-explosives-to-israel-amid-gaza-war-documents-reveal"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"premier-explosives-ltd"},{"name":"Azerbaijan","type":"Country","role":"Israel's top crude oil supplier; Israeli arms customer; gas licence holder","country":"Azerbaijan","profile":"Azerbaijan is the tank that keeps Israel's jets and tanks moving. Oil Change International finds that Azerbaijani crude supplied over 7 million tonnes, nearly 40% of all crude and fuel delivered to Israel between November 2023 and October 2025, piped through the BP-operated Baku–Tbilisi–Ceyhan line and shipped from Turkey. Tankers chartered by state oil company SOCAR, Vitol and Glencore carried it, per Data Desk. The trade runs both ways: per CNN, more than 60% of Azerbaijan's weapons imports came from Israel between 2017 and 2020. In March 2025 Israel rewarded SOCAR with operatorship of offshore gas exploration licences, shared with BP and NewMed. Charge: fuel for a genocide, paid for in drones.","id":"CTY-G-AZ","profile_src":["https://oc-media.org/azerbaijan-supplied-israel-with-40-of-its-petrol-during-gaza-war-report-finds/","https://oilchange.org/news/countries-fueling-gaza-genocide/","https://docs.datadesk.eco/public/oil-to-israel/","https://www.cnn.com/2023/10/04/middleeast/azerbaijan-israel-weapons-mime-intl/index.html","https://www.offshore-technology.com/news/israel-awards-exploration-licences-to-bp-socar-newmed/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"azerbaijan"},{"name":"Kazakhstan","type":"Country","role":"Second-largest crude supplier to Israel via Russia's CPC terminal; Abraham Accords member","country":"Kazakhstan","profile":"Kazakhstan is Israel's second barrel. Oil Change International counts around 5.3 million tonnes of Kazakh crude shipped to Israel through Russia between November 2023 and October 2025; with Azerbaijan, around 70% of Israel's crude. The CPC blend comes largely from Tengizchevroil, owned by Chevron (50%), ExxonMobil (25%), state firm KazMunayGas (20%) and Lukoil (5%), per Data Desk, so US oil majors profit at the wellhead. In November 2025, after President Kassym-Jomart Tokayev met Donald Trump and joined a call with Netanyahu, Kazakhstan's foreign ministry announced its accession to the Abraham Accords, mid-genocide. Charge: crude, then a handshake.","id":"CTY-G-KZ","profile_src":["https://oc-media.org/azerbaijan-supplied-israel-with-40-of-its-petrol-during-gaza-war-report-finds/","https://oilchange.org/news/countries-fueling-gaza-genocide/","https://docs.datadesk.eco/public/oil-to-israel/","https://astanatimes.com/2025/11/kazakh-mfa-confirms-kazakhstans-accession-to-abraham-accords-after-trump-tokayev-talks/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"kazakhstan"},{"name":"Turkey","type":"Country","role":"Transit state: Azerbaijani crude to Israel loads at Ceyhan despite trade ban","country":"Turkey","profile":"Turkey talks embargo and collects transit fees. Ankara announced a trade ban on Israel in May 2024, and Turkish exports to Israel fell from $460.3M in September 2023 to $1,200 in September 2024. Yet Azerbaijani crude bound for Israel keeps loading at Ceyhan, the last stop of the BP-owned Baku–Tbilisi–Ceyhan pipeline, which Turkish Minute says supplies around 40% of Israel's crude and earns Turkey $1.27 per barrel. Middle East Eye tracked one tanker, the Kimolos, making eight Ceyhan–Ashkelon journeys after the embargo was announced. Turkey's energy ministry insisted the shippers had \"respected\" the ban. Charge: a ban with a pipeline-shaped hole in it.","id":"CTY-G-TR","profile_src":["https://www.turkishminute.com/2024/11/15/turkey-earn-1-27-a-barrel-from-pipeline-that-supplies-much-of-israels-crude-oil/","https://www.turkishminute.com/2024/11/15/turkey-earn-1-27-a-barrel-from-pipeline-that-supplies-much-of-israels-crude-oil/","https://www.turkishminute.com/2024/11/15/turkey-earn-1-27-a-barrel-from-pipeline-that-supplies-much-of-israels-crude-oil/","https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/new-evidence-reveals-routine-oil-shipments-turkey-israel","https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/new-evidence-reveals-routine-oil-shipments-turkey-israel","https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/new-evidence-reveals-routine-oil-shipments-turkey-israel"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"turkey"},{"name":"Egypt","type":"Country","role":"Buyer of Israel's largest-ever gas export deal; gatekeeper of Rafah","country":"Egypt","profile":"Egypt, under Abdel Fattah el-Sisi, signed Israel's largest gas deal mid-genocide: on 7 August 2025 the Leviathan partners (Chevron, NewMed, Ratio) agreed to sell Egypt about 130 bcm of gas through 2040, worth $35B. Netanyahu approved it in December 2025, boasting that it \"greatly strengthens Israel's status as a regional energy power.\" At Rafah, Israel seized the Gaza side of the crossing on 7 May 2024 and aid stopped. Before that, per Middle East Eye and NPR, Hala, a firm owned by Sisi-appointed Sinai tycoon Ibrahim al-Organi, charged fleeing Palestinians at least $5,000 per adult and $2,500 per child, which a source told NPR could not happen without Egyptian security approval. Charge: buying the gas, selling the exit.","id":"CTY-G-EG","profile_src":["https://www.timesofisrael.com/in-israels-largest-gas-deal-leviathan-partners-ink-35-billion-export-deal-with-egypt/","https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/energy/2025/08/07/egypt-signs-35bn-deal-to-import-natural-gas-from-israel/","https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2025/12/17/israel-approves-35bn-gas-deal-with-egypt-netanyahu-says/","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/5/7/israel-takes-control-of-rafah-crossing-gazas-lifeline-whats-going-on","https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/egypt-firm-palestinians-fleeing-war-gaza","https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/egypt-firm-palestinians-fleeing-war-gaza","https://www.npr.org/2024/03/02/1234439113/palestinians-leave-gaza-egypt-hala"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"egypt"},{"name":"Morocco","type":"Country","role":"Abraham Accords state buying Elbit artillery and IAI missile interceptors; port calls for F-35 parts","country":"Morocco","profile":"Morocco normalised with Israel under the 2020 Abraham Accords, and was paid in US recognition of its claim to Western Sahara. Since October 2023 the relationship has deepened, not paused. In February 2025 the Royal Moroccan Armed Forces contracted Elbit Systems for 36 ATMOS 2000 self-propelled howitzers, and Elbit announced production sites in the kingdom. Military Africa reports a $500M deal for IAI's Barak MX air and missile interception system with Israel. Bilateral trade doubled to $116.7M in 2023. In April 2025 Maersk confirmed that ships calling at Tangier and Casablanca carried F-35 parts. Charge: Western Sahara in exchange, artillery on top.","id":"CTY-G-MA","profile_src":["https://www.timesofisrael.com/morocco-anti-israel-activists-set-sights-on-ports-alleging-arms-en-route-to-israel/","https://www.military.africa/2025/02/morocco-acquires-atmos-2000-artillery-from-israeli-elbit/","https://www.military.africa/2025/02/morocco-acquires-atmos-2000-artillery-from-israeli-elbit/","https://www.military.africa/2025/02/morocco-acquires-atmos-2000-artillery-from-israeli-elbit/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/morocco-anti-israel-activists-set-sights-on-ports-alleging-arms-en-route-to-israel/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"morocco"},{"name":"Brazil","type":"Country","role":"Crude supplier to Israel (about 9% of imports) despite Lula's genocide rhetoric","country":"Brazil","profile":"Brazil talks genocide and ships crude. President Lula da Silva recalled his ambassador in February 2024 after a row over his Gaza comments, yet Middle East Eye, citing Oil Change International, reports that Brazil \"quietly became the fourth largest exporter of crude oil to Israel, accounting for nine percent of its imports.\" Direct shipments halted between January and August 2025, and OCI flags evidence of Brazilian crude still reaching Israel indirectly via a Sardinian refinery. Brazil has not imposed a Colombia-style energy embargo. Charge: words for Palestine, barrels for Israel.","id":"CTY-G-BR","profile_src":["https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/colombia-stopped-energy-exports-israel-so-why-did-bds-allies-south-africa-and-brazil-continue","https://www.middleeasteye.net/news/colombia-stopped-energy-exports-israel-so-why-did-bds-allies-south-africa-and-brazil-continue","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/2/19/brazil-recalls-ambassador-to-israel-in-row-over-lulas-gaza-comments","https://oilchange.org/news/countries-fueling-gaza-genocide/"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"brazil"},{"name":"Colombia","type":"Country","role":"Former top coal supplier to Israel; banned exports 2024–2026; ban reversed by new government","country":"Colombia","profile":"Colombia is the contrast case, and the cautionary one. Per UN Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese's report, Colombian coal was 60% of Israel's coal imports in 2023–24, shipped mostly by Glencore (Cerrejón) and Drummond. President Gustavo Petro cut diplomatic ties in May 2024, calling Israel's leader \"genocidal\", banned coal exports by Decree 1047 in August 2024 and closed the loopholes in 2025. Industry estimated the ban cost $200M a year. Even so, 650,000 tonnes left Puerto Drummond for Israel in 2025. In August 2026 the new government of Abelardo de la Espriella announced that exports could resume, and Cerrejón moved to win back the market. Charge pending: relapse.","id":"CTY-G-CO","profile_src":["https://londonminingnetwork.org/2025/07/glencore-among-companies-named-in-un-report-on-israels-economy-of-genocide/","https://londonminingnetwork.org/2025/07/glencore-among-companies-named-in-un-report-on-israels-economy-of-genocide/","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/5/1/colombia-to-cut-diplomatic-ties-with-israel-over-gaza-war-petro-says","https://colombiaone.com/2026/09/29/cerrejon-israel-coal-market-after-colombia-lifts-ban/","https://colombiaone.com/2026/09/29/cerrejon-israel-coal-market-after-colombia-lifts-ban/","https://jacobin.com/2026/05/coal-exports-embargo-colombia-israel","https://colombiaone.com/2026/09/29/cerrejon-israel-coal-market-after-colombia-lifts-ban/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"colombia"},{"name":"South Africa","type":"Country","role":"ICJ genocide applicant that became Israel's largest coal supplier","country":"South Africa","profile":"South Africa took Israel to the International Court of Justice for genocide, and then sold it the coal. Per Albanese's UN report, Glencore's South African shipments were 15% of Israel's coal imports in 2023–24. BDS South Africa monitored at least 17 vessels loading at Richards Bay between October 2023 and December 2025, carrying at least 2.99 million tonnes to Hadera and Ashkelon. After Colombia's ban, exports rose 87% to 474,000 tonnes in the three months to November 2025, and News24 reports that South Africa's share of Israel's seaborne coal is heading to about 55%. No ban has followed. Charge: prosecuting by day, stoking by night.","id":"CTY-G-ZA","profile_src":["https://londonminingnetwork.org/2025/07/glencore-among-companies-named-in-un-report-on-israels-economy-of-genocide/","https://www.dailymaverick.co.za/article/2026-04-12-hypocrisy-critics-slam-sa-for-boosting-coal-exports-to-israel-despite-gaza-genocide-case/","https://www.news24.com/business/climate-future/energy/sa-is-now-israels-largest-coal-supplier-following-colombias-ban-20251218-0818","https://www.news24.com/business/climate-future/energy/sa-is-now-israels-largest-coal-supplier-following-colombias-ban-20251218-0818"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"south-africa"},{"name":"Argentina","type":"Country","role":"Milei government: pledged Jerusalem embassy move, military MoUs, Israeli rifles","country":"Argentina","profile":"Argentina under Javier Milei is Israel's loudest admirer in Latin America. Breaking Defense records Buenos Aires offering \"unwavering support for Israel in the current war\" while widening military cooperation on drones, cyber and border surveillance. On his third state visit in April 2026 Milei and Netanyahu launched the \"Isaac Accords\" and signed three memorandums on military and scientific cooperation, and Milei promised to move the embassy to Jerusalem \"as soon as conditions are met\". In September 2026 Argentine troops received the first batch of ARAD rifles made by Israel Weapon Industries. Charge: chainsaw diplomacy with a Jerusalem address.","id":"CTY-G-AR","profile_src":["https://breakingdefense.com/2024/12/israel-argentina-to-expand-defense-cooperation/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_state_visit_by_Javier_Milei_to_Israel","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_state_visit_by_Javier_Milei_to_Israel","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_state_visit_by_Javier_Milei_to_Israel","https://defensemirror.com/news/42100/Argentina_Accepts_First_Batch_of_Israeli_ARAD_5__ARAD_7_Rifles"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"argentina"},{"name":"Paraguay","type":"Country","role":"Reopened its embassy in Jerusalem in December 2024","country":"Paraguay","profile":"Paraguay moved its embassy to occupied Jerusalem in 2018, retreated to Tel Aviv five months later, and came back mid-genocide. On 12 December 2024 President Santiago Peña reopened it in person, telling Israelis \"we were with you, we are with you, we will stay with the people of Israel forever,\". Israel signed a series of bilateral agreements and a memorandum of understanding with Paraguay during the visit. The move rewards Israel's claim to Jerusalem at the height of the genocide. Charge: real estate in an occupied capital.","id":"CTY-G-PY","profile_src":["https://www.timesofisrael.com/we-are-with-you-visiting-president-reopens-paraguays-embassy-in-jerusalem/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/we-are-with-you-visiting-president-reopens-paraguays-embassy-in-jerusalem/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"paraguay"},{"name":"Philippines","type":"Country","role":"Elbit customer: light tanks, ATMOS guns, munitions; froze new deals Sept 2025 but keeps buying for old ones","country":"Philippines","profile":"The Philippines is an Israeli showroom in Southeast Asia: Elbit ATMOS howitzers and Israel Shipyards attack craft firing Rafael's Spike NLOS missiles. In August 2025 the army awarded Elbit P248M for 100 rounds of 155mm precision-guided ammunition. In September 2025 Secretary of National Defense Gilbert Teodoro told the legislature Manila would stop buying new Israeli systems, then added it would keep buying for existing ones and use its Elbit equipment \"for another twenty years.\" Charge: a pause with a twenty-year service plan.","id":"CTY-G-PH","profile_src":["https://www.bulatlat.com/2025/09/20/philippine-armys-munitions-procurement-from-israel-condemned/","https://www.jpost.com/defense-and-tech/article-867863","https://www.jpost.com/defense-and-tech/article-867863","https://www.jpost.com/defense-and-tech/article-867863"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"philippines"},{"name":"Vietnam","type":"Country","role":"Rafael Spike licence production; IAI spy satellites","country":"Vietnam","profile":"Hanoi, heir to an anti-colonial war, is buying the Israeli arsenal. Calcalist reports that in early 2026 Vietnam signed a deal worth about $250M for Rafael's Spike missiles, including the long-range Firefly, with a factory to be built in Vietnam and know-how transferred from Israel. Less than a year earlier it ordered two intelligence satellites from Israel Aerospace Industries for about $700M (ORF puts it at about $680M). Rafael's SPYDER missile system came about a decade before. Charge: anti-colonial history, colonial hardware.","id":"CTY-G-VN","profile_src":["https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/hkwzvuau11l","https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/hkwzvuau11l","https://www.calcalistech.com/ctechnews/article/hkwzvuau11l","https://www.orfonline.org/expert-speak/israel-s-defence-exports-pivot-to-asia"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"vietnam"},{"name":"Singapore","type":"Country","role":"Selected Elbit's Hermes 900 drone in November 2024","country":"Singapore","profile":"Singapore is a quiet, long-standing customer of the Israeli arms industry. In November 2024, more than a year into the Gaza genocide, Singapore announced its selection of Elbit Systems' Hermes 900, the same drone type that Adani-Elbit's Hyderabad plant was assembling for Israel. ORF counts the Asia-Pacific as 23% of Israeli arms exports in 2024. Charge: a discreet client, served promptly.","id":"CTY-G-SG","profile_src":["https://www.orfonline.org/expert-speak/israel-s-defence-exports-pivot-to-asia","https://www.orfonline.org/expert-speak/israel-s-defence-exports-pivot-to-asia"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"singapore"},{"name":"South Korea","type":"Country","role":"Arms and ammunition exports to Israel continued after October 2023","country":"South Korea","profile":"South Korea, now a top-tier arms exporter, did not stop selling to Israel. Investigative outlet Newstapa, using UN Comtrade and Korean customs data, found at least $814,000 of weapons, ammunition and parts (HS code 93) exported to Israel from October to December 2023, and $471,000 more from January to April 2024, a minimum of $1.285M during the first months of the genocide. The sums are small next to India's, but the data shows the tap was never turned off. Charge: small calibre, no conscience.","id":"CTY-G-KR","profile_src":["https://withnewstapa.org/20241113-israel-weapon/"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"south-korea"},{"name":"Japan","type":"Country","role":"Tested Israeli attack drones for its military; Itochu dropped Elbit after ICJ order","country":"Japan","profile":"Japan plays both sides of the ledger. Its Ministry of Defense spent about ¥9.9B testing multi-purpose and small attack drones, and in five of those contracts the drones were Israeli, Arab News Japan reported in July 2024. In contrast, trading house Itochu ended its memorandum with Elbit Systems in February 2024, explicitly citing the ICJ's 26 January order on preventing genocide. Itochu showed that a company could walk away; the ministry kept shopping. Charge: one arm of Japan Inc. said no, the other took delivery.","id":"CTY-G-JP","profile_src":["https://www.arabnews.jp/en/japan/article_126733/","https://www.arabnews.jp/en/japan/article_126733/","https://www.timesofisrael.com/japans-itochu-to-end-cooperation-with-israels-elbit-amid-gaza-war/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"japan"},{"name":"China","type":"Country","role":"Shanghai port operator SIPG runs Haifa Bayport","country":"China","profile":"China casts itself as a friend of Palestine, while a Shanghai port operator runs part of Israel's main northern port. Shanghai International Port Group (SIPG) holds a 25-year concession, granted in 2015, to run the Haifa Bayport terminal, which began operating in September 2021. The operator has kept the terminal running through the genocide, the war on Lebanon and the strikes on Iran, earning from every container. It is a commercial lifeline, not a weapon, but it is Chinese capital invested in Israel's economy. Charge: rhetoric in New York, cranes in Haifa.","id":"CTY-G-CN","profile_src":["https://www.seatrade-maritime.com/terminals/new-haifa-bay-terminal-inaugurated","https://www.seatrade-maritime.com/terminals/new-haifa-bay-terminal-inaugurated"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"china"},{"name":"Kenya","type":"Country","role":"Police using Israeli riot gear and Cellebrite phone-cracking tools","country":"Kenya","profile":"Kenya's security forces are shopping customers of the Israeli repression industry. During the 2024 protests against the government's fiscal policies, in which over 60 people were killed, footage showed police using \"less lethal\" riot gear made by the Israeli company Ispra, per the Database of Israeli Military and Security Export (DIMSE). In 2026 Citizen Lab found that Cellebrite's forensic extraction tools had been used on the phone of activist Boniface Mwangi while he was in police custody. Technology refined on Palestinians, field-tested on Kenyans. Charge: imported crowd control.","id":"CTY-G-KE","profile_src":["https://dimse.info/kenya/","https://dimse.info/kenya/"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"kenya"},{"name":"Nigeria","type":"Country","role":"Military intelligence identified as client of NSO-linked Circles surveillance","country":"Nigeria","profile":"Nigeria's Defence Intelligence Agency was identified by Citizen Lab in December 2020 as a likely client of Circles, the phone-location surveillance firm affiliated with Israel's NSO Group, which exploits SS7 telecom flaws to track and intercept calls and texts. Nigeria is one of seven African governments Citizen Lab tied to Israeli cyberespionage tools. No post-2023 purchase is documented here, and the profile stands as a pre-existing client relationship. Charge: on the customer list.","id":"CTY-G-NG","profile_src":["https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2020/12/8/nigerias-defence-agency-acquires-spy-equipment-says-report"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"nigeria"},{"name":"Rwanda","type":"Country","role":"NSO Pegasus client that targeted more than 3,500 numbers","country":"Rwanda","profile":"Rwanda under Paul Kagame was among NSO Group's most prolific African clients. Amnesty International and the Pegasus Project found that Rwandan authorities selected more than 3,500 phone numbers of activists, journalists, political opponents, foreign politicians and diplomats for targeting with Pegasus spyware from 2016. Pegasus is made by an Israeli company, NSO Group, and Kigali paid for the same tools that Israeli intelligence perfected on occupied Palestinians, in the opinion of this map. Charge: buying the occupation's surveillance know-how.","id":"CTY-G-RW","profile_src":["https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/press-release/2021/07/rwandan-authorities-chose-thousands-of-activists-journalists-and-politicians-to-target-with-nso-spyware/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"rwanda"},{"name":"Cameroon","type":"Country","role":"Elite BIR unit armed with IWI rifles, overseen by ex-IDF officers","country":"Cameroon","profile":"Cameroon's elite Rapid Intervention Battalion (BIR) is an Israeli product line. DIMSE reports that every BIR recruit since 2009 has been issued a new rifle from Israel Weapon Industries (Galil, Tavor, ACE, Negev), alongside Soltam mortars and howitzers and Elbit-linked hardware, and that the unit has been \"continuously overseen by former IDF officers\". No post-2023 contract is documented here. Charge: an army of occupation, exported as a franchise.","id":"CTY-G-CM","profile_src":["https://dimse.info/cameroon/","https://dimse.info/cameroon/"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"cameroon"},{"name":"Chad","type":"Country","role":"Historic Israeli arms client; recalled ambassador in November 2023","country":"Chad","profile":"Chad is a partial contrast. Israel has long armed N'Djamena's fight against northern rebels, per accounts of the 2019 restoration of ties. On 5 November 2023, Chad recalled its ambassador, accusing Israel of creating an unprecedented humanitarian catastrophe and killing innocent people in Gaza, and it closed the embassy in September 2025, citing finances, while keeping relations. Charge: a client who stepped back, without breaking off.","id":"CTY-G-TD","profile_src":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chad%E2%80%93Israel_relations","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chad%E2%80%93Israel_relations","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chad%E2%80%93Israel_relations"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"chad"},{"name":"Zohran Mamdani","type":"Person","role":"Mayor of New York City (elected Nov 2025)","country":"USA","profile":"Zohran Mamdani, then a New York State assembly member, committed the one offence New York's billionaire class does not forgive: he won. On 4 November 2025 he took just over 50% of the mayoral vote, according to TIME, after super PACs put $28.4M behind Andrew Cuomo in the general election alone, against about $4M from the three biggest pro-Mamdani PACs (Citizens Union). Michael Bloomberg's $13.3M was likely the largest individual sum ever spent backing another candidate in New York. As mayor, in July 2026 he called Benjamin Netanyahu \"the architect of a horrific genocide against the Palestinian people\" and urged Washington to execute the ICC arrest warrant.","id":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","profile_src":["https://time.com/7331119/zohran-mamdani-billionaires-ackman-bloomberg/","https://citizensunion.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/CU-Report-Super-PACs-in-the-2025-New-York-City-General-Election-Seven-Takeaways.pdf","https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/us/2026/07/23/new-york-mayor-mamdani-urges-us-to-enforce-icc-arrest-warrant-for-war-criminal-netanyahu/","https://www.cityandstateny.com/politics/2025/06/pro-cuomo-pac-responsible-nearly-half-all-outside-spending-across-all-nyc-primary-elections-year/406209/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"zohran-mamdani"},{"name":"Andrew Cuomo","type":"Person","role":"Former governor of New York; losing 2025 NYC mayoral candidate","country":"USA","profile":"Andrew Cuomo resigned as governor of New York in 2021 after the state attorney general found he had sexually harassed 11 women, nine of them current and former state employees. In November 2024, warming up for a comeback, he joined Benjamin Netanyahu's legal team to fight the ICC arrest warrants issued over Gaza. His 2025 mayoral run was then carried by billionaire money: Fix the City alone spent $28M for him by 1 November, and Michael Bloomberg gave $13.3M across both rounds. The investment failed twice. Zohran Mamdani beat him in the June primary and again on 4 November.","id":"PER-NEW-CUOMO","profile_src":["https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/politics-news/cuomo-sexually-harassed-multiple-women-including-employees-new-york-attorney-n1275806","https://www.ynetnews.com/article/rkih00s7myl","https://www.dropsitenews.com/p/campaign-spending-mamdani-cuomo-billionaires-bill-ackman-new-york-city-mayoral-race","https://citizensunion.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/CU-Report-Super-PACs-in-the-2025-New-York-City-General-Election-Seven-Takeaways.pdf","https://time.com/7331119/zohran-mamdani-billionaires-ackman-bloomberg/","https://citizensunion.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Citizens-Union-How-Big-Money-Lost-and-Small-Donors-Won-in-the-2025-NYC-Primary.pdf"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"andrew-cuomo"},{"name":"Fix the City","type":"Organization","role":"Pro-Cuomo super PAC, 2025 NYC mayoral race","country":"USA","profile":"Fix the City was the super PAC built to put Andrew Cuomo back in power. It spent $28M across the 2025 primary and general election, 55% of all independent spending in the race (Drop Site News), with Michael Bloomberg as its biggest donor. Its backers included the Lauder family, the Tisch family, Bill Ackman, Daniel Loeb and Alice Walton (Forbes). It lost.","id":"ORG-NEW-FIXTHECITY","profile_src":["https://www.dropsitenews.com/p/campaign-spending-mamdani-cuomo-billionaires-bill-ackman-new-york-city-mayoral-race","https://www.forbes.com/sites/kylemullins/2025/10/24/anyone-but-mamdani-these-billionaires-are-spending-big-to-stop-him-from-becoming-nycs-mayor/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"fix-the-city"},{"name":"For Our City","type":"Organization","role":"Pro-Cuomo super PAC, 2025 general election","country":"USA","profile":"For Our City spent $7.47M backing Andrew Cuomo in the 2025 general election (Citizens Union), including $3.5M from Michael Bloomberg in the final week.","id":"ORG-NEW-FOROURCITY","profile_src":["https://citizensunion.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/CU-Report-Super-PACs-in-the-2025-New-York-City-General-Election-Seven-Takeaways.pdf","https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/bloomberg-pumped-5m-anti-mamdani-164000539.html"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"for-our-city"},{"name":"Defend NYC","type":"Organization","role":"Anti-Mamdani super PAC, 2025 general election","country":"USA","profile":"Defend NYC spent $5.03M in the 2025 general election on the Cuomo side (Citizens Union). Bill Ackman gave it $1M and Joe Gebbia $1M (Drop Site News).","id":"ORG-NEW-DEFENDNYC","profile_src":["https://citizensunion.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/CU-Report-Super-PACs-in-the-2025-New-York-City-General-Election-Seven-Takeaways.pdf","https://www.dropsitenews.com/p/campaign-spending-mamdani-cuomo-billionaires-bill-ackman-new-york-city-mayoral-race"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"defend-nyc"},{"name":"Sensible City","type":"Organization","role":"Pro-Israel-linked anti-Mamdani super PAC","country":"USA","profile":"Sensible City spent just over $100,000 on a digital ad against Zohran Mamdani before the June 2025 primary. Its donors included an ADL board vice chair and an Israel Policy Forum board member (Jewish Insider).","id":"ORG-NEW-SENSIBLECITY","profile_src":["https://jewishinsider.com/2025/06/zohran-mamdani-pro-israel-super-pac-sensible-city/"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"sensible-city"},{"name":"New Yorkers for Lower Costs","type":"Organization","role":"Pro-Mamdani super PAC","country":"USA","profile":"Spent $2.08M supporting Zohran Mamdani in the 2025 general election (Citizens Union).","id":"ORG-NEW-NYLOWERCOSTS","profile_src":["https://citizensunion.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/CU-Report-Super-PACs-in-the-2025-New-York-City-General-Election-Seven-Takeaways.pdf"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"new-yorkers-for-lower-costs"},{"name":"WFP National PAC - NYS IE Committee","type":"Organization","role":"Working Families Party independent-expenditure committee","country":"USA","profile":"Spent $1.12M supporting Zohran Mamdani in the 2025 general election (Citizens Union).","id":"ORG-NEW-WFPIE","profile_src":["https://citizensunion.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/CU-Report-Super-PACs-in-the-2025-New-York-City-General-Election-Seven-Takeaways.pdf"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"wfp-national-pac-nys-ie-committee"},{"name":"Hotel Workers for Stronger Communities","type":"Organization","role":"Union-backed PAC","country":"USA","profile":"Spent $810K supporting Zohran Mamdani in the 2025 general election (Citizens Union).","id":"ORG-NEW-HOTELWORKERS","profile_src":["https://citizensunion.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/CU-Report-Super-PACs-in-the-2025-New-York-City-General-Election-Seven-Takeaways.pdf"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"hotel-workers-for-stronger-communities"},{"name":"Bill Ackman","type":"Person","role":"Pershing Square hedge fund founder","country":"USA","profile":"Bill Ackman gave $1M to Defend NYC and $250,000 to Fix the City in October 2025, $1.75M in total against Zohran Mamdani (Drop Site News).","id":"PER-NEW-ACKMAN","profile_src":["https://www.dropsitenews.com/p/campaign-spending-mamdani-cuomo-billionaires-bill-ackman-new-york-city-mayoral-race"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"bill-ackman"},{"name":"Ronald Lauder","type":"Person","role":"Estée Lauder heir; World Jewish Congress president","country":"USA","profile":"Ronald Lauder, president of the World Jewish Congress since 2007, and his family put over $2.5M into stopping Zohran Mamdani and electing Andrew Cuomo in 2025 (Drop Site News; TIME).","id":"PER-NEW-RLAUDER","profile_src":["https://www.dropsitenews.com/p/campaign-spending-mamdani-cuomo-billionaires-bill-ackman-new-york-city-mayoral-race","https://time.com/7331119/zohran-mamdani-billionaires-ackman-bloomberg/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"ronald-lauder"},{"name":"Joe Gebbia","type":"Person","role":"Airbnb co-founder","country":"USA","profile":"Joe Gebbia gave $1M each to Fix the City and Defend NYC on 15 October 2025 (Drop Site News).","id":"PER-NEW-GEBBIA","profile_src":["https://www.dropsitenews.com/p/campaign-spending-mamdani-cuomo-billionaires-bill-ackman-new-york-city-mayoral-race"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"joe-gebbia"},{"name":"Tisch family","type":"Family","role":"Loews Corporation owners","country":"USA","profile":"The Tisch family gave $1.2M to Fix the City (Forbes).","id":"PER-NEW-TISCH","profile_src":["https://www.forbes.com/sites/kylemullins/2025/10/24/anyone-but-mamdani-these-billionaires-are-spending-big-to-stop-him-from-becoming-nycs-mayor/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"tisch-family"},{"name":"Daniel Loeb","type":"Person","role":"Third Point hedge fund founder","country":"USA","profile":"Daniel Loeb gave $775,000 to Fix the City, New Yorkers For A Better Future Mayor 25 and Defend NYC (Forbes).","id":"PER-NEW-LOEB","profile_src":["https://www.forbes.com/sites/kylemullins/2025/10/24/anyone-but-mamdani-these-billionaires-are-spending-big-to-stop-him-from-becoming-nycs-mayor/"],"profile_status":"documented","slug":"daniel-loeb"},{"id":"PER-NEW-BIDEN","name":"Joe Biden","type":"Person","country":"United States","role":"46th US president, 'Genocide Joe'; signed off the bombs for the genocide in Gaza","profile":"Joseph Robinette \"Joe\" Biden Jr., known to the protesters who hounded him as \"Genocide Joe\" and, with his vice president Kamala Harris, as the \"Butchers of Gaza\", was the 46th US president, the self-declared Zionist who armed the genocide in Gaza. \"You don't have to be a Jew to be a Zionist. And I am a Zionist,\" he boasted at the White House in December 2023. Days into the genocide he claimed to have seen \"pictures of terrorists beheading children\", a claim his own White House walked back, admitting he had seen no such images. In December 2023 his administration twice invoked emergency powers to bypass Congress and rush tank rounds and 155mm artillery parts to Israel; by mid-2024 it had shipped at least 14,000 MK-84 2,000-lb bombs. In April 2024 he signed about $17 billion more for Israel, calling his commitment \"ironclad\". The only shipment he ever paused was one batch of 1,800 2,000-lb and 1,700 500-lb bombs in May 2024. His State Department conceded Israel \"likely\" broke international humanitarian law with US weapons, then accepted its assurances anyway. He vetoed four UN Security Council ceasefire resolutions. Brown University's Costs of War project counted at least $17.9 billion in US military aid to Israel in year one, $21.7 billion by year two. Across his career he took $5.69 million from pro-Israel groups and individuals, per OpenSecrets data.","profile_src":["https://www.malaymail.com/news/world/2023/11/05/protesters-slam-biden-at-pro-palestinian-march-in-washington/100351","https://www.foxnews.com/politics/white-house-issues-brutal-response-inappropriate-nickname-anti-israel-critics","https://www.palestinianyouthmovement.com/statements/biden-butcher-of-gaza","https://www.cbsnews.com/amp/sanfrancisco/news/pro-palestinian-demonstrators-blast-kamala-harris-outside-san-francisco-fundraiser","https://www.foxnews.com/politics/president-biden-tells-crowd-zionist-hanukkah-ceremony-condemns-silence-antisemitism","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2023/10/12/white-house-walks-back-bidens-claim-he-saw-children-beheaded-by-hamas","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/the-biden-administration-once-again-bypasses-congress-on-an-emergency-weapons-sale-to-israel","https://www.forumarmstrade.org/bidenarmsisrael.html","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/4/24/biden-signs-law-securing-billions-in-us-aid-for-ukraine-israel","https://www.npr.org/2024/05/08/1249883976/us-bomb-shipment-israel-rafah","https://theintercept.com/2024/05/10/israel-human-rights-gaza-report/","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2024/11/20/us-vetoes-un-security-council-resolution-demanding-gaza-ceasefire","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-military-aid-for-israel-tops-17-9-billion-since-last-oct-7","https://www.commondreams.org/news/us-aid-to-israel-2024","https://blackwestchester.com/opensecrets-biden-top-recipient-of-pro-israel-money-over-34-years/"],"profile_status":"reported","slug":"joe-biden"}],"rels":[{"id":"REL-00001","t":"edge","a":"PER-00001","b":"FND-00001","rel":"co_founder_chair_ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Larry Fink co-founded BlackRock with seven partners in 1988 and is its chairman and CEO. He heads the world's largest asset manager, a top shareholder in the US arms makers on this map.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0001","ex":"Laurence D. Fink is Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of BlackRock. ... He and seven partners founded BlackRock in 1988","pg":"Leadership bio"}]},{"id":"REL-00002","t":"edge","a":"PER-00002","b":"FND-00001","rel":"co_founder_president","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Robert S. Kapito co-founded BlackRock in 1988 and is its president and a director.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0002","ex":"Rob Kapito is President and a Director of BlackRock ... Prior to founding BlackRock in 1988, Mr. Kapito was a Vice President in the Mortgage Products Group at The First Boston Corporation.","pg":"Leadership bio"}]},{"id":"REL-00003","t":"edge","a":"PER-00003","b":"FND-00004","rel":"chair_ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Abigail Johnson is chairman and CEO of Fidelity's parent FMR, whose funds hold shares in Lockheed Martin, RTX, General Dynamics, Northrop Grumman and Boeing.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0003","ex":"Abigail P. Johnson ... Chairman and Chief Executive Officer","pg":"Chairman's letter / signature"}]},{"id":"REL-00004","t":"edge","a":"PER-00012","b":"COM-00002","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"James D. Taiclet is chairman, president and CEO of Lockheed Martin, maker of the F-35 jets and Hellfire missiles supplied to Israel.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0004","ex":"Lockheed Martin (NYSE: LMT) Chairman, President and CEO Jim Taiclet and CFO Evan Scott will participate in a fireside chat at Morgan Stanley's 14th Annual Laguna Conference","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0079","ex":"Lockheed Martin F-35 and F-16 fighter jets, pivotal to the Israeli air force, have significant carrying and fire capacity.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00005","t":"edge","a":"PER-00013","b":"COM-00004","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Phebe N. Novakovic is chairman and CEO of General Dynamics, named prime contractor for the $2.04B sale of bomb bodies to Israel notified in February 2025.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0005","ex":"Phebe N. Novakovic ... Chairman and Chief Executive Officer","pg":"Leadership"},{"s":"SRC-0039","ex":"estimated cost of $2.04 billion ... The prime contractors will be General Dynamics, located in Garland, TX; Ellwood National Forge","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00006","t":"edge","a":"PER-00014","b":"COM-00001","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Christopher T. Calio is chairman and CEO of RTX, co-maker of David's Sling and maker of AMRAAM missiles.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0006","ex":"the chairman and chief executive officer of RTX, leading a global team of more than 180,000 employees","pg":"Corporate governance bio"}]},{"id":"REL-00007","t":"edge","a":"PER-00015","b":"COM-00003","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Robert K. (Kelly) Ortberg is president and CEO of Boeing, maker of the JDAM kits and GBU-39 bombs used in documented strikes in Gaza.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0007","ex":"Boeing President and CEO Kelly Ortberg sat down with CNBC to discuss the company's progress following the second quarter earnings report.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00008","t":"edge","a":"PER-00016","b":"COM-00006","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Charles Woodburn joined BAE Systems in 2016 and has been chief executive since 1 July 2017.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0008","ex":"He joined BAE Systems in May 2016 as Chief Operating Officer and became Chief Executive on 1 July 2017.","pg":"Board of directors bio"}]},{"id":"REL-00009","t":"edge","a":"PER-00018","b":"COM-00007","rel":"board_chair","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"David Federmann has chaired Elbit Systems' board since August 2023, after serving as vice chair. Elbit is Israel's largest private weapons maker.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0009","ex":"David Federmann has served as chair of the Board since August 2023, after serving as vice chair","pg":"Director nominees"}]},{"id":"REL-00010","t":"edge","a":"PER-00022","b":"COM-00010","rel":"co_founder_ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Alex Karp co-founded Palantir and is its CEO. Palantir agreed a strategic partnership with Israel's Ministry of Defense in January 2024.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0010","ex":"Mr. Karp is one of our co-founders and has served in various positions with us since co-founding Palantir. He has served as our Chief Executive Officer (\"CEO\") since 2005","pg":"Nominees for Director"},{"s":"SRC-0042","ex":"Palantir Technologies Inc. ... has agreed to a strategic partnership with the Israeli Defense Ministry to supply technology to help the country's war effort.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00011","t":"edge","a":"PER-00023","b":"COM-00010","rel":"co_founder","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Peter Thiel co-founded Palantir and has chaired its board since 2003.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0010","ex":"Mr. Thiel is one of our co-founders and has served as the Chairman of our Board of Directors since 2003.","pg":"Nominees for Director"}]},{"id":"REL-00012","t":"edge","a":"PER-00024","b":"COM-00011","rel":"founder_shareholder","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":8.8,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Jeff Bezos founded Amazon in 1994 and has chaired its board since. Amazon's AWS is a Project Nimbus contractor for the Israeli government.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0011","ex":"Mr. Bezos has been Chair of the Board since founding the Company in 1994.","pg":"Director nominees"},{"s":"SRC-V0123","ex":"As of August 26, 2026, Bezos owned approximately 879.3 million Amazon shares, representing an 8.8% stake [fetch-tool rendering]","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-0044","ex":"Google Cloud today announced that it has been selected by the Israeli government to provide public cloud services","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00013","t":"edge","a":"PER-00025","b":"COM-00011","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Andy Jassy has been Amazon's president and CEO since July 2021.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0011","ex":"Mr. Jassy has been President and Chief Executive Officer of the Company since July 2021.","pg":"Director nominees"}]},{"id":"REL-00014","t":"edge","a":"PER-00026","b":"COM-00013","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Sundar Pichai is CEO of Alphabet and Google. Google Cloud is a Project Nimbus contractor for the Israeli government.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0012","ex":"Chief Executive Officer, Alphabet and Google","pg":"p.17, director nominees"},{"s":"SRC-0044","ex":"Google Cloud today announced that it has been selected by the Israeli government to provide public cloud services","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00015","t":"edge","a":"PER-00027","b":"COM-00013","rel":"co_founder","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Larry Page co-founded Google and was CEO of Google (2011–2015) and of Alphabet (2015–2019).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0012","ex":"Co-Founder ... previously served as Google's Chief Executive Officer from April 2011 to October 2015, and as Alphabet's Chief Executive Officer from October 2015 to December 2019.","pg":"p.16, director nominees"}]},{"id":"REL-00016","t":"edge","a":"PER-00028","b":"COM-00013","rel":"co_founder","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Sergey Brin co-founded Google and was president of Google and then of Alphabet.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0012","ex":"Co-Founder ... previously served as Google's President from May 2011 to October 2015, and as Alphabet's President from October 2015 to December 2019.","pg":"p.17, director nominees"}]},{"id":"REL-00017","t":"edge","a":"PER-00029","b":"COM-00016","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Satya Nadella is chairman and CEO of Microsoft, which provides Azure cloud and AI services to Israel's Ministry of Defense.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0013","ex":"Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Microsoft","pg":"Executive bio"},{"s":"SRC-0046","ex":"Microsoft provides IMOD with software, professional services, Azure cloud services, and Azure AI services, including language translation.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00018","t":"edge","a":"PER-00030","b":"COM-00017","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Sam Altman is CEO of OpenAI, whose models AP reported the Israeli military accessed through Microsoft Azure.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0014","ex":"Today, OpenAI CEO Sam Altman addressed the United Nations Security Council on artificial intelligence.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00019","t":"edge","a":"PER-00031","b":"COM-00017","rel":"co_founder_president","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Greg Brockman co-founded OpenAI and is its president.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0015","ex":"Greg Brockman, President and Co-Founder of OpenAI","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00020","t":"edge","a":"PER-00032","b":"COM-00018","rel":"co_founder_ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Dario Amodei co-founded Anthropic and is its CEO.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0016","ex":"Dario Amodei ... Co-Founder and Chief Executive Officer","pg":"Leadership"}]},{"id":"REL-00021","t":"edge","a":"PER-00033","b":"COM-00018","rel":"co_founder_president","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Daniela Amodei co-founded Anthropic and is its president.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0016","ex":"Daniela Amodei ... Co-Founder and President","pg":"Leadership"}]},{"id":"REL-00022","t":"edge","a":"PER-00004","b":"COM-00019","rel":"co_founder_chair","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Larry Ellison co-founded Oracle and is its chairman and chief technology officer. He gave $16.6M to Friends of the IDF in 2017.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0017","ex":"Larry Ellison ... Chairman of the Board and Chief Technology Officer","pg":"Executive Leadership"},{"s":"SRC-0048","ex":"Record $53.8 million raised for IDF soldiers at Beverly Hills gala","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00023","t":"edge","a":"PER-00034","b":"COM-00019","rel":"former_ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"CEO 2014 to Sep 2025; now executive vice chair","st":"documented","ctx":"Safra Catz was Oracle's chief executive from 2014 until September 2025, when Clay Magouyrk and Mike Sicilia were named co-CEOs. She is now Executive Vice Chair of Oracle's board.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0018","ex":"Safra Catz, who has served as Oracle's CEO since 2014, has been appointed to serve as Executive Vice Chair of the Oracle Board of Directors.","pg":"press release"}]},{"id":"REL-00024","t":"edge","a":"PER-00035","b":"COM-00021","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Rajeev Amara has been CEO of Arcline Investment Management since 2018. Arcline bought Kaman, maker of the FMU-152 bomb fuze, for $1.8B in 2024.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0019","ex":"Since 2018, he has served as the Chief Executive Officer of Arcline Investment Management.","pg":"Board of Directors bio"},{"s":"SRC-0041","ex":"Kaman Corporation ... today announced the completion of its acquisition by Arcline Investment Management, L.P.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00025","t":"edge","a":"PER-00037","b":"COM-00024","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Armin Papperger has been CEO of German arms maker Rheinmetall since 1 January 2013.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0020","ex":"CEO since 1 January 2013","pg":"Executive Board"}],"dup":["EUR-0001"]},{"id":"REL-00026","t":"edge","a":"PER-00039","b":"COM-00025","rel":"former_ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"CEO May 2023 to May 2026; succeeded by Lorenzo Mariani","st":"documented","ctx":"Roberto Cingolani was chief executive of the Italian arms maker Leonardo from May 2023 until May 2026. Lorenzo Mariani, nominated by the Italian Treasury as shareholder, has been CEO and General Manager since 7 May 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0021","ex":"Lorenzo Mariani has been Chief Executive Officer and General Manager of Leonardo since 7 May 2026.","pg":"About > Management"}],"dup":["EUR-0002"]},{"id":"REL-00027","t":"edge","a":"PER-00045","b":"COM-00029","rel":"founder_ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Mathios Rigas is founder and CEO of Energean, an oil and gas producer.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0022","ex":"Mathios Rigas, Chief Executive Officer of Energean","pg":null}],"dup":["EUR-0003"]},{"id":"REL-00029","t":"edge","a":"COM-00035","b":"COM-00007","rel":"controls","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":"41.2","date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Federmann Enterprises Ltd. held 19,318,508 Elbit shares as of 17 June 2026, including shares held via Heris. Through it, Michael Federmann controls the vote of about 41.2% of Elbit's shares, enough to control Israel's largest private weapons maker.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0009","ex":"Federmann Enterprises Ltd. ... 19,318,508 ... 41.2% of our outstanding Shares","pg":"Beneficial ownership table"}]},{"id":"REL-00030","t":"edge","a":"PER-00017","b":"COM-00007","rel":"indirect_economic_interest_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":"5.1","date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Michael Federmann holds about a 5.1% indirect economic interest in Elbit Systems through the Federmann family holding structure, and controls the 41.2% voting block (2026 proxy statement).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0009","ex":"with Michael Federmann holding an approximately 5.1% economic interest","pg":"Beneficial ownership, footnote (2)"}]},{"id":"REL-00031","t":"edge","a":"PER-00018","b":"COM-00007","rel":"indirect_economic_interest_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":"8.16","date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"David Federmann, Elbit's chair, holds about an 8.16% indirect economic interest in Elbit through the family holding structure (2026 proxy statement).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0009","ex":"David Federmann holding an approximately 8.16% economic interest","pg":"Beneficial ownership, footnote (2)"}]},{"id":"REL-00032","t":"edge","a":"PER-00019","b":"COM-00007","rel":"indirect_economic_interest_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":"6.12","date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Gideon Federmann holds about a 6.12% indirect economic interest in Elbit Systems through the family holding structure (2026 proxy statement).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0009","ex":"each of Gideon and Daniel Federmann holding an approximately 6.12% economic interest","pg":"Beneficial ownership, footnote (2)"}]},{"id":"REL-00033","t":"edge","a":"PER-00020","b":"COM-00007","rel":"indirect_economic_interest_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":"6.12","date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Daniel Federmann holds about a 6.12% indirect economic interest in Elbit Systems through the family holding structure (2026 proxy statement).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0009","ex":"each of Gideon and Daniel Federmann holding an approximately 6.12% economic interest","pg":"Beneficial ownership, footnote (2)"}]},{"id":"REL-00034","t":"edge","a":"PER-00021","b":"COM-00007","rel":"trust_economic_interest_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":"7.2","date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Irith Federmann-Landeau, Michael Federmann's sister, holds an indirect non-voting economic interest of about 7.2% in Elbit through a trust of which he is trustee (2026 proxy statement).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0009","ex":"holds an indirect non-voting economic interest of approximately 7.2% in our outstanding Shares","pg":"Beneficial ownership, footnote (2)"}]},{"id":"REL-00035","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00005","b":"COM-00009","rel":"owns","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":100,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The Israeli state directly holds 99.9% of Rafael Advanced Defense Systems, maker of David's Sling, SPYDER and Iron Dome interceptors. Rafael's profits go to the state waging the war.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0024","ex":"Rafael is a government-owned company, with 99.9% of its shares directly held by the Israeli government and the remainder held by various government entities, each possessing a fractional share.","pg":"p.65, Proper Corporate Governance"}]},{"id":"REL-00036","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00005","b":"COM-00008","rel":"owns","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":100,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Israel Aerospace Industries is a wholly state-owned company, founded in 1966. It is prime contractor for Arrow 3 and maker of Barak MX.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0025","ex":"Israel Aerospace Industries Ltd. (\"the Company\") was founded in 1966 and is a \"wholly-owned government company\", as this term is defined in the Israeli Government Companies Law, 1975","pg":"p.16, Note 1a"}]},{"id":"REL-00037","t":"edge","a":"COM-00003","b":"WPN-00001","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":7479640772,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-05-24","st":"documented","ctx":"Boeing makes JDAM guidance kits. In May 2024 the US Air Force awarded it a $7.48B contract for more kits, including foreign military sales. Amnesty and Bellingcat documented JDAMs in deadly strikes in Gaza.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0026","ex":"The Boeing Co., doing business as Boeing Defense Space and Security, St. Louis, Missouri, was awarded a $7,479,640,772 fixed-price-incentive-fee, firm-fixed-price, indefinite-delivery/indefinite-quantity contract action for Joint Direct Attack Munition (JDAM).","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0253","ex":"US-made Joint Direct Attack Munitions (JDAM) were used by the Israeli military in two deadly, unlawful air strikes on homes full of civilians in the occupied Gaza Strip ... On October 10, an air strike on the al-Najjar family home in Deir al-Balah killed 24 people. ... On October 22, an air strike on the Abu Mu'eileq family home in the same city killed 19 people.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0093","ex":"the analysis recorded 79 geolocated incidents where remnants of these three models of US-made munitions were either found in the aftermath of a strike or were captured in visual imagery in the moments before impact. ... Khadija school in Deir Al Balah was targeted in three rounds of airstrikes on July 27, 2024 that used both GBU-39 bombs and MK-80 series bombs equipped with JDAM kits.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0001"]},{"id":"REL-00038","t":"edge","a":"COM-00003","b":"WPN-00002","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Boeing is the maker of the KMU-556 JDAM tail kit for 2,000-lb MK-84 bombs, and was named principal contractor for the 13,000 KMU-556 kits in the US sale to Israel notified on 7 February 2025.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0027","ex":"thirteen thousand (13,000) KMU-556 ... The Boeing Company, located in St. Louis, MO; ATK Tactical Systems Company LLC, located in Rocket Center, WV","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0002"]},{"id":"REL-00039","t":"edge","a":"COM-00003","b":"WPN-00006","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The US Air Force selected Boeing as prime contractor for the GBU-39 Small Diameter Bomb. CNN and NPR traced GBU-39s to the Rafah tent-camp strike (26 May 2024) and the Nuseirat UN school strike (6 June 2024).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0028","ex":"Boeing was selected as the prime contractor to develop and produce the Small Diameter Bomb Weapon System.","pg":"Fact sheet"},{"s":"SRC-V0257","ex":"the tail of a US-made GBU-39 small diameter bomb (SDB) is visible, according to four explosive weapons experts ... The GBU-39, which is manufactured by Boeing, is a high-precision munition ... At least 45 people were killed and more than 200 others injured","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0258","ex":"The munition used was a GBU-39 small-diameter bomb, according to a Pentagon official and a former U.S. Air Force official. ... the 2 a.m. strike killed at least 32 people, including seven children","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0003"]},{"id":"REL-00040","t":"edge","a":"COM-00002","b":"WPN-00007","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Lockheed Martin (Troy, Alabama) makes the AGM-114 Hellfire and is principal contractor for the 3,000 Hellfires notified for Israel on 7 February 2025.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0029","ex":"The principal contractor will be the Lockheed Martin Corporation, located in Troy, AL.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0004"]},{"id":"REL-00041","t":"edge","a":"COM-00020","b":"WPN-00008","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"historical; the fuze unit now operates as Precision Fuzing & Sensors","st":"documented","ctx":"Kaman made the FMU-152 Joint Programmable Fuze, winning a $324M order in 2018. The business passed to Arcline in 2024 and now operates as Precision Fuzing & Sensors.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0030","ex":"Kaman Corp. (NYSE:KAMN) announced today that its Aerospace segment has been awarded a direct commercial sale (DCS) order for the procurement of Joint Programmable Fuzes (JPF) with an expected total value of $324 million.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-0041","ex":"Kaman Corporation ... today announced the completion of its acquisition by Arcline Investment Management, L.P.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0005"]},{"id":"REL-00043","t":"edge","a":"COM-00007","b":"WPN-00015","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Elbit Systems makes the PULS rocket launcher, which the Israeli army used extensively in Gaza and Lebanon and which Elbit exports to Denmark, the Netherlands, Germany and Greece.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0031","ex":"Elbit Systems Awarded Two Contracts In An Aggregate Amount of $252 Million to Supply ATMOS and PULS Artillery Systems","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0270","ex":"The PULS rocket artillery system is being used extensively by the Israeli Defence Forces (IDF) in the ongoing war in Gaza and Lebanon. ... The very accurate rockets launched by the systems have destroyed a great number of targets on the two fronts","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0269","ex":"fire a variety of ammunition types to various ranges from the same position, to ranges of up to 300km ... Hellenic Armed Forces Select Elbit Systems' PULS Rocket Artillery System","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0007"]},{"id":"REL-00044","t":"edge","a":"COM-00009","b":"WPN-00011","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Rafael Advanced Defense Systems leads the industrial team for David's Sling, co-produced with RTX. Finland chose the system in 2023.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0032","ex":"The Ministry of Defence has authorised the Finnish Defence Forces to procure the David's Sling system as the next long-range air defence system of Finland.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0008"]},{"id":"REL-00045","t":"edge","a":"COM-00009","b":"WPN-00012","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"SPYDER is a mobile anti-aircraft missile system and trademark of Rafael Advanced Defense Systems. It is part of Greece's €3B 2026 deal.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0033","ex":"One-in-All SPYDER ... a Trademark of RAFAEL Advanced Defense Systems Ltd","pg":"PDF brochure, p.1"}],"dup":["CW-0009"]},{"id":"REL-00046","t":"edge","a":"COM-00008","b":"WPN-00013","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":null,"ev":[{"s":"SRC-0034","ex":"Under the 560 million euro agreement signed in 2024, the Israel Ministry of Defense (IMOD), through its Defense Export Directorate (SIBAT), together with Israel Aerospace Industries (IAI), announced today the delivery of the BARAK MX air-defense system","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0010"]},{"id":"REL-00047","t":"edge","a":"COM-00009","b":"WPN-00010","rel":"subcontractor_for","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"reported","ctx":"Arrow 3 is an exo-atmospheric missile interceptor whose prime contractor is Israel Aerospace Industries (IAI), developed with the Israel MOD's Homa Directorate and the US Missile Defense Agency. Rafael Advanced Defense Systems and the state-owned Tomer are reported as key subcontractors for the interceptor, and Elbit Systems developed the command and control system.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0035","ex":"Tomer, a government-owned company, and Rafael Advanced Defense Systems are key subcontractors for the development and production of the Arrow 3 interceptor.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0011"]},{"id":"REL-00048","t":"edge","a":"COM-00008","b":"WPN-00010","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Israel Aerospace Industries is prime contractor for Arrow 3 development and production. In January 2026 it booked a $3.1B follow-on contract for Germany.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0036","ex":"IAI ... the prime contractor for the system's development and production","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0263","ex":"Israel Aerospace Industries has signed a contract worth approximately USD 3.1 billion with Israel Ministry of Defense for the expansion of Germany's procurement of the Arrow 3 missile defence system. ... The total value of the Arrow 3 programme is expected to exceed USD 6.5 billion, making it the largest defence export deal in Israel's history","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0012"]},{"id":"REL-00050","t":"edge","a":"COM-00001","b":"WPN-00016","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Raytheon (RTX) makes the AMRAAM air-to-air missile. On 28 September 2026 it won a $20.7B five-year multi-year contract to raise output to record levels.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0038","ex":"Raytheon, an RTX (NYSE: RTX) business, will accelerate production of AMRAAM® missiles to record-setting levels under the terms of a five-year multi-year contract","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0014"]},{"id":"REL-00051","t":"edge","a":"COM-00003","b":"CTR-00001","rel":"principal_contractor_for","amt":6750000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Boeing (with ATK Tactical Systems, L3Harris and McAlester Army Ammunition Plant) is principal contractor for the $6.75B JDAM and munitions sale to Israel notified on 7 February 2025.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0027","ex":"an estimated cost of $6.75 billion ... The Boeing Company, located in St. Louis, MO; ATK Tactical Systems Company LLC, located in Rocket Center, WV; L3Harris Fuzing and Ordnance Systems, located in Cincinnati, OH; and McAlester Army Ammunition Plant","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0015"]},{"id":"REL-00052","t":"edge","a":"CTR-00001","b":"WPN-00002","rel":"includes","amt":13000,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The 7 February 2025 US sale to Israel includes 13,000 KMU-556 JDAM guidance kits, which turn 2,000-lb MK-84 bomb bodies into GPS-guided bombs. That is enough to guide 13,000 one-ton bombs, the class of bomb the New York Times found left 208 large craters in a southern Gaza 'safe' area.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0027","ex":"thirteen thousand (13,000) KMU-556","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0255","ex":"According to the New York Times, it has identified 208 craters at least 40 feet across in an area of southern Gaza where Israel told civilians to move to safety. ... In 2024, the Biden administration blocked the transfer of 2,000-pound bombs amid public pressure urging Washington to stop Israel's invasion of Rafah, which occurred anyway.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0016"],"quantity_type":"approved maximum"},{"id":"REL-00053","t":"edge","a":"COM-00002","b":"CTR-00002","rel":"principal_contractor_for","amt":660000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Lockheed Martin is principal contractor for the 3,000 AGM-114 Hellfire missiles, estimated at $660M, in the sale to Israel notified on 7 February 2025.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0029","ex":"3,000 AGM-114 Hellfire Air-to-Ground Missiles ... an estimated cost of $660 million ... The principal contractor will be the Lockheed Martin Corporation, located in Troy, AL.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0017"]},{"id":"REL-00054","t":"edge","a":"CTR-00002","b":"WPN-00007","rel":"includes","amt":3000,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The 7 February 2025 Hellfire sale to Israel covers 3,000 AGM-114 missiles, used by Israeli Apache helicopters and drones. Bellingcat found Hellfires in Gaza strikes on a clinic, hospital-area tents and a school.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0029","ex":"3,000 AGM-114 Hellfire Air-to-Ground Missiles","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0093","ex":"A Hellfire missile was used in a June 2024 strike on a health clinic in Gaza City that killed Hani al-Jafarawi, the director of ambulance and emergency services in Gaza. ... Four of these strikes used Hellfire missiles to target tents within approximately 150 meters of the Al Aqsa Martyr's Hospital Main Complex in Deir Al Balah. ... A July 2025 strike on Cairo Basic School where five people were reported killed and where remnants of a Hellfire missile was found.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0018"],"quantity_type":"approved maximum"},{"id":"REL-00055","t":"edge","a":"COM-00004","b":"CTR-00003","rel":"named_principal_contractor_for","amt":2040000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"General Dynamics (Garland, Texas) is named prime contractor, with Ellwood National Forge and McAlester Army Ammunition Plant, for the $2.04B sale of bomb bodies and penetrators to Israel notified on 28 February 2025.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0039","ex":"estimated cost of $2.04 billion ... The prime contractors will be General Dynamics, located in Garland, TX; Ellwood National Forge Company, located in Irvine, PA; and McAlester Army Ammunition Plant","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0019"]},{"id":"REL-00056","t":"edge","a":"COM-00022","b":"COM-00004","rel":"acquired_facility_from","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2025-04-02","st":"documented","ctx":"REPKON USA announced on 2 April 2025 that it had bought General Dynamics' Ordnance and Tactical Systems operations in Garland, Texas, the site named as prime contractor in the February 2025 bomb-body sale to Israel.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0040","ex":"GARLAND, Texas, April 2, 2025 /PRNewswire/ -- REPKON USA ... announced its acquisition of one of the operating locations of General Dynamics – Ordnance and Tactical Systems, known as GD-OTS Garland Operations.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0020"]},{"id":"REL-00057","t":"edge","a":"COM-00021","b":"COM-00020","rel":"acquired","amt":1800000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Arcline Investment Management completed its $1.8B acquisition of Kaman, maker of the FMU-152 bomb fuze, in April 2024.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0041","ex":"Kaman Corporation ... today announced the completion of its acquisition by Arcline Investment Management, L.P. (\"Arcline\") in an all-cash transaction with a total enterprise value of approximately $1.8 billion.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0021"]},{"id":"REL-00058","t":"edge","a":"COM-00010","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"strategic_partnership_with","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-01","st":"reported","ctx":"On 2024-01-12 Bloomberg reported that Palantir Technologies agreed a strategic partnership with the Israel Ministry of Defense to supply technology in support of war-related missions, announced while Palantir held its first board meeting in Tel Aviv. Financial terms were not disclosed.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0042","ex":"Palantir Technologies Inc. ... has agreed to a strategic partnership with the Israeli Defense Ministry to supply technology to help the country's war effort.","pg":"p.1"}],"dup":["CW-0022","TECH-0001"]},{"id":"REL-00059","t":"edge","a":"COM-00012","b":"CTR-00004","rel":"contractor_for","amt":1200000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2021; joint contract with Google Cloud, total about $1.2bn (ILS 4bn)","st":"documented","ctx":"Project Nimbus is an Israeli government cloud-services framework led by the Government Procurement Administration; in April 2021 AWS and Google Cloud were selected as the winners, with Microsoft and Oracle losing. The project was reported at about NIS 4 billion (~$1.2 billion) in total for both providers, with an initial 7-year term extendable to 23 years; Amazon's release says Israel selected AWS as primary cloud provider and AWS committed to open a Tel Aviv region.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0043","ex":"The government of Israel announced that it has selected AWS as its primary cloud provider as part of the 'Nimbus' contract for government ministries and subsidiaries.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0079","ex":"Israel awarded Alphabet Inc (Google) and Amazon.com Inc. a $1.2 billion contract (Project Nimbus) ... Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon grant Israel virtually government-wide access to their cloud and AI technologies.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0118","ex":"Google, AWS win $1.2 billion Israel Nimbus tender for cloud services (headline)","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0023","TECH-0002"]},{"id":"REL-00060","t":"edge","a":"COM-00015","b":"CTR-00004","rel":"contractor_for","amt":1200000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2021; joint contract with AWS, total about $1.2bn (ILS 4bn)","st":"documented","ctx":"Project Nimbus is an Israeli government cloud-services framework; in April 2021 Google Cloud and AWS were selected as the winners, with Microsoft and Oracle losing. The project was reported at about NIS 4 billion (~$1.2 billion) in total for both providers, with an initial 7-year term extendable to 23 years; Google's announcement says it will serve government ministries, authorities, health organisations, higher education and municipalities.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0044","ex":"Google Cloud today announced that it has been selected by the Israeli government to provide public cloud services to help address the country's challenges within the public sector, including in healthcare, transportation, and education.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0079","ex":"Israel awarded Alphabet Inc (Google) and Amazon.com Inc. a $1.2 billion contract (Project Nimbus) ... Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon grant Israel virtually government-wide access to their cloud and AI technologies.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0118","ex":"Google, AWS win $1.2 billion Israel Nimbus tender for cloud services (headline)","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0024","TECH-0003"]},{"id":"REL-00061","t":"edge","a":"COM-00012","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"investment_in","amt":7200000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"announced Aug 2023; planned investment through 2037","st":"documented","ctx":"AWS announced in August 2023 that it plans to invest about $7.2B (ILS 26.6B) in Israel through 2037 via its new cloud region.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0045","ex":"AWS ... is planning to invest an estimated $7.2 billion (approximately ILS 26.6 billion) in Israel through 2037 via the new AWS Israel (Tel Aviv) Region.","pg":null}],"dup":["TECH-0004"]},{"id":"REL-00062","t":"edge","a":"COM-00016","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"provides_cloud_ai_services_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023-10","st":"documented","ctx":"Microsoft confirmed in May 2025 that it provides Israel's Ministry of Defense with software, Azure cloud and Azure AI services, and gave emergency support after 7 October 2023. In September 2025 it disabled some IMOD subscriptions after finding evidence supporting Guardian reporting on Azure storage of intercepted Palestinian phone calls.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0046","ex":"Microsoft provides IMOD with software, professional services, Azure cloud services, and Azure AI services, including language translation. ... Microsoft provided limited emergency support to the Israeli government in the weeks following October 7, 2023","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0274","ex":"evidence that supports elements of The Guardian's reporting. This evidence includes information relating to IMOD consumption of Azure storage capacity in the Netherlands and the use of AI services. ... specified IMOD subscriptions and their services, including their use of specific cloud storage and AI services and technologies.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0025","TECH-0005"]},{"id":"REL-00063","t":"edge","a":"COM-00017","b":"COM-00016","rel":"models_delivered_via","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"reported","ctx":"An AP investigation (February 2025) reported that the Israeli military buys OpenAI models through Microsoft's Azure cloud platform; OpenAI said it has no partnership with Israel's military. Microsoft stated on 2025-05-15 that it provides Israel's Ministry of Defense with Azure cloud and Azure AI services, and on 2025-09-25 said it would cease and disable specified IMOD subscriptions including certain cloud storage and AI services.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0047","ex":"Advanced AI models are provided through OpenAI, the maker of ChatGPT, through Microsoft's Azure cloud platform, where they are purchased by the Israeli military, the documents and data show.","pg":null}],"dup":["TECH-0006"]},{"id":"REL-00064","t":"edge","a":"PER-00004","b":"ORG-00013","rel":"donated_to","amt":16600000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"reported","ctx":"Oracle co-founder Larry Ellison gave $16.6 million to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces at its November 2017 Beverly Hills gala, described at the time as the largest single gift in FIDF history, to fund well-being facilities on a training campus for co-ed infantry units. Variety reported a separate $9 million gift from Ellison at the 2014 gala.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0048","ex":"Larry Ellison, the co-founder of Oracle and its executive chairman gave $16.6 million — the largest single gift in FIDF history.","pg":null}],"dup":["DON-0001"]},{"id":"REL-00065","t":"edge","a":"PER-00005","b":"ORG-00013","rel":"donated_to","amt":1700000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"reported","ctx":"The Paul E. Singer Foundation, the private foundation of Elliott Management founder Paul Singer, reported grants to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces on its IRS Form 990-PF, including $1,040,000 in the fiscal year ending November 2015 and smaller grants of $36,000 and $40,000 in fiscal 2012 and 2013.","ev":[],"dup":["DON-0002"]},{"id":"REL-00066","t":"edge","a":"PER-00006","b":"ORG-00013","rel":"donated_to","amt":13000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"reported","ctx":"The Marcus Foundation, the private foundation of Home Depot co-founder Bernie Marcus, reported on its 2012 IRS Form 990-PF grants of $2,025,000 to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces, mainly $2 million for the FIDF Lone Soldiers Program. IRS e-file data compiled by philanthropy.org show further FIDF grants of about $4.0 million in 2020-2022 and $4.1 million in 2023-2024.","ev":[],"dup":["DON-0003"]},{"id":"REL-00067","t":"edge","a":"PER-00008","b":"ORG-00013","rel":"donated_to","amt":6800000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"reported","ctx":"The Koum Family Foundation of WhatsApp co-founder Jan Koum gave $5.3 million to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces in 2018, according to Jewish Insider's review of its tax filing. IRS e-file data compiled by philanthropy.org show five further FIDF grants totalling about $1.1 million in 2020-2023.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0049","ex":"A $5.3 million donation was made to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces, which sponsors programs and projects for current and former IDF soldiers.","pg":null}],"dup":["DON-0004"]},{"id":"REL-00068","t":"edge","a":"PER-00011","b":"ORG-00013","rel":"former_board_member_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"national board member until about January 2017","st":"reported","ctx":"Jared Kushner served on the national board of Friends of the Israel Defense Forces until about January 2017, when his name was removed from the board listing after Haaretz asked about the affiliation as he became a senior White House adviser.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0050","ex":"Jared Kushner's name has been scrubbed from the national board of the Friends of the Israel Defense Forces, apparently following questions from the press about his continued involvement in the group.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-00069","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00008","b":"CTR-00006","rel":"funds_or_procures","amt":3500000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"initial contract signed 2023-09-28","st":"reported","ctx":"Germany signed an agreement on 2023-09-28 to buy the Israeli Arrow 3 missile-interception system from Israel Aerospace Industries, valued by Israel's Military ministry at about $3.5 billion (nearly EUR 4 billion per IAI). The first system was handed over in December 2025, and an expansion of about $3.1 billion was announced by IAI in January 2026, bringing the total above $6.5 billion.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0051","ex":"The Israeli Defense Ministryd ... $3.5 billion; IAI chairman Boaz Levy said the complete deal would reach approximately €4 billion. (fetch-tool paraphrase of article wording)","pg":null}],"dup":["EUR-0005"]},{"id":"REL-00070","t":"edge","a":"CTR-00006","b":"WPN-00010","rel":"includes","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Germany's procurement covers Arrow 3 interceptors and launchers from IAI. The first battery was handed over in December 2025, and a $3.1B follow-on contract followed in January 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0036","ex":"This follow-on contract with Germany, expanding the procurement of the Arrow 3 system represents another mega deal for Israel Aerospace Industries.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0261","ex":"Israel on Wednesday handed over its Arrow 3 long-range missile defense system to the German Air Force in a ceremony at an airbase south of Berlin ... has downed hundreds of ballistic missiles launched at Israel by Iran and the Iran-backed Houthi terror group in Yemen, with an interception rate of 86 percent during the 12-day conflict","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0026","EUR-0006"]},{"id":"REL-00071","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00009","b":"CTR-00007","rel":"funds_or_procures","amt":317000000,"cur":"EUR","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Finland's Ministry of Defence authorised the purchase of David's Sling in April 2023. The contract was signed on 12 November 2023 for about €317M (€213M main contract plus €103M options).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0032","ex":"The Ministry of Defence has authorised the Finnish Defence Forces to procure the David's Sling system as the next long-range air defence system of Finland.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0267","ex":"The contract, described as historic, is valued at around €317 million. ... a main contract for approximately €213 million and the immediate exercise of options related to the main contract for €103 million.","pg":null}],"dup":["EUR-0007"]},{"id":"REL-00072","t":"edge","a":"CTR-00007","b":"WPN-00011","rel":"includes","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Finland's procurement covers David's Sling launchers, Stunner interceptors and Israeli radars, with deliveries expected from 2025 and full capability by 2030.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0032","ex":"The Ministry of Defence has authorised the Finnish Defence Forces to procure the David's Sling system","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0276","ex":"David's Sling initial deliveries are expected in 2025, with full operational capability projected by 2030.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0027","EUR-0008"]},{"id":"REL-00073","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00010","b":"CTR-00008","rel":"funds_or_procures","amt":252000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"reported","ctx":"Denmark bought 8 PULS rocket launchers and 19 ATMOS howitzers from Elbit (announced January 2023). Elbit reported $252M in matching contracts with a European NATO country.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0052","ex":"8 PULS-raketkastere og 19 ATMOS-artilleri-pjecer fra den israelske producent Elbit","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-0031","ex":"Elbit Systems Awarded Two Contracts In An Aggregate Amount of $252 Million to Supply ATMOS and PULS Artillery Systems","pg":null}],"dup":["REL-00075","EUR-0009","EUR-0011"]},{"id":"REL-00076","t":"edge","a":"CTR-00008","b":"WPN-00015","rel":"includes","amt":133000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Denmark's January 2023 Elbit order included 8 PULS multiple rocket launchers, with deliveries starting in 2023; Janes reported the PULS contract at about USD 133 million.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0052","ex":"Konkret er der tale om 8 PULS-raketkastere og 19 ATMOS-artilleri-pjecer fra den israelske producent Elbit.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0029","EUR-0012"]},{"id":"REL-00077","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00011","b":"CTR-00009","rel":"funds_or_procures","amt":560000000,"cur":"EUR","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Slovakia agreed to pay about €560M for IAI's Barak MX anti-aircraft and anti-missile system, announced by Israel's Ministry of Defense on 23 December 2024. The first battery was delivered in April 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0053","ex":"Israel MOD Seals 560 Million Euro Agreement: Barak MX Integrated Air Defense System Produced by IAI Sold to Slovakia in Landmark Agreement","pg":null}],"dup":["EUR-0013"]},{"id":"REL-00078","t":"edge","a":"CTR-00009","b":"WPN-00013","rel":"includes","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The Slovak deal covers IAI's Barak MX anti-aircraft and anti-missile system, which IAI calls combat-proven against Iran and its proxies.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0053","ex":"Barak MX Integrated Air Defense System Produced by IAI Sold to Slovakia","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-0054","ex":"BARAK MX is an advanced, combat-proven, multi-layered air defense system that addresses a wide range of aerial threats, including ballistic threats. ... Rafael is proud to take a central role in building Greece's multi-layered air defense array and to provide another country in Europe with combat-proven, world-leading air defense solutions. ... This is the largest defense export deal in the history of Israel-Greece relations, and one of the largest in the history of the State of Israel.","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0030","EUR-0014"]},{"id":"REL-00079","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00012","b":"CTR-00010","rel":"funds_or_procures","amt":3000000000,"cur":"EUR","pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Greece signed the €3B 'Achilles Shield' interceptor deal with Israel on 31 August 2026, the largest Israel–Greece arms deal ever.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0054","ex":"the largest defense export deal in the history of Israel-Greece relations, and one of the largest in the history of the State of Israel.","pg":null}],"dup":["EUR-0015","EUR-0017","EUR-0019"]},{"id":"REL-00080","t":"edge","a":"CTR-00010","b":"WPN-00011","rel":"includes","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Greece's Achilles Shield package includes Rafael and RTX's David's Sling, marketed on Israel's wartime experience.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0054","ex":"The David's Sling system, developed by the Israeli Missile Defense Organization within the Ministry's DDR&D","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0031","EUR-0016"]},{"id":"REL-00082","t":"edge","a":"CTR-00010","b":"WPN-00012","rel":"includes","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Greece's Achilles Shield package includes Rafael's SPYDER mobile anti-aircraft missile system.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0054","ex":"The SPYDER system, manufactured by Rafael Advanced Defense Systems","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0032","EUR-0018"]},{"id":"REL-00084","t":"edge","a":"CTR-00010","b":"WPN-00013","rel":"includes","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Greece's Achilles Shield package includes IAI's Barak MX, which IAI calls combat-proven.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0054","ex":"The BARAK MX system, manufactured by Israel Aerospace Industries (IAI)","pg":null}],"dup":["CW-0033","EUR-0020"]},{"id":"OWN-0001","t":"ownership","a":"FND-00002","b":"COM-00002","rel":"shareholder_of","amt":9737891790,"cur":"USD","pct":"6.99","date":"2026-03-31","st":"documented","ctx":"Vanguard Capital Management reported beneficial ownership of 16,111,934 Lockheed Martin shares, 6.99% of the class, as of 31 March 2026 (Schedule 13G).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0055","ex":"Reporting Person: Vanguard Capital Management; Date of Event: 03/31/2026; Aggregate amount beneficially owned: 16,111,934.00; Percent of class: 6.99 %","pg":"Items 4(a)-(b)"},{"s":"SRC-V0323","ex":"Mar 31, 2026 | 604.50 | 610.00 | 598.70 | 604.39 | 596.77 | 1,327,800 (Date, Open, High, Low, Close, Adj Close, Volume)","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0324","ex":"[\"LMT\",\"LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP\",\"COM\",\"539830109\",10777913,0.2,17832713,null,null]","pg":null}],"shares":16111934,"basis":"Schedule 13G, Vanguard Capital Management"},{"id":"OWN-0002","t":"ownership","a":"FND-00001","b":"COM-00002","rel":"shareholder_of","amt":9617574000,"cur":"USD","pct":8.18,"date":"2026-06-30","st":"reported","ctx":"BlackRock reported 18,877,978 Lockheed Martin shares worth about $9.62B in its 13F for the quarter ended 30 June 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0056","ex":"[\"LMT\",\"LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP\",\"COM\",\"539830109\",9617574,0.1,18877978,null,null]  (value $000, %, shares)","pg":"Information table row: LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP, CUSIP 539830109"},{"s":"SRC-V0322","ex":"There were 230,790,753 shares of our common stock, $1 par value per share, outstanding as of July 20, 2026.","pg":null}],"shares":18877978,"basis":"13F-HR, BlackRock, Inc. (accession 0002012383-26-003238)","ev[0].ex":"LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP (CUSIP 539830109): value $9,617,574 thousand; 18,877,978 shares (13F-HR, period 30 June 2026)"},{"id":"OWN-0003","t":"ownership","a":"FND-00003","b":"COM-00002","rel":"shareholder_of","amt":16799530000,"cur":"USD","pct":"14.29","date":"2026-06-30","st":"documented","ctx":"State Street reported 32,975,170 Lockheed Martin shares worth about $16.8B (about 14.3% of shares) for the quarter ended 30 June 2026. The value and percentage come from MarketBeat's reading of the 13F.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0057","ex":"EDGAR full-text search for \"32975170\" restricted to State Street (CIK 93751) returns hits only in 0000093751-26-000507:XML_Infotable.xml and 0000093751-26-000583:XML_Infotable.xml. MarketBeat: 'The fund owned 32,975,170 shares ... about 14.29% of Lockheed Martin worth $16,799,530,000'","pg":"13F information table, Lockheed Martin rows"}],"shares":32975170,"basis":"13F-HR, State Street (Q2 2026)"},{"id":"OWN-0004","t":"ownership","a":"FND-00005","b":"COM-00002","rel":"shareholder_of","amt":1570540000,"cur":"USD","pct":"1.34","date":"2026-06-30","st":"reported","ctx":"Capital Group's investment units Capital Research Global Investors and Capital World Investors reported a combined 3.08 million Lockheed Martin shares in their 13F filings for the quarter ended 30 June 2026. That is about 1.3% of shares outstanding, with a reported value of about USD 1.57 billion.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0058","ex":"[\"LMT\",\"LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP\",\"COM\",\"539830109\",630985,0.1,1238537,null,null]  |  Capital World Investors (0001422849-26-000113): [\"LMT\",\"LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP\",\"COM\",\"539830109\",939555,0.1,1844218,null,null]","pg":"LMT row (CUSIP 539830109)"}],"shares":3082755,"basis":"13F-HR Q2 2026, Capital Research Global Investors + Capital World Investors (accessions 0001422848-26-000094, 00