":"SRC-V0080","ex":"more than $1 million supporting Adrian Boafo, who won the Democratic primary ... over $3 million opposing Rep. Thomas Massie in the Republican primary ... The super PAC also spent nearly $500,000 supporting Gallrein. ... spent over $2 million opposing Tom Malinowski, who lost a special Democratic primary [FEC data through June 30, 2026]","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0081","ex":"Independent Expenditures Total: $53,414,686.72 ... Total Receipts: $109,721,116.19 ... Ending Cash on Hand: $54,918,846.22 ... Coverage End Date: August 31, 2026","pg":null}],"ev (add source) + ctx note":"FactCheck.org's FEC-based review (through 30 June 2026) found more than $1 million supporting Adrian Boafo; FEC filings are canonical and the total may have grown since."},{"id":"REL-V0166","t":"election","a":"ORG-00003","b":"PER-V007","rel":"spent_opposing","amt":4100000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"KY-04 GOP primary · 2026 · lost to Ed Gallrein 54-45 (19 May 2026)","st":"reported","ctx":"United Democracy Project, AIPAC's super PAC, spent about $4.1M against Thomas Massie in the 2026 KY-04 GOP primary. Result: lost to Ed Gallrein 54-45 (19 May 2026).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0082","ex":null,"pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0080","ex":"more than $1 million supporting Adrian Boafo, who won the Democratic primary ... over $3 million opposing Rep. Thomas Massie in the Republican primary ... The super PAC also spent nearly $500,000 supporting Gallrein. ... spent over $2 million opposing Tom Malinowski, who lost a special Democratic primary [FEC data through June 30, 2026]","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0081","ex":"Independent Expenditures Total: $53,414,686.72 ... Total Receipts: $109,721,116.19 ... Ending Cash on Hand: $54,918,846.22 ... Coverage End Date: August 31, 2026","pg":null}],"ev (add source) + ctx note":"FactCheck.org's FEC-based review (through 30 June 2026) found over $3 million opposing Thomas Massie; FEC filings are canonical and the total may have grown since."},{"id":"REL-V0167","t":"election","a":"ORG-00003","b":"PER-V008","rel":"spent_opposing","amt":20140000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"Michigan Senate Dem primary · 2026 · won (4 Aug 2026)","st":"reported","ctx":"United Democracy Project, AIPAC's super PAC, spent about $20.1M against Abdul El-Sayed in the 2026 Michigan Senate Dem primary. Result: won (4 Aug 2026).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0284","ex":null,"pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0168","t":"election","a":"ORG-00003","b":"PER-N-BUSH","rel":"spent_opposing","amt":2460000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"MO-01 Dem primary · 2026 · lost to Wesley Bell (4 Aug 2026)","st":"reported","ctx":"United Democracy Project, AIPAC's super PAC, spent about $2.5M against Cori Bush in the 2026 MO-01 Dem primary. Result: lost to Wesley Bell (4 Aug 2026).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0284","ex":null,"pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0169","t":"election","a":"ORG-00003","b":"PER-V009","rel":"spent_opposing","amt":60000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"IL-07 Dem primary · 2026 · lost","st":"reported","ctx":"United Democracy Project, AIPAC's super PAC, spent about $0.1M against Jason Friedman in the 2026 IL-07 Dem primary. Result: lost.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0286","ex":null,"pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0170","t":"money","a":"GOV-00001","b":"CTR-2026-APACHE","rel":"approved_sale_to_israel","amt":3800000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-01-30","st":"documented","ctx":"On 30 January 2026 the US notified Congress of a $3.8B sale to Israel of 30 AH-64E Apache attack helicopters, naming Boeing (Arlington, VA) and Lockheed Martin (Orlando, FL) as principal contractors. It was part of a $6.67B set of Israel sales notified that day, which also included $1.98B of JLTVs and $740M of Namer power packs.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0001","ex":"thirty (30) AH-64E Apache attack helicopters ... $3.8 billion ... The Boeing Company, located in Arlington, VA; and Lockheed Martin, located in Orlando, FL","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0331","ex":"January 30 ... $6.67 billion ($3.8B Apache; $1.98B JLTV; $740M power packs; $150M helicopters) ... March 6 ... $151.8 million ... Emergency declaration ... May 1 ... $992.4 million ... Emergency declaration","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0670","t":"money","a":"CTR-2026-APACHE","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"sold_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-01-30","st":"documented","ctx":null,"ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0001","ex":"thirty (30) AH-64E Apache attack helicopters ... $3.8 billion ... The Boeing Company, located in Arlington, VA; and Lockheed Martin, located in Orlando, FL","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0331","ex":"January 30 ... $6.67 billion ($3.8B Apache; $1.98B JLTV; $740M power packs; $150M helicopters) ... March 6 ... $151.8 million ... Emergency declaration ... May 1 ... $992.4 million ... Emergency declaration","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0171","t":"money","a":"GOV-00001","b":"CTR-2026-APKWS","rel":"approved_sale_to_israel","amt":992400000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-05-01","st":"documented","ctx":"On 1 May 2026, during Israel's war on Iran, the State Department used emergency powers to skip congressional review of a $992.4M sale to Israel of 10,000 APKWS-II laser-guided rockets. BAE Systems (Nashua, NH) is the principal contractor.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0332","ex":"ten thousand (10,000) Advanced Precision Kill Weapon System-II All Up Round ... $992.4 million ... BAE Systems, located in Nashua, NH ... The Secretary of State has determined and provided detailed justification that an emergency exists","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0331","ex":"January 30 ... $6.67 billion ($3.8B Apache; $1.98B JLTV; $740M power packs; $150M helicopters) ... March 6 ... $151.8 million ... Emergency declaration ... May 1 ... $992.4 million ... Emergency declaration","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0671","t":"money","a":"CTR-2026-APKWS","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"sold_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-05-01","st":"documented","ctx":null,"ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0332","ex":"ten thousand (10,000) Advanced Precision Kill Weapon System-II All Up Round ... $992.4 million ... BAE Systems, located in Nashua, NH ... The Secretary of State has determined and provided detailed justification that an emergency exists","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0331","ex":"January 30 ... $6.67 billion ($3.8B Apache; $1.98B JLTV; $740M power packs; $150M helicopters) ... March 6 ... $151.8 million ... Emergency declaration ... May 1 ... $992.4 million ... Emergency declaration","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0172","t":"money","a":"GOV-00001","b":"CTR-2026-BLU110","rel":"approved_sale_to_israel","amt":151800000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-03-06","st":"documented","ctx":"In March 2026 the State Department waived congressional review on emergency grounds for a $151.8M sale to Israel of 12,000 BLU-110A/B 1,000-pound bomb bodies. Repkon USA, which runs the former General Dynamics Garland bomb-body plant, is the principal contractor; it renamed itself Paligen Technologies days later after a backlash. Emergency sales that month also included $298M for 5,000 small-diameter bombs and $209M for 10,000 500-pound bombs.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0002","ex":"12,000 BLU-110A/B general purpose 1,000-pound bomb bodies ... estimated value of $151.8m ... Repkon USA, a subsidiary of Türkiye based Repkon, has been selected as the principal contractor ... waives the Congressional review requirements under Section 36(b)","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0333","ex":"In April 2025, Repkon USA acquired \"General Dynamics Ordnance and Tactical Systems' Garland operations in Texas ... \" ... new name ... Paligen Technologies","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0334","ex":"$298 million for 5,000 ... small-diameter bombs; $209 million for 10,000 500-pound bombs; $151.8 million for 12,000 1,000-pound bombs","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0003","ex":"Israel will also receive 10,000 bombs weighing roughly 250 kilograms, 5,000 small-diameter bombs ... the only facility in the United States capable of producing bomb bodies for the MK-80 series","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0672","t":"money","a":"CTR-2026-BLU110","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"sold_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-03-06","st":"documented","ctx":null,"ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0002","ex":"12,000 BLU-110A/B general purpose 1,000-pound bomb bodies ... estimated value of $151.8m ... Repkon USA, a subsidiary of Türkiye based Repkon, has been selected as the principal contractor ... waives the Congressional review requirements under Section 36(b)","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0333","ex":"In April 2025, Repkon USA acquired \"General Dynamics Ordnance and Tactical Systems' Garland operations in Texas ... \" ... new name ... Paligen Technologies","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0334","ex":"$298 million for 5,000 ... small-diameter bombs; $209 million for 10,000 500-pound bombs; $151.8 million for 12,000 1,000-pound bombs","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0003","ex":"Israel will also receive 10,000 bombs weighing roughly 250 kilograms, 5,000 small-diameter bombs ... the only facility in the United States capable of producing bomb bodies for the MK-80 series","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0173","t":"money","a":"GOV-00001","b":"CTR-2026-MK84","rel":"proposed_sale_to_israel","amt":2800000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-09-15","st":"documented","ctx":"In September 2026 the administration informally notified Congress of a $2.8B FMF-funded package for Israel of 20,000 MK-84 and 20,000 BLU-117 2,000-pound bombs plus I-2000 penetrator warheads, which the Washington Post and AFP called the largest single sale of the munition in years. Rep. Gregory Meeks and Sen. Jeanne Shaheen placed holds on it. No contractor has been officially named; the link to General Dynamics is an inference from the 2025 case and is reported only.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0319","ex":"40,000 bombs: 20,000 MK-84 general-purpose bombs and 20,000 BLU-117s ... along with I-2000 Penetrator warheads ... The deal has been informally notified to congressional committees.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0335","ex":"Rep. Gregory Meeks ... would \"not clear this sale at this time\" ... Sen. Jeanne Shaheen ... \"placed a hold on the weapons sale\" ... the sale remains halted at the moment","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0318","ex":"Meeks Places Hold on Trump Administration's $2.8 Billion Bomb Sale to Israel ... the Trump administration's proposed sale of 40,000 2,000-pound bombs ... not provided sufficient assurances that these weapons will be used by the Netanyahu government in accordance with U.S. law","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0673","t":"money","a":"CTR-2026-MK84","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"sold_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-09-15","st":"reported","ctx":null,"ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0319","ex":"40,000 bombs: 20,000 MK-84 general-purpose bombs and 20,000 BLU-117s ... along with I-2000 Penetrator warheads ... The deal has been informally notified to congressional committees.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0335","ex":"Rep. Gregory Meeks ... would \"not clear this sale at this time\" ... Sen. Jeanne Shaheen ... \"placed a hold on the weapons sale\" ... the sale remains halted at the moment","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0001","t":"edge","a":"COM-00007","b":"WPN-NEW-ROEM","rel":"manufactures_or_supplies","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-04","st":"documented","ctx":"Elbit Systems developed the Ro'em 155mm self-propelled howitzer, first fired in combat by the Israeli army in Lebanon in April 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0077","ex":"The Israel Defense Forces conducted the first operational firing of the new self-propelled Roem howitzer during operations in Lebanon ... uses a 155mm shell ... Elbit Systems began developing in 2019 ... to attack Hezbollah targets from which fire was fired at our forces","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0002","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00007","b":"WPN-NEW-ROEM","rel":"uses","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-04","st":"documented","ctx":"The Israeli army fired the Ro'em howitzer operationally for the first time in Lebanon in April 2026, against what it called Hezbollah targets.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0077","ex":"The Israel Defense Forces conducted the first operational firing of the new self-propelled Roem howitzer during operations in Lebanon ... uses a 155mm shell ... Elbit Systems began developing in 2019 ... to attack Hezbollah targets from which fire was fired at our forces","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0003","t":"edge","a":"WPN-NEW-ROEM","b":"CTY-NEW-LEBANON","rel":"used_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-04","st":"documented","ctx":"First operational firing of Elbit's Ro'em howitzer took place during Israel's war on Lebanon in April 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0077","ex":"The Israel Defense Forces conducted the first operational firing of the new self-propelled Roem howitzer during operations in Lebanon ... uses a 155mm shell ... Elbit Systems began developing in 2019 ... to attack Hezbollah targets from which fire was fired at our forces","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0004","t":"edge","a":"WPN-00015","b":"CTY-NEW-LEBANON","rel":"used_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024–2026","st":"documented","ctx":"Israel's Lahav/PULS launchers fired on Lebanon in 2024 and again in 2026, when more than 50 'Bar' (EXTRA) rockets were launched at buildings, anti-tank teams and Hezbollah targets, according to Elbit, citing N12.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0270","ex":"The PULS rocket artillery system is being used extensively by the Israeli Defence Forces (IDF) in the ongoing war in Gaza and Lebanon. ... The very accurate rockets launched by the systems have destroyed a great number of targets on the two fronts","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0091","ex":"While fighter jets were flying back and forth to Tehran, the artillery's \"Lahav\" launchers (PULS) were working overtime: more than 50 \"Bar\" rockets (EXTRA) were launched at the beginning of Operation \"Roaring Lion\" toward anti-tank squads, buildings, and Hezbollah targets ... Battalion 334 in Lebanon operated the new missile on an unprecedented scale","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0005","t":"money","a":"COM-00001","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"approved_fms_sale_to","amt":102500000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-08-13","st":"documented","ctx":"The State Department approved 30 AIM-120C-8 AMRAAM missiles for Israel, estimated at $102.5M, with RTX (Tucson) as principal contractor. Procurement only: no documented strike link.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0316","ex":"thirty (30) AIM-120C-8 Advanced Medium Range Air-to-Air Missiles ... $102.5 million ... RTX Corporation, located in Tucson, AZ ... These items will be sourced from new production.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0317","ex":"Original DSCA PDF (HTTP 403 to our fetcher); same release mirrored by GlobalSecurity.org.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0006","t":"edge","a":"COM-00010","b":"PER-00022","rel":"Executive compensation","amt":8623000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025","st":"documented","ctx":"Alex Karp's 2025 Summary Compensation Table total was $8.623M: $1.10M salary and $7.52M in other compensation, including $2.51M for personal security, $2.00M for aircraft and $2.39M in HSR filing fees. SEC's 'compensation actually paid' is a separate accounting measure and is not used here.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0212","ex":"total compensation for fiscal 2025 was $8,623,000 ... Salary: $1,101,637 ... All other compensation: $7,521,363 ... $2,506,484 for personal security services, $1,998,476 for aircraft costs, and $2,390,000 in HSR Act filing fees","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0350","ex":"Owner-supplied link to the Summary Compensation Table; HTTP 403 to our fetcher.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0007","t":"edge","a":"COM-00006","b":"PER-00016","rel":"Executive compensation","amt":12397000,"cur":"GBP","pct":null,"date":"2025","st":"documented","ctx":"Charles Woodburn's single total figure of remuneration for 2025 was £12.4M (£12.397M per BAE's 2025 annual report), about 90% of it bonus and share awards, as BAE's F-35 rear fuselages flew in Israel's bombing of Gaza.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0205","ex":"total yearly compensation is £12.40M, comprised of 10.3% salary and 89.7% bonuses, including company stock and options.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0351","ex":"Owner-supplied primary link; our fetcher received only part of the report and could not see the single-figure table (owner reports £12,397k).","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0008","t":"edge","a":"COM-00019","b":"PER-00004","rel":"Executive compensation","amt":131015970,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"FY2026 (year to May 31, 2026)","st":"documented","ctx":"Larry Ellison's fiscal 2026 Summary Compensation Table total from Oracle was $131,015,970: $950,000 salary, $117.8M in stock awards, $4.85M in option awards and $7.44M other compensation.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0179","ex":"Lawrence J. Ellison's fiscal 2026 summary compensation table total was $131,015,970 ... Salary: $950,000 ... Stock awards: $117,777,832 ... Option awards: $4,851,178 ... Other compensation: $7,436,960","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0352","ex":"Oracle Corp Says Executive Chair & CTO Lawrence J. Ellison's 2026 Total Compensation $131 Million","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0353","ex":"Owner-supplied primary link; not fetched by us (sec.gov skipped under the anonymity rule).","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0009","t":"edge","a":"ORG-00003","b":"PER-NEW-GALLREIN","rel":"spent_supporting","amt":500000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"KY-04 GOP primary · 2026 · won (19 May 2026)","st":"reported","ctx":"United Democracy Project, AIPAC's super PAC, spent nearly $500,000 supporting Ed Gallrein against Thomas Massie (FactCheck.org, FEC data through 30 June 2026; FEC canonical).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0080","ex":"more than $1 million supporting Adrian Boafo, who won the Democratic primary ... over $3 million opposing Rep. Thomas Massie in the Republican primary ... The super PAC also spent nearly $500,000 supporting Gallrein. ... spent over $2 million opposing Tom Malinowski, who lost a special Democratic primary [FEC data through June 30, 2026]","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0010","t":"edge","a":"ORG-00001","b":"ORG-NEW-ISRAEL-LOBBY","rel":"part_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"reported","ctx":"Counted by Track AIPAC among the pro-Israel PACs and donors whose money it tallies.","ev