r 2024 [Slovakia]; post-Oct customs dataset shows Hungary only €9,070; Portugal €1.077m HS93 post-Oct customs exports","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0093","t":"money","a":"CTY-00019","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"customs_arms_exports_to","amt":9070,"cur":"EUR","pct":null,"date":"2023-10 to 2024-03","st":"reported","ctx":"Customs data (HS 93 'arms and ammunition') show €9,070 of exports from Hungary to Israel from Oct 2023 to Mar 2024. Customs figures, not military-export statistics; source table not yet verified.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0354","ex":"customs data show €5.505m of HS93 \"arms and ammunition\" exports to Israel from Oct 2023–Mar 2024 [Slovakia]; post-Oct customs dataset shows Hungary only €9,070; Portugal €1.077m HS93 post-Oct customs exports","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0094","t":"money","a":"CTY-NEW-IRELAND","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"dual_use_licences_to","amt":70370000,"cur":"EUR","pct":null,"date":"2023","st":"documented","ctx":"Ireland approved €70.37M of dual-use export licences for Israeli end users in 2023, mostly business ICT software classed as dual-use because of strong encryption (Dail answer, May 2024). Dual-use only: Ireland has no military-list licences for Israel in the EU table.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0088","ex":"€70.37 million last year ... The bulk of dual-use exports from Ireland to Israel are mainstream business ICT products, predominantly software, that are categorised as dual-use items specifically as a consequence of the fact that they incorporate strong encryption for ICT security purposes.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-O0095","t":"money","a":"CTY-NEW-SWITZERLAND","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"dual_use_exports_to","amt":24000000,"cur":"CHF","pct":null,"date":"2023-10 to 2025-03","st":"reported","ctx":"Swiss firms exported more than CHF24M of dual-use or special military goods to Israel from October 2023 to March 2025, per a SWI swissinfo.ch review of export permits; Switzerland has issued no direct war-materiel licences for Israel for years.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0090","ex"