"b":"COM-NEW-CATERPILLAR","rel":"shareholder_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":7.5,"date":"2025","ctx":"Named in the UN Special Rapporteur's report as Caterpillar's third-largest institutional investor.","id":"REL-W0026","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0004","ex":"third largest in Lockheed Martin (7.2 per cent) and Caterpillar (7.5 per cent)","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"COM-NEW-CATERPILLAR","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"supplies_equipment","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"ctx":"The UN Special Rapporteur reports Caterpillar has for decades provided Israel with equipment used to demolish Palestinian homes.","id":"REL-W0027","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0004","ex":"For decades, Caterpillar Inc. has provided Israel with equipment used to demolish Palestinian homes","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"COM-00019","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"supplies_software","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"ctx":"Who Profits reports Oracle Israel supplies software and services to the Israel Ministry of Defense and the army, and servers to the Civil Administration in the occupied West Bank.","id":"REL-W0028","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0176","ex":"Through its fully owned Israeli subsidiary, Oracle Israel, the company has developed and provides a variety of software and services to the Israeli Ministry of Defense (IMOD) and the Israeli military","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-00004","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"prosecution_witness_in_trial_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2021","ctx":"Larry Ellison is a prosecution witness in Netanyahu's corruption trial; Netanyahu holidayed on Ellison's island of Lanai in August 2021.","id":"REL-W0029","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0053","ex":"Ellison is one of several hundred prosecution witnesses in Netanyahu's corruption trial.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-00006","b":"ORG-00001","rel":"donated_to","amt":2000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023","ctx":"Bernie Marcus gave $2M to AIPAC in 2023, according to Wikipedia.","id":"REL-W0030","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0183","ex":"In 2023, he donated $2 million to the pro-Israel lobby group AIPAC.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-00006","b":"ORG-NEW-MDA","rel":"donated_to","amt":25000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2016","ctx":"Bernie and Billi Marcus gave $25M toward MDA's national blood services centre.","id":"REL-W0031","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0183","ex":"In 2016, Marcus and his wife Billi donated $25 million to the construction of the $133 million MDA Marcus National Blood Services Centre in Israel.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-BENGVIR","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"coalition_minister_under","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2022–","ctx":"Itamar Ben Gvir sits in Benjamin Netanyahu's cabinet as national security minister. He walked out over the January 2025 ceasefire and was reappointed in March 2025.","id":"REL-X0001","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0001","ex":"In 2007, however, he was convicted for incitement to racism and supporting a terrorist organization. ... Ben-Gvir has been convicted of at least eight charges. ... has served as the minister of national security since 2022, except for a two-month gap in early 2025. ... Prior to entering office Ben-Gvir was known to have a portrait in his living room of Israeli-American mass murderer Baruch Goldstein.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-BENGVIR","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"national_security_minister","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2022–","ctx":"Ben Gvir runs Israel's police and prison system. By March 2024 his ministry had approved more than 100,000 civilian gun licences.","id":"REL-X0002","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0001","ex":"In 2007, however, he was convicted for incitement to racism and supporting a terrorist organization. ... Ben-Gvir has been convicted of at least eight charges. ... has served as the minister of national security since 2022, except for a two-month gap in early 2025. ... Prior to entering office Ben-Gvir was known to have a portrait in his living room of Israeli-American mass murderer Baruch Goldstein.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0005","ex":"out of 299,354 applications submitted since the war ... more than 100,000 citizens have already been approved.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"coalition_minister_under","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2022–","ctx":"Bezalel Smotrich is Netanyahu's finance minister. In July 2026 he thanked Netanyahu for backing NIS 1.3B for 34 new settlements.","id":"REL-X0003","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0008","ex":"arrested in 2005 while in possession of 700 litres of gasoline on suspicion of participating in an attempt to blow up Ayalon Highway ... I think the village of Huwara needs to be wiped out. I think the state of Israel should do it.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0013","ex":"1.3 billion shekels ($434 million) for establishing 34 new settlements ... 1.075 billion shekels would be approved to pave roads to the new settlements ... a day of celebration for Israel and settlements","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"finance_minister_controls_budget","amt":271000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026","ctx":"Smotrich's treasury wrote Israel's record 2026 budget of NIS 850.6B ($271B). The Bank of Israel puts the fiscal cost of the wars from 2023 to 2026 at about NIS 350B.","id":"REL-X0004","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0014","ex":"NIS 850.6 billion ($271 billion) ... the largest in Israeli history ... more than NIS 142 billion ($45.3 billion), a record","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0015","ex":"The Bank of Israel estimates the fiscal cost of the war from 2023 through 2026 at about NIS 350 billion, with roughly half financed through borrowing.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"funded_military_budget","amt":45300000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026","ctx":"The 2026 budget gives the Israel Ministry of Defense more than NIS 142B ($45.3B), a record. Smotrich said its core was \"the addition of tens of billions so that we can finish the campaign\".","id":"REL-X0005","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0014","ex":"NIS 850.6 billion ($271 billion) ... the largest in Israeli history ... more than NIS 142 billion ($45.3 billion), a record","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0040","ex":"the core of the budget is the addition of tens of billions so that we can finish the campaign and dramatically improve our geopolitical and diplomatic standing","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"minister_with_west_bank_powers","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023-02-23","ctx":"Since February 2023, Smotrich, as a minister in the Israel Ministry of Defense, has controlled settlement planning, land allocation and state-land registration in Area C.","id":"REL-X0006","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0009","ex":"authority over the planning and construction bureaucracy in the West Bank, which will come under the control of the new Settlements Administration ... full authority over land purchases, land surveys and the registration of land as state land in Area C","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"directed_settlement_funding","amt":434000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-07-14","ctx":"Smotrich secured NIS 1.3B ($434M) for 34 new West Bank settlements and NIS 1.075B more for roads to them, calling it \"a day of celebration for Israel and settlements\".","id":"REL-X0007","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0013","ex":"1.3 billion shekels ($434 million) for establishing 34 new settlements ... 1.075 billion shekels would be approved to pave roads to the new settlements ... a day of celebration for Israel and settlements","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-GALLANT","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"military_minister_under","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"to 2024-11-07","ctx":"Gallant served as Netanyahu's military minister until Netanyahu fired him, effective 7 November 2024. The ICC warrants of 21 November 2024 name both men.","id":"REL-X0008","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0017","ex":"On 9 October 2023 ... Gallant said he had 'ordered a complete siege on the Gaza Strip. There will be no electricity, no food, no water, no fuel. Everything is closed. We are fighting human animals and we are acting accordingly'. ... On 5 November 2024, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced that he had dismissed Gallant, effective 7 November","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0019","ex":"On 21 November 2024, following an investigation of war crimes and crimes against humanity, the ICC issued arrest warrants for two senior Israeli officials, Benjamin Netanyahu ... and Yoav Gallant.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-GALLANT","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"headed","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"to 2024-11-07","ctx":"Gallant headed the Israel Ministry of Defense during the first 13 months of the Gaza genocide.","id":"REL-X0009","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0017","ex":"On 9 October 2023 ... Gallant said he had 'ordered a complete siege on the Gaza Strip. There will be no electricity, no food, no water, no fuel. Everything is closed. We are fighting human animals and we are acting accordingly'. ... On 5 November 2024, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced that he had dismissed Gallant, effective 7 November","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-GALLANT","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"ordered_complete_siege","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023-10-09","ctx":"On 9 October 2023, Gallant ordered \"a complete siege on the Gaza Strip... no electricity, no food, no water, no fuel\". The ICC alleges starvation as a method of warfare.","id":"REL-X0010","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0017","ex":"On 9 October 2023 ... Gallant said he had 'ordered a complete siege on the Gaza Strip. There will be no electricity, no food, no water, no fuel. Everything is closed. We are fighting human animals and we are acting accordingly'. ... On 5 November 2024, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced that he had dismissed Gallant, effective 7 November","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0018","ex":"from at least 8 October 2023 until at least 20 May 2024 ... the war crime of starvation as a method of warfare; and the crimes against humanity of murder, persecution, and other inhumane acts","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-KATZ","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"military_minister_under","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-11–","ctx":"Netanyahu named Israel Katz military minister on 5 November 2024, replacing Gallant.","id":"REL-X0011","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0020","ex":"2022–2024: Energy ... 2024: Foreign Affairs ... 2024–present: Defense ... We will win. They will not receive a drop of water or a single battery until they leave the world. ... No one is currently planning to allow any humanitarian aid into Gaza, and there are no preparations to enable such aid.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-KATZ","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"heads","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-11–","ctx":"Katz heads the Israel Ministry of Defense. He and Smotrich first agreed a NIS 112B ($34B) military budget for 2026; the final 2026 budget raised it to more than NIS 142B.","id":"REL-X0012","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0020","ex":"2022–2024: Energy ... 2024: Foreign Affairs ... 2024–present: Defense ... We will win. They will not receive a drop of water or a single battery until they leave the world. ... No one is currently planning to allow any humanitarian aid into Gaza, and there are no preparations to enable such aid.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0024","ex":"NIS 112 billion ($34 billion) ... NIS 90 billion ... NIS 140 billion","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0014","ex":"NIS 850.6 billion ($271 billion) ... the largest in Israeli history ... more than NIS 142 billion ($45.3 billion), a record","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-KATZ","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"directs","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-11–","ctx":"As military minister, Katz threatened that \"Tehran will burn\" (June 2025) and that \"the gates of hell\" would open on Gaza City (August 2025).","id":"REL-X0013","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0022","ex":"If Khamenei continues to fire missiles at the Israeli home front, Tehran will burn.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0023","ex":"The gates of hell will soon open on the heads of Hamas' murderers and rapists in Gaza — until they agree to Israel's conditions for ending the war ... turn into Rafah and Beit Hanoun","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-HERZOG","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"head_of_state","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2021-07-07–","ctx":"Isaac Herzog is Israel's president. The UN Commission of Inquiry found in September 2025 that he incited genocide.","id":"REL-X0014","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0025","ex":"was sworn in on 7 July 2021 ... He called South Africa's genocide case against Israel in the International Court of Justice (ICJ) a 'blood libel' against Jews. ... During Herzog's 2024 visit to the World Economic Forum in Switzerland, the Swiss Federal Prosecutor's Office announced that it was investigating a criminal complaint against him. ... On 30 November 2025, Netanyahu formally asked Herzog for a pardon on his corruption cases.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0025","ex":"The Commission also concluded that Israeli President Isaac Herzog, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and then Defence Minister Yoav Gallant, have incited the commission of genocide and that Israeli authorities have failed to take action against them to punish this incitement.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-HERZOG","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"holds_pardon_request_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2025-11-30","ctx":"Netanyahu asked Herzog for a pardon on 30 November 2025. In April 2026 Herzog deferred a decision and pushed for a plea deal. The UN Commission of Inquiry named both men for incitement.","id":"REL-X0015","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0025","ex":"was sworn in on 7 July 2021 ... He called South Africa's genocide case against Israel in the International Court of Justice (ICJ) a 'blood libel' against Jews. ... During Herzog's 2024 visit to the World Economic Forum in Switzerland, the Swiss Federal Prosecutor's Office announced that it was investigating a criminal complaint against him. ... On 30 November 2025, Netanyahu formally asked Herzog for a pardon on his corruption cases.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0028","ex":"it is right to first, before discussing the pardon request itself, exhaust a process that could lead to the formation of an agreement between the parties, outside the walls of the court","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0025","ex":"The Commission also concluded that Israeli President Isaac Herzog, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and then Defence Minister Yoav Gallant, have incited the commission of genocide and that Israeli authorities have failed to take action against them to punish this incitement.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"GOV-00005","b":"COM-00009","rel":"state_owner_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":99.9,"date":null,"ctx":"The Israeli state directly holds 99.9% of Rafael, and other state entities hold the rest. Rafael's profits flow to the government Netanyahu heads. This duplicates REL-00035.","indirect":true,"id":"REL-X0016","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0024","ex":"Rafael is a government-owned company, with 99.9% of its shares directly held by the Israeli government and the remainder held by various government entities, each possessing a fractional share.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"GOV-00005","b":"COM-00008","rel":"state_owner_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":100,"date":null,"ctx":"IAI is a \"wholly-owned government company\" under Israel's Government Companies Law. Its profits flow to the government Netanyahu heads. This duplicates REL-00036.","indirect":true,"id":"REL-X0017","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0025","ex":"Israel Aerospace Industries Ltd. (\"the Company\") was founded in 1966 and is a \"wholly-owned government company\", as this term is defined in the Israeli Government Companies Law, 1975","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"heads_government_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2022-12–","ctx":"Benjamin Netanyahu heads the government that has waged the wars on Gaza, Lebanon and Iran since October 2023. This duplicates REL-V0084 (prime_minister).","id":"REL-X0018","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0026","ex":"ordered an invasion of Lebanon with the stated goal of destroying the military capabilities of Hezbollah ... He presided over the 2025 Israeli strikes on Iran, which started the Twelve-Day War ... In February 2026, he launched a major air campaign against Iran, alongside the US","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0025","ex":"The Commission also concluded that Israeli President Isaac Herzog, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and then Defence Minister Yoav Gallant, have incited the commission of genocide and that Israeli authorities have failed to take action against them to punish this incitement.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00001","rel":"negotiated_and_accepted_us_military_aid","amt":38000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2016-09-14","ctx":"Netanyahu thanked Barack Obama for the $38B 10-year aid deal (2016 MOU), calling it \"the largest military aid package the US has ever given out to any nation\". It pays Israel about $3.8B a year in subsidies, mostly to buy US-made arms, until 2028.","id":"REL-X0019","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0041","ex":"This agreement will ensure an unprecedented level of defense aid for Israel in the next decade. This is the largest military aid package the US has ever given out to any nation. ... I want to thank President Obama and his administration for this historic agreement.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0042","ex":"Israel receives some $3.8 billion annually from the US, mostly in the form of subsidies to buy American-made arms. ... I want to taper off the military aid within the next 10 years","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00003","rel":"welcomed_supplemental_aid","amt":17000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-04-20","ctx":"Netanyahu thanked Congress for the April 2024 package, which included $17B in military aid to Israel: \"Thank you friends, thank you America!\"","id":"REL-X0020","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0043","ex":"The US Congress just overwhelmingly passed a much appreciated aid bill that demonstrates strong bipartisan support for Israel and defends Western civilization. Thank you friends, thank you America!","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00001","rel":"lobbied_for_weapons_deliveries","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-06-18","ctx":"In a June 2024 video Netanyahu accused Washington of \"withholding weapons and ammunitions\" and demanded: \"give us the tools and we'll finish the job a lot faster\".","id":"REL-X0021","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0044","ex":"I said it's inconceivable that in the past few months, the administration has been withholding weapons and ammunitions to Israel ... give us the tools and we'll finish the job a lot faster","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"approved_arms_industry_spending","amt":110000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-12-25","ctx":"Netanyahu said: \"I approved a total of 350 billion shekels over the coming decade to build an independent arms industry for the State of Israel\" (about $110B). The state-owned Rafael and IAI stand to gain.","id":"REL-X0022","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0045","ex":"I approved a total of 350 billion shekels over the coming decade to build an independent arms industry for the State of Israel","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"cabinet_approved_war_budget_increase","amt":10400000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-03-11","ctx":"During the 2026 war on Iran, Netanyahu's cabinet added NIS 32B ($10.4B) to the military budget, plus NIS 7B in reserves.","id":"REL-X0023","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0046","ex":"Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's cabinet approved a revised state budget for 2026 ... adds 32 billion shekels ($10.4 billion), about 1.5% of Israel's gross domestic product, for defense and an additional 7 billion shekels in reserves for possible military needs","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-GATES","b":"COM-00016","rel":"co_founder_and_shareholder","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"1975–","ctx":"Bill Gates co-founded Microsoft and remains Technology Advisor to Satya Nadella. Forbes estimates his stake at below 1% (no verified dollar value). Microsoft's Azure held Unit 8200's mass surveillance of Palestinians.","id":"REL-X0024","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0030","ex":"Bill Gates stepped down from the company's Board of Directors to dedicate more time to his philanthropic priorities ... He will continue to serve as Technology Advisor to CEO Satya Nadella and other leaders in the company.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0032","ex":"$114.2B ... his Microsoft stake is now less than 1%, Forbes estimates ... Gates, who's donated more than $63.9 billion to the Gates Foundation, announced in 2025 that the foundation will shut down in 20 years","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0011","ex":"Israel's elite cyber-intelligence unit stored vast volumes of intercepted Palestinian phone calls on Microsoft's cloud servers ... Three sources from Unit 8200 said that the cloud-based system helped guide deadly air strikes and shaped operations across the occupied Palestinian territories.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-IN","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_trade_with","amt":185000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024","ctx":"India–Israel arms trade was about $185M in 2024, per ORF; India took 29% of Israel's arms exports in 2021–25 (SIPRI).","id":"REL-G0025","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0097","ex":"In 2024, their arms trade volume was about US$185 million. Between 2020 and 2024, Israel supplied 13 percent of India's total arms imports","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0034","ex":"Israel's main recipients per Table 1: India (29%), Germany (21%), USA (7.8%) [SIPRI fact sheet, Table 1, 2021-25]; India's main suppliers (Table 2): Russia 40, France 29, Israel 15","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-IN","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"bilateral_trade_with","amt":3900000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024","ctx":"India–Israel bilateral trade reached $3.9B in 2024, and mutual investment about $800M. A bilateral investment treaty was signed with Bezalel Smotrich in September 2025.","id":"REL-G0026","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0107","ex":"Bilateral trade stood at $3.9bn in 2024, while current mutual investments are worth about $800m, according to official figures.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0107","ex":"The agreement, signed in New Delhi by Smotrich and Indian Minister of Corporate Affairs Nirmala Sitharaman, aims to boost trade and investment flows between the two countries.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"COM-G-ADANIELBIT","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"exported_drones_to","amt":20,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2024-02","ctx":"Adani-Elbit's Hyderabad plant delivered more than 20 Hermes 900 MALE drones to Israel.","id":"REL-G0027","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0059","ex":"The first private UAV manufacturing facility in India has delivered more than 20 Hermes 900 medium-altitude, long-endurance (MALE) UAVs to Israel","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0064","ex":"The Company's joint venture with Israel-based Elbit Systems exported the first ship set of the Hermes 900 fuselage to Israel","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"COM-G-ADANIELBIT","b":"COM-00007","rel":"joint_venture_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"ctx":"Adani-Elbit Advanced Systems India is a joint venture between Adani Defence & Aerospace and Elbit Systems.","id":"REL-G0028","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0064","ex":"The Company's joint venture with Israel-based Elbit Systems exported the first ship set of the Hermes 900 fuselage to Israel","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"COM-G-MUNITIONSINDIA","b":"COM-00007","rel":"supplied_artillery_rounds_to","amt":1000,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2023-10/2025-11","ctx":"Per Amnesty's 'Made in India' (July 2026), Munitions India exported 1,000 155-mm high-explosive artillery rounds to Elbit Systems.","id":"REL-G0029","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0061","ex":"Munitions India Limited exported 1,000 155-mm high-explosive artillery rounds to Elbit Systems, while Advanced Weapons and Equipment India Limited supplied 120 81-mm mortar launchers to the Israeli company in February 2024.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0060","ex":"PLR Systems Private Limited, who manufacture parts for machine guns and is a joint venture between Adani Defence & Aerospace and Israel Weapon Industries; ... the state-owned Munitions India Limited, who manufacture high-explosive artillery rounds; and Alpha Elsec Defence & Aerospace Systems Private Limited who manufacture explosive warheads and is a joint venture between Alpha Design Technologies and Elbit Systems.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"COM-G-PREMIER","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"export_order_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024","ctx":"Premier Explosives told investors that revenue from an Israel export order produced an 'exponential jump' in quarterly revenue.","id":"REL-G0030","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0065","ex":"We have received the pending revenue from the Israel export order, and this has shown an exponential jump in the revenue of the quarter.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-IN","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_workers_to","amt":16000,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2024","ctx":"Around 16,000 Indian workers replaced barred Palestinian labourers in Israel's construction sector in 2024.","id":"REL-G0031","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0062","ex":"Around 16,000 Indian workers have replaced Palestinians in Israel's construction sector in 2024","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0107","ex":"Israeli construction companies have sought permission to hire up to 100,000 Indian workers to replace Palestinians whose permits were revoked after Israel launched its brutal war on Gaza in October 2023.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-IN","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_shipments_to","amt":2596,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2023-10-07/2025-11-30","ctx":"Amnesty identified at least 2,596 shipments of arms, parts and ammunition from India to Israel.","id":"REL-G0032","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0060","ex":"Amnesty International identified at least 2,596 shipments of arms, parts and ammunition exported from India to Israel between 7 October 2023 and 30 November 2025.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0060","ex":"Records indicate that Indian companies have supplied at least 390,516 small arms parts for military grade weapons, 564,970 parts of explosive ordnance (such as drone warheads, artillery shell casings and others), and 298 components of military vehicles to large Israeli companies that are direct suppliers to the Israeli military.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-AZ","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_crude_oil_to","amt":7000000,"cur":"units","pct":40,"date":"2023-11/2025-10","ctx":"Over 7 million tonnes of Azerbaijani crude, nearly 40% of crude and fuel shipped to Israel (OCI). amt is in metric tonnes.","id":"REL-G0033","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0066","ex":"Azerbaijani product taking the lead at over 7 million tonnes, or nearly 40% of the total amount.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0067","ex":"Azerbaijan (via Turkey) and Kazakhstan (via Russia) supplied around 70% of crude oil.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-KZ","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_crude_oil_to","amt":5300000,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2023-11/2025-10","ctx":"Around 5.3 million tonnes of Kazakh CPC crude shipped to Israel via Russia (OCI). amt is in metric tonnes.","id":"REL-G0034","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0066","ex":"Kazakhstan came second at around 5.3 million tonnes shipped through Russia.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0068","ex":"Tengizchevroil, a joint venture (JV) between Chevron (50%), ExxonMobil Kazakhstan (25%), KazMunayGas (20%) and Lukoil (5%)","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-AZ","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"granted_gas_exploration_licence_by","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":33,"date":"2025-03-18","ctx":"Israel awarded offshore gas exploration licences to a SOCAR–BP–NewMed consortium, with each partner holding about one-third and SOCAR as operator.","id":"REL-G0035","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0070","ex":"Each company in the consortium will hold around one-third of the rights in each licence, with Socar acting as the operator.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-TR","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"transit_for_crude_to","amt":1.27,"cur":"USD","pct":40,"date":"2024","ctx":"Turkey collects $1.27 per barrel through the BTC pipeline, which supplies around 40% of Israel's crude, and tankers kept sailing from Ceyhan to Ashkelon after the May 2024 trade ban.","id":"REL-G0036","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0072","ex":"Turkey collects $1.27 per barrel of oil transported through the Baku-Tbilisi-Ceyhan (BTC) pipeline","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0072","ex":"BTC is known to supply around 40 percent of Israel's annual crude oil consumption","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0073","ex":"eight journeys tracked since Ankara's imposition of a trade embargo in May","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-EG","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"gas_import_deal","amt":35000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-08-07","ctx":"Egypt agreed to import about 130 bcm of Leviathan gas through 2040 for $35B. Netanyahu approved the deal in December 2025.","id":"REL-G0037","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0074","ex":"130 billion cubic meters (bcm) of natural gas to Egypt through 2040","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0075","ex":"Egypt signs $35bn deal to import natural gas from Israel","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0076","ex":"This deal greatly strengthens Israel's status as a regional energy power.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-MA","b":"COM-00007","rel":"bought_artillery_from","amt":36,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2025-02","ctx":"Morocco contracted Elbit for 36 ATMOS 2000 self-propelled howitzers.","id":"REL-G0038","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0081","ex":"The Royal Moroccan Armed Forces have contracted Elbit Systems for the delivery of 36 ATMOS 2000 self-propelled artillery systems","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-MA","b":"COM-00008","rel":"bought_missile_system_from","amt":500000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"ctx":"A $500M Barak MX deal between Israel and Morocco, per Military Africa (Barak MX is an IAI system, WPN-00013).","id":"REL-G0039","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0081","ex":"$500 million deal was concluded between Israel and Morocco for the Barak MX air and missile defence system","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-MA","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"bilateral_trade_with","amt":116700000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023","ctx":"Morocco–Israel trade doubled to $116.7M in 2023, from $56.2M in 2022.","id":"REL-G0040","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0081","ex":"In 2023, trade between Morocco and Israel doubled, reaching $116.7 million compared to $56.2 million in 2022","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-BR","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_crude_oil_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":9,"date":"2023-11/2024","ctx":"Brazil supplied about 9% of Israel's crude imports, per OCI as cited by MEE. Direct shipments halted in January–August 2025.","id":"REL-G0041","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0082","ex":"Brazil quietly became the fourth largest exporter of crude oil to Israel, accounting for nine percent of its imports, according to a report by Oil Change International.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0082","ex":"Brazilian crude exports to Israel ground to a halt between January and August 2025.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-CO","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_coal_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":60,"date":"2023-2024","ctx":"Colombian coal was 60% of Israel's coal imports in 2023–24, per the UN Special Rapporteur report. It was banned from August 2024; the ban was reversed in August 2026.","id":"REL-G0042","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0084","ex":"Coal for electricity to Israel originates primarily from Colombia (60 per cent of Israeli coal imports in 2023-24)","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0086","ex":"Colombia prohibited coal exports to Israel through Decree 1047 of Aug. 14, 2024.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0086","ex":"In August 2026, the new government of Abelardo de la Espriella announced that coal exports to Israel could resume.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-CO","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"coal_exports_halted","amt":200000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-08/2026-08","ctx":"Industry body Fenalcarbón estimated the ban cut shipments to Israel by about 3.5 million tonnes a year, worth about $200M.","id":"REL-G0043","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0086","ex":"estimated that the restriction had reduced shipments to the Israeli market by about 3.5 million metric tons a year, worth roughly US$200 million.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-ZA","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_coal_to","amt":2990000,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2023-10/2025-12","ctx":"At least 2.99 million tonnes of coal were shipped from Richards Bay to Israel on at least 17 vessels (BDS monitoring via Daily Maverick). amt is in tonnes.","id":"REL-G0044","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0088","ex":"BDS monitored at least 17 vessels being loaded at Richards Bay between October 2023 and December 2025, which transported at least 2.99 million tonnes of coal to Israel","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0089","ex":"South Africa's exports increased by 87% to 474 000 metric tonnes in the three months to November 2025 on an annual basis","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-AR","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"military_cooperation_mou","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-04","ctx":"Milei and Netanyahu signed three MoUs on military and scientific cooperation and launched the 'Isaac Accords'.","id":"REL-G0045","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0091","ex":"both countries signed three memorandums of understanding to promote military and scientific cooperation between Israel and Argentina","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-PY","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"embassy_in_jerusalem","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-12-12","ctx":"Paraguay reopened its embassy in Jerusalem.","id":"REL-G0046","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0093","ex":"we were with you, we are with you, we will stay with the people of Israel forever.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-PH","b":"COM-00007","rel":"bought_munitions_from","amt":248000000,"cur":"PHP","pct":null,"date":"2025-08-11","ctx":"The Philippine Army awarded Elbit P248M for 100 rounds of 155mm precision-guided munitions.","id":"REL-G0047","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0094","ex":"100 rounds of high explosive (HE) 155mm precision-guided munition (PGM) ... Elbit Systems ... P248 million ... notice of award August 11, 2025","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-VN","b":"COM-00009","rel":"bought_missiles_from","amt":250000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-02","ctx":"About $250M for Rafael Spike missiles, including Firefly, with local production in Vietnam.","id":"REL-G0048","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0096","ex":"The Vietnamese army will be equipped with Spike anti-tank missiles manufactured by Rafael Advanced Defense Systems in a deal worth approximately $250 million.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0096","ex":"includes provisions for the missiles to be manufactured at a factory to be established in Vietnam, with the necessary know-how transferred from Israel.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-VN","b":"COM-00008","rel":"bought_satellites_from","amt":700000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025","ctx":"About $700M for two IAI intelligence satellites (ORF gives