","ex":"after spending just over $100,000 on its digital ad ... including Rob Stavis, a partner at the venture capital firm Bessemer and a vice chair of the Anti-Defamation League's board of directors, and Modi Wiczyk, a film producer and a board member at the Israel Policy Forum","pg":null}],"t":"election"},{"a":"PER-NEW-BLOOMBERG","b":"PER-NEW-CUOMO","rel":"funded_pacs_supporting","amt":13300000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025","ctx":"Michael Bloomberg gave $13.3M to pro-Cuomo super PACs: $8.3M to Fix the City in the primary, then $1.5M to Fix the City and $3.5M to For Our City in the final week.","id":"REL-P0068","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0109","ex":"Bloomberg's $13.3 million total is likely the largest individual contribution made in support of another candidate in New York history.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0117","ex":"Michael Bloomberg donated a combined $5 million to a couple of anti-Zohran Mamdani super PACs earlier this week ... Bloomberg had given $1.5 million to Fix the City ... pumping $3.5 million into the coffers of For Our City","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0109","ex":"Michael Bloomberg $5,000,000","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-ACKMAN","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"funded_pacs_opposing","amt":1750000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-10","ctx":"Bill Ackman spent $1.75M against Mamdani through Defend NYC and Fix the City.","id":"REL-P0069","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0114","ex":"contributed $1 million to the anti-Mamdani super PAC Defend NYC on October 14, and $250,000 to Fix The City on October 15 taking his total spending to $1.75 million.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-RLAUDER","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"funded_pacs_opposing","amt":2500000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025","ctx":"The four Lauders spent over $2.5M to target Mamdani and back Cuomo.","id":"REL-P0070","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0114","ex":"The four members of the Lauder family have spent over $2.5 million to target Mamdani and back Cuomo.","pg":