.","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0106","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0084","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0084","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0098","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0083","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0107","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0083","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0081","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0094","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0083","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0097","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0108","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0102","SRC-W0086","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0093","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0103","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0063"]}],"summary":"The GBU-31 is a 2,000-lb Mk-84 bomb fitted with Boeing's KMU-556 JDAM kit. The body came from General Dynamics' Garland, Texas plant, which REPKON USA bought in April 2025; fuzes come from Kaman (now Arcline) and L3Harris. On 7 February 2025 the US notified Israel of 13,000 KMU-556 kits and on 28 February 35,529 Mk-84/BLU-117 bodies, approved maximums whose delivery is undisclosed; Bellingcat reports over 14,000 Mk-84s delivered since October 2023. OHCHR assessed GBU-31s as likely used at Jabalia market (9 Oct 2023, 42 killed), the Taj3 tower (25 Oct 2023, 105 killed) and Shuja'iya (2 Dec 2023, about nine bombs, at least 60 reported killed). A CNN/Synthetaic count found over 500 craters wider than 40 feet, consistent with 2,000-lb bombs, in Gaza's first month.","transfers":[{"date":"2025-02-07","what":"13,000 KMU-556 JDAM kits for Mk-84 (approved maximum)","value_usd":null,"src":"https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support"},{"date":"2025-02-28","what":"35,529 Mk-84 or BLU-117 bomb bodies and 4,000 I-2000 penetrators, $2.04B, emergency waiver of congressional review (approved maximum)","value_usd":2040000000,"src":"https://www.asdnews.com/news/defense/2025/02/28/israel-munitions-munitions-support"},{"date":"2023-10 to 2026-02","what":"over 14,000 Mk-84 bombs reportedly delivered since 7 Oct 2023 (Bellingcat)","value_usd":null,"src":"https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/"}],"status":"documented"},{"id":"ARS-MK84","name":"Mk-84 2,000-lb general-purpose bomb","aka":["Mark 84","BLU-117 (Mk-84 variant body)"],"class":"bomb","form":"bomb","dims":{"length_m":3.84,"diameter_m":0.46,"span_m":null,"weight_kg":925},"specs":[{"k":"Weight","v":"2,039 lb (925 kg)","src":["SRC-W0109"]},{"k":"Warhead / fill","v":"946 lb (429 kg) Tritonal, H6 or PBXN-109","src":["SRC-W0109"]},{"k":"Crater","v":"up to 15 m wide and 11 m deep","src":["SRC-W0109"]},{"k":"Lethal fragmentation radius","v":"120 m (400 ft)","src":["SRC-W0109"]},{"k":"Guidance","v":"none (unguided) unless fitted with JDAM or SPICE kit","src":["SRC-V0251"]},{"k":"Unit cost","v":"about $16,000","src":["SRC-W0109"]},{"k":"Deliveries to Israe