RC-W0092","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0093","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0103","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0063"]},{"name":"Conical fin / tail kit","maker":"COM-00003 (if JDAM)","start":0.78,"end":1,"note":"","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0079","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0080","SRC-W0081","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0080","SRC-W0083","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0080","SRC-W0084","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069"]}],"summary":"The Mk-84 is the one-ton bomb at the centre of the Gaza genocide. Its steel body was made at General Dynamics' Garland, Texas plant, now owned by REPKON USA; Wikipedia lists it at about $16,000. Bellingcat reports more than 14,000 delivered to Israel since October 2023, and on 28 February 2025 the US used an emergency waiver to notify 35,529 Mk-84/BLU-117 bodies ($2.04B), an approved maximum. With 429 kg of explosive it can leave a crater 15 m wide and throw lethal fragments 120 m. UN investigators found Jabalia camp (31 Oct 2023) consistent with 2,000-lb-class bombs; experts cited by CNN said Mawasi tent-camp damage (10 Sep 2024) suggested 2,000-lb bombs; the Wall Street Journal reported eight 2,000-lb bombs, at least one US-made, at al-Mawasi on 13 July 2024. CNN counted over 500 craters wider than 40 feet in Gaza's first month.","transfers":[{"date":"2025-02-28","what":"35,529 Mk-84 or BLU-117 bodies (approved maximum)","value_usd":2040000000,"src":"https://www.asdnews.com/news/defense/2025/02/28/israel-munitions-munitions-support"},{"date":"2023-10 to 2026-02","what":"over 14,000 Mk-84 delivered (reported)","value_usd":null,"src":"https://www.bellingcat.com/news/2026/02/04/made-in-the-usa-how-american-built-weapons-have-wrought-destruction-in-gaza/"}],"status":"documented"},{"id":"ARS-MK80","name":"Mk-80 series general-purpose bombs (Mk-82 / Mk-83 / Mk-84)","aka":["Mk-82 500-lb","Mk-83 1,000-lb","BLU-110","GBU-32 / GBU-38 when JDAM-fitted"],"class":"bomb","form":"bomb","dims":{"length_m":2.21,"diameter_m":0.273,"span_m":null,"weight_kg":241},"specs":[{"k":"Family","v":"500-lb Mk-82, 1,000-lb Mk-83, 2,000-lb Mk-84; remnants often identifiable only to family level","src":["SRC-W0112"]},{"k":"Mk-82 weight","v":"531 lb (241 kg) (dims shown are Mk-82)","src":["SRC-W0113"]},{"k":"Mk-82 fill","v":"196 lb (89 kg) Tritonal, H6 or PBXN-109","src":["SRC-W0113"]},{"k":"Mk-82 unit cost","v":"about $4,000","src":["SRC-W0113"]},{"k":"Guidance","v":"unguided; JDAM, SPICE or other kits added","src":["SRC-W0114"]},{"k":"Feb 2025 US sales","v":"2,800 Mk-82 bodies (7 Feb); 201 Mk-83 and 4,799 BLU-110 (28 Feb)","src":["SRC-V0092"]}],"makers":[{"entity":"COM-00004","role":"body (General Dynamics, per Wikipedia Mk-82 infobox)","src":["SRC-W0113"]},{"entity":"COM-00022","role":"body, principal contractor for Mk-83/BLU-110 in Feb 28, 2025 sale (Repkon USA, Tampa FL)","src":["SRC-V0092"]},{"entity":"McAlester Army Ammunition Plant","role":"principal contractor in Feb 7, 2025 package","src":["SRC-0027"]}],"parts":[{"name":"Steel case","maker"