"SRC-W0092","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0063"]},{"name":"JDAM tail kit","maker":"COM-00003","start":0.75,"end":1,"note":"Present at Younine, Bachoura, Khadija school.","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0062","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0086","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0086","SRC-W0088","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0097","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0086","SRC-W0101","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0091","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0105","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0065"]}],"summary":"Mk-80 series bombs are the workhorse US general-purpose bombs, and remnants are often identifiable only to the family. The US notified Israel of 2,800 Mk-82 bodies on 7 February 2025, and 201 Mk-83s and 4,799 BLU-110s on 28 February with Repkon USA as principal contractor; these are approved maximums. HRW identified a Mk-80 bomb with a US JDAM kit in the strike that killed 22 members of a Syrian family, 13 of them children, at Younine on 25 September 2024, with one more dying later; Amnesty identified a Mk-80 fragment of at least 500 lb at Aitou, more than 115 km from the border, where 24 people died on 14 October 2024. HRW verified a JDAM kit for Mk-80 bombs at the Bachoura strike in central Beirut (10 Oct 2024). Bellingcat found Mk-80 bombs with JDAM kits at Khadija school in Gaza (27 July 2024) and in the demolition of at least seven Gaza City high-rises in 2025. OHCHR assessed GBU-32 (1,000-lb JDAM) use at Jabalia camp.","transfers":[{"date":"2025-02-07","what":"2,800 Mk-82 500-lb bomb bodies (approved maximum)","value_usd":null,"src":"https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support"},{"date":"2025-02-28","what":"201 Mk-83 and 4,799 BLU-110 bombs with 5,000 JDAM kits, $675.7M (approved maximum; deliveries from 2028)","value_usd":675700000,"src":"https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4088252/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-and-munitions-support"}],"status":"documented"},{"id":"ARS-BLU109","name":"BLU-109 2,000-lb penetrator","aka":["GBU-31(V)3 with JDAM","bunker buster"],"class":"bunker buster","form":"bomb","dims":{"length_m":2.41,"diameter_m":0.37,"span_m":null,"weight_kg":910},"specs":[{"k":"Weight","v":"2,000 lb (910 kg)","src":["SRC-W0118"]},{"k":"Case","v":"steel casing about 25 mm thick","src":["SRC-W0118"]},{"k":"Fill","v":"550 lb (250 kg) Tritonal","src":["SRC-W0118"]},{"k":"Fuze","v":"FMU-143 delayed-action tail fuze","src":["SRC-W0118"]},{"k":"Guidance","v":"KMU-557 JDAM kit (GBU-31 configuration)","src":["SRC-0027"]},{"k":"Feb 2025 sale","v":"3,475 KMU-557 JDAM kits for BLU-109 (approved maximum)","src":["SRC-0027"]},{"k":"Earlier delivery","v":"100 BLU-109s delivered to Israel in late 2023 (reported)","src":["SRC-W0118"]}],"makers":[{"entity":"COM-00003","role":"guidance (KMU-557 JDAM kit)","src":["SRC-0027"]}],"parts":[{"name":"Thick steel penetrator case","maker":"unattributed","start":0,"end":0.75,"note":"Maker of Israel-bound cases not established in sources reviewed.","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0115","SRC-W0116","SRC-W0117","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0089","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0102","SRC-W0080","SRC-W0091","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0091"]},{"name":"Tritonal fill","maker":"unattributed","start":0.15,"end":0.7,"note":"250 kg.","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0115","SRC-W0116","SRC-W0117","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0089","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0102","SRC-W0080","SRC-W0091","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0091"]},{"name":"Delayed tail fuze","maker":"unattributed","start":0.7,"end":0.78,"note":"FMU-143.","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0115","SRC-W0116","SRC-W0117","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0089","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0102","SRC-W0080","SRC-W0091","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0091"]},{"name":"KMU-557 JDAM tail kit","maker":"COM-00003","start":0.75,"end":1,"note":"","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0106","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0084","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0084","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0098","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0083","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0107","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0083","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0081","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0094","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0083","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0097","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0108","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0102","SRC-W0086","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0093","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0103","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0063"]}],"summary":"The BLU-109 is a 2,000-lb bomb with a thick steel case built to punch through concrete before exploding, guided by Boeing's KMU-557 JDAM kit. The US delivered 100 to Israel in late 2023, and on 7 February 2025 notified 3,475 more JDAM kits for it, an approved maximum. An IDF image analysed by OSMP showed three BLU-109s with JDAM kits on an F-15I of 69 Squadron after the 27 September 2024 strike that killed Hassan Nasrallah in Haret Hreik; the New York Times cited an analyst saying eight F-15Is carried at least 15 2,000-lb munitions with US guidance. At al-Saksakieh on 23 September 2024 ARES classified debris from a strike on a family home, which killed at least two civilians, as a 2,000-lb penetrator with a JDAM kit (Airwars). Bellingcat documented BLU-109s with JDAM kits in US Department of Defense imagery from the 2026 war on Iran.","transfers":[{"date":"2023-late","what":"100 BLU-109 bombs delivered (reported)","value_usd":null,"src":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BLU-109_bomb"},{"date":"2025-02-07","what":"3,475 KMU-557 JDAM kits for BLU-109 (approved maximum)","value_usd":null,"src":"https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support"}],"status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00006","name":"GBU-39/B Small Diameter Bomb","aka":["SDB","SDB I","250-lb glide bomb"],"class":"guided bomb","form":"bomb","dims":{"length_m":1.8,"diameter_m":0.19,"span_m":1.61,"weight_kg":129},"specs":[{"k":"Weight","v":"285 lb (129 kg); '250-pound class'","src":["SRC-V0256"]},{"k":"Warhead","v":"36 lb (16 kg) AFX-757 insensitive explosive; penetrates >0.9 m of reinforced concrete","src":["SRC-V0256"]},{"k":"Guidance","v":"GPS/INS","src":["SRC-0028"]},{"k":"Accuracy (CEP)","v":"about 1 m","src":["SRC-V0256"]},{"k":"Range","v":"more than 40 nmi (US Air Force); over 60 nmi air-dropped (Wikipedia)","src":["SRC-0028"]},{"k":"Unit cost","v":"about $40,000 (FY2021)","src":["SRC-0028"]},{"k":"Fragment hazard","v":"113 kg bombs that can throw metal fragments hundreds of metres (Amnesty)","src":["SRC-W0122"]},{"k":"Earlier Israeli buys","v":"3,450 (2012) and 4,100 (2015)","src":["SRC-V0256"]}],"makers":[{"entity":"COM-00003","role":"prime","src":["SRC-0028"]},{"entity":"MBDA Inc (Huntsville, Alabama; MBDA group)","role":"wings ('sole known supplier', Disclose)","src":["SRC-W0123"]}],"parts":[{"name":"Penetrating warhead (AFX-757)","maker":"COM-00003","start":0,"end":0.55,"note":"16 kg explosive.","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0064"