W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0103","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0093","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0062","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0094","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0062","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0073"]}],"summary":"The GBU-39 is Boeing's 129-kg satellite-guided glide bomb; MBDA Inc in Alabama makes its wings, according to Disclose. Israel bought 3,450 in 2012 and 4,100 in 2015; on 7 February 2025 the US notified 2,166 more, an approved maximum. It has become a signature weapon of strikes on shelters. OHCHR assessed four at al-Bureij camp (2 Nov 2023, 15 verified killed) and two at al-Buraq school (10 Nov 2023, at least 34 killed). Amnesty identified GBU-39s at the Nofal home in Tal al-Sultan (9 Jan 2024, 18 killed) and at the Kuwaiti Peace Camp in Rafah (26 May 2024, at least 36 killed). Bellingcat found GBU-39 remnants at 20 of 28 school strikes involving US munitions, including Khadija school and Fahmi al-Jarjawi. The Lebanese Army identified two in the Ain Saadeh strike of 5 April 2026.","transfers":[{"date":"2025-02-07","what":"2,166 GBU-39/B (approved maximum)","value_usd":null,"src":"https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support"},{"date":"2026-03","what":"Boeing contract for up to 5,000 Small Diameter Bombs for Israel, $289M (reported by Reuters citing Bloomberg; not fetched by us)","value_usd":289000000,"src":"https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/boeing-signs-289-million-israel-contract-5000-smart-bombs-bloomberg-n