27","ex":"two thousand one hundred sixty-six (2,166) GBU-39/B Small Diameter Bombs Increment 1 ... thirteen thousand (13,000) KMU-556E/B ... JDAM Guidance Kits ... seventeen thousand four hundred seventy-five (17,475) FMU-152A/B fuzes ... $6.75 billion","pg":null}],"quantity_type":"approved maximum"},{"id":"REL-V0065","t":"edge","a":"COM-00025","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"supplies_naval_guns_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Leonardo's OTO Melara 76mm guns arm Israel's Sa'ar 4.5, 5 and 6 warships. A Sa'ar 6 was first used in combat against Gaza on Oct 16, 2023.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0145","ex":"The Sa'ar 6 warship was used operationally for the first time on Oct. 16, 2023, during Israel's massive attacks on Gaza. ... In 2012, Israel acquired 30 Aermacchi M-346 planes, known in Israel as the Lavi, in a deal worth some $1 billion.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0066","t":"edge","a":"COM-00025","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"supplied_aircraft_to","amt":1000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2012","st":"documented","ctx":"Israel bought 30 M-346 'Lavi' trainers for about $1B.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0145","ex":"The Sa'ar 6 warship was used operationally for the first time on Oct. 16, 2023, during Israel's massive attacks on Gaza. ... In 2012, Israel acquired 30 Aermacchi M-346 planes, known in Israel as the Lavi, in a deal worth some $1 billion.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0067","t":"edge","a":"COM-00029","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplies_gas_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"H1 2026","st":"documented","ctx":"Energean sold 2.13 bcm of gas into Israel's domestic market in H1 2026 and paid $26M in current Israeli tax.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0022","ex":"Energean sold 2.13 bcm of gas into the domestic Israeli market ... production was impacted by the temporary suspension of operations for 41 days between 28 February and 9 April 2026, following a directive from the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0068","t":"money","a":"PER-N-TRUMP","b":"CTR-00001","rel":"approved_arms_sale","amt":6750000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-02-07","st":"documented","ctx":"Two weeks into his second term, Donald Trump's State Department approved a $6.75B sale of munitions, guidance kits and fuzes to Israel, including 13,000 JDAM kits, with Boeing as lead contractor.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0027","ex":"WASHINGTON, February 7, 2025 - The State Department has approved a possible Foreign Military Sale to the Government of Israel of Munitions, Guidance Kits, Fuzes, and Munitions Support and related equipment for an estimated cost of $6.75 billion.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-0027","ex":"thirteen thousand (13,000) KMU-556 ... The Boeing Company, located in St. Louis, MO","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0069","t":"money","a":"PER-N-TRUMP","b":"CTR-00002","rel":"approved_arms_sale","amt":660000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-02-07","st":"documented","ctx":"The Trump administration approved 3,000 Lockheed Martin Hellfire missiles for Israel, worth $660M.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0029","ex":"3,000 AGM-114 Hellfire Air-to-Ground Missiles ... an estimated cost of $660 million ... The principal contractor will be the Lockheed Martin Corporation, located in Troy, AL.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0070","t":"money","a":"PER-N-TRUMP","b":"CTR-00003","rel":"approved_arms_sale_emergency","amt":2040000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-02-28","st":"documented","ctx":"Trump's Secretary of State declared an emergency to bypass Congressional review and approve $2.04B in bomb bodies and penetrators for Israel, with General Dynamics a prime contractor.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0039","ex":"The Secretary of State has made a determination approving a possible Foreign Military Sale to the Government of Israel of Munitions ... an emergency exists that requires the immediate sale","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-0039","ex":"estimated cost of $2.04 billion ... The prime contractors will be General Dynamics, located in Garland, TX","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0071","t":"edge","a":"PER-N-TRUMP","b":"LBL-U-S-MILITARY-OPERATIONS-AGAINST-IRAN","rel":"authorized","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-02-27","st":"documented","ctx":"Donald Trump authorized Operation Epic Fury on 27 February 2026; US and Israeli strikes on Iran began the next day. OCHA counts more than 3,400 civilians killed in Iran.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0020","ex":"On 27 February at 3:38 p.m. EST, Trump, traveling on Air Force One to Texas, authorized Operation Epic Fury.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0020","ex":"Per OCHA: 3,400+ civilians killed 33,000+ civilians injured","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0072","t":"edge","a":"PER-N-TRUMP","b":"COM-00018","rel":"ordered_federal_ban","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-02-27","st":"documented","ctx":"Donald Trump ordered every federal agency to stop using Anthropic after it refused Pentagon demands to allow fully autonomous weapons and mass domestic surveillance.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0236","ex":"I am directing EVERY Federal Agency in the United States Government to IMMEDIATELY CEASE all use of Anthropic's technology.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0236","ex":"no use of its artificial intelligence for fully autonomous weapons ... no mass domestic surveillance","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0073","t":"edge","a":"PER-N-TRUMP","b":"COM-00003","rel":"administration_awarded_contract","amt":8600000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-12","st":"documented","ctx":"In late December 2025 Trump's Pentagon awarded Boeing a contract worth up to $8.6B to build F-15IA fighter jets for Israel.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0018","ex":"In late December 2025, the U.S. Department of Defense awarded Boeing a contract valued at up to $8.6 billion to manufacture F-15IA fighter jets for Israel.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0074","t":"edge","a":"PER-00004","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"co_announced_stargate","amt":500000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-01-21","st":"documented","ctx":"Larry Ellison joined Donald Trump, Sam Altman and Masayoshi Son at the White House on Trump's first full day back in office to unveil the $500B Stargate AI infrastructure project.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0023","ex":"he gathered Oracle founder Larry Ellison, OpenAI CEO Sam Altman and SoftBank chief Masayoshi Son at the Roosevelt Room in the White House to unveil a $500 billion artificial intelligence project","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0075","t":"edge","a":"PER-00030","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"donated_to_inaugural_committee","amt":1000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-12","st":"documented","ctx":"Sam Altman gave $1M to Donald Trump's inaugural committee, then joined him to launch Stargate.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0233","ex":"An OpenAI spokesperson confirmed to ABC News that Altman donated $1 million to the inaugural committee in December.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0023","ex":"I think if it were a different President, it might not have been possible. But we are thrilled to get to do this.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0076","t":"edge","a":"PER-00031","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"donated_to_pro_trump_super_pac","amt":25000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-09","st":"documented","ctx":"Greg Brockman gave $12.5M to MAGA Inc, Donald Trump's super PAC, and his wife Anna gave the same amount the same day, $25M combined.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0022","ex":"Brockman, whose OpenAI is at the center of the artificial intelligence boom, gave $12.5 million to the Trump super PAC in September. ... His wife, Anna, appears to have also donated the same amount that same day.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0077","t":"edge","a":"PER-00022","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"donated_to_pro_trump_super_pac","amt":1000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-12","st":"documented","ctx":"Palantir CEO Alex Karp gave $1M to MAGA Inc, Donald Trump's super PAC, in December 2024.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0022","ex":"$1 million donation to MAGA Inc. in December 2024","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0078","t":"edge","a":"PER-00009","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"donated_to_support","amt":106000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024","st":"reported","ctx":"Miriam Adelson was the third-largest donor to Donald Trump's 2024 campaign, at $106M, and sought his support for Israel's annexation of the West Bank.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0021","ex":"She was the third largest donor to Trump's 2024 election bid, donating $106 million. ... sought support from Trump for Israel's annexation of the West Bank","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0079","t":"edge","a":"PER-00005","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"donated_to_support","amt":5000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024","st":"reported","ctx":"Elliott Management founder Paul Singer gave $5M to Donald Trump's 2024 re-election effort.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0182","ex":"In 2024, he donated $5 million to Trump's re-election campaign.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0080","t":"edge","a":"PER-00001","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"lobbied","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2025-03","st":"documented","ctx":"Larry Fink phoned Donald Trump's White House directly to pitch BlackRock's deal for CK Hutchison's ports, including two at the Panama Canal, a deal that would hand the seller $19B.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0163","ex":"Within weeks, Wall Street billionaire Larry Fink was on the line with the White House. ... The deal, which will hand the seller $19 billion","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0081","t":"edge","a":"COM-00011","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"donated_to_inaugural_committee","amt":1000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-01","st":"documented","ctx":"Amazon gave $1M to Donald Trump's inauguration, which Jeff Bezos attended after blocking The Washington Post's endorsement of Kamala Harris.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0219","ex":"Amazon subsequently donated $1 million to Trump's inauguration, at which Bezos was in attendance.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0082","t":"edge","a":"PER-00011","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"son_in_law_and_adviser","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2017–2021; 2025–","st":"documented","ctx":"Jared Kushner, Donald Trump's son-in-law, was a senior White House adviser in 2017–2021 and has acted for the second Trump administration, including in early 2026 nuclear talks with Iran.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0190","ex":"He also served in the Trump administration from 2017 to 2021.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0083","t":"edge","a":"PER-N-TRUMP","b":"GOV-00001","rel":"sanctioned_icc_personnel","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2025-02","st":"documented","ctx":"In February 2025 Donald Trump signed Executive Order 14203 sanctioning International Criminal Court personnel, after the court issued an arrest warrant for Benjamin Netanyahu.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0019","ex":"In February 2025, the second Donald Trump administration signed Executive Order 14203 sanctioning ICC personnel with asset freezes and travel bans.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0084","t":"edge","a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"prime_minister","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2022–","st":"documented","ctx":"Benjamin Netanyahu heads the Israeli government that has waged the wars on Gaza, Lebanon and Iran since October 2023.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0026","ex":"Netanyahu's government has been orchestrating the genocide in Gaza","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0085","t":"edge","a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"directs_war","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023–2026","st":"documented","ctx":"Netanyahu directed Israel's military campaign in Gaza, ordered the October 2024 invasion of Lebanon and launched the 2025 and 2026 air campaigns against Iran. The ICC issued a warrant for his arrest in November 2024 and the UN Commission of Inquiry found in September 2025 that he incited genocide.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0019","ex":"On 21 November 2024, following an investigation of war crimes and crimes against humanity, the International Criminal Court (ICC) issued arrest warrants for two senior Israeli officials, Benjamin Netanyahu, the prime minister of Israel, and Yoav Gallant ... alleging responsibility for the war crime of starvation as a method of warfare and the crimes against humanity of murder, persecution, and other inhumane acts","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0025","ex":"Israeli President Isaac Herzog, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and then Defence Minister Yoav Gallant, have incited the commission of genocide","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0086","t":"edge","a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"lobbied_for_joint_strike","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026","st":"reported","ctx":"In early 2026 Benjamin Netanyahu lobbied Donald Trump for a joint military strike on Iran; the war began on 28 February 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0020","ex":"In early 2026, Israeli prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu lobbied President Donald Trump for a joint military strike on Iran.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0087","t":"edge","a":"PER-00004","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"offered_board_seat","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"reported","ctx":"The Intercept reported that Larry Ellison once offered Benjamin Netanyahu a seat on Oracle's board and invited him to his private Hawaiian island.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0027","ex":"Once offered Netanyahu a seat on Oracle's board of directors ... Invited Netanyahu to visit his private Hawaiian island","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0088","t":"edge","a":"ORG-00003","b":"PER-N-BOWMAN","rel":"spent_opposing","amt":9900000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-06-25","st":"documented","ctx":"UDP spent almost $9.9M opposing Representative Jamaal Bowman in the June 2024 NY-16 Democratic primary, the most expensive House primary in US history. Bowman lost to George Latimer, 41.4% to 58.6%.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0132","ex":"United Democracy Project spent almost $9.9 million to oppose Bowman and nearly $4.8 million to support Latimer.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0089","t":"edge","a":"ORG-00003","b":"PER-N-LATIMER","rel":"spent_supporting","amt":4800000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-06-25","st":"documented","ctx":"UDP spent nearly $4.8M supporting George Latimer in the June 2024 NY-16 primary; he defeated Jamaal Bowman.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0132","ex":"United Democracy Project spent almost $9.9 million to oppose Bowman and nearly $4.8 million to support Latimer.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0090","t":"edge","a":"ORG-00003","b":"PER-N-BUSH","rel":"spent_opposing","amt":5200000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-08-06","st":"documented","ctx":"UDP spent more than $5.2M against Representative Cori Bush in the August 2024 MO-1 Democratic primary, after she introduced a Gaza ceasefire resolution. Bush lost to Wesley Bell.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0132","ex":"United Democracy Project spent more than $5.2 million against Democratic Rep. Cori Bush of Missouri.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0091","t":"edge","a":"ORG-00003","b":"PER-N-BELL","rel":"spent_supporting","amt":3300000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-08-06","st":"documented","ctx":"UDP spent $3.3M backing Wesley Bell in the August 2024 MO-1 primary; he defeated Cori Bush and beat her again in 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0132","ex":"UDP spent $3.3 million backing Wesley Bell's candidacy","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0092","t":"edge","a":"PER-N-RAMJI","b":"FND-00002","rel":"ceo","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-07–","st":"documented","ctx":"Salim Ramji, a former BlackRock executive, has been Vanguard's CEO since July 2024.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0030","ex":"In May 2024, Vanguard announced the appointment of Salim Ramji...as its next CEO...effective July 2024.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0093","t":"money","a":"FND-00004","b":"ORG-00013","rel":"affiliated_daf_granted_to","amt":2200000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"reported 2024-04","st":"reported","ctx":"Fidelity Charitable, the donor-advised fund of Abigail Johnson's Fidelity, passed $2.2M to Friends of the IDF, according to Rolling Stone, while blocking donations to UNRWA USA in 2024.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0172","ex":"$2.2 million to Friends of the Israel Defense Forces","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0094","t":"edge","a":"PER-00008","b":"ORG-00001","rel":"donated_to","amt":2000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2022","st":"reported","ctx":"WhatsApp co-founder Jan Koum gave $2M to AIPAC during the 2022 Democratic primaries.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0188","ex":"In 2022, he donated $2 million to AIPAC during the Democratic Party primaries.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0095","t":"edge","a":"PER-00005","b":"ORG-00006","rel":"board_member","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"reported","ctx":"Paul Singer sits on the board of the Republican Jewish Coalition.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0182","ex":"He serves on the board of the Republican Jewish Coalition","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0096","t":"edge","a":"PER-00023","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"founders_met_and_partnered","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-01","st":"documented","ctx":"Peter Thiel and Alex Karp met Israeli military officials in Tel Aviv in January 2024, when Palantir held a board meeting there 'in solidarity with Israel' and agreed a strategic partnership with the Israel Ministry of Defense.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0042","ex":"a Thursday meeting between Israeli defense officials and Palantir co-founders Peter Thiel and Alex Karp in Tel Aviv","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-0042","ex":"Both parties have mutually agreed to harness Palantir's advanced technology in support of war-related missions ... Palantir held a board meeting in Tel Aviv for the first time this week in solidarity with Israel.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0097","t":"edge","a":"PER-00034","b":"COM-00019","rel":"executive_vice_chair","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2025-09–","st":"documented","ctx":"Safra Catz, Oracle's CEO from 2014 to September 2025, is now executive vice chair. The Intercept reported she told staff: 'if you're not for America or Israel, don't work here.'","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0027","ex":"For employees, it's clear: if you're not for America or Israel, don't work here—this is a free country.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0098","t":"edge","a":"ORG-00001","b":"ORG-00002","rel":"operates","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2021-12-15","st":"documented","ctx":"AIPAC runs AIPAC PAC, its federal bundling PAC registered in December 2021, which gave $53.7M to other committees in 2023–24 and $47.8M in 2025–Aug 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0279","ex":"Coverage January 1, 2023 – December 31, 2024. Total receipts: $57,871,196.42 ... Total spending: $57,417,825.13 ... Contributions to other committees: $53,699,474.91","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0281","ex":"Coverage January 1, 2025 – August 31, 2026. Total Receipts: $52,335,344.82; Total Disbursements: $50,496,735.50; Contributions to Other Committees: $47,763,399.34","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0099","t":"edge","a":"ORG-00001","b":"ORG-00003","rel":"operates","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2022-01-03","st":"documented","ctx":"AIPAC launched the United Democracy Project super PAC in January 2022. Louisville Public Media describes UDP as 'largely funded by' AIPAC.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0082","ex":"Spending $4.1 million on mostly attack ads against Massie was United Democracy Project, a PAC largely funded by the American Israel Public Affairs Committee (AIPAC). ... Spending $3.9 million on mostly positive Gallrein ads was the Republican Jewish Coalition Victory Fund.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0280","ex":"Coverage January 1, 2023 – December 31, 2024. Total Receipts: $87,176,557.14; Total Disbursements: $61,373,652.54; Independent Expenditures: $37,859,810.12","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0100","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00007","b":"WPN-00006","rel":"used_in_documented_strikes","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-05-26","st":"documented","ctx":"The IDF used Boeing GBU-39 bombs in the Rafah tent-camp strike of 26 May 2024 (at least 45 killed, CNN) and the Nuseirat UN school strike of 6 June 2024 (at least 32 killed, NPR).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0257","ex":"the tail of a US-made GBU-39 small diameter bomb (SDB) is visible, according to four explosive weapons experts ... The GBU-39, which is manufactured by Boeing, is a high-precision munition ... At least 45 people were killed and more than 200 others injured","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0258","ex":"The munition used was a GBU-39 small-diameter bomb, according to a Pentagon official and a former U.S. Air Force official. ... the 2 a.m. strike killed at least 32 people, including seven children","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0101","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00007","b":"WPN-00001","rel":"used_in_documented_strikes","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023-10-10","st":"documented","ctx":"Amnesty found JDAM parts in two October 2023 IDF strikes on family homes in Deir al-Balah that killed 43 civilians. Bellingcat documented JDAM-guided bombs destroying Gaza City towers in 2025.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0253","ex":"US-made Joint Direct Attack Munitions (JDAM) were used by the Israeli military in two deadly, unlawful air strikes on homes full of civilians in the occupied Gaza Strip ... On October 10, an air strike on the al-Najjar family home in Deir al-Balah killed 24 people. ... On October 22, an air strike on the Abu Mu'eileq family home in the same city killed 19 people.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0093","ex":"Bellingcat was able to identify that at least seven high-rise buildings in Gaza City, including Al Soussi Tower, Al Roya Tower, and Al Roya 2 Tower, were issued evacuation notices then destroyed using MK-80 series bombs with JDAM kits. ... the JDAM kit is one of several guidance kits that can attach to bombs like the MK-84 but which is only produced by the US.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0102","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00007","b":"WPN-00007","rel":"used_in_documented_strikes","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-06","st":"documented","ctx":"Bellingcat found Hellfire missiles in IDF strikes on a Gaza City clinic (June 2024), on tents near Al-Aqsa Martyrs Hospital and on Cairo Basic School (July 2025, five killed).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0093","ex":"A Hellfire missile was used in a June 2024 strike on a health clinic in Gaza City that killed Hani al-Jafarawi, the director of ambulance and emergency services in Gaza. ... Four of these strikes used Hellfire missiles to target tents within approximately 150 meters of the Al Aqsa Martyr's Hospital Main Complex in Deir Al Balah. ... A July 2025 strike on Cairo Basic School where five people were reported killed and where remnants of a Hellfire missile was found.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0103","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00007","b":"WPN-00015","rel":"uses","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-02","st":"reported","ctx":"The Israeli army used Elbit's PULS launcher extensively in Gaza and Lebanon, according to Arms industry Europe (Feb 2024).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0270","ex":"The PULS rocket artillery system is being used extensively by the Israeli Defence Forces (IDF) in the ongoing war in Gaza and Lebanon. ... The very accurate rockets launched by the systems have destroyed a great number of targets on the two fronts","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0104","t":"edge","a":"ORG-00006","b":"ORG-00003","rel":"co_targeted_with","amt":3900000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-05-19","st":"documented","ctx":"In the May 2026 Kentucky primary, the RJC Victory Fund spent $3.9M backing Ed Gallrein while UDP spent $4.1M attacking Thomas Massie, who lost 54–45.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0082","ex":"Spending $4.1 million on mostly attack ads against Massie was United Democracy Project, a PAC largely funded by the American Israel Public Affairs Committee (AIPAC). ... Spending $3.9 million on mostly positive Gallrein ads was the Republican Jewish Coalition Victory Fund.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0282","ex":"lost his bid for re-election to primary opponent Ed Gallrein 54% to 45% ... supported a series of war powers votes as a major critic of Trump's war on Iran","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0105","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00001","b":"CTY-00002","rel":"government_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The U.S. federal government is the governing body of the United States country node.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0031","ex":"2024-09-30 | $874,040,585,085.73 ... 2025-09-30 | $916,648,676,662.05 (National Defense, current FYTD outlays)","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0106","t":"money","a":"CTY-00002","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"military_aid_to","amt":21700000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023-10-07 to 2025-09-30","st":"documented","ctx":"Costs of War counts at least $21.7B in US military aid to Israel in the first two years of the Gaza genocide: $17.9B in year one and $3.8B in year two.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0035","ex":"The United States has provided at least $21.7 billion in military aid to Israel since the start of the war in Gaza on October 7, 2023. ... the U.S. provided $17.9 billion in the first year of war and $3.8 billion in the second year.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0107","t":"money","a":"CTY-00002","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"cumulative_aid_to","amt":298000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"1946–2024 (constant 2024 dollars)","st":"documented","ctx":"CRS estimates total US aid obligated to Israel from 1946 to 2024 at $298B in inflation-adjusted 2024 dollars ($174B in current dollars).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0036","ex":"To date, the United States has provided Israel $174 billion (current, or non-inflation-adjusted, dollars) in bilateral assistance and missile defense funding. ... in constant 2024 U.S. dollars (inflation-adjusted), total U.S. aid to Israel obligated from 1946-2024 is an estimated $298 billion.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0108","t":"ownership","a":"CTY-00002","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_supplier_share","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":68,"date":"2021–2025","st":"documented","ctx":"SIPRI: the US accounted for 68% of Israel's imports of major arms in 2021–25.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0034","ex":"The USA was the largest supplier to Israel in 2021–25 (accounting for 68 per cent of Israeli arms imports), followed by Germany (31 per cent).","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0109","t":"money","a":"CTY-00002","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_sales_notified","amt":3800000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-01-30","st":"documented","ctx":"DSCA notified AH-64E Apache helicopters for Israel, principal contractors Boeing and Lockheed Martin.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0001","ex":"AH-64E Apache Helicopters and related equipment ... $3.8 billion ... The Boeing Company, located in Arlington, VA; and Lockheed Martin, located in Orlando, FL","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0110","t":"money","a":"CTY-00002","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_sales_notified","amt":1980000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-01-30","st":"documented","ctx":"DSCA notified Joint Light Tactical Vehicles for Israel (AM General).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0343","ex":"Joint Light Tactical Vehicle and related equipment ... The estimated total cost is $1.98 billion ... AM General LLC, located in Auburn Hills, MI and Mishawaka, IN","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0111","t":"money","a":"CTY-00002","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_sales_notified","amt":740000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-01-30","st":"documented","ctx":"DSCA notified Namer armoured personnel carrier power packs for Israel (Rolls-Royce Solutions America).","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0344","ex":"Namer Armored Personnel Carrier Power Packs Less Transmissions and Integrated Logistics Support ... $740 million ... Rolls-Royce Solutions America, Inc., located in Novi, MI","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0112","t":"money","a":"CTY-00002","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"emergency_arms_sale","amt":650000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-03-08","st":"documented","ctx":"Secretary of State Marco Rubio invoked an emergency to waive congressional review for more than 20,000 bombs, including 12,000 BLU-110A/B 1,000-lb bomb bodies, during the Iran war.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0037","ex":"Secretary of State Marco Rubio determined that an emergency existed that required an immediate sale to Israel and waived the congressional review requirements. (sale of more than 20,000 bombs, including 12,000 BLU-110A/B 1,000-pound bomb bodies, about $650 million)","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0113","t":"money","a":"CTY-00002","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_sale_planned","amt":2800000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-09-17","st":"documented","ctx":"Proposed $2.8B taxpayer-funded sale of 40,000 one-ton bombs for Israel, informally notified to Congress in Sept 2026 and held by Rep. Gregory Meeks from 16 Sept 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0345","ex":"$2.8 billion arms package for Israel ... 40,000 one-ton bombs ... funded with US taxpayer dollars","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0318","ex":"Meeks Places Hold on Trump Administration's $2.8 Billion Bomb Sale to Israel ... the Trump administration's proposed sale of 40,000 2,000-pound bombs ... not provided sufficient assurances that these weapons will be used by the Netanyahu government in accordance with U.S. law","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0319","ex":"40,000 bombs: 20,000 MK-84 general-purpose bombs and 20,000 BLU-117s ... along with I-2000 Penetrator warheads ... The deal has been informally notified to congressional committees.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0114","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00002","b":"CTY-00002","rel":"part_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The U.S. Department of Defense is the military department of the United States.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0031","ex":"2024-09-30 | $874,040,585,085.73 ... 2025-09-30 | $916,648,676,662.05 (National Defense, current FYTD outlays)","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0115","t":"edge","a":"COM-00001","b":"COM-R2S","rel":"joint_venture_partner_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-02-21 (Camden groundbreaking)","st":"documented","ctx":"Raytheon, an RTX business, is one of the two partners in R2S, which builds Tamir interceptors in East Camden, Arkansas.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0038","ex":"The R2S facility, a joint venture between Raytheon (RTX) and Rafael Advanced Defense System, will produce the Tamir missile for the Iron Dome Weapon System. ... This facility represents a $63 million investment for R2S and will create 60 new jobs in the region.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0009","ex":"The Raytheon-Rafael Protection Systems (R2S) joint venture was awarded a $1.25 billion contract ... The companies used a $33 million capital investment to establish the new facility, which opened earlier this month in East Camden, Arkansas. The new site will produce the Tamir missiles for the Iron Dome Weapon System and its U.S. variant, SkyHunter.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0116","t":"edge","a":"COM-00009","b":"COM-R2S","rel":"joint_venture_partner_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-02-21 (Camden groundbreaking)","st":"documented","ctx":"Rafael, owned by the State of Israel, is R2S's other partner; Iron Dome was developed by Rafael.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0038","ex":"The R2S facility, a joint venture between Raytheon (RTX) and Rafael Advanced Defense System, will produce the Tamir missile for the Iron Dome Weapon System. ... This facility represents a $63 million investment for R2S and will create 60 new jobs in the region.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0009","ex":"The Raytheon-Rafael Protection Systems (R2S) joint venture was awarded a $1.25 billion contract ... The companies used a $33 million capital investment to establish the new facility, which opened earlier this month in East Camden, Arkansas. The new site will produce the Tamir missiles for the Iron Dome Weapon System and its U.S. variant, SkyHunter.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0117","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00006","b":"COM-R2S","rel":"contract_awarded_to","amt":1250000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-11-21","st":"documented","ctx":"$1.25B Tamir interceptor production contract tied to the Israel Missile Defense Organization (Israel MOD/DDR&D) programme to accelerate Iron Dome interceptor production.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0009","ex":"The Raytheon-Rafael Protection Systems (R2S) joint venture was awarded a $1.25 billion contract ... The companies used a $33 million capital investment to establish the new facility, which opened earlier this month in East Camden, Arkansas. The new site will produce the Tamir missiles for the Iron Dome Weapon System and its U.S. variant, SkyHunter.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0009","ex":"The facility was established to support the Israel Missile Defense Organization's (IMDO), operating within the Israeli MOD's Directorate of Defense Research and Development (DDR&D), initiative to accelerate serial production of Iron Dome interceptors.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0118","t":"edge","a":"COM-R2S","b":"CTY-00002","rel":"capital_investment_in","amt":63000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-02-21","st":"documented","ctx":"R2S raised the capital investment in its Camden, Arkansas, plant from $33M to $63M, promising 60 jobs.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0038","ex":"The R2S facility, a joint venture between Raytheon (RTX) and Rafael Advanced Defense System, will produce the Tamir missile for the Iron Dome Weapon System. ... This facility represents a $63 million investment for R2S and will create 60 new jobs in the region.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0119","t":"edge","a":"COM-00018","b":"COM-00010","rel":"ai_model_integrated_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"since 2024","st":"documented","ctx":"Anthropic's Claude is embedded in Palantir's Maven Smart System. The Washington Post reported that during the Iran campaign Maven, powered by Claude, suggested hundreds of targets, supplied precise coordinates and ranked them by importance; Reuters reported that Maven uses multiple prompts and workflows built with Claude.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0308","ex":"To strike 1,000 targets in 24 hours in Iran, the U.S. military leveraged the most advanced AI it's ever used in warfare. Anthropic's Claude partnered with the military's Maven Smart System, suggesting targets and issuing precise location coordinates.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0115","ex":"Claude is central to Palantir's Maven Smart System, which provides real-time targeting for military operations against Iran.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0346","ex":"the US military is extensively using Palantir's Maven Smart System in the conflict, which has had Anthropic's Claude chatbot integrated since 2024. ... the Wall Street Journal first reported on the Pentagon's use of Claude to select attack targets in Iran","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0309","ex":"Article body not fetchable from our environment (HTTP 403); claim corroborated by the Post's own X post and by Responsible Statecraft's summary.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0307","ex":"Palantir's Maven Smart Systems – a software platform that supplies militaries with intelligence analysis and weapons targeting – uses multiple prompts and workflows that were built using Anthropic's Claude code, according to two people familiar with the matter.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0120","t":"edge","a":"COM-00010","b":"GOV-00002","rel":"targeting_system_linked_to_strike","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-02-28","st":"reported","ctx":"A Bloomberg investigation (Sept 18, 2026) tied overreliance on Palantir's Maven Smart System and seven-year-old satellite imagery to the US Tomahawk strike on the Shajareh Tayyebeh girls' school in Minab, Iran, which killed about 120 children. Palantir told Bloomberg there was no evidence its software was at fault.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0310","ex":"artificial intelligence embedded in the Maven Smart System owned by Palantir Technologies Inc. ... relied on satellite imagery that had not been updated in seven years ... killed 123 children at Shajarah Tayyebeh Elementary School in Iran's Minab on 28 February","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0347","ex":"A Bloomberg investigation published Sept 18 says overreliance on Palantir's Maven Smart System — which uses Anthropic's Claude to semi-autonomously rank targets ... Palantir told Bloomberg there is no evidence its software was at fault and has since added disqualifier flags to Maven.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0348","ex":"Inside US Military 'Kill Chain' That Destroyed an Iranian School (headline; body not fetchable — robots.txt)","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0122","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00008","b":"CTY-00003","rel":"government_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The Germany government node governs the Germany country node.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0034","ex":"The USA was the largest supplier to Israel in 2021–25 (accounting for 68 per cent of Israeli arms imports), followed by Germany (31 per cent).","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0123","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00010","b":"CTY-00014","rel":"government_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The Denmark government node governs the Denmark country node.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0069","ex":"Danish media Danwatch and Information revealed in 2023 that Israel's F-35s were equipped with parts made by Danish company Terma.","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0124","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00012","b":"CTY-00015","rel":"government_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The Greece government node governs the Greece country node.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0049","ex":"France granted some €362m of arms-export licences to Israel in 2024 ... Germany granted €169m ... Greece €114m ... Romania €103m ... the Czechs €35m ... Finland €17m ... Hungary (€6m), Latvia (€4m), and Croatia (€2m) ... Austria, Bulgaria, Cyprus, Estonia, Lithuania, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, and Poland each also issued €1m or fewer","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0125","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00009","b":"CTY-00017","rel":"government_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The Finland government node governs the Finland country node.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0072","ex":"There are no talks about cancelling the deal, it is proceeding as planned","pg":null}]},{"id":"REL-V0126","t":"edge","a":"GOV-00011","b":"CTY-00018","rel":"government_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"The Slovakia government node governs the Slovakia country node.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0058","ex":"Between 2014-2022 the total value of export licences between Bulgaria and Israel total €49 million ... from Slovakia to Israel totalled €117 million ... Hungary ... over €15 million ... the Czech Republic has 