,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026","ctx":"Claude was embedded in Maven during the 2026 Iran campaign and reported by the Washington Post to support target generation and prioritization. No public evidence establishes that Claude selected, recommended or processed the Minab school target.","id":"REL-W0003","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0006","ex":"Maven, powered by Claude, suggested hundreds of targets, issued precise location coordinates, and prioritized those targets according to importance","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0007","ex":"uses multiple prompts and workflows that were built using Anthropic's Claude code","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"GOV-00007","b":"WPN-NEW-LAVENDER","rel":"uses","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023-2024","ctx":"Lavender marked some 37,000 Palestinians as suspected militants for assassination, +972 and Local Call reported.","id":"REL-W0004","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0004","ex":"Lavender has marked some 37,000 Palestinians as suspected 'Hamas militants,'","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"GOV-00007","b":"WPN-NEW-GOSPEL","rel":"uses","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023","ctx":"The Gospel generates building targets almost automatically; a former officer called it a 'mass assassination factory'.","id":"REL-W0005","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0005","ex":"essentially facilitates a 'mass assassination factory.'","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"GOV-00007","b":"WPN-NEW-WHERESDADDY","rel":"uses","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023-2024","ctx":"'Where's Daddy?' tracked marked people so they could be bombed at home with their families.","id":"REL-W0006","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0004","ex":"were used specifically to track the targeted individuals and carry out bombings when they had entered their family's residences","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"COM-00016","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"sold_engineering_support_to","amt":10000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023-10 to 2024-06","ctx":"The Israel Ministry of Defense spent $10M on 19,000 hours of Microsoft engineering support in the first months of the Gaza genocide.","id":"REL-W0007","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0008","ex":"Between October 2023 and June 2024 alone, the Israeli Defense Ministry spent $10 million to purchase 19,000 hours of engineering support from Microsoft.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"COM-00019","b":"COM-00009","rel":"ai_partnership_with","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024","ctx":"Oracle announced a partnership with the state weapons maker Rafael to provide cloud-based AI for military missions.","id":"REL-W0008","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0027","ex":"cloud-based AI solutions for defense missions","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"COM-00019","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"supplies_data_systems_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"ctx":"Oracle Israel's databases serve logistical, intelligence and operational functions in the Israeli military, Who Profits reports.","id":"REL-W0009","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0176","ex":"Oracle databases and systems implemented in the military serve logistical, intelligence and operational aspects in the military.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"GOV-NEW-UNIT8200","b":"COM-00012","rel":"planned_data_transfer_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2025-09","ctx":"After Microsoft disabled some services, Unit 8200 planned to move its surveillance data to AWS, sources told +972 and The Guardian.","id":"REL-W0010","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0009","ex":"the unit planned to transfer the data to the Amazon Web Services cloud platform instead","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-BLOOMBERG","b":"ORG-NEW-MDA","rel":"donated_to","amt":44000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023-10","ctx":"Michael Bloomberg matched nearly $44M from about 34,000 donors for an $88M gift to Magen David Adom after 7 October 2023, paying for ambulances, ballistic vests and helmets.","id":"REL-W0011","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0036","ex":"Michael Bloomberg announced 