ing office Ben-Gvir was known to have a portrait in his living room of Israeli-American mass murderer Baruch Goldstein.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0005","ex":"out of 299,354 applications submitted since the war ... more than 100,000 citizens have already been approved.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"coalition_minister_under","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2022–","ctx":"Bezalel Smotrich is Netanyahu's finance minister. In July 2026 he thanked Netanyahu for backing NIS 1.3B for 34 new settlements.","id":"REL-X0003","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0008","ex":"arrested in 2005 while in possession of 700 litres of gasoline on suspicion of participating in an attempt to blow up Ayalon Highway ... I think the village of Huwara needs to be wiped out. I think the state of Israel should do it.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0013","ex":"1.3 billion shekels ($434 million) for establishing 34 new settlements ... 1.075 billion shekels would be approved to pave roads to the new settlements ... a day of celebration for Israel and settlements","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"finance_minister_controls_budget","amt":271000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026","ctx":"Smotrich's treasury wrote Israel's record 2026 budget of NIS 850.6B ($271B). The Bank of Israel puts the fiscal cost of the wars from 2023 to 2026 at about NIS 350B.","id":"REL-X0004","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0014","ex":"NIS 850.6 billion ($271 billion) ... the largest in Israeli history ... more than NIS 142 billion ($45.3 billion), a record","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0015","ex":"The Bank of Israel estimates the fiscal cost of the war from 2023 through 2026 at about NIS 350 billion, with roughly half financed through borrowing.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"funded_military_budget","amt":45300000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026","ctx":"The 2026 budget gives the Israel Ministry of Defense more than NIS 142B ($45.3B), a record. Smotrich said its core was \"the addition of tens of billions so that we can finish the campaign\".","id":"REL-X0005","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0014","ex":"NIS 850.6 billion ($271 billion) ... the largest in Israeli history ... more than NIS 142 billion ($45.3 billion), a record","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0040","ex":"the core of the budget is the addition of tens of billions so that we can finish the campaign and dramatically improve our geopolitical and diplomatic standing","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"minister_with_west_bank_powers","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023-02-23","ctx":"Since February 2023, Smotrich, as a minister in the Israel Ministry of Defense, has controlled settlement planning, land allocation and state-land registration in Area C.","id":"REL-X0006","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0009","ex":"authority over the planning and construction bureaucracy in the West Bank, which will come under the control of the new Settlements Administration ... full authority over land purchases, land surveys and the registration of land as state land in Area C","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"directed_settlement_funding","amt":434000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-07-14","ctx":"Smotrich secured NIS 1.3B ($434M) for 34 new West Bank settlements and NIS 1.075B more for roads to them, calling it \"a day of celebration for Israel and settlements\".","id":"REL-X0007","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0013","ex":"1.3 billion shekels ($434 million) for establishing 34 new settlements ... 1.075 billion shekels would be approved to pave roads to the new settlements ... a day of celebration for Israel and settlements","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-GALLANT","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"military_minister_under","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"to 2024-11-07","ctx":"Gallant served as Netanyahu's military minister until Netanyahu fired him, effective 7 November 2024. The ICC warrants of 21 November 2024 name both men.","id":"REL-X0008","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0017","ex":"On 9 October 2023 ... Gallant said he had 'ordered a complete siege on the Gaza Strip. There will be no electricity, no food, no water, no fuel. Everything is closed. We are fighting human animals and we are acting accordingly'. ... On 5 November 2024, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced that he had dismissed Gallant, effective 7 November","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0019","ex":"On 21 November 2024, following an investigation of war crimes and crimes against humanity, the ICC issued arrest warrants for two senior Israeli officials, Benjamin Netanyahu ... and Yoav Gallant.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-GALLANT","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"headed","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"to 2024-11-07","ctx":"Gallant headed the Israel Ministry of Defense during the first 13 months of the Gaza genocide.","id":"REL-X0009","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0017","ex":"On 9 October 2023 ... Gallant said he had 'ordered a complete siege on the Gaza Strip. There will be no electricity, no food, no water, no fuel. Everything is closed. We are fighting human animals and we are acting accordingly'. ... On 5 November 2024, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced that he had dismissed Gallant, effective 7 November","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-GALLANT","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"ordered_complete_siege","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023-10-09","ctx":"On 9 October 2023, Gallant ordered \"a complete siege on the Gaza Strip... no electricity, no food, no water, no fuel\". The ICC alleges starvation as a method of warfare.","id":"REL-X0010","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0017","ex":"On 9 October 2023 ... Gallant said he had 'ordered a complete siege on the Gaza Strip. There will be no electricity, no food, no water, no fuel. Everything is closed. We are fighting human animals and we are acting accordingly'. ... On 5 November 2024, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced that he had dismissed Gallant, effective 7 November","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0018","ex":"from at least 8 October 2023 until at least 20 May 2024 ... the war crime of starvation as a method of warfare; and the crimes against humanity of murder, persecution, and other inhumane acts","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-KATZ","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"military_minister_under","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-11–","ctx":"Netanyahu named Israel Katz military minister on 5 November 2024, replacing Gallant.","id":"REL-X0011","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0020","ex":"2022–2024: Energy ... 2024: Foreign Affairs ... 2024–present: Defense ... We will win. They will not receive a drop of water or a single battery until they leave the world. ... No one is currently planning to allow any humanitarian aid into Gaza, and there are no preparations to enable such aid.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-KATZ","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"heads","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-11–","ctx":"Katz heads the Israel Ministry of Defense. He and Smotrich first agreed a NIS 112B ($34B) military budget for 2026; the final 2026 budget raised it to more than NIS 142B.","id":"REL-X0012","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0020","ex":"2022–2024: Energy ... 2024: Foreign Affairs ... 2024–present: Defense ... We will win. They will not receive a drop of water or a single battery until they leave the world. ... No one is currently planning to allow any humanitarian aid into Gaza, and there are no preparations to enable such aid.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0024","ex":"NIS 112 billion ($34 billion) ... NIS 90 billion ... NIS 140 billion","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0014","ex":"NIS 850.6 billion ($271 billion) ... the largest in Israeli history ... more than NIS 142 billion ($45.3 billion), a record","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-KATZ","b":"GOV-00007","rel":"directs","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-11–","ctx":"As military minister, Katz threatened that \"Tehran will burn\" (June 2025) and that \"the gates of hell\" would open on Gaza City (August 2025).","id":"REL-X0013","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0022","ex":"If Khamenei continues to fire missiles at the Israeli home front, Tehran will burn.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0023","ex":"The gates of hell will soon open on the heads of Hamas' murderers and rapists in Gaza — until they agree to Israel's conditions for ending the war ... turn into Rafah and Beit Hanoun","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-HERZOG","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"head_of_state","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2021-07-07–","ctx":"Isaac Herzog is Israel's president. The UN Commission of Inquiry found in September 2025 that he incited genocide.","id":"REL-X0014","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0025","ex":"was sworn in on 7 July 2021 ... He called South Africa's genocide case against Israel in the International Court of Justice (ICJ) a 'blood libel' against Jews. ... During Herzog's 2024 visit to the World Economic Forum in Switzerland, the Swiss Federal Prosecutor's Office announced that it was investigating a criminal complaint against him. ... On 30 November 2025, Netanyahu formally asked Herzog for a pardon on his corruption cases.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0025","ex":"The Commission also concluded that Israeli President Isaac Herzog, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and then Defence Minister Yoav Gallant, have incited the commission of genocide and that Israeli authorities have failed to take action against them to punish this incitement.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-NEW-HERZOG","b":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","rel":"holds_pardon_request_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2025-11-30","ctx":"Netanyahu asked Herzog for a pardon on 30 November 2025. In April 2026 Herzog deferred a decision and pushed for a plea deal. The UN Commission of Inquiry named both men for incitement.","id":"REL-X0015","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0025","ex":"was sworn in on 7 July 2021 ... He called South Africa's genocide case against Israel in the International Court of Justice (ICJ) a 'blood libel' against Jews. ... During Herzog's 2024 visit to the World Economic Forum in Switzerland, the Swiss Federal Prosecutor's Office announced that it was investigating a criminal complaint against him. ... On 30 November 2025, Netanyahu formally asked Herzog for a pardon on his corruption cases.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0028","ex":"it is right to first, before discussing the pardon request itself, exhaust a process that could lead to the formation of an agreement between the parties, outside the walls of the court","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0025","ex":"The Commission also concluded that Israeli President Isaac Herzog, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and then Defence Minister Yoav Gallant, have incited the commission of genocide and that Israeli authorities have failed to take action against them to punish this incitement.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"GOV-00005","b":"COM-00009","rel":"state_owner_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":99.9,"date":null,"ctx":"The Israeli state directly holds 99.9% of Rafael, and other state entities hold the rest. Rafael's profits flow to the government Netanyahu heads. This duplicates REL-00035.","indirect":true,"id":"REL-X0016","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0024","ex":"Rafael is a government-owned company, with 99.9% of its shares directly held by the Israeli government and the remainder held by various government entities, each possessing a fractional share.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"GOV-00005","b":"COM-00008","rel":"state_owner_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":100,"date":null,"ctx":"IAI is a \"wholly-owned government company\" under Israel's Government Companies Law. Its profits flow to the government Netanyahu heads. This duplicates REL-00036.","indirect":true,"id":"REL-X0017","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0025","ex":"Israel Aerospace Industries Ltd. (\"the Company\") was founded in 1966 and is a \"wholly-owned government company\", as this term is defined in the Israeli Government Companies Law, 1975","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00005","rel":"heads_government_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2022-12–","ctx":"Benjamin Netanyahu heads the government that has waged the wars on Gaza, Lebanon and Iran since October 2023. This duplicates REL-V0084 (prime_minister).","id":"REL-X0018","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-V0026","ex":"ordered an invasion of Lebanon with the stated goal of destroying the military capabilities of Hezbollah ... He presided over the 2025 Israeli strikes on Iran, which started the Twelve-Day War ... In February 2026, he launched a major air campaign against Iran, alongside the US","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0025","ex":"The Commission also concluded that Israeli President Isaac Herzog, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and then Defence Minister Yoav Gallant, have incited the commission of genocide and that Israeli authorities have failed to take action against them to punish this incitement.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00001","rel":"negotiated_and_accepted_us_military_aid","amt":38000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2016-09-14","ctx":"Netanyahu thanked Barack Obama for the $38B 10-year aid deal (2016 MOU), calling it \"the largest military aid package the US has ever given out to any nation\". It pays Israel about $3.8B a year in subsidies, mostly to buy US-made arms, until 2028.","id":"REL-X0019","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0041","ex":"This agreement will ensure an unprecedented level of defense aid for Israel in the next decade. This is the largest military aid package the US has ever given out to any nation. ... I want to thank President Obama and his administration for this historic agreement.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0042","ex":"Israel receives some $3.8 billion annually from the US, mostly in the form of subsidies to buy American-made arms. ... I want to taper off the military aid within the next 10 years","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00003","rel":"welcomed_supplemental_aid","amt":17000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-04-20","ctx":"Netanyahu thanked Congress for the April 2024 package, which included $17B in military aid to Israel: \"Thank you friends, thank you America!\"","id":"REL-X0020","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0043","ex":"The US Congress just overwhelmingly passed a much appreciated aid bill that demonstrates strong bipartisan support for Israel and defends Western civilization. Thank you friends, thank you America!","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00001","rel":"lobbied_for_weapons_deliveries","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-06-18","ctx":"In a June 2024 video Netanyahu accused Washington of \"withholding weapons and ammunitions\" and demanded: \"give us the tools and we'll finish the job a lot faster\".","id":"REL-X0021","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0044","ex":"I said it's inconceivable that in the past few months, the administration has been withholding weapons and ammunitions to Israel ... give us the tools and we'll finish the job a lot faster","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"approved_arms_industry_spending","amt":110000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-12-25","ctx":"Netanyahu said: \"I approved a total of 350 billion shekels over the coming decade to build an independent arms industry for the State of Israel\" (about $110B). The state-owned Rafael and IAI stand to gain.","id":"REL-X0022","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0045","ex":"I approved a total of 350 billion shekels over the coming decade to build an independent arms industry for the State of Israel","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-N-NETANYAHU","b":"GOV-00006","rel":"cabinet_approved_war_budget_increase","amt":10400000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-03-11","ctx":"During the 2026 war on Iran, Netanyahu's cabinet added NIS 32B ($10.4B) to the military budget, plus NIS 7B in reserves.","id":"REL-X0023","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0046","ex":"Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's cabinet approved a revised state budget for 2026 ... adds 32 billion shekels ($10.4 billion), about 1.5% of Israel's gross domestic product, for defense and an additional 7 billion shekels in reserves for possible military needs","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-GATES","b":"COM-00016","rel":"co_founder_and_shareholder","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"1975–","ctx":"Bill Gates co-founded Microsoft and remains Technology Advisor to Satya Nadella. Forbes estimates his stake at below 1% (no verified dollar value). Microsoft's Azure held Unit 8200's mass surveillance of Palestinians.","id":"REL-X0024","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0030","ex":"Bill Gates stepped down from the company's Board of Directors to dedicate more time to his philanthropic priorities ... He will continue to serve as Technology Advisor to CEO Satya Nadella and other leaders in the company.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0032","ex":"$114.2B ... his Microsoft stake is now less than 1%, Forbes estimates ... Gates, who's donated more than $63.9 billion to the Gates Foundation, announced in 2025 that the foundation will shut down in 20 years","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0011","ex":"Israel's elite cyber-intelligence unit stored vast volumes of intercepted Palestinian phone calls on Microsoft's cloud servers ... Three sources from Unit 8200 said that the cloud-based system helped guide deadly air strikes and shaped operations across the occupied Palestinian territories.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-IN","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_trade_with","amt":185000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024","ctx":"India–Israel arms trade was about $185M in 2024, per ORF; India took 29% of Israel's arms exports in 2021–25 (SIPRI).","id":"REL-G0025","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0097","ex":"In 2024, their arms trade volume was about US$185 million. Between 2020 and 2024, Israel supplied 13 percent of India's total arms imports","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-V0034","ex":"Israel's main recipients per Table 1: India (29%), Germany (21%), USA (7.8%) [SIPRI fact sheet, Table 1, 2021-25]; India's main suppliers (Table 2): Russia 40, France 29, Israel 15","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-IN","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"bilateral_trade_with","amt":3900000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024","ctx":"India–Israel bilateral trade reached $3.9B in 2024, and mutual investment about $800M. A bilateral investment treaty was signed with Bezalel Smotrich in September 2025.","id":"REL-G0026","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0107","ex":"Bilateral trade stood at $3.9bn in 2024, while current mutual investments are worth about $800m, according to official figures.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0107","ex":"The agreement, signed in New Delhi by Smotrich and Indian Minister of Corporate Affairs Nirmala Sitharaman, aims to boost trade and investment flows between the two countries.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"COM-G-ADANIELBIT","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"exported_drones_to","amt":20,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2024-02","ctx":"Adani-Elbit's Hyderabad plant delivered more than 20 Hermes 900 MALE drones to Israel.","id":"REL-G0027","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0059","ex":"The first private UAV manufacturing facility in India has delivered more than 20 Hermes 900 medium-altitude, long-endurance (MALE) UAVs to Israel","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0064","ex":"The Company's joint venture with Israel-based Elbit Systems exported the first ship set of the Hermes 900 fuselage to Israel","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"COM-G-ADANIELBIT","b":"COM-00007","rel":"joint_venture_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"ctx":"Adani-Elbit Advanced Systems India is a joint venture between Adani Defence & Aerospace and Elbit Systems.","id":"REL-G0028","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0064","ex":"The Company's joint venture with Israel-based Elbit Systems exported the first ship set of the Hermes 900 fuselage to Israel","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"COM-G-MUNITIONSINDIA","b":"COM-00007","rel":"supplied_artillery_rounds_to","amt":1000,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2023-10/2025-11","ctx":"Per Amnesty's 'Made in India' (July 2026), Munitions India exported 1,000 155-mm high-explosive artillery rounds to Elbit Systems.","id":"REL-G0029","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0061","ex":"Munitions India Limited exported 1,000 155-mm high-explosive artillery rounds to Elbit Systems, while Advanced Weapons and Equipment India Limited supplied 120 81-mm mortar launchers to the Israeli company in February 2024.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0060","ex":"PLR Systems Private Limited, who manufacture parts for machine guns and is a joint venture between Adani Defence & Aerospace and Israel Weapon Industries; ... the state-owned Munitions India Limited, who manufacture high-explosive artillery rounds; and Alpha Elsec Defence & Aerospace Systems Private Limited who manufacture explosive warheads and is a joint venture between Alpha Design Technologies and Elbit Systems.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"COM-G-PREMIER","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"export_order_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024","ctx":"Premier Explosives told investors that revenue from an Israel export order produced an 'exponential jump' in quarterly revenue.","id":"REL-G0030","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0065","ex":"We have received the pending revenue from the Israel export order, and this has shown an exponential jump in the revenue of the quarter.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-IN","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_workers_to","amt":16000,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2024","ctx":"Around 16,000 Indian workers replaced barred Palestinian labourers in Israel's construction sector in 2024.","id":"REL-G0031","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0062","ex":"Around 16,000 Indian workers have replaced Palestinians in Israel's construction sector in 2024","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0107","ex":"Israeli construction companies have sought permission to hire up to 100,000 Indian workers to replace Palestinians whose permits were revoked after Israel launched its brutal war on Gaza in October 2023.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-IN","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_shipments_to","amt":2596,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2023-10-07/2025-11-30","ctx":"Amnesty identified at least 2,596 shipments of arms, parts and ammunition from India to Israel.","id":"REL-G0032","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0060","ex":"Amnesty International identified at least 2,596 shipments of arms, parts and ammunition exported from India to Israel between 7 October 2023 and 30 November 2025.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0060","ex":"Records indicate that Indian companies have supplied at least 390,516 small arms parts for military grade weapons, 564,970 parts of explosive ordnance (such as drone warheads, artillery shell casings and others), and 298 components of military vehicles to large Israeli companies that are direct suppliers to the Israeli military.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-AZ","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_crude_oil_to","amt":7000000,"cur":"units","pct":40,"date":"2023-11/2025-10","ctx":"Over 7 million tonnes of Azerbaijani crude, nearly 40% of crude and fuel shipped to Israel (OCI). amt is in metric tonnes.","id":"REL-G0033","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0066","ex":"Azerbaijani product taking the lead at over 7 million tonnes, or nearly 40% of the total amount.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0067","ex":"Azerbaijan (via Turkey) and Kazakhstan (via Russia) supplied around 70% of crude oil.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-KZ","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_crude_oil_to","amt":5300000,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2023-11/2025-10","ctx":"Around 5.3 million tonnes of Kazakh CPC crude shipped to Israel via Russia (OCI). amt is in metric tonnes.","id":"REL-G0034","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0066","ex":"Kazakhstan came second at around 5.3 million tonnes shipped through Russia.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0068","ex":"Tengizchevroil, a joint venture (JV) between Chevron (50%), ExxonMobil Kazakhstan (25%), KazMunayGas (20%) and Lukoil (5%)","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-AZ","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"granted_gas_exploration_licence_by","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":33,"date":"2025-03-18","ctx":"Israel awarded offshore gas exploration licences to a SOCAR–BP–NewMed consortium, with each partner holding about one-third and SOCAR as operator.","id":"REL-G0035","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0070","ex":"Each company in the consortium will hold around one-third of the rights in each licence, with Socar acting as the operator.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-TR","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"transit_for_crude_to","amt":1.27,"cur":"USD","pct":40,"date":"2024","ctx":"Turkey collects $1.27 per barrel through the BTC pipeline, which supplies around 40% of Israel's crude, and tankers kept sailing from Ceyhan to Ashkelon after the May 2024 trade ban.","id":"REL-G0036","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0072","ex":"Turkey collects $1.27 per barrel of oil transported through the Baku-Tbilisi-Ceyhan (BTC) pipeline","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0072","ex":"BTC is known to supply around 40 percent of Israel's annual crude oil consumption","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0073","ex":"eight journeys tracked since Ankara's imposition of a trade embargo in May","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-EG","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"gas_import_deal","amt":35000000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-08-07","ctx":"Egypt agreed to import about 130 bcm of Leviathan gas through 2040 for $35B. Netanyahu approved the deal in December 2025.","id":"REL-G0037","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0074","ex":"130 billion cubic meters (bcm) of natural gas to Egypt through 2040","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0075","ex":"Egypt signs $35bn deal to import natural gas from Israel","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0076","ex":"This deal greatly strengthens Israel's status as a regional energy power.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-MA","b":"COM-00007","rel":"bought_artillery_from","amt":36,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2025-02","ctx":"Morocco contracted Elbit for 36 ATMOS 2000 self-propelled howitzers.","id":"REL-G0038","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0081","ex":"The Royal Moroccan Armed Forces have contracted Elbit Systems for the delivery of 36 ATMOS 2000 self-propelled artillery systems","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-MA","b":"COM-00008","rel":"bought_missile_system_from","amt":500000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":null,"ctx":"A $500M Barak MX deal between Israel and Morocco, per Military Africa (Barak MX is an IAI system, WPN-00013).","id":"REL-G0039","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0081","ex":"$500 million deal was concluded between Israel and Morocco for the Barak MX air and missile defence system","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-MA","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"bilateral_trade_with","amt":116700000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023","ctx":"Morocco–Israel trade doubled to $116.7M in 2023, from $56.2M in 2022.","id":"REL-G0040","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0081","ex":"In 2023, trade between Morocco and Israel doubled, reaching $116.7 million compared to $56.2 million in 2022","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-BR","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_crude_oil_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":9,"date":"2023-11/2024","ctx":"Brazil supplied about 9% of Israel's crude imports, per OCI as cited by MEE. Direct shipments halted in January–August 2025.","id":"REL-G0041","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0082","ex":"Brazil quietly became the fourth largest exporter of crude oil to Israel, accounting for nine percent of its imports, according to a report by Oil Change International.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0082","ex":"Brazilian crude exports to Israel ground to a halt between January and August 2025.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-CO","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_coal_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":60,"date":"2023-2024","ctx":"Colombian coal was 60% of Israel's coal imports in 2023–24, per the UN Special Rapporteur report. It was banned from August 2024; the ban was reversed in August 2026.","id":"REL-G0042","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0084","ex":"Coal for electricity to Israel originates primarily from Colombia (60 per cent of Israeli coal imports in 2023-24)","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0086","ex":"Colombia prohibited coal exports to Israel through Decree 1047 of Aug. 14, 2024.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0086","ex":"In August 2026, the new government of Abelardo de la Espriella announced that coal exports to Israel could resume.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-CO","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"coal_exports_halted","amt":200000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2024-08/2026-08","ctx":"Industry body Fenalcarbón estimated the ban cut shipments to Israel by about 3.5 million tonnes a year, worth about $200M.","id":"REL-G0043","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0086","ex":"estimated that the restriction had reduced shipments to the Israeli market by about 3.5 million metric tons a year, worth roughly US$200 million.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-ZA","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"supplied_coal_to","amt":2990000,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2023-10/2025-12","ctx":"At least 2.99 million tonnes of coal were shipped from Richards Bay to Israel on at least 17 vessels (BDS monitoring via Daily Maverick). amt is in tonnes.","id":"REL-G0044","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0088","ex":"BDS monitored at least 17 vessels being loaded at Richards Bay between October 2023 and December 2025, which transported at least 2.99 million tonnes of coal to Israel","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0089","ex":"South Africa's exports increased by 87% to 474 000 metric tonnes in the three months to November 2025 on an annual basis","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-AR","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"military_cooperation_mou","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026-04","ctx":"Milei and Netanyahu signed three MoUs on military and scientific cooperation and launched the 'Isaac Accords'.","id":"REL-G0045","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0091","ex":"both countries signed three memorandums of understanding to promote military and scientific cooperation between Israel and Argentina","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-PY","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"embassy_in_jerusalem","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-12-12","ctx":"Paraguay reopened its embassy in Jerusalem.","id":"REL-G0046","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0093","ex":"we were with you, we are with you, we will stay with the people of Israel forever.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-PH","b":"COM-00007","rel":"bought_munitions_from","amt":248000000,"cur":"PHP","pct":null,"date":"2025-08-11","ctx":"The Philippine Army awarded Elbit P248M for 100 rounds of 155mm precision-guided munitions.","id":"REL-G0047","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0094","ex":"100 rounds of high explosive (HE) 155mm precision-guided munition (PGM) ... Elbit Systems ... P248 million ... notice of award August 11, 2025","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-VN","b":"COM-00009","rel":"bought_missiles_from","amt":250000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2026-02","ctx":"About $250M for Rafael Spike missiles, including Firefly, with local production in Vietnam.","id":"REL-G0048","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0096","ex":"The Vietnamese army will be equipped with Spike anti-tank missiles manufactured by Rafael Advanced Defense Systems in a deal worth approximately $250 million.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0096","ex":"includes provisions for the missiles to be manufactured at a factory to be established in Vietnam, with the necessary know-how transferred from Israel.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-VN","b":"COM-00008","rel":"bought_satellites_from","amt":700000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025","ctx":"About $700M for two IAI intelligence satellites (ORF gives about $680M).","id":"REL-G0049","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0096","ex":"Less than a year ago, Vietnam ordered two intelligence satellites from Israel Aerospace Industries (IAI) in a deal valued at approximately $700 million","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0097","ex":"The two countries reportedly finalised a deal worth approximately US$680 million for two advanced surveillance satellites from Israel","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-SG","b":"COM-00007","rel":"selected_drone_from","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-11","ctx":"Singapore selected Elbit's Hermes 900 drone.","id":"REL-G0050","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0097","ex":"Singapore announced in November this year its selection of Israel's Elbit Systems' Hermes 900 unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV)","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-KR","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_exports_to","amt":1285000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023-10/2024-04","ctx":"At least $1.285M in Korean weapons, ammunition and parts exported to Israel, per UN Comtrade and Korean customs data (Newstapa).","id":"REL-G0051","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0098","ex":"이스라엘에 HS코드 93에 해당하는 '무기총포탄과 이들의 부품과 부속품' 814,000달러를 수출했다 ... 최소 128만 5천 달러 규모다","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-JP","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"tested_drones_from","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023/2024","ctx":"Japan's MoD spent about ¥9.9B on drone verification tests. In five contracts the drones tested were Israeli.","id":"REL-G0052","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0099","ex":"approximately 9.9 billion yen was allocated for verification testing of multi-purpose UAVs and small attack UAVs","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0099","ex":"In five of these contracts, actual UAVs used for verification are products of Israel.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-CN","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"operates_port_in","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2021-09","ctx":"SIPG runs the Haifa Bayport terminal on a 25-year concession.","id":"REL-G0053","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0101","ex":"A new port at Haifa, Israel, developed and operated by Shanghai International Port (SIPG), has officially commenced operation.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0101","ex":"In 2015, Israel Port authority granted SIPG a 25-year concession to run the port.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-RW","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"spyware_client_of_israeli_firm","amt":3500,"cur":"units","pct":null,"date":"2016-2021","ctx":"Rwanda selected more than 3,500 numbers for Pegasus targeting (NSO Group, Israel).","id":"REL-G0054","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0104","ex":"The Rwandan authorities have selected more than 3,500 phone numbers of activists, journalists, political opponents, foreign politicians, and diplomats to target with NSO Pegasus spyware since 2016.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"CTY-G-CM","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"arms_client_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2009-2022","ctx":"BIR armed with IWI rifles and overseen by ex-IDF officers (DIMSE).","id":"REL-G0055","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0105","ex":"Each new recruit since 2009 has received a brand-new firearm produced by Israel Weapon Industries (IWI)","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0105","ex":"continuously overseen by former IDF officers","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-KE","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"surveillance_client_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024/2026","ctx":"Kenyan police used Ispra riot gear in 2024, and Cellebrite tools were used on an activist's phone (DIMSE, Citizen Lab).","id":"REL-G0056","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0102","ex":"In 2024, over 60 people died during civil protests against the government's fiscal policies and handling of the economic crisis. Footage from these demonstrations show the police used \"less lethal\" riot gear produced by the Israeli company Ispra","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0102","ex":"In 2026 an investigation by CitizenLab found that Cellebrite's forensic extraction tools were used on the phone of Boniface Mwangi","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-NG","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"surveillance_client_of","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2020","ctx":"Nigeria's Defence Intelligence Agency was identified as a likely client of Circles, an NSO affiliate.","id":"REL-G0057","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0103","ex":"The other client appears to be the Nigerian Defence Intelligence Agency (DIA), as its firewall IPs are in AS37258, a block of IP addresses registered to \"HQ Defence Intelligence Agency Asokoro, Nigeria, Abuja,\" it added.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-TD","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"recalled_ambassador","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2023-11-05","ctx":"Chad recalled its ambassador over Gaza.","id":"REL-G0058","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0106","ex":"On 5 November 2023, Chad recalled its ambassador to Israel, accusing the country of creating an unprecedented humanitarian catastrophe and killing innocent people in Gaza.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"CTY-G-CO","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"cut_diplomatic_ties","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2024-05-01","ctx":"Petro announced the break, calling Israel's leader 'genocidal'.","id":"REL-G0059","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0085","ex":"announces that tomorrow we will break diplomatic relations with the state of Israel … for having a government, for having a president who is genocidal.","pg":null}],"t":"edge"},{"a":"COM-G-ADANIELBIT","b":"CTY-G-IN","rel":"based_in","ctx":"Adani-Elbit Advanced Systems India builds Hermes drones at its plant in Hyderabad, India.","id":"REL-G0060","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0059","ex":null,"pg":null}],"amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"t":"edge"},{"a":"COM-G-MUNITIONSINDIA","b":"CTY-G-IN","rel":"state_owned_by","ctx":"Munitions India Limited is owned by the Government of India.","id":"REL-G0061","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0060","ex":null,"pg":null}],"amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"t":"edge"},{"a":"COM-G-PREMIER","b":"CTY-G-IN","rel":"based_in","ctx":"Premier Explosives Ltd is an Indian explosives maker based in Hyderabad.","id":"REL-G0062","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0065","ex":null,"pg":null}],"amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"t":"edge"},{"a":"ORG-NEW-FIXTHECITY","b":"PER-NEW-CUOMO","rel":"spent_supporting","amt":28000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025","ctx":"Fix the City spent $28M across the 2025 primary and general election to elect Andrew Cuomo, 55% of all independent spending in the race.","id":"REL-P0063","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0114","ex":"Fix The City, has alone spent $28 million, or 55% of all independent expenses in the election.","pg":null}],"t":"election"},{"a":"ORG-NEW-FIXTHECITY","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"spent_opposing","amt":5900000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-06","ctx":"By 20 June 2025, Fix the City had spent $5.9M against Zohran Mamdani in the primary (part of its $28M).","id":"REL-P0064","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0111","ex":"$5.9 million in opposition to his biggest competition in the race, Assembly Member Zohran Mamdani","pg":null}],"t":"election"},{"a":"ORG-NEW-FOROURCITY","b":"PER-NEW-CUOMO","rel":"spent_supporting","amt":7470170,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-11","ctx":"For Our City spent $7.47M supporting Cuomo in the general election.","id":"REL-P0065","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0109","ex":"For Our City $7,470,170","pg":null}],"t":"election"},{"a":"ORG-NEW-DEFENDNYC","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"spent_opposing","amt":5030000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-11","ctx":"Defend NYC spent $5.03M on the Cuomo side in the general election; press called it anti-Mamdani.","id":"REL-P0066","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0109","ex":"Defend NYC $5,030,000","pg":null}],"t":"election"},{"a":"ORG-NEW-SENSIBLECITY","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"spent_opposing","amt":100000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-06","ctx":"Sensible City spent just over $100,000 on an anti-Mamdani digital ad.","id":"REL-P0067","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0118","ex":"after spending just over $100,000 on its digital ad ... including Rob Stavis, a partner at the venture capital firm Bessemer and a vice chair of the Anti-Defamation League's board of directors, and Modi Wiczyk, a film producer and a board member at the Israel Policy Forum","pg":null}],"t":"election"},{"a":"PER-NEW-BLOOMBERG","b":"PER-NEW-CUOMO","rel":"funded_pacs_supporting","amt":13300000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025","ctx":"Michael Bloomberg gave $13.3M to pro-Cuomo super PACs: $8.3M to Fix the City in the primary, then $1.5M to Fix the City and $3.5M to For Our City in the final week.","id":"REL-P0068","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0109","ex":"Bloomberg's $13.3 million total is likely the largest individual contribution made in support of another candidate in New York history.","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0117","ex":"Michael Bloomberg donated a combined $5 million to a couple of anti-Zohran Mamdani super PACs earlier this week ... Bloomberg had given $1.5 million to Fix the City ... pumping $3.5 million into the coffers of For Our City","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0109","ex":"Michael Bloomberg $5,000,000","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-ACKMAN","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"funded_pacs_opposing","amt":1750000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-10","ctx":"Bill Ackman spent $1.75M against Mamdani through Defend NYC and Fix the City.","id":"REL-P0069","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0114","ex":"contributed $1 million to the anti-Mamdani super PAC Defend NYC on October 14, and $250,000 to Fix The City on October 15 taking his total spending to $1.75 million.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-RLAUDER","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"funded_pacs_opposing","amt":2500000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025","ctx":"The four Lauders spent over $2.5M to target Mamdani and back Cuomo.","id":"REL-P0070","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0114","ex":"The four members of the Lauder family have spent over $2.5 million to target Mamdani and back Cuomo.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-GEBBIA","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"funded_pacs_opposing","amt":2000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-10-15","ctx":"Joe Gebbia gave $1M each to Fix the City and Defend NYC.","id":"REL-P0071","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0114","ex":"Joe Gebbia...donated $1 million each to both Fix The City and Defend NYC on October 15.","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-TISCH","b":"PER-NEW-CUOMO","rel":"funded_pacs_supporting","amt":1200000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025","ctx":"The Tisch family gave $1.2M to Fix the City.","id":"REL-P0072","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0116","ex":"Tisch Family: $1.2 million to Fix the City","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"PER-NEW-LOEB","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"funded_pacs_opposing","amt":775000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025","ctx":"Daniel Loeb gave $775,000 to anti-Mamdani super PACs.","id":"REL-P0073","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0116","ex":"Daniel Loeb: $775,000 to Fix the City, New Yorkers For A Better Future Mayor 25, Defend NYC","pg":null}],"t":"money"},{"a":"ORG-NEW-NYLOWERCOSTS","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"spent_supporting","amt":2084602,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-11","ctx":"Spent $2.08M supporting Mamdani in the general election.","id":"REL-P0074","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0109","ex":"Supporting Zohran Mamdani: New Yorkers for Lower Costs $2,084,602","pg":null}],"t":"election"},{"a":"ORG-NEW-WFPIE","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"spent_supporting","amt":1119346,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-11","ctx":"Spent $1.12M supporting Mamdani in the general election.","id":"REL-P0075","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0109","ex":"WFP National PAC - NYS IE Committee $1,119,346","pg":null}],"t":"election"},{"a":"ORG-NEW-HOTELWORKERS","b":"PER-NEW-MAMDANI","rel":"spent_supporting","amt":810322,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2025-11","ctx":"Spent $810K supporting Mamdani in the general election.","id":"REL-P0076","st":"documented","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0109","ex":"Hotel Workers for Stronger Communities $810,322","pg":null}],"t":"election"},{"a":"PER-NEW-BIDEN","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"approved_arms_for","amt":null,"cur":null,"t":"edge","ctx":"Emergency sales bypassing Congress (Dec 2023), at least 14,000 MK-84 2,000-lb bombs, ~$17B April 2024 package; Costs of War: $17.9B military aid in year one.","id":"REL-U0077","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0273","ex":"The United States has provided at least $17.9 billion in military aid to Israel since October 7, 2023 ... \"artillery shells to 2,000-pound bunker-busters and precision-guided bombs\"","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0253","ex":"\"at least 14,000 of the MK-84 2,000-pound bombs, 6,500 500-pound bombs\"","pg":null}],"pct":null,"date":null},{"a":"PER-NEW-HARRIS","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"pledged_arms_for","amt":null,"cur":null,"t":"edge","ctx":"'I will always ensure Israel has the ability to defend itself' (DNC, Aug 2024); said 'No' to changing arms policy; adviser: she 'has not supported an arms embargo'.","id":"REL-U0078","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0280","ex":"\"Let me be clear, I will always stand up for Israel's right to defend itself and I will always ensure Israel has the ability to defend itself.\"","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0281","ex":"\"I'm unequivocal and unwavering in my commitment to Israel's defense and its ability to defend itself, and that's not going to change.\"","pg":null}],"pct":null,"date":null},{"a":"PER-NEW-HARRIS","b":"PER-NEW-BIDEN","rel":"vice_president_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"t":"edge","ctx":"Vice president in the administration that armed Israel and vetoed four UNSC ceasefire resolutions.","id":"REL-U0079","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0272","ex":"the fourth veto of a UNSC Gaza ceasefire resolution under President Joe Biden's administration","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0278","ex":"\"@VP has not supported an arms embargo on Israel. She will continue to work to protect civilians in Gaza.\" ... \"People we love are being killed with American bombs\"","pg":null}],"pct":null,"date":null},{"a":"ORG-00008","b":"PER-NEW-HARRIS","rel":"donated_to_campaign_of","amt":6000000,"cur":"USD","t":"money","ctx":"More than $6 million raised for her 2024 campaign through J Street (Sludge, Oct 2024).","id":"REL-U0080","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0282","ex":"\"The Kamala Harris campaign has received more than $6 million from the pro-Israel lobbying group J Street\"","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0265","ex":"\"We are here to denounce the hypocrisy of our elected officials, Killer Kamala and Genocide Joe!\"","pg":null}],"pct":null,"date":null},{"a":"PER-00023","b":"PER-NEW-VANCE","rel":"funded_super_pac_for","amt":15000000,"cur":"USD","t":"money","ctx":"Thiel gave $15M to Protect Ohio Values super PAC for Vance's 2022 Senate run and employed him at Mithril Capital (CBS News).","id":"REL-U0081","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0284","ex":"\"Thiel made $15 million in donations to Vance's SuperPAC, Protect Ohio Values, a staggering amount from a single individual for a Senate race\" ... Thiel hired Vance at Mithril Capital","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0283","ex":"JD Vance ... $53,985 in pro-Israel PAC support in past federal races (2022)","pg":null}],"pct":null,"date":null},{"a":"PER-NEW-VANCE","b":"COM-00010","rel":"linked_via_patron","amt":null,"cur":null,"t":"edge","ctx":"Palantir, co-founded by his patron Thiel, partnered with Israel's military for 'war-related missions' (Jan 2024); UN rapporteur cites AI targeting.","id":"REL-U0082","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0285","ex":"\"Both parties have mutually agreed to harness Palantir's advanced technology in support of war-related missions.\"","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0288","ex":"\"signed a declaration to use emergency authorities to expedite the delivery of approximately $4 billion in military assistance to Israel\" ... over 35,500 MK 84 and BLU-117 bombs","pg":null}],"pct":null,"date":null},{"a":"PER-NEW-VANCE","b":"PER-N-TRUMP","rel":"vice_president_to","amt":null,"cur":null,"t":"edge","ctx":"Vice president in the administration that rushed ~$4B in arms to Israel in March 2025 and launched the war on Iran in Feb 2026.","id":"REL-U0083","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0288","ex":"\"signed a declaration to use emergency authorities to expedite the delivery of approximately $4 billion in military assistance to Israel\" ... over 35,500 MK 84 and BLU-117 bombs","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0289","ex":"\"I don't think that the Israelis are purposely trying to go in and murder every Palestinian.\"","pg":null}],"pct":null,"date":null},{"a":"PER-NEW-VANCE","b":"CTY-00001","rel":"political_support_for","amt":null,"cur":null,"t":"edge","ctx":"Rejected the genocide charge (June 2025); defended the 2025 and 2026 US-Israeli strikes and war on Iran.","id":"REL-U0084","st":"reported","ev":[{"s":"SRC-W0293","ex":"\"I wouldn't call it a war. Right now, there is no active shooting.\" ... US-Israeli war on Iran","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-W0284","ex":"\"Thiel made $15 million in donations to Vance's SuperPAC, Protect Ohio Values, a staggering amount from a single individual for a Senate race\" ... Thiel hired Vance at Mithril Capital","pg":null}],"pct":null,"date":null}],"facts":[{"id":"FIN-00001","t":"financial","a":"COM-00001","b":null,"rel":"revenue","amt":238300000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023–2025","st":"documented","ctx":"Company-wide figures;","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0093","ex":"Sales of $88.6 billion, up 10 percent versus prior year (FY2025); FY2024 sales $80,738M; FY2023 sales $68,920M","pg":"Consolidated statement of operations"}]},{"id":"FIN-00002","t":"financial","a":"COM-00001","b":null,"rel":"profit_or_net_earnings","amt":14700000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023–2025","st":"documented","ctx":"Company-wide figures;","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0093","ex":"Net income attributable to common shareowners: $6,732M (2025); $4,774M (2024); $3,195M (2023)","pg":"Consolidated statement of operations"}]},{"id":"FIN-00003","t":"financial","a":"COM-00001","b":null,"rel":"revenue","amt":46800000