 months"}]},{"id":"FIN-00049","t":"financial","a":"COM-00007","b":null,"rel":"backlog_or_reported_stat","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026","st":"documented","ctx":"Record $32B backlog","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0108","ex":"Order backlog as of June 30, 2026: $32.0 billion","pg":"Backlog"}],"amt/cur/date":"32000000000 / USD / as of 2026-06-30"},{"id":"FIN-00050","t":"financial","a":"COM-00008","b":null,"rel":"revenue","amt":18820000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023–2025","st":"documented","ctx":"Company-wide figures;","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0109","ex":"Sales (USD millions): 2025 7,384; 2024 6,112; 2023 5,327","pg":"p. 15, Consolidated Statements of Profit or Loss"}]},{"id":"FIN-00051","t":"financial","a":"COM-00008","b":null,"rel":"profit_or_net_earnings","amt":1520000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023–2025","st":"documented","ctx":"Company-wide figures;","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0109","ex":"Net income (USD millions): 2025 712; 2024 493; 2023 318","pg":"p. 15, Consolidated Statements of Profit or Loss"}]},{"id":"FIN-00052","t":"financial","a":"COM-00008","b":null,"rel":"revenue","amt":4280000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"H1 2026","st":"documented","ctx":"Company-wide figures;","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0110","ex":"Sales in H1 2026 reached USD 4,275 million compared with USD 3,228 million in H1 2025.","pg":"Press release"}]},{"id":"FIN-00053","t":"financial","a":"COM-00008","b":null,"rel":"profit_or_net_earnings","amt":449000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"H1 2026","st":"documented","ctx":"Company-wide figures;","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0110","ex":"40% increase in net income in H1 2026 to USD 449 million compared with USD 320 million in H1 2025.","pg":"Press release"}]},{"id":"FIN-00054","t":"financial","a":"COM-00008","b":null,"rel":"cumulative_revenue","amt":23100000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023–H1 2026","st":"documented","ctx":"Company-wide figures;","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0109","ex":"Sales: 2025 $7,384m; 2024 $6,112m; 2023 $5,327m (consolidated statement of profit or loss)","pg":"p.15, Consolidated Statement of Profit or Loss"}]},{"id":"FIN-00055","t":"financial","a":"COM-00008","b":null,"rel":"cumulative_profit","amt":1970000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023–H1 2026","st":"documented","ctx":"Company-wide figures;","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0109","ex":"Net income: 2025 $712m; 2024 $493m; 2023 $318m","pg":"p.15, Consolidated Statement of Profit or Loss"}]},{"id":"FIN-00056","t":"financial","a":"COM-00008","b":null,"rel":"backlog_or_reported_stat","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026","st":"reported","ctx":"(unchanged)","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0111","ex":"First-half revenue reached $4.275 billion, compared with $3.88 billion in the same period last year. ... first-half net profit jumping 40% to $449 million from $320 million ... order backlog also climbed to an all-time high of $35 billion","pg":null},{"s":"SRC-0110","ex":"The Company's order backlog leaped to USD 35 billion, representing 4.7 years of operation compared with USD 29 billion at the end of FY25.","pg":null}],"amt/cur/date/source":"35000000000 / USD / as of 2026-06-30 (IAI press release)"},{"id":"FIN-00057","t":"financial","a":"COM-00009","b":null,"rel":"revenue","amt":15400000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023–2025","st":"reported","ctx":"Rafael Advanced Defense Systems is an Israeli state-owned arms company that reports in shekels. Its sales rose from NIS 14.0bn in 2023 to NIS 17.8bn in 2024 and NIS 21.7bn in 2025. Using the company's own dollar figures, that is about $3.8B, $4.8–4.9B and $6.8B.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0112","ex":"2025: Sales $6.8 billion; net profit $423 million; order backlog $23.3 billion. 2024: Sales $4.9B; net profit $260M; backlog $17.8B.","pg":null}]},{"id":"FIN-00058","t":"financial","a":"COM-00009","b":null,"rel":"profit_or_net_earnings","amt":840000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023–2025","st":"reported","ctx":"Rafael's reported net profit rose from NIS 588m in 2023 to NIS 950m in 2024 and NIS 1.35bn in 2025. The company's dollar figures for those years are about $157M, $257–260M and $423M. These are company-wide results, not results attributable to any single war.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0112","ex":"2025 net profit $423 million; 2024 net profit $260M","pg":null}]},{"id":"FIN-00059","t":"financial","a":"COM-00009","b":null,"rel":"revenue","amt":10630000000,"cur":"ILS","pct":null,"date":"H1 2026","st":"reported","ctx":"H1 2026 sales (reported in ILS). Company-wide.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0113","ex":"H1 2026 sales 10.63 billion NIS (growth of 13.6%); Q2 2026 sales 5.68 billion NIS","pg":null}]},{"id":"FIN-00060","t":"financial","a":"COM-00009","b":null,"rel":"profit_or_net_earnings","amt":663000000,"cur":"ILS","pct":null,"date":"H1 2026","st":"reported","ctx":"H1 2026 net profit (reported in ILS). Company-wide;","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0113","ex":"H1 2026 net profit 663 million NIS (growth of ~8%); Q2 2026 ~329 million NIS","pg":null}]},{"id":"FIN-00061","t":"financial","a":"COM-00009","b":null,"rel":"cumulative_revenue","amt":18900000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023–H1 2026","st":"reported","ctx":"Approximate: sum of annual figures 2023-2025 plus H1 2026 converted to USD. Company-wide.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0113","ex":"H1 2026 sales 10.63 billion NIS","pg":null}]},{"id":"FIN-00062","t":"financial","a":"COM-00009","b":null,"rel":"cumulative_profit","amt":1053000000,"cur":"USD","pct":null,"date":"2023–H1 2026","st":"reported","ctx":"Rafael's company-wide net profit from 2023 through June 2026 is about $1.05 billion when its own dollar figures are combined with NIS 663m for H1 2026. Net profit for H1 2026 was up 8% year on year in shekels.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0113","ex":"H1 2026: sales NIS 10.63bn (+13.6%); net profit 663 million NIS (+8% y/y); in USD terms net profit grew ~28% in H1; order backlog grew 33% versus the corresponding period.","pg":null}]},{"id":"FIN-00063","t":"financial","a":"COM-00009","b":null,"rel":"backlog_or_reported_stat","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":"2026","st":"reported","ctx":"Rafael reported a consolidated order backlog of about NIS 74.4bn at the end of 2025, per its 2025 annual report. The backlog rose to NIS 76.4bn (about $24B) by 31 March 2026.","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0114","ex":"Order Backlog: 76.4 billion shekels, or $24 billion, up 23% year-on-year; net profit 334 million shekels (Q1 2026).","pg":null}]},{"id":"LOB-0001","t":"lobbying","a":"ORG-00001","b":null,"rel":"501(c)(4) lobbying organization","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Lobbying / political engagement / education","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0133","ex":"Designated as a 501(c)(4)","pg":null}]},{"id":"LOB-0002","t":"lobbying","a":"ORG-00002","b":null,"rel":"Federal multicandidate PAC","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Direct candidate contributions","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0134","ex":"Monthly Membership Organization PAC - Qualified; Lobbyist/Registrant PAC; registered December 15, 2021","pg":null}]},{"id":"LOB-0003","t":"lobbying","a":"ORG-00003","b":null,"rel":"527 Super PAC","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Independent expenditures","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0135","ex":"Monthly Super PAC (Independent Expenditure-Only); Registration Date: January 3, 2022; Committee ID C00799031","pg":null}]},{"id":"LOB-0004","t":"lobbying","a":"ORG-00004","b":null,"rel":"Political organization","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Political advocacy / electoral activity","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0136","ex":"501(c)(4) - Civic leagues, social welfare organizations","pg":null}]},{"id":"LOB-0005","t":"lobbying","a":"ORG-00006","b":null,"rel":"Political organization","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Political advocacy / electoral activity","ev":[{"s":"SRC-0137","ex":"Designated as a 501(c)(4)","pg":null}]},{"id":"LOB-0006","t":"lobbying","a":"ORG-00010","b":null,"rel":"Christian Zionist advocacy organization","amt":null,"cur":null,"pct":null,"date":null,"st":"documented","ctx":"Adv