,000-lb penetrator with a JDAM kit (Airwars). Bellingcat documented BLU-109s with JDAM kits in US Department of Defense imagery from the 2026 war on Iran.","transfers":[{"date":"2023-late","what":"100 BLU-109 bombs delivered (reported)","value_usd":null,"src":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BLU-109_bomb"},{"date":"2025-02-07","what":"3,475 KMU-557 JDAM kits for BLU-109 (approved maximum)","value_usd":null,"src":"https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support"}],"status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00006","name":"GBU-39/B Small Diameter Bomb","aka":["SDB","SDB I","250-lb glide bomb"],"class":"guided bomb","form":"bomb","dims":{"length_m":1.8,"diameter_m":0.19,"span_m":1.61,"weight_kg":129},"specs":[{"k":"Weight","v":"285 lb (129 kg); '250-pound class'","src":["SRC-V0256"]},{"k":"Warhead","v":"36 lb (16 kg) AFX-757 insensitive explosive; penetrates >0.9 m of reinforced concrete","src":["SRC-V0256"]},{"k":"Guidance","v":"GPS/INS","src":["SRC-0028"]},{"k":"Accuracy (CEP)","v":"about 1 m","src":["SRC-V0256"]},{"k":"Range","v":"more than 40 nmi (US Air Force); over 60 nmi air-dropped (Wikipedia)","src":["SRC-0028"]},{"k":"Unit cost","v":"about $40,000 (FY2021)","src":["SRC-0028"]},{"k":"Fragment hazard","v":"113 kg bombs that can throw metal fragments hundreds of metres (Amnesty)","src":["SRC-W0122"]},{"k":"Earlier Israeli buys","v":"3,450 (2012) and 4,100 (2015)","src":["SRC-V0256"]}],"makers":[{"entity":"COM-00003","role":"prime","src":["SRC-0028"]},{"entity":"MBDA Inc (Huntsville, Alabama; MBDA group)","role":"wings ('sole known supplier', Disclose)","src":["SRC-W0123"]}],"parts":[{"name":"Penetrating warhead (AFX-757)","maker":"COM-00003","start":0,"end":0.55,"note":"16 kg explosive.","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0064"