W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0103","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0093","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0062","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0094","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0062","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0073"]}],"summary":"The GBU-39 is Boeing's 129-kg satellite-guided glide bomb; MBDA Inc in Alabama makes its wings, according to Disclose. Israel bought 3,450 in 2012 and 4,100 in 2015; on 7 February 2025 the US notified 2,166 more, an approved maximum. It has become a signature weapon of strikes on shelters. OHCHR assessed four at al-Bureij camp (2 Nov 2023, 15 verified killed) and two at al-Buraq school (10 Nov 2023, at least 34 killed). Amnesty identified GBU-39s at the Nofal home in Tal al-Sultan (9 Jan 2024, 18 killed) and at the Kuwaiti Peace Camp in Rafah (26 May 2024, at least 36 killed). Bellingcat found GBU-39 remnants at 20 of 28 school strikes involving US munitions, including Khadija school and Fahmi al-Jarjawi. The Lebanese Army identified two in the Ain Saadeh strike of 5 April 2026.","transfers":[{"date":"2025-02-07","what":"2,166 GBU-39/B (approved maximum)","value_usd":null,"src":"https://www.dsca.mil/Press-Media/Major-Arms-Sales/Article-Display/Article/4060920/israel-munitions-guidance-kits-fuzes-and-munitions-support"},{"date":"2026-03","what":"Boeing contract for up to 5,000 Small Diameter Bombs for Israel, $289M (reported by Reuters citing Bloomberg; not fetched by us)","value_usd":289000000,"src":"https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/boeing-signs-289-million-israel-contract-5000-smart-bombs-bloomberg-news-reports-2026-03-10/"},{"date":"2012 / 2015","what":"3,450 and 4,100 GBU-39/B purchases","value_usd":null,"src":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GBU-39_Small_Diameter_Bomb"}],"status":"documented"},{"id":"ARS-MPR500","name":"MPR-500 multi-purpose bomb","aka":["MPR 500"],"class":"bomb","form":"bomb","dims":{"length_m":1.7,"diameter_m":0.273,"span_m":null,"weight_kg":230},"specs":[{"k":"Weight","v":"230 kg (510 lb)","src":["SRC-W0125"]},{"k":"Explosive","v":"89 kg HE","src":["SRC-W0125"]},{"k":"Guidance","v":"unguided body; compatible with Paveway II and GBU-38 JDAM kits","src":["SRC-W0125"]},{"k":"Maker","v":"Elbit Systems (previously IMI Systems)","src":["SRC-W0125"]},{"k":"Guidance found in Rafah","v":"precision guidance package with CAGE 0UVG2 (AeroAntenna, California)","src":["SRC-W0099"]},{"k":"Guidance found in Habbarieh","v":"US-made Boeing JDAM kit","src":["SRC-W0126"]}],"makers":[{"entity":"COM-00007","role":"prime / body (ex-IMI Systems)","src":["SRC-W0126"]},{"entity":"COM-00003","role":"tail kit (JDAM found with MPR-500 at Habbarieh)","src":["SRC-W0126"]},{"entity":"AeroAntenna Technology","role":"guidance package component (CAGE 0UVG2)","src":["SRC-W0099"]}],"parts":[{"name":"Bomb body with pre-formed fragments","maker":"COM-00007","start":0,"end":0.7,"note":"","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0084","SRC-W0106","SRC-W0124","SRC-W0088","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0087"]},{"name":"HE fill","maker":"COM-00007","start":0.1,"end":0.6,"note":"89 kg.","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0084","SRC-W0106","SRC-W0124","SRC-W0088","SRC-W0087","SRC-W0087"]},{"name":"Guidance kit (JDAM)","maker":"COM-00003","start":0.7,"end":1,"note":"Antenna component by AeroAntenna (CAGE 0UVG2) at Rafah, 19 Apr 2024.","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0066","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0094","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0070","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0067","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0062","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0097","SRC-W0097","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0105","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0093","SRC-W0085","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0062","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0105","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0074","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0093","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0082","SRC-W0077","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0071","SRC-W0092","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0105","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0078","SRC-W0075","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0076","SRC-W0069","SRC-W0067"]}],"summary":"The MPR-500 is a 500-lb bomb made by Elbit Systems, which absorbed its original maker IMI Systems, and it shows how Israeli bomb bodies and US guidance combine. HRW found an Elbit-marked MPR-500 fitted with a Boeing JDAM kit at Habbarieh, South Lebanon, where a strike killed seven emergency and relief volunteers on 27 March 2024. In Rafah on 19 April 2024 Amnesty identified an MPR-500 whose guidance package carried CAGE code 0UVG2 of California's AeroAntenna; nine members of the Abu Radwan family, six of them children, were killed. The owner's outline linked the MPR-500 to the 16 April 2024 al-Maghazi strike, but Amnesty attributes that strike to small drone-launched precision munitions, not an MPR-500. Elbit supplies, by AOAV's account, about 80% of the Israeli army's land weapons and equipment.","transfers":[],"status":"documented"},{"id":"WPN-00007","name":"AGM-114 Hellfire","aka":["Hellfire","R9X variant"],"class":"missile","form":"missile","dims":{"length_m":1.6,"diameter_m":0.18,"span_m":0.33,"weight_kg":49},"specs":[{"k":"Weight","v":"45-49 kg (100-108 lb)","src":["SRC-V0259"]},{"k":"Warheads","v":"shaped charge, tandem anti-armour, metal-augmented charge or blast fragmentation (about 18-20 lb)","src":["SRC-V0259"]},{"k":"Guidance","v":"semi-active laser or millimetre-wave radar","src":["SRC-V0259"]},{"k":"Range","v":"0.5-11 km","src":["SRC-V0259"]},{"k":"Unit cost","v":"about $150,000 (FY2021)","src":["SRC-V0259"]},{"k":"Israeli launchers","v":"AH-64 Apache helicopters and drones","src":["SRC-V0259"]},{"k":"Feb 2025 sale","v":"3,000 missiles, $660M, deliveries from 2028","src":["SRC-0029"]}],"makers":[{"entity":"COM-00002","role":"prime (Troy, Alabama)","src":["SRC-0029"]},{"entity":"COM-00005","role":"seeker (AGM-114L Longbow only)","src":["SRC-V0259"]}],"parts":[{"name":"Seeker","maker":"COM-00002 (COM-00005 for AGM-114L)","start":0,"end":0.15,"note":"","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0