7","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0073","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0080","SRC-W0128","SRC-W0096","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0065","SRC-W0072","SRC-W0090","SRC-W0068","SRC-W0129"]}],"summary":"Spike is Rafael's family of electro-optically guided missiles, also built in Europe by EuroSpike with Diehl and Rheinmetall. A US Army Spike NLOS cost $249,966 in 2022. Israel fires it from ships, Apache helicopters and Elbit's Hermes 450 drone, which can carry four. Its documented use in this period is mostly by platform: Israeli Apache crews interviewed by The War Zone said Spike was the main air-to-ground missile seen in photos of their 7 October 2023 missions, and Wikipedia records Spike NLOS strikes on the Gaza coastline in 2023. Some reporting claims Spikes fired from a Hermes 450 killed seven World Central Kitchen workers on 1 April 2024, but Bellingcat could not identify the munition without fragments. That strike stays unresolved here, and no event in this catalogue is attributed to Spike.","transfers":[],"status":"reported"},{"id":"ARS-M339","name":"M339 120mm HE-MP-T tank round","aka":["M339 multipurpose tank projectile"],"class":"tank round","form":"shell","dims":{"length_m":0.984,"diameter_m":0.12,"span_m":null,"weight_kg":27},"specs":[{"k":"Round weight","v":"about 27 kg (projectile 17 kg)","src":["SRC-W0130"]},{"k":"Cartridge length","v":"984 mm","src":["SRC-W0130"]},{"k":"Explosive","v":"2.3 kg CLX663","src":["SRC-W0130"]},{"k":"Fuze modes","v":"programmable: point detonation, point detonation delay, airburst","src":["SRC-W0130"]},{"k":"Effect","v":"penetrates reinforced concrete up to 200 mm","src":["SRC-W0130"]},{"k":"Platforms","v":"Merkava 3 and 4 and NATO 120mm smoothbore guns","src":["SRC-W0130"]}],"makers":[{"entity":"COM-00007","role":"prime (Elbit Systems Land, formerly IMI Systems)","src":["SRC-W0130"]}],"parts":[{"name":"Programmable fuze","maker":"COM-00007","start":0,"end":0.1,"note":"","src":["SRC-W0062","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0063","SRC-W0064","SRC-W0065","SR