s.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hermes-450.jpg"},"ARS-H900":{"data":"img/ca23f436dcf3f956.jpg","credit":"Photo: Nehemia Gershuni-Aylho / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hermes_900_Takeoff.jpg"},"ARS-MK84":{"data":"img/33bbbf0c7834b73a.jpg","credit":"Photo: STAFF SGT. LEE F. CORKRAN / Wikimedia Commons, Public domain","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mark-84_bomb.jpg"},"ARS-SPIKE":{"data":"img/72becf348927a7d2.jpg","credit":"Photo: Admiralis-generalis-Aladeen / Wikimedia Commons, CC0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spike_SR.jpg"},"PER-NEW-HARRIS":{"data":"img/417753894911f36d.jpg","credit":"Photo: Lawrence Jackson / Wikimedia Commons, Public domain","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kamala_Harris_Vice_Presidential_Portrait_(close_cropped).jpg"},"PER-NEW-VANCE":{"data":"img/b3a5f8c6f72bf094.jpg","credit":"Photo: Emily J. Higgins / Wikimedia Commons, Public domain","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:March_2026_Official_Vice_Presidential_Portrait_of_JD_Vance_(head-and-shoulders_cropped).jpg"},"CTY-G-IN":{"data":"img/9abd37e4d9b0c8d0.jpg","credit":"Photo: Prime Minister's Office / Wikimedia Commons, GODL-India","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prime_Minister_of_Bharat,_Shri_Narendra_Damodardas_Modi_is_welcomed_by_the_Prime_Minister_of_Israel,_Mr._Benjamin_Netanyahu_on_his_arrival_to_Israel.jpg"},"PER-NEW-BENGVIR":{"data":"img/62ae95310c964f61.jpg","credit":"Photo: דוד דנברג / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Itamar_Ben_Gvir_(portrait)_(3x4_cropped).jpg"},"PER-NEW-CUOMO":{"data":"img/f91111d08737d4d1.jpg","credit":"Photo: New York National Guard / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 2.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Governor_Andrew_Cuomo_in_2021_(cropped).jpg"},"PER-NEW-GALLANT":{"data":"img/3772b59338a0f756.jpg","credit":"Photo: Avi Ohayon / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yoav_Galant_1_(cropped).jpg"},"PER-NEW-GATES":{"data":"img/2ad51130f371f764.jpg","credit":"Photo: European Commission - Photographer: Lukasz Kobus / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 4.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bill_Gates_-_2023_-_P062021-967902_(cropped).jpg"},"PER-NEW-HERZOG":{"data":"img/80e69eef58c65124.jpg","credit":"Photo: U.S. Department of State / Wikimedia Commons, Public domain","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Israeli_President_Isaac_Herzog_in_2024_(cropped).jpg"},"PER-NEW-KATZ":{"data":"img/637731e206eabef3.jpg","credit":"Photo: U.S. Embassy Jerusalem / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 2.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Israel_Katz_on_July_3,_2024_(cropped).jpg"},"PER-NEW-MAMDANI":{"data":"img/6103e1c51ddb98dc.jpg","credit":"Photo: Karamccurdy / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_York_State_Assemblymember_Zohran_Mamdani.jpg"},"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH":{"data":"img/eb3c6eedb5d18844.jpg","credit":"Photo: איתן פולד. The original uploader was Atbannett at Hebrew Wikipedia. / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bezalel_Smotrich_(cropped).jpg"},"PER-NEW-BIDEN":{"data":"img/881b0b13ecf7b368.jpg","credit":"Photo: Adam Schultz / Wikimedia Commons, Public domain","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joe_Biden_presidential_portrait_(3x4_close_cropped).jpg"},"EVT-018":{"data":"img/ae33476c8213c314.jpg","credit":"Photo: IDF Spokesperson's Unit photographer / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Targetted-Killing-of-Muhammad-Deif,_I.jpg","cap":"Israeli aerial footage of the strike on the al-Mawasi displacement zone, Khan Younis, 13 July 2024, during the Gaza genocide. More than 90 Palestinians were killed in an area Israel had declared a safe zone."},"EVT-026":{"data":"img/82672d212b79f8ee.jpg","credit":"Photo: A.H.T Videomapping / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:White_Phosphorus_near_Lebanon,_October_16,_2023.jpg","cap":"White phosphorus smoke over the border area of South Lebanon, 16 October 2023, the day Amnesty International documented white phosphorus shelling of Dhayra."},"EVT-029":{"data":"img/ca014311c712234d.jpg","credit":"Photo: Unknown (CCTV footage) / Wikimedia Commons, Public domain","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CCTV_video_of_pager_explosion_in_a_Beirut_market.webm","cap":"Still from CCTV footage of a booby-trapped pager exploding in a Beirut market on 17 September 2024, one of thousands detonated across Lebanon that day in the attacks on civilian spaces."},"EVT-034":{"data":"img/caf4f26401edc282.jpg","credit":"Photo: Jimmyp84 / Wikimedia Commons, CC0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hezbollah_Headquarter_Airstrike_2024.jpg","cap":"Smoke over Haret Hreik in Beirut's southern suburbs after the 27 September 2024 strike that killed Hassan Nasrallah, during the destruction of South Lebanon. Residential buildings were flattened."},"EVT-035":{"data":"img/f2f3a9c8c98bfe6a.jpg","credit":"Photo: Hamed Malekpour / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 4.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2024_Bachoura_strike.jpg","cap":"Aftermath of the 10 October 2024 Israeli strike on residential buildings in Bachoura, central Beirut."},"EVT-038":{"data":"img/1313dd4d99a10820.jpg","credit":"Photo: שלמה רודד / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 2.5","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:129817_the_lebanese_shiite_village_of_kila_in_ruins_PikiWiki_Israel.jpg","cap":"Kfar Kila in ruins, April 2025: one of the South Lebanon border villages razed by Israel in the destruction of the southern border belt."},"EVT-049":{"data":"img/68d75e8ece9d3132.jpg","credit":"Photo: Megaphone / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:8_April_2026_Isreali_attacks_on_Beirut_(2).jpg","cap":"Rescuers at a destroyed building in Beirut on 8 April 2026, when Israel launched more than 100 strikes on Lebanon in under 10 minutes."},"EVT-051":{"data":"img/ab4aca44670968e1.jpg","credit":"Photo: United States Air Force / Wikimedia Commons, Public domain","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_B-2_Spirit_supports_Operation_MIDNIGHT_HAMMER.jpg","cap":"A US B-2 bomber prepared at Whiteman Air Force Base for Operation Midnight Hammer, the 22 June 2025 US strikes on Iran's nuclear sites during Israel's war on Iran."},"EVT-052":{"data":"img/3ce5f95f67aa54fd.jpg","credit":"Photo: Abbas Zakeri / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 4.0","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shajareh_Tayyebeh_school_in_Minab_photos_from_Mehr_(9).jpg","cap":"Rescuers dig through the rubble of the Shajareh Tayyebeh girls' school in Minab, Iran, on 28 February 2026, the day it was struck during Israel's war on Iran."}},"profits":{"PER-NEW-BENGVIR":{"usd":669424,"metric":"salary since Jan 2023, estimate","period":null,"src":"SRC-W0007","note":"Estimate: 43 months (Jan 2023 to Sep 2026 minus the two-month gap in 2025) x $15,568/month gross, the May 2025 rate reported by the Times of Israel. Salary only; earlier rates were lower, so this slightly overstates. No documented personal enrichment."},"PER-NEW-SMOTRICH":{"usd":700560,"metric":"salary since Jan 2023, estimate","period":null,"src":"SRC-W0007","note":"Estimate: 45 months (Jan 2023 to Sep 2026) x $15,568/month gross, the May 2025 rate reported by the Times of Israel. Salary only; earlier rates were lower, so this slightly overstates. No documented personal enrichment."},"PER-NEW-GALLANT":{"usd":342496,"metric":"salary since Jan 2023, estimate","period":null,"src":"SRC-W0007","note":"Estimate: 22 months (Jan 2023 to Sep 2026 cut to Jan 2023 to Oct 2024, his time as minister) x $15,568/month gross, the May 2025 rate reported by the Times of Israel. Salary only; earlier rates were lower, so this slightly overstates. No documented personal enrichment."},"PER-NEW-KATZ":{"usd":700560,"metric":"salary since Jan 2023, estimate","period":null,"src":"SRC-W0007","note":"Estimate: 45 months (Jan 2023 to Sep 2026) x $15,568/month gross, the May 2025 rate reported by the Times of Israel. Salary only; earlier rates were lower, so this slightly overstates. No documented personal enrichment."},"PER-NEW-HERZOG":{"usd":844380,"metric":"salary since Jan 2023, estimate","period":null,"src":"SRC-W0007","note":"Estimate: 45 months (Jan 2023 to Sep 2026) x $18,764/month gross, the May 2025 rate reported by the Times of Israel. Salary only; earlier rates were lower, so this slightly overstates. No documented personal enrichment."},"PER-NEW-GATES":{"usd":10200000000,"metric":"net worth change since Jan 2023","period":"2023-03-10 to 2026-10-03","src":"SRC-W0032","note":"Forbes net worth $104B (2023-03-10) to $114.2B (2026-10-03). Closest documented baseline to Jan 2023 is the Forbes 2023 list (prices of 10 Mar 2023). No node yet for Bill Gates."},"COM-00001":{"usd":18899000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-0093","note":"2023 $3.20B; 2024 $4.77B; 2025 $6.73B; H1 2026 $4.20B (net income attributable to common shareowners)."},"COM-00002":{"usd":20597000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-0095","note":"2023 $6.92B; 2024 $5.34B; 2025 $5.02B; H1 2026 $3.32B."},"COM-00003":{"usd":-12268000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-0097","note":"2023 -$2.24B; 2024 -$11.83B; 2025 $2.24B; H1 2026 -$435M. A cumulative loss driven by the commercial jet business; its weapons unit kept supplying JDAM kits and bombs to Israel."},"COM-00004":{"usd":13592000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-W0119","note":"2023 $3.32B; 2024 $3.78B; 2025 $4.21B; H1 2026 $2.29B."},"COM-00005":{"usd":12375000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-W0120","note":"2023 $2.05B; 2024 $4.17B; 2025 $4.18B; H1 2026 $1.97B."},"COM-00006":{"usd":9629240000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-0104","note":"Profit for the year: 2023 £1.94B; 2024 £2.04B; 2025 £2.15B; H1 2026 £1.05B. Total £7.19B, converted at $1.34 per £."},"COM-00007":{"usd":1404900000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-W0121","note":"Elbit's own reports, net income attributable to shareholders: 2023 $215.1M; 2024 $321.1M; 2025 $534.3M; H1 2026 $334.4M. Profit grew about 2.5 times from 2023 to 2025."},"COM-00008":{"usd":1972000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-0109","note":"IAI's own statements: 2023 $318M; 2024 $493M; 2025 $712M; H1 2026 $449M."},"COM-00009":{"usd":683000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2024 to FY2025 in USD (plus NIS amounts below)","src":"SRC-W0122","note":"2023 NIS 588M; 2024 $260M; 2025 $423M; H1 2026 NIS 663M. usd counts only the two USD-reported years; the NIS years are left unconverted."},"COM-00010":{"usd":4229400000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-V0337","note":"2023 $209.8M; 2024 $462.2M; 2025 $1,625M; H1 2026 $1,932.4M (attributable to common stockholders). Its H1 2026 profit alone exceeds its 2023 and 2024 combined by about four times."},"COM-00011":{"usd":260243000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-W0123","note":"2023 $30.4B; 2024 $59.2B; 2025 $77.7B; Q1 2026 $30.3B; Q2 2026 $62.6B. Q2 2026 profit more than tripled from $18.2B a year earlier."},"COM-00013":{"usd":480854000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-W0124","note":"2023 $73.8B; 2024 $100.1B; 2025 $132.2B; H1 2026 $174.8B (vs $62.7B in H1 2025)."},"COM-00016":{"usd":396078000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to FY2026 (years to 30 June)","src":"SRC-W0125","note":"FY2023 $72.4B; FY2024 $88.1B; FY2025 $101.8B; FY2026 $133.7B. Microsoft's fiscal year ends 30 June, so FY2023 starts July 2022."},"COM-00019":{"usd":53130000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to Q1 FY2027 (years to 31 May; Q1 FY27 to 31 Aug 2026)","src":"SRC-W0126","note":"FY2023 $8.5B; FY2024 $10.5B; FY2025 $12.4B; FY2026 $17.0B; Q1 FY2027 $4.76B. FY2023 starts June 2022."},"COM-00024":{"usd":1905880000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2024 to FY2025","src":"SRC-V0339","note":"Earnings after taxes: 2024 €808M; 2025 €835M (total €1.64B at $1.16 per €). 2023 not verified. 2026: Q1 net income €111M and Q2 earnings after taxes €167M reported by secondary sources, not added because the two use different measures."},"COM-00025":{"usd":4245600000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-W0127","note":"Net result: 2023 €711M (pro-forma); 2024 €1,159M; 2025 €1,334M; H1 2026 €456M. Total €3.66B at $1.16 per €."},"COM-00029":{"usd":159600000,"metric":"net income","period":"H1 2026 only","src":"SRC-0022","note":"H1 2026 profit after tax $159.6M (H1 2025 $110.5M). 2023 to 2025 not verified in this pass."},"COM-NEW-CATERPILLAR":{"usd":36153000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-W0128","note":"Profit: 2023 $10.34B; 2024 $10.79B; 2025 $8.88B; H1 2026 $6.14B."},"FND-00001":{"usd":21550000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-W0129","note":"Net income attributable to BlackRock: 2023 $5.50B; 2024 $6.37B; 2025 $5.55B; H1 2026 $4.13B."},"FND-00003":{"usd":8849000000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-W0130","note":"2023 $1.82B and 2025 $2.7B are net income available to common shareholders; 2024 $2.48B (secondary); H1 2026 $1.85B is net income (Q1 $764M + Q2 $1,084M). Mixed measures, so treat the total as approximate."},"FND-00004":{"usd":12700000000,"metric":"operating income (private firm)","period":"FY2025","src":"SRC-W0131","note":"Fidelity is private. It reported 2025 operating income of $12.7B on revenue of $37.7B; 2024 revenue $32.7B. Operating income for 2023 and 2024 not verified, so usd is 2025 only."},"COM-NEW-BLACKSTONE":{"usd":9065600000,"metric":"net income","period":"FY2023 to H1 2026","src":"SRC-W0132","note":"Net income attributable to Blackstone: 2023 $1.39B; 2024 $2.78B; 2025 $3.02B; H1 2026 $1.88B."},"PER-00004":{"usd":131015970,"metric":"pay 2023–2025","period":"FY2026 (to 31 May 2026)","src":"SRC-V0352","note":"Only Oracle FY2026 is in site data: $131.0M, mostly stock awards."},"PER-00024":{"usd":257200000000,"metric":"net worth change since Jan 2023","period":"2023-03-10 to 2026-10-05","src":"SRC-V0218","note":"Forbes net worth $114B (2023-03-10) to $371.2B (2026-10-05). Closest documented baseline to Jan 2023 is the Forbes 2023 list (prices of 10 Mar 2023). "},"PER-NEW-BLOOMBERG":{"usd":400000000,"metric":"net worth change since Jan 2023","period":"2023-03-10 to 2026-10-04","src":"SRC-W0039","note":"Forbes net worth $94.5B (2023-03-10) to $94.9B (2026-10-04). Closest documented baseline to Jan 2023 is the Forbes 2023 list (prices of 10 Mar 2023). "},"PER-00009":{"usd":-3600000000,"metric":"net worth change since Jan 2023","period":"2023-03-10 to 2026-09-27","src":"SRC-V0189","note":"Forbes net worth $35B (2023-03-10) to $31.4B (2026-09-27). Closest documented baseline to Jan 2023 is the Forbes 2023 list (prices of 10 Mar 2023). "},"PER-00008":{"usd":4900000000,"metric":"net worth change since Jan 2023","period":"2023-03-10 to 2026-09-19","src":"SRC-V0187","note":"Forbes net worth $13.7B (2023-03-10) to $18.6B (2026-09-19). Closest documented baseline to Jan 2023 is the Forbes 2023 list (prices of 10 Mar 2023). "},"PER-N-TRUMP":{"usd":4400000000,"metric":"net worth change since Jan 2023","period":"2023-10 to 2026-10-04","src":"SRC-V0016","note":"Forbes $2.6B (Oct 2023 Forbes 400 estimate) to $7B (4 Oct 2026); more than 2.5 times richer during his second term."},"PER-00013":{"usd":72302000,"metric":"pay 2023–2025","period":"2023–2025","src":"SRC-0115","note":"$22.6M (2023), $23.8M (2024), $25.9M (2025); site rel BEN-0001."},"PER-00012":{"usd":70021000,"metric":"pay 2023–2025","period":"2023–2025","src":"SRC-0116","note":"$22.8M, $23.8M, $23.5M; site rel BEN-0002.